PAU_KHARIF_2026:pdf_page_4:001,PAU_KHARIF_2026,initial_verified_action_rag,Package of Practices for Crops of Punjab — Kharif 2026,Punjab Agricultural University,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,Punjab state,rice,fertilizer;crop_protection,https://www.pau.edu/content/ccil/pf/pp_kharif.pdf,2026-03-31,,March 2026,pdf_page_4,1,"12. Rational Use of Poor Quality Irrigation Water...........................................................155-157 13. Spray Technology.........................................................................................................158-159 14. Management of Rodents and Birds.............................................................................160-164 Annexure - I to X...................................................................................................................165-200 Annexure - I Minimum Support Price of Different Crops..........................................................165 Annexure - II District-wise Area, Production and Yield of various Kharif crops in Punjab during 2024-25...........................................................................................166 Annexure - III List of Bt cotton hybrids recommended for cultivation in Punjab state..................171 during Kharif 2026 Annexure IV(A) Field Standards for the Production of Foundation and Certified Seeds.............172 Annexure IV(B) Seed Certification Standards for Foundation and Certified Seeds.......................173 Annexure - V Agricultural",30142d84b17afce725fe48bc5458b03bc029f3d57734e322bf5290a84f7215c0
PAU_KHARIF_2026:pdf_page_4:002,PAU_KHARIF_2026,initial_verified_action_rag,Package of Practices for Crops of Punjab — Kharif 2026,Punjab Agricultural University,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,Punjab state,rice,fertilizer;crop_protection,https://www.pau.edu/content/ccil/pf/pp_kharif.pdf,2026-03-31,,March 2026,pdf_page_4,2,Engineering.......................................................................................174 Annexure - VI Grain Storage and Management of Stored Grain Insects......................................186 Annexure - VII Fertilizer Sources for the supply of Plant Nutrients...............................................188 Annexure - VIII Agricultural Accidents- Preventive and Curative Measures..............................190 Annexure - IX Antidotes for Pesticides for Human Beings............................................................194 Annexure - X Important Telephone Numbers of the Punjab Agricultural University.....................197,30142d84b17afce725fe48bc5458b03bc029f3d57734e322bf5290a84f7215c0
PAU_KHARIF_2026:pdf_page_5:001,PAU_KHARIF_2026,initial_verified_action_rag,Package of Practices for Crops of Punjab — Kharif 2026,Punjab Agricultural University,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,Punjab state,rice,fertilizer;crop_protection,https://www.pau.edu/content/ccil/pf/pp_kharif.pdf,2026-03-31,,March 2026,pdf_page_5,1,"NEW RECOMMENDATIONS CROP V ARIETIES PR 133 (Rice): It is medium duration variety with an average plant height of 109 cm. It matures in 111 days after transplanting and its average paddy yield is 30.5 quintals per acre. NK 7328 (Maize): This single cross hybrid matures in 99 days and its average grain yield is 24.7 quintals per acre. PBD 88 ( Desi Cotton): It is high yielding and shattering tolerant variety. Its average seed cotton yield is 10.9 quintals per acre. PRODUCTION TECHNIQUES Rice: Sow rice nursery on 1 metre wide beds in medium to heavy soils to produce healthy and vigorous seedlings. Mat-type rice nursery raised for mechanical transplanting can also be used for manual transplanting. Cotton: During field preparation before sowing cotton, the wheat straw left after combine harvesting should be incorporated into the soil using a rotavator or super seeder. Soak one acre of cotton seed for 2 hours in a solution of 100 mL Bacillus thaonhiensis diluted in 125-150 mL of water, then shade dry for 30 mintures before sowing to improve productivity. Sunnhemp intercropping in cotton and its incorporation as in-situ green manure after 1st irrigation (at 35-40 DAS), increases cotton",30142d84b17afce725fe48bc5458b03bc029f3d57734e322bf5290a84f7215c0
PAU_KHARIF_2026:pdf_page_5:002,PAU_KHARIF_2026,initial_verified_action_rag,Package of Practices for Crops of Punjab — Kharif 2026,Punjab Agricultural University,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,Punjab state,rice,fertilizer;crop_protection,https://www.pau.edu/content/ccil/pf/pp_kharif.pdf,2026-03-31,,March 2026,pdf_page_5,2,"yield and improves soil physical properties. Application of 120 kg urea (55 kg N) per acre is recommended to obtain higher yield in Bt cotton hybrids. Multiple cropping: Maize-Gobhi sarson+Toria-Mentha (relay crop) and Maize- Toria-Mentha cropping systems are recommended for higher productivity and profitability. Conservation agriculture based cropping systems such as “Direct Seeded Rice- Wheat, Maize/ Arhar-Wheat, Rice-Wheat-Summer Moong, Maize/Soybean-Wheat- Summer Moong” are recommended.",30142d84b17afce725fe48bc5458b03bc029f3d57734e322bf5290a84f7215c0
PAU_KHARIF_2026:pdf_page_6:001,PAU_KHARIF_2026,initial_verified_action_rag,Package of Practices for Crops of Punjab — Kharif 2026,Punjab Agricultural University,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,Punjab state,rice,fertilizer;crop_protection,https://www.pau.edu/content/ccil/pf/pp_kharif.pdf,2026-03-31,,March 2026,pdf_page_6,1,"PROTECTION TECHNIQUES Rice: To prevent the spread of rice dwarfing disease (caused by Southern rice black-streaked dwarf virus ), keep field bunds/channels weed-free, remove and bury infected plants, and spray recommended insecticides to control the vector. Cotton: Spray 240 mL per acre of Simodis 10 DC (isocycloseram) for the management of thrips. Moong and Mash: Spray 300 mL per acre of imazethapyr 10 SL at 15-20 days after sowing to control grassy, broadleaf weeds and sedges. Sugarcane: Apply 7.5 kg per acre of Ferterra 0.4 GR (chlorantraniliprole*) mixed with 20 kg moist soil for the management of early shoot borer. Spray 150 mL per acre of Markgen 18.5 SC (chlorantraniliprole*) for the management of early shoot borer in sugarcane. To control red rot and smut diseases, treat the sugarcane setts with 0.1% solution of Amistar Top 325 SC (azoxystrobin 18.2% + difenoconazole 11.4%) and spray the crop with 0.1 % solution of Amistar Top 325 SC at 60 and 90 days after planting. Rodent management in rice nursery: To reduce rodent damage, make 1.5 m wide water channel around the rice nursery and keep it filled with water especially at night. Details of above recommendations are provided",30142d84b17afce725fe48bc5458b03bc029f3d57734e322bf5290a84f7215c0
