ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_8:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_8,1,"FOREWORD This publication oﬀers practical guidance on region-based suitable varieties, nutrient management, pest and disease control, and harvesting practices tailored for major Kharif crops such as rice, maize, pulses, oilseeds, and cotton. It is the result of collaborative eﬀorts by ICAR Institutes, Agricultural Universities, Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs), and Subject Matter Experts working at the grassroots level. Agriculture in India stands at a critical juncture. While it continues to serve as the backbone of rural livelihoods, it faces unprecedented challenges due to climate variability, resource degradation, pest dynamics, and market volatility. In this context, the role of timely and location-speci␀ic agro-advisories has become more crucial than ever. These advisories act as a bridge between cutting-edge agricultural research and its practical application in farmers' ␀ields. I extend my heartfelt appreciation to all scientists, experts, and ␀ield professionals who have contributed to the preparation of this publication. I am con␀ident that this agro-advisory compilation will serve as a valuable resource for farmers during upcoming Kharif season, enabling them to make",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_8:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_8,2,"informed decisions that lead to improved productivity, pro␀itability, and sustainability. Let us move forward together to build a resilient, prosperous, and empowered farming community #Viksit Bharat 2047. Jai Kisan, Jai Vigyan! At ICAR, we remain committed to the vision of a knowledge-driven, inclusive, and sustainable agricultural system. The advisories compiled herein re␀lect our continuous eﬀorts to translate scienti␀ic knowledge from laboratories into actionable insights for every farmer. I urge extension of␀icers, KVK teams, farmer producer organizations (FPOs), and progressive farmers to widely disseminate and implement the recommendations provided in this book. (M.L. Jat) It is with great pleasure that I present the “ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025”- a timely and comprehensive guide developed to empower India's farming community with science-based, region-speci␀ic advisories for the upcoming Kharif season. This publication marks a signi␀icant step toward strengthening climate- resilient agriculture and enhancing farm productivity across diverse agro-climatic zones. Dr. M.L. Jat Secretary (DARE) & Director General (ICAR) (v) lR;eso t;rs",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
