ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_15:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_15,1,CONTENTS Messages i Preface vii Foreword v S.No. Particulars Page No. Executive Summary ix 1. Andaman and Nicobar Islands 1 2. Andhra Pradesh 5 3. Arunachal Pradesh 19 4. Assam 24 5. Bihar 32 6. Chhattisgarh 39 7. Goa 46 8. Gujarat 49 9. Haryana & Delhi 61 10. Himachal Pradesh 68 11. Jammu and Kashmir 83 12. Jharkhand 104 13. Karnataka 110 14. Kerala 120 15. Ladakh 125 16. Lakshadweep 131 17. Madhya Pradesh 133 18. Maharashtra 139 19. Manipur 162 20. Meghalaya 168 21. Mizoram 172 22. Nagaland 178 23. Odisha 187 24. Punjab 191 25. Rajasthan 209 26. Sikkim 233 27. Tamil Nadu & Puducherry 237 28. Telangana 243 29. Tripura 250 30. Uttar Pradesh 253 31. Uttarakhand 264 32. West Bengal 280 33. List of Contributors 293,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_16:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_16,1,"1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands The Andaman and Nicobar Islands have a warm, humid tropical climate with high annual rainfall and fertile loamy soils, making them well-suited for diverse agricultural activities. The climatic conditions are ideal for cultivating paddy along with plantation crops such as coconut and arecanut. Major fruit crops include banana, mango, sapota, papaya, pineapple, and citrus, while vegetables like brinjal, okra, chilli, cowpea and cucurbits, tuber crops- tapioca, sweet potato, dioscorea and elephant foot yam as well as spices-black pepper, cinnamon, turmeric and ginger are also widely grown. CEREAL CROPS Rice Recommended varieties of medium duration are Dweep Dhan 1,2,3,6 and 7, Jaya, ANR-47, and Gayatri whereas long duration varieties are Dweep Dhan 4, 5 and ANR 40. Soak paddy seeds in normal water for 12-24 hours, discard the ␀loating seeds, and use only the fully submerged seeds for sowing. It is recommended to treat seeds with Bijamrut @ 300 ml/kg seed. About 1000 m² nursery area is adequate for one hectare of ␀ield. Apply FYM @ 10q or vermicompost @ 5 q along with along Azospirillum @ 2 kg/1000 m² at 2-3 days prior to sowing in nursery. For nursery,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_16:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_16,2,"prepare beds of 10 m × 1.25 m; apply 20-30 kg FYM per bed. Maintain a 30 cm drainage channel between beds. Sow 650-1000 g of sprouted seed per bed. Maintain saturated condition of 2-3 cm standing water 2-3 days before uprooting seedlings. Before transplanting, root dipping of seedlings with Jeevamrit @ 50 ml/L may be followed for better establishment. In main ␀ield, spacing should be maintained by 20 cm x 20 cm in ICM and 25 cm x 25 cm for SRI methods. Apply either FYM@ 2.6 t/ha or vermicompost @2.5 t/ha in the main ␀ield. Cono-weeder can be used for weeding purpose. Ensure bunds are repaired and 20-30 cm high to retain water. Use neem-based formulations (@ 0.5% or 5 ml/L) 2-3 times for pest control.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_17:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_17,1,"1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands The Andaman and Nicobar Islands have a warm, humid tropical climate with high annual rainfall and fertile loamy soils, making them well-suited for diverse agricultural activities. The climatic conditions are ideal for cultivating paddy along with plantation crops such as coconut and arecanut. Major fruit crops include banana, mango, sapota, papaya, pineapple, and citrus, while vegetables like brinjal, okra, chilli, cowpea and cucurbits, tuber crops- tapioca, sweet potato, dioscorea and elephant foot yam as well as spices-black pepper, cinnamon, turmeric and ginger are also widely grown. CEREAL CROPS Rice Recommended varieties of medium duration are Dweep Dhan 1,2,3,6 and 7, Jaya, ANR-47, and Gayatri whereas long duration varieties are Dweep Dhan 4, 5 and ANR 40. Soak paddy seeds in normal water for 12-24 hours, discard the ␀loating seeds, and use only the fully submerged seeds for sowing. It is recommended to treat seeds with Bijamrut @ 300 ml/kg seed. About 1000 m² nursery area is adequate for one hectare of ␀ield. Apply FYM @ 10q or vermicompost @ 5 q along with along Azospirillum @ 2 kg/1000 m² at 2-3 days prior to sowing in nursery. For nursery,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_17:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_17,2,"prepare beds of 10 m × 1.25 m; apply 20-30 kg FYM per bed. Maintain a 30 cm drainage channel between beds. Sow 650-1000 g of sprouted seed per bed. Maintain saturated condition of 2-3 cm standing water 2-3 days before uprooting seedlings. Before transplanting, root dipping of seedlings with Jeevamrit @ 50 ml/L may be followed for better establishment. In main ␀ield, spacing should be maintained by 20 cm x 20 cm in ICM and 25 cm x 25 cm for SRI methods. Apply either FYM@ 2.6 t/ha or vermicompost @2.5 t/ha in the main ␀ield. Cono-weeder can be used for weeding purpose. Ensure bunds are repaired and 20-30 cm high to retain water. Use neem-based formulations (@ 0.5% or 5 ml/L) 2-3 times for pest control.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 FRUIT AND VEGETABLE CROPS To establish a new coconut orchard, plant 12 month-old, healthy, disease-free seedlings with vigorous growth at a spacing of 7.5 m × 7.5 m in 1 m³ pits enriched with organic matter such as compost or farmyard manure. To rejuvenate old gardens, replace unproductive palms with high-yielding varieties like Andaman Ordinary Tall, Katchal Tall, Dweep Annapurna, Dweep Harita and Dweep Sona. For the management of rhinoceros beetles, place naphthalene balls (10 g/palm) in the leaf axils and use pheromone or bio-traps to attract and control the beetles. For diseases like bud rot or stem bleeding, spray a 1% Bordeaux mixture and improve drainage conditions. Fruit crops such as banana, papaya, and pineapple; spices like cinnamon, black pepper, clove, nutmeg, ginger, and turmeric; and tuber crops like elephant foot yam are suitable for cultivation in the Islands. Arecanut Recommended varieties are Samrudhi and Mangala. Seedlings aged 12-18 months with ␀ive or more leaves are preferred for transplanting in the main ␀ield. Regularly remove dried leaves and maintain clean basins around the plants. Intercropping with legumes, spices, or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,2,"vegetables is encouraged in young plantations to enhance income and improve soil fertility. Select well-drained, loamy soil and prepare raised beds or ridges to prevent water stagnation due to high rainfall during the kharif season. For fruit crops, ensure planting in high and well-drained locations; use trench or pit method. Apply well-decomposed FYM @ 10-15 kg/pit before planting and mulch with organic material to retain moisture and control weeds. For vegetable crops, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride or Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 10 g/kg to avoid soil-borne diseases. Use raised nursery beds with good drainage to avoid waterlogging. Grow legumes such as cowpea or sunhemp as cover crops and incorporate them into the soil to ␀ix atmospheric nitrogen. Ensure timely weeding and earthing-up. Use organic mulching or black polythene to conserve soil moisture and suppress weed growth. For vegetable crops, use FYM@10 t/ha, neem cake @ 100 kg/ha and vermicompost @ 5t/ha to supply proper nutrients. Monitor regularly for pests like fruit borers, white␀lies and sucking and for control use neem oil @ 5 ml/L or install pheromone and sticky traps. For fungal diseases, use copper oxychloride as",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,3,"per symptoms. Ensure proper drainage, especially in low-lying ␀ields. During dry spells, provide life-saving irrigation. Harvest fruits and vegetables at proper maturity to avoid post-harvest losses and use shade nets for temporary storage. SPICES Black Pepper Coconut Apply 10 kg FYM, 500 g neem cake, 500 g wood ash and 2 kg vermicompost per vine annually. Also apply biofertilizers- Azospirillum and phosphorus-solubilizing bacteria 20 g each per vine. Use biocontrol agents like Trichoderma (50 g) and Pseudomonas ␀luorescens (50 g) per vine disease control. For foliar diseases, apply 1% Bordeaux mixture and neem oil (5 ml/L of water). Incorporate coir pith compost at 1.25 t/ha to enhance soil fertility. Andaman & Nicobar Islands Use raised beds or ridges for better drainage. Treat planting materials with Trichoderma to prevent rots. Use high-yielding varieties for sweet potato- CIARI Swarna, CIARI Aparna and Bhu Sona; for Cassava- Sree Vijaya and Sree Jaya; for elephant foot yam- Gajendra; for Taro- Mega Taro -2, Sree Kiran, Sree Pallavi and Sree Rashmi; and for dioscorea- Nicobari Alu (Traditional variety). Apply compost (10-15 t/ha) and biofertilizers like Azospirillum and PSB.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,4,"Install pheromone traps- one trap/100 m² area to control sweet potato weevil. Prefer well-drained, loamy soils rich in organic matter for planting. Prepare raised beds of 15 cm height and 1 m width, ensuring proper drainage. Incorporate organic manures like FYM at 25-30 t/ha during bed preparation. Use healthy and disease- free rhizome for planting. Treat seed rhizomes with Trichoderma harzianum before planting to prevent fungal diseases. Apply neem cake at 2 t/ha and vermicompost at 5 t/ha. Also incorporate biofertilizers like Azospirillum and phosphate-solubilizing bacteria to enhance nutrient availability. Adopt crop rotation with legumes to break pest cycles. Use neem-based products and Trichoderma formulations to manage common pests and diseases. Follow strict bio-security measures-i) sprinkling of disinfectant solution (phenyl solution, bleaching powder and fumigation with KMnO₄ and formalin), ii) use of foot bath/tray at the entry of livestock/poultry shed with KMnO₄/phenyl/savlon at the farm. Deworm livestock/poultry and practice dipping with proper medicines suggested by the Veterinarians to prevent them from internal and external parasites infestations. Vaccinate",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,5,"livestock/ poultry to prevent them from diseases. Protect livestock/poultry from heavy rain and provide well ventilated shelter. Arti␀icial heat along with dry ␀loor space should be ensured for neonates to avoid neonatal mortality. Wound should be treated immediately with proper medication including topical application of ␀ly repellent ointment or spray to avoid development of myiasis (maggot wound). Trimming of hooves should be done in cattle to prevent foot-rots and other complications. Provide balanced feed for livestock/poultry preferably with home-made low-cost locally available feed ingredients viz. broken rice, rice Cinnamon Use healthy rhizomes (2000-2500 kg/ha) for planting and maintain spacing at 40 cm × 40 cm. Use Trichoderma for seed treatment and to control rhizome rot. Apply 20-25 t/ha of compost. Also mulch with locally available dry leaves to retain moisture and suppress weeds. Irrigate during dry spells but avoid waterlogging. Turmeric Ginger Root and Tuber Crops Transfer six months old seedlings to polythene bags when they attain a height of 15 cm. Employ air layering techniques during the ␀irst week of July, using coir pith compost as a rooting medium. Apply 10",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_18:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_18,6,kg of FYM/plant/year and mulch with leaves to retain soil moisture. Utilize neem-based products and Trichoderma formulations to manage common pests and diseases. LIVESTOCK 32,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_19:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_19,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 FRUIT AND VEGETABLE CROPS To establish a new coconut orchard, plant 12 month-old, healthy, disease-free seedlings with vigorous growth at a spacing of 7.5 m × 7.5 m in 1 m³ pits enriched with organic matter such as compost or farmyard manure. To rejuvenate old gardens, replace unproductive palms with high-yielding varieties like Andaman Ordinary Tall, Katchal Tall, Dweep Annapurna, Dweep Harita and Dweep Sona. For the management of rhinoceros beetles, place naphthalene balls (10 g/palm) in the leaf axils and use pheromone or bio-traps to attract and control the beetles. For diseases like bud rot or stem bleeding, spray a 1% Bordeaux mixture and improve drainage conditions. Fruit crops such as banana, papaya, and pineapple; spices like cinnamon, black pepper, clove, nutmeg, ginger, and turmeric; and tuber crops like elephant foot yam are suitable for cultivation in the Islands. Arecanut Recommended varieties are Samrudhi and Mangala. Seedlings aged 12-18 months with ␀ive or more leaves are preferred for transplanting in the main ␀ield. Regularly remove dried leaves and maintain clean basins around the plants. Intercropping with legumes, spices, or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_19:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_19,2,"vegetables is encouraged in young plantations to enhance income and improve soil fertility. Select well-drained, loamy soil and prepare raised beds or ridges to prevent water stagnation due to high rainfall during the kharif season. For fruit crops, ensure planting in high and well-drained locations; use trench or pit method. Apply well-decomposed FYM @ 10-15 kg/pit before planting and mulch with organic material to retain moisture and control weeds. For vegetable crops, treat seeds with Trichoderma viride or Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 10 g/kg to avoid soil-borne diseases. Use raised nursery beds with good drainage to avoid waterlogging. Grow legumes such as cowpea or sunhemp as cover crops and incorporate them into the soil to ␀ix atmospheric nitrogen. Ensure timely weeding and earthing-up. Use organic mulching or black polythene to conserve soil moisture and suppress weed growth. For vegetable crops, use FYM@10 t/ha, neem cake @ 100 kg/ha and vermicompost @ 5t/ha to supply proper nutrients. Monitor regularly for pests like fruit borers, white␀lies and sucking and for control use neem oil @ 5 ml/L or install pheromone and sticky traps. For fungal diseases, use copper oxychloride as",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_19:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_19,3,"per symptoms. Ensure proper drainage, especially in low-lying ␀ields. During dry spells, provide life-saving irrigation. Harvest fruits and vegetables at proper maturity to avoid post-harvest losses and use shade nets for temporary storage. SPICES Black Pepper Coconut Apply 10 kg FYM, 500 g neem cake, 500 g wood ash and 2 kg vermicompost per vine annually. Also apply biofertilizers- Azospirillum and phosphorus-solubilizing bacteria 20 g each per vine. Use biocontrol agents like Trichoderma (50 g) and Pseudomonas ␀luorescens (50 g) per vine disease control. For foliar diseases, apply 1% Bordeaux mixture and neem oil (5 ml/L of water). Incorporate coir pith compost at 1.25 t/ha to enhance soil fertility. Andaman & Nicobar Islands Use raised beds or ridges for better drainage. Treat planting materials with Trichoderma to prevent rots. Use high-yielding varieties for sweet potato- CIARI Swarna, CIARI Aparna and Bhu Sona; for Cassava- Sree Vijaya and Sree Jaya; for elephant foot yam- Gajendra; for Taro- Mega Taro -2, Sree Kiran, Sree Pallavi and Sree Rashmi; and for dioscorea- Nicobari Alu (Traditional variety). Apply compost (10-15 t/ha) and biofertilizers like Azospirillum and PSB.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
