ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_19:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_19,6,kg of FYM/plant/year and mulch with leaves to retain soil moisture. Utilize neem-based products and Trichoderma formulations to manage common pests and diseases. LIVESTOCK 32,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_20:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_20,1,"Seed production bran, coconut cake, chunni (pulse), till cake, azolla, noni fruits, dry ␀ish, hatchery waste etc. Store feed in a dry and cool place in order to prevent from fungus. Supplementation of Mineral mixture (@ 50g cattle) should be provided for better productivity and reproductive performance in livestock. Cultivate fodder viz. para grass, guinea grass, hybrid napier (CO-5), supper napier, sorghum etc. for ensuring proper nutrition around the year. Fodder trees like jackfruits, noni, gliricidia, moringa, sesbania etc. may be planted for higher survivability during monsoon. For poultry, litter materials should be frequently turned and mixed with lime powder and fresh saw-dust to prevent dampening and cake formation leading fungal growth. Arti␀icial brooding should be provided to the chick's up to 4-6 weeks for healthy growth and to reduce mortality. FISHERIES Prior to the onset of monsoon rains (April-May), it is advisable to desilt the ␀ish ponds and apply agricultural lime (CaCO ) to maintain water pH between 7.0 and 8.5. 3 Adequate drainage systems should be in place to prevent over␀low or contamination from runoﬀ, and inlet-outlet structures must be ␀itted with screens",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_20:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_20,2,"to prevent the entry of predators or wild ␀ish during rains. Species selection and stocking of ␀ingerlings Feeding during the monsoon should be balanced and regular. Use either commercial feed with 24-28%CP or a mixture of rice bran and oilcake. Organic manures like cow dung (500 kg/ha/month) and poultry dropping may be applied to enhance pond fertility and plankton production. Water colour should be monitored regularly, as deep green or blackish water may indicate harmful algal blooms, which can be fatal to ␀ish. Be vigilant for symptoms of common ␀ish diseases like bacterial gill rot, EUS, and fungal infections. Diseased ␀ish should be isolated immediately, and disinfectants like KMnO₄ and salt treatment may be used under expert guidance. Harvest ␀ish during last week of September. For the production of quality ␀ish seed, healthy and disease-free broodstock aged 2-3 years should be selected and provided with a protein-rich diet (25-30% CP). Induce breeding between June to August using synthetic hormones like Ovaprim or WOVA- FH. The recommended male-to-female ratio for breeding in hapas is between 1:1 to 2:1. Pre-stocking management (Pond preparation) Stocking of ␀ish ␀ingerlings",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_20:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_20,3,"should be planned early in the kharif season (June-July) to take advantage of rising water levels. For composite ␀ish culture, IMC (Katla, Rohu, and Mrigal) is recommended. Side by side, consider species like GIFT Tilapia, Pangasius or Magur based on the market demand. A stocking density of 4000-6000 ␀ingerlings per ha is recommended, depending on the level of management and availability of inputs. Post stocking management ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Andhra Pradesh Godavari Zone: Swarna, Indra, Amara, Bhima, Pushyami, Ksheera, Sravani, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1212, 1280, 1281, 1293, 1310, 1321, 1318, 1232, Varieties Late Nursery Transplanting: Swarna, Indra, Amara, Maruteru Masoori, MTU Rice 1318, Bapatla Masoori, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Teja, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. BPH (Brown Plant Hopper) Infestation-Prone Areas: Krishnaveni, Indra, Amara, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1271, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Teja, Sasya, BPT Rice 2846, Nellore Siri. CEREAL CROPS North Coastal Zone: Pushkala, Srisatya, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Dhanyarashi, NLR Rice 3238. HAT Zone: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Chandra, Pushkala, Srisatya, NLR 3238. Krishna Zone: Swarna,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_20:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_20,4,"Indra, Amara, Krishnaveni, Varam, MTU Rice 1318, MTU 1232, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103, Samba Masoori, Akshaya, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Bapatla Masoori, Nellore Siri, Teja, Bhavathi, Sasya, BPT Rice 2841 & 2846, Maruteru Samba, Maruteru Masoori, MTU Rice 1271 & 1278, Nellore Sona, Nellore Siri, NLR 3238. Flood-Prone Areas: Amara, Indra, Bhima, MTU Rice 1232 & 1318. Saline Soils: Indra, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Paddy Late Planting: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, MTU 1293, Nellore Sona, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Siri, NLR 3238. Drought-Prone Areas: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Vijetha, Tarangini, Chandar, MTU 1293, NLR 3238. Southern Zone: Sweta, Bharani, Somasila, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Dhanyarashi, Nellore Sugandha, NLR 3238, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Chandra. 54",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_21:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_21,1,"Seed production bran, coconut cake, chunni (pulse), till cake, azolla, noni fruits, dry ␀ish, hatchery waste etc. Store feed in a dry and cool place in order to prevent from fungus. Supplementation of Mineral mixture (@ 50g cattle) should be provided for better productivity and reproductive performance in livestock. Cultivate fodder viz. para grass, guinea grass, hybrid napier (CO-5), supper napier, sorghum etc. for ensuring proper nutrition around the year. Fodder trees like jackfruits, noni, gliricidia, moringa, sesbania etc. may be planted for higher survivability during monsoon. For poultry, litter materials should be frequently turned and mixed with lime powder and fresh saw-dust to prevent dampening and cake formation leading fungal growth. Arti␀icial brooding should be provided to the chick's up to 4-6 weeks for healthy growth and to reduce mortality. FISHERIES Prior to the onset of monsoon rains (April-May), it is advisable to desilt the ␀ish ponds and apply agricultural lime (CaCO ) to maintain water pH between 7.0 and 8.5. 3 Adequate drainage systems should be in place to prevent over␀low or contamination from runoﬀ, and inlet-outlet structures must be ␀itted with screens",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_21:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_21,2,"to prevent the entry of predators or wild ␀ish during rains. Species selection and stocking of ␀ingerlings Feeding during the monsoon should be balanced and regular. Use either commercial feed with 24-28%CP or a mixture of rice bran and oilcake. Organic manures like cow dung (500 kg/ha/month) and poultry dropping may be applied to enhance pond fertility and plankton production. Water colour should be monitored regularly, as deep green or blackish water may indicate harmful algal blooms, which can be fatal to ␀ish. Be vigilant for symptoms of common ␀ish diseases like bacterial gill rot, EUS, and fungal infections. Diseased ␀ish should be isolated immediately, and disinfectants like KMnO₄ and salt treatment may be used under expert guidance. Harvest ␀ish during last week of September. For the production of quality ␀ish seed, healthy and disease-free broodstock aged 2-3 years should be selected and provided with a protein-rich diet (25-30% CP). Induce breeding between June to August using synthetic hormones like Ovaprim or WOVA- FH. The recommended male-to-female ratio for breeding in hapas is between 1:1 to 2:1. Pre-stocking management (Pond preparation) Stocking of ␀ish ␀ingerlings",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_21:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_21,3,"should be planned early in the kharif season (June-July) to take advantage of rising water levels. For composite ␀ish culture, IMC (Katla, Rohu, and Mrigal) is recommended. Side by side, consider species like GIFT Tilapia, Pangasius or Magur based on the market demand. A stocking density of 4000-6000 ␀ingerlings per ha is recommended, depending on the level of management and availability of inputs. Post stocking management ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Andhra Pradesh Godavari Zone: Swarna, Indra, Amara, Bhima, Pushyami, Ksheera, Sravani, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1212, 1280, 1281, 1293, 1310, 1321, 1318, 1232, Varieties Late Nursery Transplanting: Swarna, Indra, Amara, Maruteru Masoori, MTU Rice 1318, Bapatla Masoori, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Teja, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. BPH (Brown Plant Hopper) Infestation-Prone Areas: Krishnaveni, Indra, Amara, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1271, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Teja, Sasya, BPT Rice 2846, Nellore Siri. CEREAL CROPS North Coastal Zone: Pushkala, Srisatya, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Dhanyarashi, NLR Rice 3238. HAT Zone: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Chandra, Pushkala, Srisatya, NLR 3238. Krishna Zone: Swarna,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_21:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_21,4,"Indra, Amara, Krishnaveni, Varam, MTU Rice 1318, MTU 1232, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103, Samba Masoori, Akshaya, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Bapatla Masoori, Nellore Siri, Teja, Bhavathi, Sasya, BPT Rice 2841 & 2846, Maruteru Samba, Maruteru Masoori, MTU Rice 1271 & 1278, Nellore Sona, Nellore Siri, NLR 3238. Flood-Prone Areas: Amara, Indra, Bhima, MTU Rice 1232 & 1318. Saline Soils: Indra, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Paddy Late Planting: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, MTU 1293, Nellore Sona, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Siri, NLR 3238. Drought-Prone Areas: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Vijetha, Tarangini, Chandar, MTU 1293, NLR 3238. Southern Zone: Sweta, Bharani, Somasila, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Dhanyarashi, Nellore Sugandha, NLR 3238, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Chandra. 54",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_22:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_22,1,"Scarce Rainfall Zone: Nellore Sona, Masoori, Siri, NLR 3238, Samba Masoori, BPT 2841, 2846, Varam, Maruteru Samba & Maruteru Masoori, MTU 1271, MCM Rice 103, Nandyala Sona. Drought-Prone Areas: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Vijetha, Tarangini, Chandra, Maruteru Samba, MTU 1293, NLR 3238. BPH-Prone Areas: Vijetha, Amara, Indra, Sujatha, Pushyami, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2646, Nellore Siri. Saline Soils: Nellore Masoori, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Flood-Prone Areas: Amara, Indra, Bhima, MTU 1232, 1318. Late Nursery Planting: Parthiva, Bapatla Masoori, Teja, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Maruteru Masoori. Late Planting: MTU 1293, NLR 3238, Nellore Masoori, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Chandara. BPH-Prone Areas: Maruteru Samba & Maruteru Masoori, MTU 1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2846, Parthiva. Late Nursery Transplanting: Swarna, Indra, Amara, MTU 1318, Maruteru Masoori, Srikakulam Sannalu. Late Nursery Planting: Swarna, MTU 1318, Maruteru Masoori, Srikakulam Sannalu. BPH-Prone Areas: Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU Rice -1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT Rice- 2846, Parthiva, Nandyala Sona. Flood-Prone Areas: Srikakulam Sannalu, Indra, Bapatla Masoori, Bhima, Amara, Ksheera, MTU 1318, 1232.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_22:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_22,2,"Saline Soils: Indra, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Southern Region: Nellore Sona, Nellore Masoori, Nellore Dhanyarashi, Nellore Siri, Somasila, Bharani, Sweta, NLR 3238, Samba Masoori, Bapatla Masoori, Teja, Bhavathi, Sasya, BPT Rice-2841, BPT Rice-2846, Varam, Maruteru Samba & Maruteru Masoori, MTU Rice-1232, MTU Rice-1271, MCM Rice-103, Nandyala Sona. BPH-Prone: Krishnaveni, Indra, Amara, Pushyami, Maruteru Samba, MTU 1271, BPT 2846. Drought-Prone Areas: Sona Masoori, Swarna, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Vijetha, Chandra, Tarangini, Sujatha, Maruteru Samba, MTU 1293. North Coastal Region: Swarna, Indra, Amara, Bhima, Pushyami, Ksheera, Sravani, Maruteru Samba, Masoori, MTU 1310, 1318, 1232, 1271, 1275, Samba Masoori, Teja, Bhavathi, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2841, 2846, MCM Rice 103. Late Nursery Planting: Bapatla Masoori, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Maruteru Masoori. Saline Soils: Indra, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Late Planting: Vasundhara, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, Sridhruti, Chandra, MTU 1293, NLR 3238. Late Planting: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Tarangini, MTU 1293, Nellore Siri, NLR 3238. 1271, 1275, Samba Masoori, Teja, Bhavathi, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2841, MCM Rice 103. Andhra Pradesh Trap Barrier",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_22:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_22,3,"System (TBS): Erect 2 ft height polythene sheet barrier around the crop at 15 days after transplanting. The polythene barrier is provided with 3 inch radius holes above the water level at 15-30 m distance and wonder traps are arranged ␀irmly inside the crop, their entry mouths matching the holes made in the polythene sheet. Arrange a soil moat before the entry hole to facilitate the animal to enter easily inside the trap. Maintain water around the TBS and collect the successful traps every day and replace with new / emptied traps. Precautions during natural calamities: If the crop is submerged in water for more than 1 to 2 days in the boot leaf or ␀lowering stage, the panicle exertion may be incomplete. Water accumulation in the spikelets, would also result in reduced fertilization and formation of chaﬀy seeds. Spraying with Carbendiazim @ 1g/L or Carbendiazim + Mancozeb @ 2g/L or Propiconazole @1ml/L is recommended to avoid discoloration of grains. If the harvested sheaves in the ␀ield are drenched, 5% salt solution should be sprayed on the sheaves to prevent seed germination. The sheaves should be turned over, dried and threshed after cessation of the rains. In Fertilizer",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_22:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_22,4,"Application: Grow green manure crops (Dhaincha, Sunhemp, Pillipesara and Cowpea) as preceding crop to Paddy and apply soil test-based fertilizers. The entire dose of phosphorus fertilizer should be applied during the ␀inal puddling stage. In heavy soils, the full dose of potash fertilizer should be applied at the ␀inal puddling. In light soils, half the dose should be applied during puddling and the remaining half at the panicle initiation stage. Weed Control: In wet direct-seeded rice ␀ields, within 3-5 days of sowing, apply Pyrazosulfuron-ethyl 10% WP @ 250 g/ha or use Pretilachlor + Safener 37% EW @ 1500 ml/ha mixed with 50 kg of dry sand and broadcast evenly over the ␀ield. In transplanted paddy ␀ields, within 3-5 days of planting, when the ␀ield has shallow standing water, apply either Pyrazosulfuron-ethyl 10% WP @ 200 g/ha mixed with 50 kg sand, or Butachlor 50% EC @ 2.5-3.12 litres/ha, or Pretilachlor 50% EC 1000 ml/ha. If the ␀ield has a heavy infestation of grassy, sedge and broadleaf weeds, use Bensulfuron Methyl 0.6% + Pretilachlor 6.0% Granules @ 10 kg/ha mixed with 50 kg sand and broadcast evenly. At 20 days after transplanting, for grassy weed control, apply",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_22:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_22,5,"Cyhalofop-P-butyl 10% EC @ 1000 ml/ha. If weed infestation is high, apply Bispyribac Sodium 10% SL @ 250 ml/ha or Triafamone + Ethoxysulfuron 30% WG at 225 g/ha in 500 liters of water. False smut: Spraying of propiconazole@ 200ml/acre two times at booting stage and at 50% panicle emergence stage. At severe incidence of diseases spray tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin 75WG@80g/acre. Late Planting: Samba Masoori, Nandyala Sannalu, MTU Rice-1293, NLR Rice -3238, Nellore Masoori, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Chandra. Bacterial leaf blight: Aﬀected stubbles are to be destroyed by burning or through ploughing, judicious use of nitrogenous fertilizers, avoid clipping of tip of seedling at the time of transplanting. Avoid ␀looded conditions or drying of the ␀ield (not at the time of ␀lowering). Application of potassium two time @ 15 kg/acre at planting time and 20 kg/acre at panicle initiation stage. ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 76",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_23:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_23,1,"Scarce Rainfall Zone: Nellore Sona, Masoori, Siri, NLR 3238, Samba Masoori, BPT 2841, 2846, Varam, Maruteru Samba & Maruteru Masoori, MTU 1271, MCM Rice 103, Nandyala Sona. Drought-Prone Areas: Cotton Dora Sannalu, Vijetha, Tarangini, Chandra, Maruteru Samba, MTU 1293, NLR 3238. BPH-Prone Areas: Vijetha, Amara, Indra, Sujatha, Pushyami, Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU 1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2646, Nellore Siri. Saline Soils: Nellore Masoori, Panduranga, MCM Rice 103. Flood-Prone Areas: Amara, Indra, Bhima, MTU 1232, 1318. Late Nursery Planting: Parthiva, Bapatla Masoori, Teja, Bhavapuri Sannalu, Maruteru Masoori. Late Planting: MTU 1293, NLR 3238, Nellore Masoori, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Chandara. BPH-Prone Areas: Maruteru Samba & Maruteru Masoori, MTU 1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT 2846, Parthiva. Late Nursery Transplanting: Swarna, Indra, Amara, MTU 1318, Maruteru Masoori, Srikakulam Sannalu. Late Nursery Planting: Swarna, MTU 1318, Maruteru Masoori, Srikakulam Sannalu. BPH-Prone Areas: Maruteru Samba & Masoori, MTU Rice -1271, Bapatla Masoori, BPT Rice- 2846, Parthiva, Nandyala Sona. Flood-Prone Areas: Srikakulam Sannalu, Indra, Bapatla Masoori, Bhima, Amara, Ksheera, MTU 1318, 1232.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
