ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_23:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_23,3,"System (TBS): Erect 2 ft height polythene sheet barrier around the crop at 15 days after transplanting. The polythene barrier is provided with 3 inch radius holes above the water level at 15-30 m distance and wonder traps are arranged ␀irmly inside the crop, their entry mouths matching the holes made in the polythene sheet. Arrange a soil moat before the entry hole to facilitate the animal to enter easily inside the trap. Maintain water around the TBS and collect the successful traps every day and replace with new / emptied traps. Precautions during natural calamities: If the crop is submerged in water for more than 1 to 2 days in the boot leaf or ␀lowering stage, the panicle exertion may be incomplete. Water accumulation in the spikelets, would also result in reduced fertilization and formation of chaﬀy seeds. Spraying with Carbendiazim @ 1g/L or Carbendiazim + Mancozeb @ 2g/L or Propiconazole @1ml/L is recommended to avoid discoloration of grains. If the harvested sheaves in the ␀ield are drenched, 5% salt solution should be sprayed on the sheaves to prevent seed germination. The sheaves should be turned over, dried and threshed after cessation of the rains. In Fertilizer",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_23:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_23,4,"Application: Grow green manure crops (Dhaincha, Sunhemp, Pillipesara and Cowpea) as preceding crop to Paddy and apply soil test-based fertilizers. The entire dose of phosphorus fertilizer should be applied during the ␀inal puddling stage. In heavy soils, the full dose of potash fertilizer should be applied at the ␀inal puddling. In light soils, half the dose should be applied during puddling and the remaining half at the panicle initiation stage. Weed Control: In wet direct-seeded rice ␀ields, within 3-5 days of sowing, apply Pyrazosulfuron-ethyl 10% WP @ 250 g/ha or use Pretilachlor + Safener 37% EW @ 1500 ml/ha mixed with 50 kg of dry sand and broadcast evenly over the ␀ield. In transplanted paddy ␀ields, within 3-5 days of planting, when the ␀ield has shallow standing water, apply either Pyrazosulfuron-ethyl 10% WP @ 200 g/ha mixed with 50 kg sand, or Butachlor 50% EC @ 2.5-3.12 litres/ha, or Pretilachlor 50% EC 1000 ml/ha. If the ␀ield has a heavy infestation of grassy, sedge and broadleaf weeds, use Bensulfuron Methyl 0.6% + Pretilachlor 6.0% Granules @ 10 kg/ha mixed with 50 kg sand and broadcast evenly. At 20 days after transplanting, for grassy weed control, apply",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_23:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_23,5,"Cyhalofop-P-butyl 10% EC @ 1000 ml/ha. If weed infestation is high, apply Bispyribac Sodium 10% SL @ 250 ml/ha or Triafamone + Ethoxysulfuron 30% WG at 225 g/ha in 500 liters of water. False smut: Spraying of propiconazole@ 200ml/acre two times at booting stage and at 50% panicle emergence stage. At severe incidence of diseases spray tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin 75WG@80g/acre. Late Planting: Samba Masoori, Nandyala Sannalu, MTU Rice-1293, NLR Rice -3238, Nellore Masoori, Cotton Dora Sannalu, Chandra. Bacterial leaf blight: Aﬀected stubbles are to be destroyed by burning or through ploughing, judicious use of nitrogenous fertilizers, avoid clipping of tip of seedling at the time of transplanting. Avoid ␀looded conditions or drying of the ␀ield (not at the time of ␀lowering). Application of potassium two time @ 15 kg/acre at planting time and 20 kg/acre at panicle initiation stage. ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 76",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,1,"Fall army worm: Summer ploughing, collection & destruction of egg masses, installation of pheromone traps (S. frugiperda) @ 4/acre sowing of border crop with grain sorghum & inter crop with cowpea (few rows) spraying of Azadirachtin 10000 ppm @ 2ml/l (10 to 15 DAS), EPN or Bt spray @ 2 ml/l (15 to 21 DAS). First insecticide spray - Emamectin Benzoate 5SG @ 0.4g/l (or) Spinosad 480SC @ 0.5 ml/l (21-28 DAS). Metarhizium anisopliae spray (1x107) @ 2 ml/l (30 -35DAS). Second Insecticide spray - Flubendiamide 480SC @ 0.3 ml/l (or) Chlorontriliniprole 18.5SC @ 0.3ml/l or Spinetoram 11.7 SC @ 0.3 ml/l (36 - 42 DAS). Poison Baiting - 45- 65 DAS using Thiodicarb 75WP (250 g thiodicardb + 25kg rice bran + 5 kg jaggery / ha). Farmers are also suggested to follow seed treatment with imidacloprid 600 FS @ 1ml per kg seed and followed by tebuconazole 2 DS @ 1g or mancozeb @ 3 g/kg or Trichoderma viride @ 10g/kg seed. Take up sowing of bajra/jowar (4-8 rows) as border crops all around the ␀ield to avoid transmission of vectors like thrips which spread PSND/PBND diseases. Spray KNO @ 0.5% or 19:19:19 immediately after dry 3 spell. Provide supplemental irrigation 20mm at ␀lowering and peg",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,2,"penetration stage. Install sticky traps (10/acre) and pheromone traps (4/acre) in ␀ield to monitor case of stormy weather conditions, while heaping of incompletely dried paddy sheaves, 25 kg of salt per acre of paddy sheaves may be sprinkled and heaped to avoid damage. In normal conditions, rainfed crop should be sown between June 15 and July 15. In the Kharif season, under rainfed conditions, maize should be sown only after a substantial rainfall (more than 50 mm). Seed rate is 17.5-20 kg/ha for normal hybrids, 7.5-10 kg/ha for sweetcorn, 12.5 kg/ha for popcorn and 25 kg/ha for baby corn. Within two to three days after sowing the crop, spray Atrazine herbicide @ 2 kg/ha in light soils and 3 kg/ha in heavy soils mixed with 500 liters of water when there is suf␀icient moisture which helps in controlling broadleaved and some grassy weeds for about 30 DAS. To control broadleaved and grassy weeds in normal and zero tillage maize crop at 15-18 DAS or 4 leaf weed stage, Tembotrione 34.4% SC @ 287.5 ml/ha + Atrazine 50% WP @ 1000 g/ha or Topramezone 33.6% SC 75 ml + Atrazine 50% WP @ 1000 g/ha should be sprayed. If the problem of Cyperus spp. is more, spray Halosulfuron methyl @ 100 g/ha",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,3,"mixed with 500 L of water. OILSEED CROPS Groundnut Farmers are advised to take up summer ploughing and also suggested to select high yielding varieties like TCGS 1694, K-Chitravathi, K-Lepakshi. The suitable time for sowing of rainfed groundnut is July to ␀irst week of August. Farmers are advised to adopt intercropping with redgram at 7:1/11:1/15:1 ratio as per their convenience and availability of sowing equipment. Use fertilizer cum seed drill instead of manual labour for sowing behind the country plough. Formation of conservation furrows every 3.6m interval at sowing/20-30 days after sowing will help in soil moisture conservation. Maize Andhra Pradesh ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 98 sucking and leaf eating pests. Intensity of infestation to spray imidacloprid 17.8 SL @ 0.3 ml/l of water for the control of sucking pests at ETL. Install bird perches (4/acre for collection and destruction of egg, larval populations by nesting birds). Spray quinalphos @ 2.0 ml and neem oil @ 5 ml/L of water at initial stages and at later stages. Spray emamectin benzoate 5% SG @ 0.4 g/l of water. Spray 2 g Chlorothalonil or 2 ml. Hexaconazole or 1 ml. Tebuconazole per liter of water for control of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,4,"Tikka leaf spot and spray twice at an interval of 15 days. Spray Monocrotophos 1.6 ml or Fipronil 2 ml or Dimethoate 2 ml/L of water for control of peanut bud necrosis virus. To prevent this pest, treat the seeds with 2 ml imidacloprid 600 FS per kg of seed for the next crop. Sesamum Sun␀lower Farmers are advised to choose high-yielding hybrid sun␀lower such as NDSH-1012, LSFH-171, DRSH-1 and KBSH-44. Farmers are advised to take up intercrops such as groundnut and redgram (Sun␀lower: Groundnut-2:4 ratio) (Sun␀lower: redgram- 2:1 ratio). Farmers are advised to treat the seed with Iprodione 25% + Carbendazim 25%) or Fluxapyroxad FS @ 1.5 g/kg or Saaf (Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63%) @ 2 g/kg for controlling alternaria leaf spot. In areas prone to necrosis virus in sun␀lower, treat seeds with Thiamethoxam (Cruiser) @ 4 g/kg or Imidacloprid (Gaucho) @ 5 g/kg. Farmers are advised to apply (26 kg urea) at sowing, 13 kg at 30 days during the bud stage, and 13 kg at 50 days during ␀lowering. Apply the full dose of phosphorus (150 kg SSP) and potash (20 kg MOP) during the ␀inal ploughing. In sulphur-de␀icient soils, apply 10 kg sulphur per acre in gypsum form (55 kg/acre) to improve oil",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,5,"content and yield. If boron de␀iciency is noticed in sun␀lower, spray 2 g of borax per litre of water using 200 litre per acre. Castor Farmers are advised to take up sowings during II FN of May and high yielding varieties like Sarada, Goutham, Varaha, Madhavi, and Gowri can be taken up. 2 kg of seeds per acre should be sown in rows mixed with sand or sawdust in equal proportions. Farmers are advised to do treat sesame seeds with 3 g of Carbendazim/Mancozeb per kg of seed. This will prevent leaf spot, root rot and stem rot. Sesame farmers should apply fertilizers that supply 16 kg of nitrogen, 8 kg of phosphorus, and 8 kg of potash per acre. Farmers are advised to spray Pendimethalin 30% @ 4-5 ml per litre of water to control weeds immediately after sowing in sesamum. Select high yielding varieties such as Haritha, Kiran, Jwala, Pragathi and hybrids i.e DCH. 117, PCH-111, GCH.8, ICH.66 and ICH 5. Optimum sowing time for castor is June 15␀␀ to July 31␀␀ Seed rate of castor is 2-2.5 kg/acre and to fallow spacing 90 cm x 60 cm and suggested to take up thinning and remove excess population @ 10-15 DAS by retaining one seedling per hill and maintaining the optimum plant population.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_24:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_24,6,"Farmers are advised to utilizing the available soil moisture and take up top dressing of urea @13 kg /acre at 30 to 35, 60 to 65 and for hybrids apply additional dose of urea @ 13 kg/acre at 90 to 95 days under suf␀icient soil moisture condition.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
