ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_29:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_29,5,"stalks during June-July, followed by spray 1% Bordeaux mixture. Fertilisers should be applied as per the leaf analysis i.e. trees more than 10 years age and in full bearing should be applied with N P and K @1 kg each ( 2.2 kg Urea, 1.6 kg Coconut Cultivate turmeric, ginger, yam, colacasia, seasonal vegetables, pulses and ground nut in young gardens of below 5 years age. Plant cocoa, banana, pepper, pineapple, papaya, heliconia as intercrops in old and bearing gardens. Oilpalm Prune during June-July and ploughing in bearing orchards. Cultivate vegetables, dwarf banana varieties, ␀lower crops, chilli, ginger, turmeric, pineapple as intercrops in young garden and cocoa and pepper in old and bearing gardens. Use of harvesting poles can reduce labour use. Timely harvesting of matured bunches to avoid damage due to kharif rains. 1312",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_30:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_30,1,"Sow green manure crops in the interspaces after receiving ␀irst rain and incorporate at 50% ␀lowering. Spray micronutrient on newly emerged vegetative ␀lush. Apply copper oxychloride @ 30g+Streptocycline@ 1g in 10 L of water to control citrus bacterial canker. Apply cartap hydrochloride@ 1g/L after emergence of new vegetative ␀lush to control leaf miner damage and spray carbendazim@ 1g/L to control gummosis. Dairy Calves: Ensure timely colostrum feeding, adequate milk supply, and deworming to prevent neonatal mortality. Turmeric and Yam Dairy Farming MOP and 6 kg SSP) in basins 1.5 to 2 m distance from the main trunk. Micro nutrient de␀iciencies can be controlled by spraying 5 g Zinc Sulphate+2.5 g Ferrous Sulphate+ 2 g Borax+ 2 g Calcium Sulphate + 3 g Magnesium Sulphate 3 times per year in the months of June/July, September/October and December/January. Treat the seed material with Mancozeb (3g/l) and Imidacloprid @ 1ml/l and grow on ridges to avoid rhizome rot/ collar rot. Apply Trichoderma viride (5 kg)+ FYM (100 kg) culture at the time of planting. Raise the nursery during May-June with hybrids Arka Abhed, Arka Samrat and Arka Rakshak in pro-tray to prevent damping oﬀ",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_30:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_30,2,"diseases. Seed rate for hybrids is 60-80 g/ acre and varieties is 200 g/acre. Treat the seed with Imidacloprid @ 5 g/kg to prevent sucking pests. Apply Trichoderma viride @ 5kg/ha and Pseudomonas ␀luorescence @ 5kg/ha in soil after curing with 225kg FYM and 25kg Neem cake to manage soil borne diseases and nematode. Install pheromone traps @ 25/ha to manage South American Pin worm. Raise the nursery during May-June with varieties Arka Anand and VNR-51 in protray to prevent damping oﬀ diseases. Seed rate for hybrids is 120 g/ acre and for varieties 260 g/acre. Treat the seed with Imidacloprid @ 5 g/kg to prevent sucking pests. Apply Trichoderma viride @ 5kg/ha and Pseudomonas ␀luorescence @ 5kg/ha after curing with 225kg FYM and 25kg neem cake to manage soil borne disease and nematode. Install pheromone traps @ 25/ha to manage shoot and fruit borer. Apply Arka Microbial Consortium @ 12.5kg/ha along with 25 t FYM/ha and 75% RDF (75:45:100 kg N:P₂O₅:K₂O/ ha). LIVESTOCK Acid lime Banana Procure healthy planting material from virus free ␀ields, treat the sucker with Mancozeb (3g/l) and Dimethoate @ 2ml/L, apply Trichoderma viride@ (5 kg) + FYM @ 100 kg while planting. Green manure crops",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_30:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_30,3,"to be incorporated. Fertilizer application should be taken up after 40 days of planting in Grand Naine variety @ 110 g Urea and 80 g MOP per plant applied in 10 cm trench on both sides of the plant. Brinjal Tomato Andhra Pradesh ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Stage-Based Feeding: Implement a feeding strategy based on the pig's life stages for optimal growth. Sheep Farming Health & Disease Control: Implement regular vaccination and deworming schedules and provide practical training on poultry health management. Young Lamb Management: Ensure colostrum feeding, deworming, and timely vaccinations to improve lamb health and reduce mortality. Heifers & Dairy Animals: Provide mineral supplementation, hormonal interventions for repeat breeding, and manage endometritis to improve reproductive ef␀iciency. Backyard Poultry Farming Housing & Welfare: Use low-cost, secure enclosures for bird safety, and improve transportation practices to reduce stress. Feeding Strategies: Promote Azolla cultivation as a cost-eﬀective, high-protein feed supplement and use locally available feed ingredients to cut costs. Swine Farming Breed Improvement: Replace non-descriptive breeds with the SVVU T-17 breed to",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_30:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_30,4,"enhance productivity. Dairy Buﬀaloes: Promote clean milking practices, calcium supplementation to prevent milk fever, and strategies to avoid ketosis and ruminal acidosis. Breed Improvement: Replace native low-productive breeds with high- performance breeds like Rajasri and Gramapriya. Feeding Strategy: Avoid feeding swill and provide balanced concentrate feed to improve reproductive performance. Fodder Supply: Promote high-yielding fodder varieties, use crop residues, and implement silage making to combat fodder shortages. Provide green fodder during the day and roughages at night to manage heat stress. Breeding Stock: Replace non-descriptive breeds with the Macherla breed, which is well-adapted to local conditions. Supplementary Feeding & Genetic Diversity: Provide supplementary feeding during pregnancy and exchange rams for improved genetic diversity. Sub soiler results cutting soil strata up to a depth of 40 to 75 cm and creates more space for rain water entry and storage. In-situ water conservation and to sustain crop in prolonged dry spell. Easily operated by any 35 to 45 hp tractor. It is useful in dryland agricultural crops. Use Trampler for green manure mixing, it cuts and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
