ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_37:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_37,4,"kg N P₂O₅ K₂O/ha. One weeding should be done at 20 days after sowing by khurpi or hoe. Five (5) Apis cerena colonies/ha (1 colony/ bigha) should be installed for eﬀective pollination of sesame and optimization of productivity. In phytophthora blight endemic areas, sesamum is to be rotated with cereals at every two years. In the case of phyllody disease, the infected plants should be rogued out. Sesame Tomato cultivating farmers are advised to grow disease resistant varieties viz. Arka Raksak, Arka Abhed, Arka Samrat with a seed rate of 200-250 gm/acre. The seeds can be mixed with Trichoderma viride and (@ 5 gm/100 gm of seeds. This will help in the control of early blight and other pathogens.To control the diﬀerent pest of tomato, farmers can use garlic chilli extract spray in the evening and also advised to install pheromone traps @ 5/acre for monitoring adult moths activity. Replace the lures with fresh lures after every 2-3 weeks. The recommended varieties are SBC 40, SBC 47, AAU SHN Urd 02 (Lakhi). The land is to be ploughed 2-3 times followed by leveling. Sow black gram seeds @ 22.5 kg/ha or 3 kg/bigha by keeping the spacing of 30 × 10 cm. Compost or FYM @ 1 t/ha or 1.3",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_37:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_37,5,"q/bigha should be applied. The recommended fertilizer dose for black gram is 15:35:15 kg N P₂O₅ K₂O/ha. One weeding at 20-25 days after sowing has to be done.The spread of yellow mosaic virus can be checked by placing yellow sticky traps (5 per acre) to attract and capture white␀lies. Also, spraying of 5% neem seed kernel extract or Azadiractin 1500 ppm @ 5ml/l of water is recommended. To control the leaf spot, spray copper oxychloride @ 0.3% (1.8-2.0 kg/ha in 600-700 liters of water) at an interval of 7-10 days. 2120",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_38:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_38,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 LIVESTOCK To control the white ␀ly in king chilly neem oil (1500 ppm) spray during initial stage of infestation is recommended. If the infestation of white ␀ly is more than ETL, Buprofezin @ 1 ml/l should be spray at weekly interval. Piggery In case of brinjal, farmers can grow long variety such as Pusa Purple Cluster, Borbengena, JC-1, Kuchia and BWR-34; round variety Pusa Purple Round, Pusa Vairab, BWR-12 with a seed rate of 700-800 g/ha. The ideal spacing for brinjal cultivation is 75 cm × 60 cm (row to row and plant to plant). Farmers are advised to use low-cost rain shelters for raising the vegetable seedlings. Seeds of King chilly and other hard seed coat seeds should be treated with Pseudomonas. Sowing of cucurbit seeds should be done in nursery plug system or in thermocol or paper cups in order to protect from climatic hazards. Biodegradable plastic mulching should be used in king chilly and brinjal crops for soil conservation and weed management. The Ginger/Turmeric ␀ield should be well prepared having drainage facility to prevent the water stagnation causing rhizome rot. Farmers are advised to spray neem-based formulation @ 3-5 ml/l of water",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_38:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_38,2,"or Bacillus thuringinsis @ 2g/L or Metarhiziumanisopliae @ 5ml/L for insects and pests and copper oxychloride @ 0.25% diseases management. Farmers can rear the pig breed like Large white Yorkshire, HDK-75. Wash and disinfect the pens at regular basis and avoid dampness. Administer iron dextran in newly born piglets to prevent anemia. Ensure vaccination of pig against swine fever at the age of 3 months old pig and repeat annually. Deworm at regular interval with fenbendazole @ 3mg/kg body weight, fo l l o we d by l ive r t o n i c . Re p e a t deworming once in 3 months. Ensure Tomato cultivation by using black polythene as a mulching material Cultivation of king chilli under low cost polyhouse conditions Shelter management of crossbreed pig Arunachal Pradesh Poultry adequate fodder storage and clean water during wet seasons. Exposure to wet and cold conditions can lead to stress, reduced feed intake, and increased risk of diseases like foot rot and respiratory infections. Regularly monitor for signs of illness to ensure timely treatment. If any sign of illness is suspected, the pig should be isolated and treated. For better income of the farmers, it is advised to rear dual purpose",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_38:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_38,3,"poultry breed like Vanaraja, Kalinga brown, BV 380. Facilitate one-day old chicks with arti␀icial brooding in a con␀ined area and check backup power for brooding. Provide dry and suf␀icient litter to keep them warm in the brooding area. Provide adequate clean drinking water with electrolyte and ad libitum feeding. Ensure proper vaccination of birds against Ranikhet disease within the age of 5-7days old. Repeat the same when chicks become 28 days old. Deworm the birds with fenbendazole @ 30- 40ml/100 birds in drinking water. Repeat the same after 21 days. Multivitamins may be added in drinking water every once-twice in a week. Provide warm, dry and mold free feed. Wet and humid conditions may increase the risk of coccidiosis and respiratory disorders. Strict biosecurity should be maintained, and visit of outsiders should be avoided. If any disease outbreak occurs, maintain 45days of interval between the next batches. 2322",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
