ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_39:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_39,3,"poultry breed like Vanaraja, Kalinga brown, BV 380. Facilitate one-day old chicks with arti␀icial brooding in a con␀ined area and check backup power for brooding. Provide dry and suf␀icient litter to keep them warm in the brooding area. Provide adequate clean drinking water with electrolyte and ad libitum feeding. Ensure proper vaccination of birds against Ranikhet disease within the age of 5-7days old. Repeat the same when chicks become 28 days old. Deworm the birds with fenbendazole @ 30- 40ml/100 birds in drinking water. Repeat the same after 21 days. Multivitamins may be added in drinking water every once-twice in a week. Provide warm, dry and mold free feed. Wet and humid conditions may increase the risk of coccidiosis and respiratory disorders. Strict biosecurity should be maintained, and visit of outsiders should be avoided. If any disease outbreak occurs, maintain 45days of interval between the next batches. 2322",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_40:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_40,1,"Assam CEREAL CROPS Sali rice Selection of varieties: The Semi dwarf varieties are: AAU-TTB-Dhan 44 (Prachur), AAU-TTB-Dhan 43(Shatabdi), AAU-TTB-Dhan 42 (Patkai). Farmers interested in multiple cropping situation can select the medium duration varieties like Numoli, Dholi, Shraboni. For staggered planting in sali season suitable varieties are Prafulla and Gitesh. Farmers of ␀lood prone district can take submergence tolerant rice varieties for ␀lash-␀lood situation: Ranjit Sub1, Bahadur Sub1, Jalashree, Jalkunwari, Dholi. In case of late planting in ␀lood-aﬀected area/direct seeded late Sali are Luit, Kapilee, Dishang. Seed treatment: Put the seeds in normal water, stirred well, sunken seeds are selected and the ␀loated ones are rejected. For wet method, selected seeds should be soaked directly in fungicidal suspensions of carboxin @ 2.0 g/l of water for 24 hours. One liter of fungicide solution is required to treat one kg of seed. In case of dry method, put the seeds in a container and add carboxin @ 2.0 g/kg seed and mixed thoroughly by agitating them for ␀ive minutes. Nursery management: Land is thoroughly puddled and seedbeds of 10 m length and 1.25 m breadth are prepared with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_40:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_40,2,"30 cm gap in between the beds. The length of the bed may vary according to convenience. In each seedbed 20-30 kg cow dung/compost, 80 g urea, 80g SSP and 40g MOP are to be applied and mixed well with the soil. Well germinated seeds are to be sown @ 650 g to 1 kg per bed depending on grain size. Requirement of seed for transplanting one hectare of main ␀ield is 40-45 kg. Irrigation water should be applied in furrows to maintain saturated condition in the surface soil of the nursery bed. However, standing water to a depth of 2-3 cm should be maintained at least 2-3 days before uprooting. As soon as one or two blast spots are seen, ediphenphos @ 1 ml/l of water is to be sprayed. For management of root knot nematode, apply, Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 20 g /sq. m at the time of sowing. Assam Transplanting: One ploughing should be given at least 21 days prior to transplanting. An irrigation for land soaking should be applied before preparatory tillage. The ␀inal puddling should be done 4-5 days prior to transplanting. One irrigation should be applied before ␀inal puddling. 25 days old seedlings of short and medium duration varieties should be transplanted by maintaining a row-to-row and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_40:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_40,3,"plant-to-plant spacing of 20 cm × 15 cm. In case of long duration varieties, 35-40 days old seedlings are to be transplanted at 25 cm × 15 cm spacing. It is advised to plant 2- 3 seedlings per hill, at a depth of 4-5 cm, for all varieties. Nutrient management: Well rotten FYM or compost @ 10 t/ha has to be applied during ␀ield preparation. In addition, for semidwarf varieties, 60 kg N/ha, 20 kg P₂O₅/ha and 40 kg K₂O/ha and for tall varieties, 20 kg N/ha, 10 kg P₂O₅/ha and 10 kg K₂O/ are to be applied in areas with moderate fertility level. In case of poor soil, the rates of fertilizers may be required to increase to the extent of 60:30:30 kg/ha N, P₂O₅ and K₂O respectively. Half of urea and whole of super phosphate and muriate of potash should be applied at the time of ␀inal puddling. Of the remaining part of urea, half at tillering stage i.e. 20-30 days after transplanting and other half at panicle initiation stage should be applied. Two weedings should be given with paddy weeder or hoe at 20 and 40 days after transplanting. For weed control, pretilachlor @ 0.75 kg/ha or anilofos is to be applied @ 0.4 kg/ha at 3 days after transplanting. In sali rice, application of 5 cm",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_40:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_40,4,"irrigation water 3 days after disappearance of ponding water is recommended in medium and heavy soils. In rainfed kharif rice, height of bunds should be 30 cm to retain rainwater. Plant protection measures: To control the rice stem borer, whorl maggot, gall midge and leaf folder, spray ␀ipronil 5SC @1.5-2 ml/l of water. To control thrips and plant hopper, spray imidacloprid 70 WG @0.3 g/l of water or thiamethoxam 25 WG@0.03 g/l of water. Against Rice Hispa, spray lamda-cyhalothrin 5 EC @ 12.5g /per ha. To control rice pests, erect 50 'T'-perches per ha 2 ft (60 cm) above crop canopy as roosting site for insectivorous birds, which are to be removed before ␀lowering in order to prevent activity of granivorous birds. To prevent rice blast, spray hexaconazole 5EC @ 2g/l of water at tillering stage (40-55 days after sowing) and subsequently give two more sprays of ediphenphos @ 1ml/l of water, one at panicle initiation stage and the other when the tip of the panicle just comes out. Management of direct seeded late Sali: Field should be prepared just after recession of ␀lood by ploughing, cross ploughing and laddering to bring it to a puddle Seedlings of Flood Tolerant Rice variety-",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_40:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_40,5,Ranjit sub-1 during ␀lood Installation of T Perch in Rice Field 2524,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_41:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_41,1,"Assam CEREAL CROPS Sali rice Selection of varieties: The Semi dwarf varieties are: AAU-TTB-Dhan 44 (Prachur), AAU-TTB-Dhan 43(Shatabdi), AAU-TTB-Dhan 42 (Patkai). Farmers interested in multiple cropping situation can select the medium duration varieties like Numoli, Dholi, Shraboni. For staggered planting in sali season suitable varieties are Prafulla and Gitesh. Farmers of ␀lood prone district can take submergence tolerant rice varieties for ␀lash-␀lood situation: Ranjit Sub1, Bahadur Sub1, Jalashree, Jalkunwari, Dholi. In case of late planting in ␀lood-aﬀected area/direct seeded late Sali are Luit, Kapilee, Dishang. Seed treatment: Put the seeds in normal water, stirred well, sunken seeds are selected and the ␀loated ones are rejected. For wet method, selected seeds should be soaked directly in fungicidal suspensions of carboxin @ 2.0 g/l of water for 24 hours. One liter of fungicide solution is required to treat one kg of seed. In case of dry method, put the seeds in a container and add carboxin @ 2.0 g/kg seed and mixed thoroughly by agitating them for ␀ive minutes. Nursery management: Land is thoroughly puddled and seedbeds of 10 m length and 1.25 m breadth are prepared with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_41:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_41,2,"30 cm gap in between the beds. The length of the bed may vary according to convenience. In each seedbed 20-30 kg cow dung/compost, 80 g urea, 80g SSP and 40g MOP are to be applied and mixed well with the soil. Well germinated seeds are to be sown @ 650 g to 1 kg per bed depending on grain size. Requirement of seed for transplanting one hectare of main ␀ield is 40-45 kg. Irrigation water should be applied in furrows to maintain saturated condition in the surface soil of the nursery bed. However, standing water to a depth of 2-3 cm should be maintained at least 2-3 days before uprooting. As soon as one or two blast spots are seen, ediphenphos @ 1 ml/l of water is to be sprayed. For management of root knot nematode, apply, Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 20 g /sq. m at the time of sowing. Assam Transplanting: One ploughing should be given at least 21 days prior to transplanting. An irrigation for land soaking should be applied before preparatory tillage. The ␀inal puddling should be done 4-5 days prior to transplanting. One irrigation should be applied before ␀inal puddling. 25 days old seedlings of short and medium duration varieties should be transplanted by maintaining a row-to-row and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_41:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_41,3,"plant-to-plant spacing of 20 cm × 15 cm. In case of long duration varieties, 35-40 days old seedlings are to be transplanted at 25 cm × 15 cm spacing. It is advised to plant 2- 3 seedlings per hill, at a depth of 4-5 cm, for all varieties. Nutrient management: Well rotten FYM or compost @ 10 t/ha has to be applied during ␀ield preparation. In addition, for semidwarf varieties, 60 kg N/ha, 20 kg P₂O₅/ha and 40 kg K₂O/ha and for tall varieties, 20 kg N/ha, 10 kg P₂O₅/ha and 10 kg K₂O/ are to be applied in areas with moderate fertility level. In case of poor soil, the rates of fertilizers may be required to increase to the extent of 60:30:30 kg/ha N, P₂O₅ and K₂O respectively. Half of urea and whole of super phosphate and muriate of potash should be applied at the time of ␀inal puddling. Of the remaining part of urea, half at tillering stage i.e. 20-30 days after transplanting and other half at panicle initiation stage should be applied. Two weedings should be given with paddy weeder or hoe at 20 and 40 days after transplanting. For weed control, pretilachlor @ 0.75 kg/ha or anilofos is to be applied @ 0.4 kg/ha at 3 days after transplanting. In sali rice, application of 5 cm",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_41:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_41,4,"irrigation water 3 days after disappearance of ponding water is recommended in medium and heavy soils. In rainfed kharif rice, height of bunds should be 30 cm to retain rainwater. Plant protection measures: To control the rice stem borer, whorl maggot, gall midge and leaf folder, spray ␀ipronil 5SC @1.5-2 ml/l of water. To control thrips and plant hopper, spray imidacloprid 70 WG @0.3 g/l of water or thiamethoxam 25 WG@0.03 g/l of water. Against Rice Hispa, spray lamda-cyhalothrin 5 EC @ 12.5g /per ha. To control rice pests, erect 50 'T'-perches per ha 2 ft (60 cm) above crop canopy as roosting site for insectivorous birds, which are to be removed before ␀lowering in order to prevent activity of granivorous birds. To prevent rice blast, spray hexaconazole 5EC @ 2g/l of water at tillering stage (40-55 days after sowing) and subsequently give two more sprays of ediphenphos @ 1ml/l of water, one at panicle initiation stage and the other when the tip of the panicle just comes out. Management of direct seeded late Sali: Field should be prepared just after recession of ␀lood by ploughing, cross ploughing and laddering to bring it to a puddle Seedlings of Flood Tolerant Rice variety-",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_41:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_41,5,Ranjit sub-1 during ␀lood Installation of T Perch in Rice Field 2524,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_42:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_42,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 OILSEED CROPS Selection of varieties: Recommended hybrid variety are Ganga 5, Vivek Maize Hybrid 47, Vivek Maize Hybrid 53, Bio 9544 and composite variety are Dhawal, Navjot Nutrient management and intercultural operation: A combination of organic and inorganic fertilizer gives better results than inorganic fertilizer alone. Compost or FYM @ 5 t/ha should be applied. In addition, 60 kg N/ha, 40 kg P₂O₅/ha and 40 kg K₂O/ha should be applied. For Hills Zone, a dose of 90 kg N/ha, 40 kg P₂O₅/ha and 40 kg K₂O/ha are recommended under rainfed condition. FYM or compost should be applied during land preparation. The entire quantity of phosphorus and potash and half of the total urea is to be applied in furrows (8-10 cm deep) and covered with 4- 5cm of soil. Sowing of seed should be done at least 2 days after fertilizer application. Light hoeing and earthing up should be done as and when necessary. For further adequate control of weed, simazine should be applied @ 0.5-1.0 kg a.i/ha in 1000 liters of water a pre-emergence spray. Land preparation & sowing: Any well drained soil is suitable for maize. Sandy and sandy loam fertile soils are preferable. It",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_42:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_42,2,"requires a deep ␀ine and ␀irm tilth. Depending upon the seed size, about 18-22.5 kg of seeds/ha (2.5-3 kg/ bigha) are required. Seeds should be dressed with carboxin @ 2 g/kg of seed. Seeds should be dibbled at a depth of 3-4 cm in rows 65-75 cm apart and at a distance of 20- 25 cm from seed to seed within the rows. Two seeds per hill are to be sown followed by thinning10 days after germination retaining one seedling/ hill. condition. Sprouted seeds should be sown in lines 20 cm apart with a seed rate of 75 kg/ha should be maintained. Need based fertilizer application is advocated. Pre- emergence herbicide pretilachlor @ 0.75 kg a.i./ha should be applied 2-3 days after sowing. Wherever, water management is possible, two irrigations at panicle initiation and ␀lowering stages are recommended. Plant protection: When infestation of stem borer is noticed, ␀ipronil 5 SC @ 1.0 kg/ha in 200-250 liters of water should be sprayed with power sprayer or in 700-800 liters of water with hand sprayer. To control the fall army worm apply emamectin benzoate3% WG+ thiamethoxam 12% WG @ 0.1 % followed by application of chlorantraniliprole 18.5 % Sc @ 0.025% at 7 days interval. Sesamum Selection of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_42:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_42,3,"varieties: Varieties like ST 1683, AST-1, SP 1181 (Madhavi), Gouri, Vinayak are suitable for Assam condition. Well drained sandy loam soils are preferable. Land should be prepared to a ␀ine tilth by 3-4 ploughings followed by laddering. Sow the seeds from July to ␀irst fortnight of August@ 4 kg/ha for both Maize Maize Variety Bio 9544 Assam Blackgram Land preparation & sowing: The land is to be ploughed 2-3 times followed by leveling. Surface drains should be provided to facilitate quick removal of excess water from the ␀ield. Requisite amount of lime is to be applied after soil test to bring soil pH around 6.0. For seed inoculation with Rhizobium cultures of Shillongani, Ahatguri, Kamalabari or any other suitable strains should be used. Seeds are inoculated with 50 g/kg of seeds. Also inoculate seeds with PSB @ 50 g/kg seed along with rhizobium. Sow black gram seeds @ 22.5 kg/ha or 3 kg/bigha with a spacing of 30 cm row to row and 10 cm plant to plant. Plant protection: For control of leaf spot, spray copper oxychloride @0.3% (1.8- 2.0 kg/ha in 600-700 liters of water) at an interval of 7-10 days. Alternatively, tebuconazole 25 EC @ 600-700 ml (0.1%) mixed with 600- 700 liter of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_42:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_42,4,"water/ha (80-90 ml in 80 - 90 liters of water/bigha) should be applied. For web blight, spray tebuconazole 25 EC @ 0.1% (600 ml -700 ml mixed with 600-700 liters of water/ha) three times starting from the appearance of the disease at 10 - 15 days interval. Against aphids, jassids, ␀lea beetle, pod borers, pod bug sand leaf folder, spray chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC @ 20 g a.i./ha in 500-700 liters of water. The spread of yellow mosaic virus (YVM) can be checked by controlling white ␀ly by applying thaimethoxam 25 WG @ 0.3g/l. Nutrient management and intercultural operation: Compost or FYM @ 1 t/ha or1.3 q/bigha should be applied. Recommended fertilizer dose is 15 kg N/ha, 35 kg P₂O₅/ha and 15 kg K₂O/ha. The quantity of N is to be reduced proportionately to the quantity of N added in the form of FYM or compost. One weeding at 20-25 days after sowing is to be done. Apply propaquizafop 2.5% + imazethapyr 3.75% (ready mix) @ 125 g /ha (commercial product @ 2 l / ha) at 15-20 DAS as post emergence. Selection of varieties: For normal sowing, Pant U 19, SBC 40, SBC 47, AAU SHN Urd 02 (Lakhi), PU-31, Manas. In case of late sowing Beki (SB 27-3), Kolong (SB 25-19), Sonkush (SB 23-5). PULSE",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_42:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_42,5,"CROPS broadcasting and line sowing and maintain the spacing 30 cm between rows 15 cm between plants Nutrient management and intercultural operation: Compost or FYM should be applied @ 10 t/ha. Fertilizer @ 30 kg N/ha, 20 kg P O /ha and 20 kg K O/ha should 2 5 2 also be applied at the time of sowing. One weeding should be done at 20 days after owing by khurpi or hoe. The crop should be thinned out simultaneously to maintain the required spacing within the rows. Plant protection: Seeds should be treated with metalaxyl or carboxin @2 g /kg of seed against stem rot as well as phytophthora blight. Alternatively, seeds should be treated with a commercial formulation of Trichoderma spp. @5 g/kg of seeds against stem rot and phytophthora blight. In phytophthora blight endemic areas, sesamum is to be rotated with cereals at every two years. In the case of phyllody disease, the infected plants should be rouged out. Seed treatment with imidacloprid 70 WG @6 g/kg of seed followed by three sprays of thiomethoxam 25WG @ 2 g/10 liters of water at 20, 35 and 50 days after germination of sesame seeds. 2726",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
