ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_47:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_47,4,"measures need to be taken care for better growth and successful culture operation. Maintenance of proper pH of water body. Congenial pH for ␀ish culture is 6.5-7.8. If pH goes down apply lime (quick lime/ Agri lime whichever is available) as per recommended dose. Suf␀icient sun light exposure in the culture pond. Apply supplementary feed according to the feeding habit of the culture ␀ish. The rate of feed application may be @3-5% of body weight. Periodic monitoring of water quality parameters like Dissolved Oxygen, Alkalinity, Hardness, Ammonia, Transparency etc. Trial netting in stocking pond fortnightly to check the ␀ish growth and health management. Flood mitigation measures need to be taken care well in advance. Fishery 3130",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_48:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_48,1,"Bihar Under low land area farmers are advised for selection of paddy varieties of long duration like Swarna sub-1, Rajendra Mahsuri, Rajendra Bhagwati, Rajendra Rajshree, Rajendra Neelum, Swarna Samridhi, Sabour Deep, Sabour Sampan and for medium duration varieties like Rajendra Sweta, Sonam, SS-1, DRR Dhan 44 DBW- 187, Swarn Shakti, BPT-5204, Arize -6444, Rupali, MTU-1001, MTU-1001, Sabour Harshit. Farmers. Under upland condition the short duration paddy varieties like Sabour Ardhjal, Sahbhagi, CR Dhaan-40, Turanta, Sabour Sri, Shushk Samrat, Swarn Shreya etc. can be selected and sown directly through DSR method. Raise nursery sowing 25 May to 10 June and transplanting during 15 June to 20 June is advised. Seedling age at transplanting is 20-25 days and spacing is 20 x 15 cm (line transplanting preferred). Paddy Farmers must treat their seed before sowing of seedling through carbendazim-2.5 g / k g p l u s S t r e p t o c y c l i n e @ 1 . 0 g p e r 3 k g s e e d . A p p l i c a t i o n o f Mancozeb+Carbendazim (2g/kg seed) or Trichoderma viride (10g/kg seed) can also use for seed treatment. Prepare slurry and coat thoroughly for fungal suppression. For nutrient management (kg/ha)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_48:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_48,2,"of short-duration varieties consists of basal dose of 44 N (neem-coated urea), 190 P₂O₅(SSP), 34 K₂O (MOP) and topdressing is 44 N + 17 K₂O at 25 DAP; 44 N at 45 DAP and for long duration varieties basal dose is 58 N + 250 P₂O₅+ 45 K₂O and top dressing: 58 N + 23 K₂O at 30 DAP; 58 N at 50 DAP is advised. For weed control in paddy nursery, application of N: P: K 1:1:1 kg for (100 m²) area and Pyrazosulfuron Ethyl 10 WP @6g/Kattha (1365 sq. feet or 151 m²) before 12 hours of sowing is advised. Soil fertility can be enhanced with incorporation with Dhaincha (Sesbania aculeata) as a green manure 60-70 days pre-transplanting, ploughed under 15-20 days before transplanting. CEREAL CROPS Bihar Eﬀective management of yellow stem borer (Tryporyza incertulus) and leaf folder (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) in paddy can be achieved by clipping terminal shoots prior to transplanting, followed by the application of Cartap Hydrochloride @2.0 g/L of water. A second application at the same concentration should be administered 20 days after the ␀irst treatment. To protect paddy nursery and other crops from grasshopper by spraying of cypermethrin 25% EC @1ml/L water or cypermethrin 10% EC @2.5 ml/L water",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_48:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_48,3,"or Deltamethrin 2.8% EC @1.5 ml/L of water is advised. After 2-3 days spray Neem oil @5ml/L of water. For successful maize cultivation, farmers are advised to begin land preparation in May and incorporate 3-4 quintals of lime per hectare. Sowing should be carried out in the ␀irst week of June or with the onset of the monsoon. During land preparation, the application of 100-150 quintals of well-decomposed cow dung compost is recommended to enrich soil fertility. Preferred maize varieties include PMH-3, Orange Flint, HQPM-1, and HQPM-5 short to medium duration hybrids: HQPM-1, Rajendra Shankar Makka-3, Vivek-27. Bio 9681, All Rounder and P-3522 are the Long-duration hybrids. A seed rate of 20 kg per hectare with a spacing of 60 cm × 20 cm is advised for optimal plant growth. Additionally, proper drainage systems must be established to prevent water stagnation in the ␀ield. Maize For eﬀective management of Fall Armyworm (Spodoptera frugiperda) in maize, application of sand should be carried out at the whorl formation stage and upon the Nursey raising for transplantation in paddy Management of fall army wall 3332",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_49:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_49,1,"Bihar Under low land area farmers are advised for selection of paddy varieties of long duration like Swarna sub-1, Rajendra Mahsuri, Rajendra Bhagwati, Rajendra Rajshree, Rajendra Neelum, Swarna Samridhi, Sabour Deep, Sabour Sampan and for medium duration varieties like Rajendra Sweta, Sonam, SS-1, DRR Dhan 44 DBW- 187, Swarn Shakti, BPT-5204, Arize -6444, Rupali, MTU-1001, MTU-1001, Sabour Harshit. Farmers. Under upland condition the short duration paddy varieties like Sabour Ardhjal, Sahbhagi, CR Dhaan-40, Turanta, Sabour Sri, Shushk Samrat, Swarn Shreya etc. can be selected and sown directly through DSR method. Raise nursery sowing 25 May to 10 June and transplanting during 15 June to 20 June is advised. Seedling age at transplanting is 20-25 days and spacing is 20 x 15 cm (line transplanting preferred). Paddy Farmers must treat their seed before sowing of seedling through carbendazim-2.5 g / k g p l u s S t r e p t o c y c l i n e @ 1 . 0 g p e r 3 k g s e e d . A p p l i c a t i o n o f Mancozeb+Carbendazim (2g/kg seed) or Trichoderma viride (10g/kg seed) can also use for seed treatment. Prepare slurry and coat thoroughly for fungal suppression. For nutrient management (kg/ha)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
