ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_50:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_50,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Farmers are advised to select recommended varieties for cultivation of pulse crops are as follows: Pigeonpea/Arhar: Medium (150- 160 days) UPAS-120, Bahar, Pusa9, Pusa- 992, Asha and for long duration 170-180 days T-21, IPA-203, C-11. Birsa Arhar-1, Bahar, UPAS, IPA-203, Narendra Arhar-1, Narendra Arhar-2. Black Gram: Birsa Urad- 1, WBU-09, Pant U-31. Green Gram: SML- 668, IPM-2,3, HUM-16. Horse gram: Birsa Kulthi-1, Indira Kulthi-1, VLG-19. Farmers are advised to select and sow pigeon pea in upland area where good water drainage facility is available. Use variety Narendra Arhar-1, Malviya Arhar (MAL-13) for drought tolerant area. Farmer are advice to harvest the crop when 80-85% pods turn brown but delay in harvesting may lead to pod shattering and yield loss. For eﬀective management of Wilt (Fusarium spp.) farmers are advised to use resistant varieties (e.g., Bahar); practice crop rotation. For Podborer (Helicoverpa armigera) spray Spinosad 45 SC @0.3 ml/L or Emamectin Benzoate 5 SG @0.5 g/L at ␀lowering and pod formation stages and Sterility Mosaic Virus can be controlled by removing infected plants; control white␀ly/vector using Imidacloprid 17.8",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_50:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_50,2,"SL @0.5 ml/L. Weed management can be done and ␀irst intercultural operation 20-25 days after sowing and Second operation can be done 40-45 days after sowing. Apply Pendimethalin 1.0 kg a.i./ha as pre-emergence herbicide (within 2 days of sowing). PULSE CROPS Farmers are advice to select recommended varieties for cultivation of oil seed crops are as follows: Groundnut: K-1812, K-6, Dharni, Birsa Mungfali-3, Birsa Mungfali-4, Birsa Bold, Niger: Birsa Niger-1, Birsa Niger-3, Sesame: RT-351, Krishna, Kanke Safed, Shekhar, Soyabean: Birsa Safed Soyabean-2, JS-2098, Sun␀lower: DCS-107. Groundnut is a promising oilseed crop for the kharif season in the rainfed uplands and medium lands of Bihar Zones IIIA and IIIB. The optimal sowing period is between 15␀␀ June to 5␀␀ July, in line with monsoon onset. Avoid delay beyond mid-July to reduce risk of wilt and pod borer incidence. Seed rate: 12-15 kg/ha with Spacing: 60 cm (row to row) × 20 cm (plant to plant) is practice. Recommended varieties include TG-37A, JL-24, ICGV- 91114, ICGS-44, and Girnar-2, which are early to medium maturing and resistant to foliar diseases. Groundnut seeds should be treated with Carbendazim or Mancozeb (2 g/kg) and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_50:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_50,3,"inoculated with Rhizobium and PSB cultures to enhance nitrogen ␀ixation and phosphorus uptake. Use a seed rate of 80-100 kg/ha and maintain 30 x 10 cm spacing for optimal plant population. appearance of 5% damage symptoms. This should be followed by a spray of Emamectin Benzoate 5 SG at 0.4 g per litre of water, ␀ive days after sand application. Subsequently, a second spray using a combination formulation of Thiamethoxam 12.6% + Lambda-Cyhalothrin 9.5% @0.5 ml per litre of water should be administered 15 days after the ␀irst insecticidal application. OILSEED CROPS Diagnostic visit in pulse ␀ield Bihar Nutrient management involves basal application of 20:40:30 kg/ha N:P₂O₅: K₂O (through urea, SSP, and MOP), with an additional 250 kg/ha gypsum at ␀lowering for better pod development. In zinc-de␀icient soils, apply 25 kg ZnSO₄/ha. Provide life- saving irrigation at ␀lowering and pod development stages if monsoon rains are erratic. Proper soil moisture during pegging is crucial for good pod formation. Major pests and diseases include leaf spot, collar rot, aphids and bud necrosis virus. Leaf spots can be managed by spraying Mancozeb 75 WP @2.5 g/L while sucking pests should be",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_50:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_50,4,"controlled using Imidacloprid 17.8 SL 0.3 ml/L. Harvest should be done when most leaves yellow and pods mature internally (dark shell markings). Avoid delay in harvesting to prevent a␀latoxin contamination. Under recommended practices, yields of 15-18 q/ha can be achieved with potential to exceed 25 q/ha under favourable conditions. Storing of oilseed in new bags after proper sun drying and treatments. Farmers are advised to purchase the inputs like seed, fertilizers and fungicide for seed treatment well in advance. FRUIT & VEGETABLE CROPS Farmers are advised to grow fruit crops like Mango, Litchi, Guava, Papaya and Citrus fruit. Irrigate mango and litchi plants at weekly interval for proper fruit growth and development. To control premature fruit dropping in mango and litchi, farmers are advised to spray Plano␀ix@4ml/10 L of water at an interval of 10-12 days. Fruit cracking is major problem in Litchi, it can be prevented with regular irrigation, mulching and fresh water spraying during dry spells. For better fruit development farmers are advice to apply n-triacontanol (Miraculan) @0.5 ml/L and moisture conservation can be done by the practice of basin mulching using",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_50:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_50,5,"straw/grasses. For control of mango mealy bug spraying of Dimethoate 30EC @1.0 ml/L or Neem oil @5ml/L twice at 10-12 days interval followed by 2 spray of Plano␀ix @4 ml/10 L water at 10-12 interval to check fruit drop. For fruit borer in mango, spray chlorpyriphos 50 % EC+Cypermethrin 5% EC @2.5 ml/L water or Lamda-cyhalothrin 5% EC @0.5 ml /L water or Indoxacarb 14.5 SC @0.5 -1 ml /L water. For fruit ␀ly control, spray Deltamethrin 2.8 EC @1 ml/L water or Spinoza 45 SC @1 ml/water at 15 days internal. For setting of pheromone traps in mango orchards, 10 traps per ha is advised in Mango orchards. For Mango hopper, spray with Imidacloprid 17.8 SL @0.5- 1 ml/L water at 15 days internal. To control Field preparation 3534",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
