ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_53:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_53,5,"monsoon to improve soil fertility and farmer income. The onset of the monsoon in June increases humidity and causes a spike in vector- borne and waterborne diseases in livestock. Farmers are advised to ensure clean housing and proper drainage to avoid water stagnation around sheds. Ensure adequate drinking water and shade (thatched or tree-based) in animal sheds. Clean water should be provided to the animals three times a day. Milk utensils and other equipment should be frequently cleaned. Maintain strict biosecurity and avoid overcrowding in livestock and poultry farm. Suf␀icient space should be maintained to avoid overcrowding. The ␀loor of the animal shed should be cleaned regularly to avoid disease infestations. Sanitize the vehicle/cart used by infected animals, premises, shed and other equipment properly by solution of 2% red potash. Dusting of bleaching powder or lime in the vicinity. For poultry, ensure dry bedding with rice husk or sawdust, and use potassium permanganate or lime powder around sheds to reduce microbial load. Avoid overgrazing during monsoon as it increases the risk of parasitic infections. Regular deworming should be done before the rainy season especially",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_53:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_53,6,in young calves and kids using albendazole or fenbendazole under veterinary guidance. Deworming of birds with Piperazin hydrochloride @5ml per 10 birds is recommended. Proper Mulching in crop ␀ield 3736,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_54:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_54,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Fisheries To increase the feed intake in high yielding dairy animal during heat stress, farmers should practice urea treatment of dry straw (4 kg urea in 40 litres water per 100 kg straw) to enhance its digestibility. Supplement animal diets with mineral mixture and common salt, and in lactating animals, give bypass protein and calcium supplements to maintain milk production. Ensure availability of green fodder during this season. Cultivate fodder crops like Maize, Sorghum, Cowpea and Napier to provide fresh and nutritious feed. In goats and sheep, provide bamboo slat ␀looring or dry raised platforms to prevent foot rot during wet months. Clean water should be provided to the animals three times a day. Farmers are advised to administer Electrol Powder 2g and Vimeral 5 ml per 5 litre water for adults. In case of disease outbreak in animals, wash the infected animal tongue, mouth, feet and nose by 1% red potash or 2% baking soda 2-3 times in a day. For adult birds, mix 2 g of Electrol powder and 5 ml of Vimeral in 5 litres of water. If the chick shows symptoms like drowsiness, cough and distorted feet appearing or change in colour of excreta then",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_54:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_54,2,"immediately consult the nearest Veterinarian. Fisherman are advised to prepare their own feed from locally available materials like oil cake, undecomposed grains, rice bran, mineral salt etc. (To prepare 100 kg ␀ish feed there is need of 40 kg oil cake, 19 kg undecomposed grain (␀loor), 40 kg rice bran and 1 kg mineral mixture). In order to maintain the water colour light green, ␀ill the pond with fresh water as and when needed. Also to maintain the proper water quality, apply lime @250 kg/ha and Potassium permagnate 500g/ha. Harvest only that much quantity which can be sold locally. Beware of gathering of ␀ish while catching and selling the ␀ish and at any cost maintain the social distancing. vaccination schedule should be followed before the onset of rainy season for prevention of Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD), Haemorrhagic Septicaemia (HS), Black Quarter (BQ) in cattle and buﬀaloes, and Peste des Petits Ruminants (PPR) in goats. Poultry must be protected from Ranikhet and fowl pox. Diagnostic visit to pond Chhatisgarh CEREAL CROPS Varieties: Farmers are advised to grow high-yielding varieties rice varieties for sowing in the Kharif season, such as Vikram-TCR, Durgeshwari,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_54:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_54,3,"Chhattisgarh Sugandhit Bhog, Indira Aerobic-1, CG-1919, MTU-1318, CG Devbhog. Paddy Seeds should be treated with Azospirillum and PSB @ 5-10 g/kg of seed before sowing. Line sowing method should be adopted in paddy cultivation and a pre-emergence herbicide to be sprayed three days after sowing. Line sowing can be done using a seed-cum-fertilizer drill in a well-pulverized ␀ield. In leveled ␀ields, sowing should be carried out at a row spacing of 20 cm using implements such as a tractor-drawn seed drill, Indira seed drill, Nari plough, or Bhoramdev seed drill. The seeding depth should not exceed 3-4 cm. Proper calibration of the seed drill is essential to maintain the recommended seed rate accurately. Rice Field preparation: Cleaning of the ␀ield and bund management should be done before the monsoon, and summer ploughing to done which helps to destroy pathogens and weed seeds. Weed management: Paddy should be sown in line and pre-emergence herbicide like Pretilachlor 50% EC @1500 ml/ha or Pyrazosulfuron 10% WP@ 200 ml/ha Soil testing: Farmers are advised to get their soil tested. For this, they should contact the local agricultural of␀icer or nearby Krishi Vigyan Kendra. Based on",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_54:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_54,4,"the soil test results, balanced fertilizers should be applied accordingly. Seed rate: Paddy seeds should be treated with a 17% salt solution before raising the nursery or direct seeding. Use the recommended seed rate: for line sowing, 80-90 kg/ha; for the Biasi and broadcast methods, 100-120 kg/ha. For the transplanting method, prepare the nursery in approximately 1/10␀␀ of the total ␀ield area. Use 50 kg/ha of seed for thick-grained varieties and 40 kg/ha for thin-grained varieties. 3938",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
