ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_61:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_61,6,"wheat, maize, wheat bran, oilcakes and salt. They can also prepare silage for their adult dairy animals. Due to increased maximum temperatures, goats should be kept in shaded areas and given clean, fresh water three times daily. Vaccinate goats against PPR (Peste des Petits Ruminants), Contagious Pneumonia, and ETV (Enterotoxaemia). Also, implement control measures for ticks and lice. To control ectoparasites, apply Butox or Cleaner @ 2 ml/L of water over the animal's body, ensuring the mouth is covered during application. Use smoke in animal shelters to keep away mosquitoes and other insects. Pit for planting of fruit sapling Vaccination of animals 4544",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_62:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_62,1,"Goa Prepare land for Kharif paddy and new orchards. Begin nursery sowing of Kharif rice Crop-wise Advisory. Mango Banana Harvest stage: Remove fallen fruits; orchard hygiene. Fruit rot risk: Hot water treat fruits (48°C, 1 hr). Anthracnose: Spray Carbendazim @2g/L on seedlings. New planting: Space 5×5m; ␀ill pits with FYM, neem cake, rock phosphate Sowing of Kharif rice in nursery can be done. Procure good quality seeds, fertilizers and other inputs. As the Rainy season is approaching, all the farmers are advised to repair the bunds of rice ␀ields and keep bunds weed free. While pudding the ␀ield, green leaf manures or biomass could be added and incorporated @5t/ha. When the intensity of rainfall is low, apply 1 kg urea per 100 m² to the rice nursery. Control the crabs in the rice ␀ield by collecting during night time. FRUIT CROPS Clear drainage; avoid waterlogging. Provide staking support to young plants Paddy CEREAL CROPS Goa's tropical monsoon climate, with high humidity and heavy rainfall, supports Kharif crops like paddy (the staple), pulses, groundnut, and vegetables. The region's lateritic and alluvial soils, ample rain, and moderate temperatures favor crop growth. To",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_62:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_62,2,"optimize yields and manage risks such as pest outbreaks and waterlogging, timely and location-speci␀ic practices are essential. This advisory provides key guidelines on land preparation, crop choice, pest and nutrient management, and sustainable farming for the Kharif season in Goa. Coconut Arecanut Cashew nut Apply fertilizer in early June. Remove dried/diseased leaves. Fruit rot: Spray 1% Bordeaux. Prepare pits with FYM before planting. Ensure drainage; staking for young plants. Apply ␀irst fertilizer split early June. P r u n e d a m a g e d b ra n c h e s ; a p p ly B o r d e a u x p a s t e . C S R B : A p p l y Fipronil/Imidacloprid on trunk/roots. Remove grubs, apply Chlorpyrifos or Neem oil/neem cake. Clear drainage, provide staking. New planting: Space 7×7m (normal), 5×5m (high density). LIVESTOCK Neem-garlic spray for mites, starch for white␀ly. Use sticky traps; ␀ill axils with neem cake + sand. Mulch basins; irrigate. New planting: Pit size 1.2×1.2×1.2m; spacing 7.5×7.5m To protect animals from lightning, ensure shelters are dry and provide a gunny bag on the body of the animal for insulation. Identify high-ground sites for building shelters to prevent ␀looding.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_62:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_62,3,"Implement mass vaccination programs for Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD), Hemorrhagic Septicemia (HS), and Black Quarter (BQ) to safeguard animal health. Regular veterinary visits should be ensured for proper care, and proper carcass disposal must be followed. Store dry fodder in a well-ventilated area to avoid mouldy feed, which can be harmful to animals. Grow Hybrid Napier CO- 5 for green fodder to provide a nutritious feed source. To control tick infestations, spray Deltamethrin and ␀lame the shed every 10-15 days to maintain hygiene and prevent diseases. Poultry To maintain optimal conditions for poultry during the monsoon season, it is crucial to prevent litter wetness by using fresh litter or applying lime to absorb excess moisture. Clean the waterers and feeders daily to avoid contamination and ensure the birds have access to clean drinking water. Adding 5% fat to the feed during rains can help maintain energy levels and support egg production. Use arti␀icial lighting to maintain consistent egg production during shorter daylight hours. Adhere to the vaccination schedule to prevent diseases like Fowl Pox and Infectious Bursal Disease (IBD). Ensure the poultry house is well- Goa",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_62:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_62,4,Diagnostic visit on cashew Back yard poultry rearing by Woman farmer with KVK scientist 4746,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
