ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_63:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_63,4,Diagnostic visit on cashew Back yard poultry rearing by Woman farmer with KVK scientist 4746,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_64:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_64,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 l Reduction in day length hamper egg production in layers. Hence, ␀lorescence light may be provided which mimic the daylight l Vaccination should be done strictly as per vaccination schedule for poultry maintained with a functional drainage system before the monsoon begins, and keep the doors closed with curtains to prevent rainwater from entering the shed. In areas with heavy rainfall, such as Goa, it is recommended to raise the ␀loor and install a generous roof overhang (4-5 feet) over the entrance to protect the birds. If the litter material becomes excessively wet, replenish it with fresh material or treat it with slaked lime at 1 kg per 10 square meters. Always check for mould growth in feeders and waterers, and provide clean drinking water or use chlorinated water by adding 2 g of bleaching powder per 1000 liters of water. The feed storage should be regularly checked for moulds and fungus infection. Toxin binder may be provided in feed formulation especially in duck feed. l Hence, adequate hygiene and biosecurity measures should be strictly followed to curb the outbreak of any disease. l High energy source such as fat @ 5% may be added in feed",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_64:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_64,2,"Gujarat Groundnut SOUTH SAURASHTRA Gujarat provides region-speci␀ic, science-based recommendations to help farmers improve productivity and resilience during the monsoon season. With climate variability and resource constraints in mind, it promotes integrated crop management, timely pest-disease control, ef␀icient water-nutrient use, and adoption of improved seed varieties. Tailored to the state's varied soils and rainfall patterns, this guidance aims to support sustainable farming and secure farmer livelihoods across Gujarat. This region includes Amreli, Bhavnagar, Botad, Devbhumi-Dwarka, Gir-Somnath, Jamnagar, Junagadh, Morbi, Porbandar, Rajkot, and Surendranagar, SAU: Junagarh Agricultural University, Junagarh (Gujarat). They have an average rainfall of 400- 1000 mm. Soils are shallow to medium black soils, often aﬀected by salinity and alkalinity. Groundnut cultivation begins with deep ploughing the ␀ield 2-3 times to achieve a ␀ine tilth up to 25-30 cm depth. Incorporating 5-7 t/ha of well-decomposed farmyard manure (FYM) before sowing improves soil fertility. Sowing is generally done during June-July. Recommended semi-spreading varieties include GJG-22, GG-20, and Girnar-4,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_64:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_64,3,"while erect types include GJG-32, GJG-17, and KDG-128. For optimal plant spacing, maintain 60 × 10 cm for semi-spreading types and 45 × 10 cm for erect ones. Seeds should be treated with Vitavax and Rhizobium at 375-500 g/ha to promote healthy germination and nitrogen ␀ixation. Weed control involves pre-emergence application of Pendimethalin at 1.0 kg/ha, followed by two hand weedings at 20 and 40 days after sowing (DAS), or alternatively, post-emergence application of Quizalofop-P-ethyl at 50 g/ha. Timely irrigation is crucial, especially during ␀lowering, pegging, and pod development stages in case of dry spells. 4948",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
