ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_74:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_74,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Groundnut Brinjal To improve milk yield in lactating animals, formulate a proper feed rich in essential nutrients. Consider using Azolla as a green fodder replacement to enhance protein intake. During rainy seasons, keep livestock indoors and ensure proper fodder storage. Vaccinate animals against FMD (Foot and Mouth Disease) and Brucellosis, along with other necessary vaccines. Maintain clean and hygienic animal sheds to prevent mastitis. Deworm animals with Fenbendazole, and control ectoparasites using Deltamethrin or Amitraz. This region of the state includes the regions of Banaskantha, Patan, Mehsana, Sabarkantha, Aravalli, and Gandhinagar. The local agricultural university is Sardarkrushinagar Dantiwara Agricultural University (S.K.Nagar, Banaskantha). The region receives rainfall between 700-1000 mm annually and is characterized by loamy sand soil. NORTH GUJARAT-KUTCHH For brinjal cultivation, use recommended varieties: Gujarat Anand Oblong Brinjal 2 and hybrid varieties. The seed rate is 250-300 g/ha, with spacing of 90x60 cm. For nursery management, use Trichoderma virdi and water as needed. For plant protection, control White␀ly with Neem",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_74:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_74,2,"powder/oil spray, and manage Little Leaf by removing aﬀected plants and applying Pyriproxyfen spray. For groundnut cultivation, the latest improved variety GG 37 (Bunchy type) is recommended. The ideal sowing period is from June 15␀␀ to July 10␀␀, with a seed rate of 100-120 kg/ha and a row spacing of 45 cm. Employ the FIR approach (Fungicide, Insecticide, Rhizobium) for seed treatment, using Mancozeb @ 2.5 g, Quinalphos 25 ml, and Rhizobium 10 ml/kg of seed to manage white grub and collar rot. Apply a fertilizer dose of 12.5:25:0 NPK kg/ha, along with 8-10 t/ha of FYM. Supplement with secondary nutrient sulfur at 20 kg/ha. For collar rot management, apply Chilli For chili cultivation, recommended varieties include GVC-101, Anand Jwala, and hybrid varieties. The seed rate is 750 g/ha, with spacing of 60x60 cm. Apply a basal fertilizer of 50:50:50 (NPK) kg/ha. For plant protection, control Thrips with Neem powder/oil spray and use Spinosad for severe infestations. Manage Leaf Curl virus with Pyriproxyfen or Fenprofethin spray. For plant protection, control Heliothis with marigold planting, manage Sterility Mosaic with Propargite spray, and control Powdery Mildew with Sulfur or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_74:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_74,3,"Carbendazim spray. Tomato For tomato cultivation, recommended varieties include Gujarat Tomato-2, Gujarat Tomato-5, and Anand Tomato-8. The seed rate is 200-250 g/ha, and the ideal spacing is 90x75 cm or 70x60 cm. For nursery management, apply Metalaxil MZ to prevent root rot and use micro-nutrient sprays. For plant protection, control Leaf Miner with Neem powder/oil spray, and use Spinosad for severe infestations. Manage Early Blight with Mancozeb or Chlorothalonil spray. Gujarat Pomegranate Black Gram Pearl Millet For new pomegranate plantations, use varieties like Bhagwa and Solapur Red, planting in June-July at a spacing of 4 × 3 m using 60 × 60 × 60 cm pits. In old orchards, practice bahar management by withholding irrigation for up to 30 days. After leaf drop, apply the recommended dose of fertilizers (RDF) and manure in the pits. Spray Ethaphon @ 2 ml/litre of water + 5 g of 0:52:34 fertilizer to aid ␀lowering. Provide light irrigation via drip. For disease management, spray Copper Oxychloride @ 3 g/litre or a combination of Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63% WP @ 2 g/litre. For castor cultivation, use the latest improved hybrids, GCH 7 and GCH 8, which are wilt-tolerant. The",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_74:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_74,4,"ideal sowing time is after 15␀␀ August, with recommended spacing of 150 cm × 120 cm. Apply a fertilizer dose of 135:37.5:0 NPK (kg/ha) along with 8- 10 t/ha of FYM Additionally, use sulfur as a secondary nutrient at 20 kg/ha. To manage semi looper infestations, ensure proper sowing time, ␀ield sanitation to remove plant debris, and remove infected leaves from plants. For pest control, use a foliar spray of Emamectin benzoate 5% SG (3 g), Spinosad 45 SC (3 ml), or Flubendiamide 39.35 SC (10 ml) per 10 litres of water. Green Gram Trichoderma viridi @ 2.5 kg/ha. To address iron chlorosis, use a foliar spray of ferrous sulfate @ 0.5%. For Heliothis and leaf-eating caterpillars, apply a foliar spray of Neem seed extract 5%, Chlorpyriphos 20 EC 20 ml, Spinosad 45 SC 3 ml, Flubendiamide 48 SC 3 ml, or Novaluron 10 EC 20 ml per 10 litres of water. Castor For optimal growth, sow the latest improved hybrid seed with a seed treatment of Azotobacter (5 ml per kg of seed). The recommended seed rate is 4 kg/ha, with a spacing of 45 cm × 10 cm. Apply a fertilizer dose of 80:40:0 NPK (kg/ha) along with 10 tons of FYM per hectare to ensure healthy plant development. For greengram cultivation, use",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_74:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_74,5,"the latest improved varieties such as GM 4, GAM 5, and GM 6. Sow at the onset of the monsoon using a seed rate of 17.5 kg/ha with a spacing of 45 cm × 10 cm. Treat seeds with a fungicide @ 2 g/kg, followed by PSB and Rhizobium inoculation @ 5 ml/kg. Apply fertilizers at 20:40:0 NPK kg/ha along with 5 t/ha of FYM. To manage pod borer, practice deep summer ploughing and maintain proper ␀ield sanitation by removing plant debris and infected plants. Install light or pheromone traps, and apply a foliar spray of Neem oil (30 ml), Emamectin benzoate 5% SG (3 g), or Spinosad 45 SC (3 ml) per 10 litres of water. For black gram cultivation, use improved varieties like GU 1, GU 2, and GU 3. Sow at the onset of the monsoon with a seed rate of 17.5 kg/ha and spacing of 45 cm × 10 cm. Treat seeds with a fungicide @ 2 g/kg, followed by PSB and Rhizobium @ 5 ml/kg. Apply fertilizers at 20:40:0 NPK kg/ha along with 5 t/ha of FYM. For pod borer management, conduct deep summer ploughing, maintain ␀ield sanitation by removing debris and infected plants, and use light or pheromone traps. Spray Neem oil (30 ml), Emamectin benzoate 5% SG (3 g), or Spinosad 45 SC (3 ml) per 10 liters of water for eﬀective",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
