ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_75:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_75,6,control. 5958,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_76:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_76,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Vaccinate livestock against HS and FMD. Protect animals from heat stress by providing shade, clean water, and cooling measures. Maintain hygiene by cleaning udders and controlling ectoparasites with Butox or Taktic (avoid spraying in mangers). Deworm calves older than 3 months and adult livestock regularly. Feed a balanced ration with 30 g salt and 50 g mineral mix daily, ensuring adequate Vitamin A supplementation. Tomato LIVESTOCK Use high-yielding tomato varieties like GAT-8, Arka Rakshak, and other hybrids. Transplant pro-tray raised seedlings onto raised beds with silver-black plastic mulch at 90 × 60 cm spacing. Apply a fertilizer dose of 100:50:50 NPK kg/ha along with 10 tons of FYM/ha. Spray micronutrient mixture during ␀lowering and fruiting for better yield. For early blight and fruit rot, apply Copper Oxychloride @ 3 g/L or Carbendazim 12% + Mancozeb 63% WP @ 2 g/L as symptoms appear. To control fruit borer, spray Spinosad 45 SC @ 3 ml per 10 litres of water. Haryana & Delhi Rice Nursery sowing: For early duration varieties: 15 May to 31 June. Medium, mid-early and hybrid rice: 15 May to 31 May. Seed rate & seed treatment: 20-25 kg/ha seed",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_76:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_76,2,"is suf␀icient for transplanting. Soaking of 1 ha seed (20-30 kg seed) in 25 litre water solution with 25 g bavistin and 2.5 g streptocycline is done for 24 hrs. Treated seed should be covered with wet gunny bags for 24-36 hrs for getting germination of seeds. CEREAL CROPS Improved Varieties: Medium duration: HKR-127, HKR-126, HKR-120, HSD-1, Jaya, PR-106. Mid to early duration: HKR-47, IR-64, HKR 46, HKR 128, Pusa-1509, Pusa- 1121. Early duration: HKR-48, Govind. Seed selection: Select bold and disease-free seed for better results. Treatment of seed with 10 % salt solution should be done to get bold seeds. Transplanting: Manually transplant 2-3 seedlings per hill in lines. Maintain spacing of 15 x 15 cm and depth of should not be more than 2-3 cm. Mechanical transplanting is done by paddy transplanter in puddled and un-puddled conditions. Raising of mat type nursery is required for mechanical transplanting. Nursery raising: Apply 15 to 20 tonnes of FYM per hectare in the nursery ␀ield before sowing of the nursery. Apply 25 kg N, 25 kg P and 25 kg ZnSO₄ per hectare for raising the nursery. Apply second doze of 25 kg N/ha at two weeks after sowing of nursery. If de␀iciency symptoms",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_76:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_76,3,"of iron appear in the nursery, foliar application of 0.5% FeSo₄ should be done. For managements of weeds in the nursery, apply 1.5 kg Pretilachlore 30 EC or 3 litre Butachlore or Thiobencarb at 1-3 days after sowing of the nursery. For management of broad leaf and grassy weeds, apply 250 ml Bispyribak sodium 10 SL at 15 days after sowing of nursery. 6160",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
