ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_77:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_77,2,"is suf␀icient for transplanting. Soaking of 1 ha seed (20-30 kg seed) in 25 litre water solution with 25 g bavistin and 2.5 g streptocycline is done for 24 hrs. Treated seed should be covered with wet gunny bags for 24-36 hrs for getting germination of seeds. CEREAL CROPS Improved Varieties: Medium duration: HKR-127, HKR-126, HKR-120, HSD-1, Jaya, PR-106. Mid to early duration: HKR-47, IR-64, HKR 46, HKR 128, Pusa-1509, Pusa- 1121. Early duration: HKR-48, Govind. Seed selection: Select bold and disease-free seed for better results. Treatment of seed with 10 % salt solution should be done to get bold seeds. Transplanting: Manually transplant 2-3 seedlings per hill in lines. Maintain spacing of 15 x 15 cm and depth of should not be more than 2-3 cm. Mechanical transplanting is done by paddy transplanter in puddled and un-puddled conditions. Raising of mat type nursery is required for mechanical transplanting. Nursery raising: Apply 15 to 20 tonnes of FYM per hectare in the nursery ␀ield before sowing of the nursery. Apply 25 kg N, 25 kg P and 25 kg ZnSO₄ per hectare for raising the nursery. Apply second doze of 25 kg N/ha at two weeks after sowing of nursery. If de␀iciency symptoms",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_77:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_77,3,"of iron appear in the nursery, foliar application of 0.5% FeSo₄ should be done. For managements of weeds in the nursery, apply 1.5 kg Pretilachlore 30 EC or 3 litre Butachlore or Thiobencarb at 1-3 days after sowing of the nursery. For management of broad leaf and grassy weeds, apply 250 ml Bispyribak sodium 10 SL at 15 days after sowing of nursery. 6160",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_78:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_78,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Weed management: Several grassy weeds, broad leaf weeds and sedges infest paddy crop. Weeds can be managed eﬀectively by chemical method. Apply 30 kg butachlor or 15 kg thiobencarb granuls/ ha in 4-5 cm deep water at 2-3 days after transplanting. Apply 3 litre butachlor 50 EC or thiobencarb EC or 1325 ml Anilphose 30 EC or 2 litre Pretilachlor 50 EC or 125 g oxydiazeril 80 % WP after mixing with 150 kg sand and broadcast in standing water at 2-5 days after transplanting. Apply 20 g ready mix of metsulphuron and chlorimuron or 125 g ethoxysulphuron 15 % WG or 1 kg 2,4-D ester at 20-25 DAT against broad leaf weeds. Apply 93.75 ml/ha in 500 liters of water phenoxulam 24 % SC at 8-12 DAT for control of broad leaf weeds. Apply 250 ml bispyribac sodium 10 % SL/ha in 500 litres of water at 15-25 DAT for the control of mix weeds ␀lora in rice. Bajra Seed Treatment: Treat seed with biomix (Azotobactor+ Azospirillum + PSB) @ 250 g for per ha seed. Seed Rate and sowing: Use about 4-5 kg of seed per hectare to get around 175000 plants population per ha. Sowing should be done in lines at the spacing of 45 cm, at depth not more than 2.0 cm. Recommended varieties:",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_78:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_78,2,"HHB 50, HHB 60, HHB 67, HHB 94, HHB 117, HHB 146, HHB 197, HHB 216, HHB 223, HHB 226, HHB 234, HHB 272, HHB 299, HHB 311, HHB 67 (improved 2), HC 10, and HC 20. Nutrient Management: For hybrid varieties in irrigated condition apply 160 kg N/ha + 62.5 kg P₂O₅/ha. For short duration varieties apply 40 kg N/ha + 20 kg P₂O₅/ha. Apply full phosphorus and half of the Nitrogen at the time of the sowing, remaining nitrogen may be applied in two splits, ␀irst at thinking and second at ear formation stage. Plant protection: Coragen (Chlorantraniliprole) 18.5 SC @150 ml/ha, Fame (␀lubendiamide) 480 SC@ 50 ml/ha for rice stem borer and leaf folder. Ulala (␀lonicamid) 50 WG @ 150 g/ha and Osheen (Dinotefuran) 20 SG @ 200 g/ha for plant hoppers. Nativo (tri␀loxystrobin+ tebuconazole) 75 WG @200 g/ha in 500 litre of water for BLB. Awancer Glow (azoxystrobin 8.3 % + mancozeb 66.7 %) 75 WG @ 1.5 kg/ha for sheath blight Amistar Top (azoxystrobin + difenoconazole) 325 SC @ 500 ml in 500 L water per ha for blast. Sowing Time: The appropriate sowing time is July 1-15 but can be sown at the onset of the monsoon, even in whole month of June, if good rainfall is there. Manure and fertilizer management:",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_78:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_78,3,"Application of 15 tonnes of FYM/ha before transplanting of the crop is useful for obtaining good productivity of rice-wheat system continuously. In medium, mid-early and hybrids of rice: Apply 150 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg ZnSO₄ per hectare. In early duration varieties: Apply 120 kg, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg/ha ZnSO₄. Apply 1/3␀␀ N and full P, K and zinc at the time of puddling. Remaining N fertilizers should be applied in two equal splits at 3 and 6 weeks after transplanting. Water Management: If irrigation is available, apply water during critical growth stages: at tillering, ␀lowering, and grain ␀illing. This is especially important under extended dry periods to avoid moisture stress. Haryana & Delhi Fertilizer Application: Rainfed or low rainfall condition, drill 50 kg of N and 20 kg P₂O₅ per hectare in rows at sowing. Irrigated condition, apply 50 kg of N and 20 kg P₂O₅ per hectare at the time of sowing and another 50 kg N per hectare about one month later. Plant protection: Seed treatment with Slayer (thiamethoxam) 30 FS @10 ml/kg seed for the control of shoot ␀ly. Seed treatment with Sulphur dust @ 4 g/kg seed for grain smut. Seed treatment: Inoculation of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_78:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_78,4,"Arhar seed with Rhizobium and PSB biofertilizers are essential for getting better yield of the crop. Improved Varieties: Manak, Paras, Pant Arhar-291, Pant Arhar-16, Rajiv lochan, Pant Arhar-6. Time of Sowing: Under irrigated conditions, sowing of crop should be done in the month of June and under rainfed conditions sowing should be done at the onset of monsoon. Arhar Weed Management: For eﬀective weed control, apply Pendimethalin @ 0.75 kg a.i./ha pre-emergence. Perform manual weeding at 20-25 and 45-50 days after sowing. Use Imazethapyr @ 100 g a.i./ha post-emergence at 20-25 days to control broadleaf and grassy weeds. PULSE CROPS Fertilizer management: Incorporation of 20 kg/ha N, 60 kg/ha P as basal application with sowing and 5 t/ha FYM. Treat seeds with Rhizobium and PSB. For better yield, apply 60 kg/ha sulphur and 25 kg/ha zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21% Zn) or 15 kg/ha monohydrate (33% Zn) in de␀icient soils. Seed rate & spacing: A seed rate of 12.5 to 15 kg/ha is required. Maintain spacing (RxP) of 40x15 cm. Weed Management: Two hand weeding (hoeing) at 20 and 35 days after sowing (DAS). This removes competing weeds and helps conserve soil moisture. Otherwise, apply",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_78:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_78,5,"Atrazine 50% WP at 0.5 kg/ha as a pre-emergence herbicide, and follow with one hand-weeding later. Pest and Disease Management: White Grubs: Apply 0.05% quinalphos 25EC on the trees in and around the ␀ield after ␀irst, second and third rainfall of the season to control the adult. Smut: Treat seeds with Thiram at 4 g/kg to prevent kernel smut. Jowar Downy Mildew: Treat seeds with Metalaxyl 35% @ 6 g/kg seed before planting to prevent seed-borne infection. Time of Sowing: Optimum period of sowing is mid-June to mid-July; Early green fodder- 2ⁿ␀ fortnight of March- 1␀␀ fortnight of April. Improved Varieties: HC-136, HC-171, HC-308, HG-541, HJ-513; Fodder purpose: SSG 59-3 Seed Rate & Spacing: Grain purpose: 12-15 kg/ha at 45 cm line spacing, Fodder Purpose: 35-40 kg/ha at 25-30 cm line spacing. 6362",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_79:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_79,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Weed management: Several grassy weeds, broad leaf weeds and sedges infest paddy crop. Weeds can be managed eﬀectively by chemical method. Apply 30 kg butachlor or 15 kg thiobencarb granuls/ ha in 4-5 cm deep water at 2-3 days after transplanting. Apply 3 litre butachlor 50 EC or thiobencarb EC or 1325 ml Anilphose 30 EC or 2 litre Pretilachlor 50 EC or 125 g oxydiazeril 80 % WP after mixing with 150 kg sand and broadcast in standing water at 2-5 days after transplanting. Apply 20 g ready mix of metsulphuron and chlorimuron or 125 g ethoxysulphuron 15 % WG or 1 kg 2,4-D ester at 20-25 DAT against broad leaf weeds. Apply 93.75 ml/ha in 500 liters of water phenoxulam 24 % SC at 8-12 DAT for control of broad leaf weeds. Apply 250 ml bispyribac sodium 10 % SL/ha in 500 litres of water at 15-25 DAT for the control of mix weeds ␀lora in rice. Bajra Seed Treatment: Treat seed with biomix (Azotobactor+ Azospirillum + PSB) @ 250 g for per ha seed. Seed Rate and sowing: Use about 4-5 kg of seed per hectare to get around 175000 plants population per ha. Sowing should be done in lines at the spacing of 45 cm, at depth not more than 2.0 cm. Recommended varieties:",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_79:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_79,2,"HHB 50, HHB 60, HHB 67, HHB 94, HHB 117, HHB 146, HHB 197, HHB 216, HHB 223, HHB 226, HHB 234, HHB 272, HHB 299, HHB 311, HHB 67 (improved 2), HC 10, and HC 20. Nutrient Management: For hybrid varieties in irrigated condition apply 160 kg N/ha + 62.5 kg P₂O₅/ha. For short duration varieties apply 40 kg N/ha + 20 kg P₂O₅/ha. Apply full phosphorus and half of the Nitrogen at the time of the sowing, remaining nitrogen may be applied in two splits, ␀irst at thinking and second at ear formation stage. Plant protection: Coragen (Chlorantraniliprole) 18.5 SC @150 ml/ha, Fame (␀lubendiamide) 480 SC@ 50 ml/ha for rice stem borer and leaf folder. Ulala (␀lonicamid) 50 WG @ 150 g/ha and Osheen (Dinotefuran) 20 SG @ 200 g/ha for plant hoppers. Nativo (tri␀loxystrobin+ tebuconazole) 75 WG @200 g/ha in 500 litre of water for BLB. Awancer Glow (azoxystrobin 8.3 % + mancozeb 66.7 %) 75 WG @ 1.5 kg/ha for sheath blight Amistar Top (azoxystrobin + difenoconazole) 325 SC @ 500 ml in 500 L water per ha for blast. Sowing Time: The appropriate sowing time is July 1-15 but can be sown at the onset of the monsoon, even in whole month of June, if good rainfall is there. Manure and fertilizer management:",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_79:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_79,3,"Application of 15 tonnes of FYM/ha before transplanting of the crop is useful for obtaining good productivity of rice-wheat system continuously. In medium, mid-early and hybrids of rice: Apply 150 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg ZnSO₄ per hectare. In early duration varieties: Apply 120 kg, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg/ha ZnSO₄. Apply 1/3␀␀ N and full P, K and zinc at the time of puddling. Remaining N fertilizers should be applied in two equal splits at 3 and 6 weeks after transplanting. Water Management: If irrigation is available, apply water during critical growth stages: at tillering, ␀lowering, and grain ␀illing. This is especially important under extended dry periods to avoid moisture stress. Haryana & Delhi Fertilizer Application: Rainfed or low rainfall condition, drill 50 kg of N and 20 kg P₂O₅ per hectare in rows at sowing. Irrigated condition, apply 50 kg of N and 20 kg P₂O₅ per hectare at the time of sowing and another 50 kg N per hectare about one month later. Plant protection: Seed treatment with Slayer (thiamethoxam) 30 FS @10 ml/kg seed for the control of shoot ␀ly. Seed treatment with Sulphur dust @ 4 g/kg seed for grain smut. Seed treatment: Inoculation of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_79:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_79,4,"Arhar seed with Rhizobium and PSB biofertilizers are essential for getting better yield of the crop. Improved Varieties: Manak, Paras, Pant Arhar-291, Pant Arhar-16, Rajiv lochan, Pant Arhar-6. Time of Sowing: Under irrigated conditions, sowing of crop should be done in the month of June and under rainfed conditions sowing should be done at the onset of monsoon. Arhar Weed Management: For eﬀective weed control, apply Pendimethalin @ 0.75 kg a.i./ha pre-emergence. Perform manual weeding at 20-25 and 45-50 days after sowing. Use Imazethapyr @ 100 g a.i./ha post-emergence at 20-25 days to control broadleaf and grassy weeds. PULSE CROPS Fertilizer management: Incorporation of 20 kg/ha N, 60 kg/ha P as basal application with sowing and 5 t/ha FYM. Treat seeds with Rhizobium and PSB. For better yield, apply 60 kg/ha sulphur and 25 kg/ha zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21% Zn) or 15 kg/ha monohydrate (33% Zn) in de␀icient soils. Seed rate & spacing: A seed rate of 12.5 to 15 kg/ha is required. Maintain spacing (RxP) of 40x15 cm. Weed Management: Two hand weeding (hoeing) at 20 and 35 days after sowing (DAS). This removes competing weeds and helps conserve soil moisture. Otherwise, apply",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_79:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_79,5,"Atrazine 50% WP at 0.5 kg/ha as a pre-emergence herbicide, and follow with one hand-weeding later. Pest and Disease Management: White Grubs: Apply 0.05% quinalphos 25EC on the trees in and around the ␀ield after ␀irst, second and third rainfall of the season to control the adult. Smut: Treat seeds with Thiram at 4 g/kg to prevent kernel smut. Jowar Downy Mildew: Treat seeds with Metalaxyl 35% @ 6 g/kg seed before planting to prevent seed-borne infection. Time of Sowing: Optimum period of sowing is mid-June to mid-July; Early green fodder- 2ⁿ␀ fortnight of March- 1␀␀ fortnight of April. Improved Varieties: HC-136, HC-171, HC-308, HG-541, HJ-513; Fodder purpose: SSG 59-3 Seed Rate & Spacing: Grain purpose: 12-15 kg/ha at 45 cm line spacing, Fodder Purpose: 35-40 kg/ha at 25-30 cm line spacing. 6362",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_80:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_80,1,"Haryana & Delhi Fertilizer use: Apply 80-100 Kg N per ha for American Cotton and 50 kg N for desi cotton along with 30 kg P₂O₅/ha. In case of hybrid cotton, 150 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg ZnSo₄ per ha has been recommended. Apply 1/3 dose of N, full dose of P₂O₅, full dose of potash and full dose of ZnSo₄ at time of sowing. Remaining dose of N should be applied in two equal splits at square formation and ␀lowering stage. In sandy soil the research results have revealed that 90 per cent dose of fertilizer through soil application and 10 per cent through foliar spray at the boll development stage gave the highest seed cotton yield. Inoculation of cotton seed with C2, M4 and Azospirillum culture resulted into saving of 25-27 kg N/ha. Seed rate: Use 15-20 kg delinted seed of improved American cotton varieties for sowing in one ha area. 12.5 kg of seed/ha is required for Desi cotton varieties. Seed rate of 3-3.750 kg /ha is required for American cotton hybrids and desi cotton hybrids. Seed rate of 2.125 kg/ha is required for Bt Cotton hybrids. Seed treatment and seed soaking: Before sowing, seed should be dipped in water up to 5-6 hours for better germination. Treat the seed",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_80:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_80,2,"with 5 gm Emisan, 1 gm streptocyclin and 1 gm succinic acid in 10 litres of water. In termite aﬀected areas treat the seed with 10 ml chlorpyriphos apart from above mentioned chemicals. Seed treatment with carbendazim @ 2 gm/kg in the root rot aﬀected areas is essential. Seed treatment with Imidacloprid @ 7.5 gm/kg seed to escape the crops from sucking pests up to 40-60 days. Mango Method of Sowing: Sow the crop in lines 67.5 cm apart with a cotton sowing drill or cotton planter and plant to plant spacing of 60 cm or row to row spacing of 100cm and plant to plant spacing of 45 cm. Sowing should be done at a depth of 4-5 cm. In horticultural crops at fruiting stage such as mango, while carrying out ␀ield operations related to nutrient sprays and crop protection adequate precautions in handling of inputs, Varieties and hybrids: Improved American cotton varieties: HS-6, H-1117, H-1126, H- 1098 Improved, H-1236, H-1300. Recommended improved hybrids- HHH-223, HHH- 287. Desi Cotton varieties- HD-123, HD-324, HD-432. Desi Cotton hybrid - AAH-1 results in yield reduction. For all desi cotton varieties/hybrids, best sowing time is mid-April to 1␀␀ week of May. The mortality of seedling is",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_80:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_80,3,"very high during May & June. Plant protection: Leaf sucking pest & Leaf Curl Virus disease: seed should be treated with 4 g Thiamethaxom 70 WS/kg seed before sowing. Close monitoring on white ␀ly host plants like vegetables, ␀lower plants, weeds & unwanted plants. These host plants must be uprooted & burnt from time to time. Some vegetables like Ladies Finger, Brinjal, Tomato & Chilli also act as host plants for white␀ly, accordingly, as per need these must be sprayed with Thiamethaxom 25 WG @ 0.5g/litre water. Bacterial blight: seed should be treated with soaking in 1 g Streptomycin or 10 g Plantomycin/10 litre water before sowing. Spray Thiamethaxom 25 WG @ 100g/ha and Profenophos 50 EC @1250 ml/ha for sucking pest. Proclaim (emamectin benzoate) 5 SG @250g/ha for pink, spotted and American bollworm. FRUIT & VEGETABLE CROPS ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Summer moong Seed rate: The seed rate depends on the size of kernels of the varieties. However, for medium size kernels varieties, seed rate of 80 kg per hectare is required. Improved Varieties: MH-4, HNG-69, GJG-19. Method of sowing: Sowing should be done preferably in rows at a spacing of 30 cm and maintaining plant to plant",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_80:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_80,4,"spacing of 15 cm. Time of sowing: Optimum time of sowing of groundnut is month of June. Under irrigated conditions, sowing should be completed by second fortnight of June, whereas under rainfed conditions sowing at the onset of monsoon should be done. Sowing of crop after 15 July should be avoided. COMMERCIAL CROP If infestation of Jassid and white ␀ly is observed, apply 1.0 litre malathion 50 EC or 625 dimethioate 30 EC per hectare in 625 litres of water. Harvest the crop at ripening of 70-80 percent pods to allow timely sowing of the kharif crop. Fertilizer use: Application of 15 kg N, 50 kg P₂O₅, 25 kg K₂O and 25 kg Zinc sulphate per hectare is required for obtaining good crop yield. It will be desirable to apply doses of all the nutrients before sowing. Use of gypsum as sulphur source has been found bene␀icial in groundnut crop. Cotton Disease management: Sterility mosaic virus can be controlled by using resistant varieties and removing infected plants early to limit virus spread. For vector control, spray Neem oil (5 ml/litre) or NSKE 5% every 15 days. Seed treatment with Imidacloprid 70 WS (5 g/kg seed) helps protect seedlings. Alternaria blight can be managed by spraying",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_80:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_80,5,"Mancozeb (2.5 g/litre) or Carbendazim (1 g/litre), planting on raised beds for better drainage, and using resistant cultivars. Phytophthora blight can be controlled by seed treatment with Metalaxyl (8g/kg), maintaining good drainage, minimizing stem injury, and using resistant genotypes. Groundnut Seed treatment: Treatment of seed with Thiram or Captan or Emisan 3 g/kg seed is essential for management of seed and soil borne diseases. For management of termites and white grub treat the seed with 15 ml Chloropyriphos 20 EC/kg seed. Plant protections: For the management of pod borer application of chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC @ 150 ml/ha followed by ␀lubendiamide 480 SC @ 125 ml/ha is advised to minimize the larval population or Spinosad (150 mL/ha) at ␀lowering and pod initiation. In incidence of blister beetles deep ploughing, ␀ield sanitation, light traps, and neem-based products (NSKE 5% or Azadirachtin 0.03% WSP @ 2500-5000 g/ha) can be used. OILSEED CROPS Time of sowing: Sowing of the crop is done from April to ␀irst fortnight of June. However, in case of American cotton optimum time of sowing is May. Delay in sowing 6564",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_81:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_81,1,"Haryana & Delhi Fertilizer use: Apply 80-100 Kg N per ha for American Cotton and 50 kg N for desi cotton along with 30 kg P₂O₅/ha. In case of hybrid cotton, 150 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O and 25 kg ZnSo₄ per ha has been recommended. Apply 1/3 dose of N, full dose of P₂O₅, full dose of potash and full dose of ZnSo₄ at time of sowing. Remaining dose of N should be applied in two equal splits at square formation and ␀lowering stage. In sandy soil the research results have revealed that 90 per cent dose of fertilizer through soil application and 10 per cent through foliar spray at the boll development stage gave the highest seed cotton yield. Inoculation of cotton seed with C2, M4 and Azospirillum culture resulted into saving of 25-27 kg N/ha. Seed rate: Use 15-20 kg delinted seed of improved American cotton varieties for sowing in one ha area. 12.5 kg of seed/ha is required for Desi cotton varieties. Seed rate of 3-3.750 kg /ha is required for American cotton hybrids and desi cotton hybrids. Seed rate of 2.125 kg/ha is required for Bt Cotton hybrids. Seed treatment and seed soaking: Before sowing, seed should be dipped in water up to 5-6 hours for better germination. Treat the seed",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
