ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_81:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_81,4,"spacing of 15 cm. Time of sowing: Optimum time of sowing of groundnut is month of June. Under irrigated conditions, sowing should be completed by second fortnight of June, whereas under rainfed conditions sowing at the onset of monsoon should be done. Sowing of crop after 15 July should be avoided. COMMERCIAL CROP If infestation of Jassid and white ␀ly is observed, apply 1.0 litre malathion 50 EC or 625 dimethioate 30 EC per hectare in 625 litres of water. Harvest the crop at ripening of 70-80 percent pods to allow timely sowing of the kharif crop. Fertilizer use: Application of 15 kg N, 50 kg P₂O₅, 25 kg K₂O and 25 kg Zinc sulphate per hectare is required for obtaining good crop yield. It will be desirable to apply doses of all the nutrients before sowing. Use of gypsum as sulphur source has been found bene␀icial in groundnut crop. Cotton Disease management: Sterility mosaic virus can be controlled by using resistant varieties and removing infected plants early to limit virus spread. For vector control, spray Neem oil (5 ml/litre) or NSKE 5% every 15 days. Seed treatment with Imidacloprid 70 WS (5 g/kg seed) helps protect seedlings. Alternaria blight can be managed by spraying",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_81:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_81,5,"Mancozeb (2.5 g/litre) or Carbendazim (1 g/litre), planting on raised beds for better drainage, and using resistant cultivars. Phytophthora blight can be controlled by seed treatment with Metalaxyl (8g/kg), maintaining good drainage, minimizing stem injury, and using resistant genotypes. Groundnut Seed treatment: Treatment of seed with Thiram or Captan or Emisan 3 g/kg seed is essential for management of seed and soil borne diseases. For management of termites and white grub treat the seed with 15 ml Chloropyriphos 20 EC/kg seed. Plant protections: For the management of pod borer application of chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC @ 150 ml/ha followed by ␀lubendiamide 480 SC @ 125 ml/ha is advised to minimize the larval population or Spinosad (150 mL/ha) at ␀lowering and pod initiation. In incidence of blister beetles deep ploughing, ␀ield sanitation, light traps, and neem-based products (NSKE 5% or Azadirachtin 0.03% WSP @ 2500-5000 g/ha) can be used. OILSEED CROPS Time of sowing: Sowing of the crop is done from April to ␀irst fortnight of June. However, in case of American cotton optimum time of sowing is May. Delay in sowing 6564",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_82:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_82,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Improved varieties: HG 365, HG 563, HG 870, HG 2-20 Weed management: Two manual weeding at 25 and 45 DAS are usually suf␀icient. To control weed Basaline @2.0 litre per ha in 650 litre of water at pre-sowing can also be applied. Citrus mixing, delivery and washing of equipment is to be undertaken. For management of fruit drop in mango spray 2% urea and 0.5 % ZnSO₄ or 20 ppm 2, 4-D (2 g 2,4-D in 100 litre of water) in month of April-May. For management of black tip in mango apply 0.6% borax. For management of mango Jassid, spray 1250 ml malathion 50 EC in 1250 litre water per hectare. Manage irrigation in mango, citrus, and other fruit crops. Ber In case of Ber plants last week April month to May month is best time for pruning because plants are in dormant condition. Cluster bean Time of Sowing: Under rainfed conditions, sowing should coincide with the onset of the monsoon, ideally within the ␀irst two weeks of July. In Citrus plants of seven years or more age, apply 750 g of urea per plant followed by inter-culture and irrigation. To control pre-harvest fruit drop in citrus, apply 6 g 2, 4- D, 3 Kg Zinc Sulphate, 12g Aureofungin and 1.5 kg lime in 550",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_82:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_82,2,"litres of water per acre. In case of intercropping with sun␀lower and cotton do not spray 2, 4-D. In this case application of 20 ppm NAA is recommended. Keeping in view of forecasted high temperature, farmers are advised for harvesting of mature vegetables at morning and evening hours and keep harvested crops in shadow. Optimum moisture level should be maintained in cucurbitaceous crops by light and frequent irrigation as dry conditions may lead to poor pollination and thus drop in yield of the crop. After harvesting of mature okra application of urea @ 5-10 kg/ acre should be done. Constant monitoring of crop against attack of mite is advised. If population is above ETL then, spraying of Ethion @ 1.5-2 ml/litre of water is advised. Due to prevailing high temperature, light irrigation at short interval is advised. To control shoot and fruit borer in brinjal and tomato crops, infested fruits and shoots should be collected and buried inside the soil. If pest population is high, spraying of Spinosad 48 EC @ 1 ml /4 litres of water is advised. In tomato, brinjal, chillies, bhendi, and other vegetables, apply hoeing and irrigation as needed and give the required amount of nitrogen",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_82:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_82,3,"fertilizer. Farmers are also advised to take short duration vegetable crops during this summer and the public to grow vegetable in their kitchen garden. Fertilizer management: Apply 40 kg phosphorus and 20 kg Nitrogen at the time of sowing. Water management: It is mainly grown as a rainfed crop; lifesaving irrigation at pod formation is critical. Seed rate & spacing: Seed rate of 15 kg/ha is recommended with spacing of 30 cm x 15 cm, prior to sowing treat seeds with Rhizobium culture. Also treat seed with streptocycline @ 6 g/kg seed in 6 L of water. Haryana & Delhi Disease management: To manage bacterial blight eﬀectively two sprays with Streptocycline @ 75g and copper oxychloride @ 500g in 500L water per ha at initiation stage of disease or at 55-60 days after sowing is bene␀icial. Plant protection: Application of Malathion 50 EC @ 0.75-1.25 ml/L of water eﬀectively controls sucking pests like jassids, aphids, and white␀ly. Transplanting of rice requires huge volume of water. It can be saved by bringing change in planting method of the crop. Direct seeding of rice crop has been found very successful technology and is helpful in conservation of water resources. Levelling of ␀ields",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_82:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_82,4,"with laser Level Machine helps in water saving in transplanting conditions. Temperatures are high during this month and some areas experience severs dust storms accompanied by thunder showers. Heat related diseases in animals that can be seen to aﬀect animals during this time are fever, dehydration, decrease in body salts, loss of appetite and decrease in productivity. Animals should be protected from the heat and strong, hot, and dry summer afternoon winds. Adequate eﬀorts should be made for fodder collection/purchase and storage for periods of shortage. To avoid loss of essential body salts in animals ensure that a salt mixture in appropriate quantity is mixed with the feed and water and given to animals. Depending upon the season, the content of the animal feed should be changed. Currently increase the quantity of wheat chaﬀ and Jowar in the feed. Give dairy animals a balanced feed so that their milk production capacity is enhanced. Deworming of animals should be carried out. Maize, perennial grasses and other fodder species should be harvested now. Sheep should be sheared during this month. LIVESTOCK The period between harvesting of wheat crop and transplanting of rice crop",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_82:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_82,5,(May- June) can be utilized for growing of green manure crops. Dhaincha (Sesbania sesban) is very suitable cover crop which can be grown for green manuring. Sowing of dhaincha @30 kg seed/ ha is done in ␀irst week of May. The crop is ploughed up in 3␀␀ week of June (45-50 DAS). Transplanting of rice is done after one week of ploughing of dhaincha crop. Apply 2/3␀␀ dose of NPK fertilizers in ␀ields where green manuring is done. GREEN MANURING PRACTICES WATER CONSERVATION PRACTICES 6766,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
