ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_83:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_83,5,(May- June) can be utilized for growing of green manure crops. Dhaincha (Sesbania sesban) is very suitable cover crop which can be grown for green manuring. Sowing of dhaincha @30 kg seed/ ha is done in ␀irst week of May. The crop is ploughed up in 3␀␀ week of June (45-50 DAS). Transplanting of rice is done after one week of ploughing of dhaincha crop. Apply 2/3␀␀ dose of NPK fertilizers in ␀ields where green manuring is done. GREEN MANURING PRACTICES WATER CONSERVATION PRACTICES 6766,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_84:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_84,1,"Summer Ploughing: Deep summer ploughing after Rabi season helps to destroy soil-borne pathogens and conserves rainwater by reducing runoﬀ and also aids in groundwater recharge. Himachal Pradesh is a climatically diverse hill state where various crops are cultivated according to the distinct climatic and geographical conditions. To ensure the successful cultivation of these crops, it is essential to educate farmers about scienti␀ic farming technique through agro-advisories. The primary objective of agro- advisories is to promote scienti␀ically validated agricultural practices that enhance farm productivity and income through the ef␀icient use of available resources. The following agro-advisory outlines recommended agricultural activities and operations for farmers to undertake during the Kharif season. Soil Sample Collection: After harvest of Rabi season crops, this is the ideal time to collect soil samples for analysis, as ␀ields are vacant. Farmers should collect soil samples in zig-zag manner for accurate nutrient analysis. For collecting soil sample, remove surface debris, collect soil upto 15 cm depth for shallow-rooted crops using auger or khurpi & collect at least 10 to 15",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_84:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_84,2,"samples from each s a m p l i n g u n i t . M i x t h e s a m p l e s thoroughly and remove foreign materials like roots, stones, pebbles and gravels. Reduce the bulk to about half to one kilogram by quartering the sample & put the sample in clean cloth or polythene bag and label with farmer and ␀ield information and send to nearby soil testing laboratory for nutrient analysis. GENERAL ADVISORY FOR FARMERS Himachal Pradesh Demonstration of method of soil sampling in ␀ield Himachal Pradesh Demonstration on rainwater harvesting Pro Tray Seedling Production: Adopt pro tray seedling technology using coco peat, perlite and vermiculite mixture for crops like tomato, brinjal, capsicum, and cauli␀lower. This method ensures healthy, uniform seedlings, reduces disease risk, supports timely transplanting, and is especially suitable for women farmers. Post-Harvest Storage: Ensure grains, pulses and millets are thoroughly dried before storage. Avoid reusing old gunny bags; instead, use treated bags soaked in 5 per cent neem solution or insecticide to prevent pest infestation. Snails attack: To prevent snail attacks, maintain clean and weed-free bunds. In case of infestation, apply metaldehyde",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_84:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_84,3,"baits as a control measure. Rainwater Harvesting: Farmers are advised to adopt low-cost rainwater harvesting through silpaulin-lined ponds. These structures are easy to construct, cost-eﬀective, and help store rainwater for irrigation during dry spells. Select a low-lying area, dig a pond, and line it with a durable silpaulin sheet to minimize seepage. This method enhances water availability during lean period and supports sustainable farming practices. Use of Compost/Farm Yard Manure (FYM): Apply compost or Farm Yard Manure (FYM) at least 3 weeks before sowing to improve soil fertility and water retention. Enriching FYM with bio-agents like Trichoderma and Pseudomonas enhances its eﬀectiveness. DEMONSTRATION OF METHOD OF SOIL SAMPLING IN FIELD Optimum seed rate for maize is 20 kg per hectare. Sowing should be done at a depth of 3.5 cm, with a spacing of 60 cm between rows and 20 cm between plants to ensure optimal plant population (75,000-83,000 plants/ha). Kera method should be used for sowing of seed instead of broadcasting. Complete sowing 12-15 days before the monsoon (last week of June). In high hills, the best time for sowing of maize is from 15␀␀ April to 15␀␀ May using",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_84:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_84,4,"Girija variety for timely sowing and Bajaura Makka, Bajaura Popcorn, Bajaura sweet corn for late sowing condition. In mid and low hills, sowing operation should be done from 20␀␀ May to 15␀␀ June and 15␀␀ June to 30␀␀ June, respectively. University tested hybrids such as PSC-3322 Gold, PSC-4455, SMS-137, K-25 Super, Star-35, Vyas Gold, AHC-2337. HP-333 Gold, Sambha Gold can also be procured from the agriculture department sale centres at subsidized rates. Maize CEREAL CROPS 6968",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_85:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_85,1,"Summer Ploughing: Deep summer ploughing after Rabi season helps to destroy soil-borne pathogens and conserves rainwater by reducing runoﬀ and also aids in groundwater recharge. Himachal Pradesh is a climatically diverse hill state where various crops are cultivated according to the distinct climatic and geographical conditions. To ensure the successful cultivation of these crops, it is essential to educate farmers about scienti␀ic farming technique through agro-advisories. The primary objective of agro- advisories is to promote scienti␀ically validated agricultural practices that enhance farm productivity and income through the ef␀icient use of available resources. The following agro-advisory outlines recommended agricultural activities and operations for farmers to undertake during the Kharif season. Soil Sample Collection: After harvest of Rabi season crops, this is the ideal time to collect soil samples for analysis, as ␀ields are vacant. Farmers should collect soil samples in zig-zag manner for accurate nutrient analysis. For collecting soil sample, remove surface debris, collect soil upto 15 cm depth for shallow-rooted crops using auger or khurpi & collect at least 10 to 15",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
