ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_85:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_85,4,"Girija variety for timely sowing and Bajaura Makka, Bajaura Popcorn, Bajaura sweet corn for late sowing condition. In mid and low hills, sowing operation should be done from 20␀␀ May to 15␀␀ June and 15␀␀ June to 30␀␀ June, respectively. University tested hybrids such as PSC-3322 Gold, PSC-4455, SMS-137, K-25 Super, Star-35, Vyas Gold, AHC-2337. HP-333 Gold, Sambha Gold can also be procured from the agriculture department sale centres at subsidized rates. Maize CEREAL CROPS 6968",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_86:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_86,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Paddy nursery sowing @ 25 kg seed/ha after seed treatment with bavistin @ 2.5 g/kg for timely sown conditions may be completed from 20␀␀ May to ␀irst week of June using high yielding varieties HPR 1068, HPR 2143, RP 2421, HPR 2720, HPR 2880 and transplanting may be completed using 25-30 days old seedlings by end of June. In case of basmati rice, high yielding and disease resistant varieties Kasturi and HPR 2612 could be used. For late sowing conditions also, high yielding short duration variety HPR 2612 can be used. Varieties Bhrighu Dhan, Varun Dhan and Naggar Dhan could be used in Kullu valley and other colder areas. Red rice varieties HPR 2795 (upland areas) and HPR 2720 for irrigated transplanted area can be sown by mid-June. University tested hybrids Super- 120, Star-795, AHR-8213 can be purchased from agriculture department. In areas where cutworm and white grubs are serious pests, chlorpyriphos @ 2.0 litre per ha mixed in 60-70 kg sandy soil may be used for soil amendment before sowing or cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml per litre may be used for foliar application. Monitor the crop regularly for fall armyworm incidence. If the leaves are damaged or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_86:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_86,2,"insect faeces are seen, then apply ␀lubendamide (Fame) or emamectin benzoate or chlorantraniliprol @ 0.5 ml/L and repeat application at 15 days interval if needed. Proper earthing up should be done to prevent lodging of kharif maize due to high wind, cyclone etc. If there is heavy rainfall, care must be taken for drainage of excessive water from the maize ␀ield. Paddy Apply 10-15 t of FYM per hectare 2-3 weeks before sowing. In hybrid varieties, apply NPK @ 120:60:40 kg and 90:45:30 kg per hectare in high and low rainfall areas, respectively. In local varieties, apply NPK @ 80:40:30 and 60:30:20 kg per hectare in high and low rainfall areas respectively. Apply full dose of P & K at sowing and two split doses of N at ␀irst earthing up and one month thereafter. In case of Zn de␀iciency, apply 25 kg of zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21%) or 16.25 kg zinc sulphate monohydrate (33%) per ha during sowing. For weed control, use pre-emergence herbicides like Atrazine @ 1.5-2.0 kg a.i/ha for sole crops while alachlor @ 1.5 kg /ha for mixed cropping systems. Weeds can also be controlled post emergence by application of herbicide Tembotrione @120 g a.i/ha with surfactant 1 L/ha at 2-3 leaf stage",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_86:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_86,3,"or herbicide Topramezone 25.2 g a.i/ha + atrazine 750 g a.i/ha at 2-3 leaf stage. Demonstration of post-emergence herbicide in maize at farmers ␀ield Use of Kera method for seed sowing in maize Himachal Pradesh The transplanted rice crop should be fertilized with NPK @ 90:40:40 with 50% N and entire dose of P & K at the time of transplanting and remaining N in two equal doses at 3 and 6 weeks after transplanting. In case of zinc de␀iciency symptoms in previous crop, apply 60 kg of zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21%) or 40 kg zinc sulphate monohydrate (33%) per hectare at puddling. The fertilizers should be applied 10-12 cm away from the base of the plant to avoid plant injury. Soon after application, the fertilizer on the soil surface should be covered to minimize losses. Nursery raising of Paddy Transplanting of Paddy In transplanted rice, apply Butachlor 5 g @ 30 kg/ha or broadcast Butachlor 50EC @ 3L after mixing within 72 hrs of transplanting for weed management. Post emergence herbicide Bispyribac sodium @ 250 ml/ ha can also be sprayed at 20-25 days after transplanting. In case of direct seeded rice, high yielding varieties HPR 1156 (Sukara dhan), HPR 2656 and HPR 2795 could be",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_86:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_86,4,"sown by end May or ␀irst week of June @ 60 kg seed/ ha. In irrigated conditions, apply ␀irst irrigation at 25 days after sowing and schedule succeeding irrigations as per monsoon rains. For the management of stem borer and leaf folder, apply Carbofuron granules (furadan 3g) @ 33 kg/ ha in standing water after 10 days of transplanting or spray the crop after appearance of pest incidence with Chlorpyriphos @ 3ml/ L or Emamectine Benzoate @ 0.5 g/ L water. In case of blast/ false smut incidence, spray Copper Oxychloride @ 3g/ L or Hexaconazole @1 ml/L water at panicle initiation stage. The harvesting of the crop is generally done when 85% of the grains turn straw coloured. Azolla is a good biofertilizer in irrigated rice crop which not only add organic matter in the ␀ield but also supplies enough N to the rice crops & reduce 10-20 per cent of nitrogen and phosphorus fertilizer requirement. Continuous ␀looding of water generally provides the best growth environment for rice. After transplanting, water levels should be around 3 cm initially, and gradually increase to 5-10 cm (with increasing plant height) until the ␀ield is drained 7-10 days before harvest. Demonstration of paddy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
