ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_87:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_87,4,"sown by end May or ␀irst week of June @ 60 kg seed/ ha. In irrigated conditions, apply ␀irst irrigation at 25 days after sowing and schedule succeeding irrigations as per monsoon rains. For the management of stem borer and leaf folder, apply Carbofuron granules (furadan 3g) @ 33 kg/ ha in standing water after 10 days of transplanting or spray the crop after appearance of pest incidence with Chlorpyriphos @ 3ml/ L or Emamectine Benzoate @ 0.5 g/ L water. In case of blast/ false smut incidence, spray Copper Oxychloride @ 3g/ L or Hexaconazole @1 ml/L water at panicle initiation stage. The harvesting of the crop is generally done when 85% of the grains turn straw coloured. Azolla is a good biofertilizer in irrigated rice crop which not only add organic matter in the ␀ield but also supplies enough N to the rice crops & reduce 10-20 per cent of nitrogen and phosphorus fertilizer requirement. Continuous ␀looding of water generally provides the best growth environment for rice. After transplanting, water levels should be around 3 cm initially, and gradually increase to 5-10 cm (with increasing plant height) until the ␀ield is drained 7-10 days before harvest. Demonstration of paddy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_87:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_87,5,variety HPR 2612 7170,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_88:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_88,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Soybean is the main oilseed crop grown in Kharif season in Himachal Pradesh. Sowing of soybean should be completed from May end to mid-June using high yielding varieties Palam Soya, Harit Soya or Palam Hara Soya 1. For getting optimum population, 75-80 kg per ha seed is required. The row to row spacing of 45 cm and plant to plant spacing of 15 cm should be maintained with depth of seed not more than 3-4 cm. Farmers are advised to do seed treatment with carbendazim or Thiram @ 3 -5 g/kg and with Rhizobium @ 20g /kg of seed before sowing. In case of aphid incidence apply thiametoxam @0.4 g/ L of water. Apply 20:60:40 dose of NPK kg/ha at sowing. Add sulphur @ 20 kg/ha for better oil content. Apply pendimethalin 750 g/ha or Oxadiazon 500 g/ha as pre-emergence for controlling many annual and broad leaf weeds. For post emergence weed control use Imazethapyr 100 g/ha or Imazethapyr 14 g/ha + Imazemox 14 g/ha in soybean. Blackgram OILSEED Among pulses, blackgram is the main pulse grown in Himachal Pradesh. Sowing of black gram should be started by June end and completed in ␀irst fortnight of July using high yielding varieties UG 218, Him Mash 1 and PB 114 in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_88:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_88,2,"low and mid hills and Palampur 93 in high hills (>1500 m amsl) using basal dose of NPK @ 20:40:20 at the time of sowing. Seed bio forti␀ication with Rhizobium and PSB culture should be done before sowing for better plant stand and yield. For weed control, apply pre emergence herbicide Pendimethalin @ 1.5 kg /ha for weed control. PULSE CROPS Demonstration of soybean variety Palam Soya Seed Treatment with Biofertilizer Demonstration of blackgram variety Him Mash 1 at farmers ␀ield Rajmash (Kidney Bean) High yielding varieties Jawala, Him-1, Kanchan, Triloki, Baspa of Kidney bean (Rajmash) can be sown in the month of May in high altitude areas and in the month of June in low lying areas. Weed control in kidney bean can be done using pre- emergence herbicide Pendimethalin @ 1.5 kg /ha. For management of anthracnose, Himachal Pradesh Diseases Management: For the management of leaf spots /blight, the farmers are advised to spray mancozeb (600 g/200L of water) as the protectant application in May month. However, where these spots/blights are observed, the farmers are advised to spray alternatively the formulations consisting of, hexaconazole 4% + Zineb 68% WP (500g/200L of water) or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_88:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_88,3,"carbendazim 25% + ␀lusilazole 12.5% SC (160ml/200L of water) at 10-12 days interval in the infected orchards. Fertilizer Application: After fruit setting in apple apply second dose of nitrogen in the form of Calcium Nitrate (300 g / tree) to the soil. Overuse or high rates of N applications can lead to excessive shoot growth and poor fruit colour. Apple FRUIT & VEGETABLE CROPS seed treatment with bavistin @ 2g per kg seed can also be done or foliar application with bavisitn @ 1g/ L water can be followed, while in case of blister beetle incidence apply cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml/ L and for bean bug/ white␀ly management apply thiamethoxam @ 0.4g/ L water. Hail Damage: Spray 100 g carbendazim or 600 g mancozeb in 200 L of water immediately after hail. Spray 200 g Boric acid + 500 g Zinc Sulphate + 250 g Quick lime in 200 L of water within 3-4 days of hail storm. After 10 to 12 days, a spray of micro-nutrients like Agromin, Multiplex or Microvit @ 400 to 600 g per 200 L of water is also recommended. Spray the hail aﬀected apple orchard with 1 kg Urea in 200L of water. High Density Plantation of Apple High density apple orchards: Through summer pruning remove excess upright growing shoots",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_88:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_88,4,"during May-June and bend branches to blow horizontal to encourage spur formation in the month of June -July. Through fertigation apply N-P₂O₅ -K₂O @ 35-17.5- 35 g/tree/year age of plant in 14 splits at weekly interval starting from 15␀␀ March till the end of June. Stone fruits For management of leaf curling due to insect and fungal attack in plum and peaches, spray Oxydemeton-methyl or Dimethoate 1 ml + copper oxychloride 3 g per litre of water at pink bud stage (7-10 day before ␀lowering). If not sprayed and the infestation is high then spray after petal fall. 7372",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
