ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_89:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_89,4,"during May-June and bend branches to blow horizontal to encourage spur formation in the month of June -July. Through fertigation apply N-P₂O₅ -K₂O @ 35-17.5- 35 g/tree/year age of plant in 14 splits at weekly interval starting from 15␀␀ March till the end of June. Stone fruits For management of leaf curling due to insect and fungal attack in plum and peaches, spray Oxydemeton-methyl or Dimethoate 1 ml + copper oxychloride 3 g per litre of water at pink bud stage (7-10 day before ␀lowering). If not sprayed and the infestation is high then spray after petal fall. 7372",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_90:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_90,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Citrus Pomegranate Gummosis: For management of gummosis in stone fruits, clean the oozing spots after breaking of dormancy and apply Mashobra paste. After one month or before rainy season apply moshobra paste again. Spray Streptocycline 20 g per 200L of water before rainy season and copper oxychloride 600 g per 200 litres of water before leaf fall. Fruit ␀ly: For the management of fruit ␀ly in Mango, citrus and guava, mix carbaryl 10 D in soils @ 50-100 g/tree, Install Palam trap 2/bigha /pheromone fruit ␀ly traps @ 10/acre. Foliar spray with malathion 2 ml/L + gur 20 g a month before harvesting the fruit crop and repeat it after 15 days. Spray Cypermethrin 10 EC (100 ml in 100 litre of water) during ␀irst week of May for the control of Anar butter␀ly attack. After 15-20 days of ␀irst spray apply Quinalphos 200 ml per 100 litres of water. If needed repeat the above mentioned insecticides. Tomato Wilt management: To manage wilt problem in pomegranate, three drenching at 20 days interval with propiconazole 25 EC @ 2 ml/L + Chlorpyriphos 20 EC @ 2 ml/L starting from appearance of ␀irst symptoms of wilt. Use 5-10 L solution/plant. Mango Maintain",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_90:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_90,2,"suf␀icient moisture during May -June to prevent fruit cracking by providing irrigation at 3 days intervals. Mulching with grass around tree basin is helpful for moisture conservation. Application of calcium @ 2 g/l or Gibberellins @ 20 mg/l or NAA@ 20 mg/litre as spray after fruit set is also helpful in reducing cracking of fruits. Evergreen fruit plants like Mango, litchi, Guava, Citrus fruits are planted in rainy season during July- August. Generally, a pit of 1 m³ (1 x 1 x1 m) should be prepared well in advance i.e. one month before planting. For the management of mango hopper spray pesticide at ␀lower bud initiation i.e imidacloprid 0.5 ml/L or Cyantraniliprole 10.26 OD @ 0.3 ml/L or methyl demeton 25EC @ 1ml/L at emergence of in␀lorescence stalks and before ␀lower opening . When fruits are of pea size, imidacloprid 0.5 ml/L or dimethoate (0.03%) (1ml/L) is recommended. Adding sulphur3.5g/L to the insecticide based on need to check mites and sooty may be done. To get quality and higher fruit yield in summer tomato production system, earthing up and rope staking should be completed by the end of April and split doses of urea @ 5 kg/bigha should be applied in the months of April",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_90:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_90,3,"and May, respectively. Split doses of potash @ 30 kg per hectare may also be applied in May-June to reduce the incidence of fruit rot disease. Before the onset of monsoon, lower leaves of tomato up to 20 cm from ground level should be removed to avoid the infection of buckeye rot Spray Zinc sulphate 1 kg + Lime 500 g in 200 litres of water during March, June and September to control zinc de␀iciency & Blitox @ 600 g per 200 litres of water during June- July to manage gummosis. Litchi Himachal Pradesh and blight diseases. Drip irrigation with mulching should be used for better crop management and conservation of water. In Kharif tomato production system, nursery raising may be started in the month of June and transplanting should be completed by July. In areas where blossom end rot is a problem apply calcium chloride @ 5g/ L of water as foliar application. For the management of early blight, buckeye rot and fruit rot diseases, apply copper oxychloride @ 3g/ L, Ridomil MZ @ 2.5 g/L and Mancozeb 45 @ 2.5 g or Kavach @ 2g/ L respectively as and when symptoms appear. For the management of fruit borer, apply Profenophos @ 1ml/ L or Chlorpyriphos @2ml or Cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml per litre",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_90:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_90,4,"of water . Bell pepper Cultural Practices along with Fertilizer application: Elite open pollinated varieties viz., California Wonder, Solan Bharpur, Solan Shakti should be planted up to end of April to get higher yields. Optimum spacing of 60 cm may be maintained between row to row and 45 cm between plant to plant while transplanting of open pollinated varieties or hybrids. Apply total FYM (250q/ha), Single Super Phosphate (475kg/ha), Muriate of Potash (90kg/ha) with half of Urea (200kg/ha) at the time of ␀ield preparation. Remaining half of urea should be applied in two equal split doses one after one month of sowing and another before ␀lowering. Under protected conditions, capsicum (coloured/ green) can be transplanted by May end. Apply FYM @ 120t/ha and NPK mixture @ 50kg/ ha before transplanting. Urea 11g, SSP 30g and MOP 8.4g per square meter should also be applied to get higher yield. Apply soluble fertilizers like Polyfeed (19:19:19) @150 kg/ha twice a Demonstration of mulch with drip irrigation at farmer's ␀ields in Solan disrict Demonstration on coloured bell peppers under protected conditions Solan Shakti variety of bell pepper 7574",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_91:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_91,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Citrus Pomegranate Gummosis: For management of gummosis in stone fruits, clean the oozing spots after breaking of dormancy and apply Mashobra paste. After one month or before rainy season apply moshobra paste again. Spray Streptocycline 20 g per 200L of water before rainy season and copper oxychloride 600 g per 200 litres of water before leaf fall. Fruit ␀ly: For the management of fruit ␀ly in Mango, citrus and guava, mix carbaryl 10 D in soils @ 50-100 g/tree, Install Palam trap 2/bigha /pheromone fruit ␀ly traps @ 10/acre. Foliar spray with malathion 2 ml/L + gur 20 g a month before harvesting the fruit crop and repeat it after 15 days. Spray Cypermethrin 10 EC (100 ml in 100 litre of water) during ␀irst week of May for the control of Anar butter␀ly attack. After 15-20 days of ␀irst spray apply Quinalphos 200 ml per 100 litres of water. If needed repeat the above mentioned insecticides. Tomato Wilt management: To manage wilt problem in pomegranate, three drenching at 20 days interval with propiconazole 25 EC @ 2 ml/L + Chlorpyriphos 20 EC @ 2 ml/L starting from appearance of ␀irst symptoms of wilt. Use 5-10 L solution/plant. Mango Maintain",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
