ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_91:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_91,4,"of water . Bell pepper Cultural Practices along with Fertilizer application: Elite open pollinated varieties viz., California Wonder, Solan Bharpur, Solan Shakti should be planted up to end of April to get higher yields. Optimum spacing of 60 cm may be maintained between row to row and 45 cm between plant to plant while transplanting of open pollinated varieties or hybrids. Apply total FYM (250q/ha), Single Super Phosphate (475kg/ha), Muriate of Potash (90kg/ha) with half of Urea (200kg/ha) at the time of ␀ield preparation. Remaining half of urea should be applied in two equal split doses one after one month of sowing and another before ␀lowering. Under protected conditions, capsicum (coloured/ green) can be transplanted by May end. Apply FYM @ 120t/ha and NPK mixture @ 50kg/ ha before transplanting. Urea 11g, SSP 30g and MOP 8.4g per square meter should also be applied to get higher yield. Apply soluble fertilizers like Polyfeed (19:19:19) @150 kg/ha twice a Demonstration of mulch with drip irrigation at farmer's ␀ields in Solan disrict Demonstration on coloured bell peppers under protected conditions Solan Shakti variety of bell pepper 7574",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_92:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_92,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Proper drainage should be maintained in ␀ield of bell pepper in rainy season to avoid the problems of diseases. For the management of powdery mildew and fruit rot diseases, use Hexaconazole or Contaf @ 0.5 ml/ L and Mancozeb or Ridomil MZ @ 2.5g as and when symptoms appear. For the management of fruit borer, spray Lambda Cyahalothrin @ 0.8ml/ L or Imidacloprid @ 0.5 ml/L or Flubendiamide @ 0.2 g/ litre of water. Cultural Practices along with Fertilizer application: Varieties, K-75, Solan Srijan are recommended for open cultivation of cucumber while seedless varieties Him Palam Kheera-1 and Him Palam Kheera-2 are suitable for protected cultivation. Australian Green, Pusa Alankar and Solan Aadvik varieties of summer squash have been recommended for cultivation. Nursery of cucurbits should be produced in polybags or plug trays for healthy nursery production. Cucurbits planting may be completed by April end using FYM and Fertilizers (NPK @ 100:50:60) before sowing with Nitrogen in 3 split doses at 30, 45, 70 days after transplanting. CUCURBITS & COLE CROPS week through drip irrigation after three weeks of transplanting and repeat it again 15 days before",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_92:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_92,2,"harvesting to get higher yields under protected conditions in capsicum and tomato crops. Brinjal Open pollinated varieties viz., Pusa Purple Long, Pusa Purple Cluster, Arka Nidhi, Arka Keshav should be grown to get higher yield. Transplanting of brinjal may be completed by April end at a spacing of 60x 45 cm. Application of FYM @100 q/ha, IFFCO mixture (12:32:16) @188 kg/ha, Muriate of Potash @ 33 kg/ha and urea @ 168 kg/ha should be applied to get higher yield in brinjal. Urea should be applied in split doses. For brinjal fruit and shoot borer apply Cypermethrin @ 1ml per litre may be applied at ␀lowering stage. For the management of Phomopsis blight apply COC @3g/ L or Ridomil MZ @2.5 g/ L. Seedless cucumber production in protected conditions Demonstration of Palam Fruit Fly Trap Variability in shape and colour of fruit in Brinjal Himachal Pradesh SPICE S Pole type varieties viz., Laksmi and SVM-I should be planted at a distance of 90x15 cm for better crop management and higher production. Application of FYM @ 200 q/ha, IFFCO mixture (12:32:16) @ 313 kg/ha, and urea @ 27.5 kg/ha should be applied to get higher yield in french bean. Urea should be applied in splits. Management of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_92:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_92,3,"Anthracnose and angular leaf spot diseases can be achieved by applying Bavistin @ 1g/L as and when symptoms appear in end May. For fruit ␀ly management, Use Palam Fruit Fly traps @ 25 traps per hectare in May and use Malathion 30 ml + Jaggery 150 g per 15 L water at 15 days interval. Farmers are also advised to collect and dispose infested fruits in a pit apart from deep ploughing before plantation in summer. Use Bavistin (1g/L) + Mancozeb (2g/L) of water for management of fungal diseases and Imidacloprid @ 0.5 ml per litre for the management of sucking pests. Him Palam Phul Gobhi Hybrid-1 and Him Palam Gobhi Hybrid-1 has been released for commercial cultivation in cauli␀lower and cabbage, respectively. Early varieties of cabbage and cauli␀lower should be transplanted at a distance of 45x30 cm and late varieties at a distance of 60x45 cm for getting higher production. Transplanting of cole crops in high hill areas can be started in the month of June using NPK @ 125:75:70 at the time of sowing with nitrogen in 3 splits (30, 60, 90DAT). For the management of cutworms apply cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml/ L of water. LEGUME French bean French bean is a shy nodulator and in order to encourage",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_92:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_92,4,"good nodulation and better nitrogen ␀ixation, treating seeds with Rhizobium culture should be done a day before sowing and sowing should be completed by end of April or ␀irst week of May. Bush type varieties viz., Falguni, Solan Naina, Contender, Bahaar should be done at a distance of 45x15 cm for better aeration and to minimize the rapid spread of foliar diseases. Land preparations and application of FYM and Fertilizers (NPK @ 100:50:50) should be done before sowing, nitrogen should be applied in 3 splits (30, 60, 90 days after sowing) for ginger crop. Turmeric sowing may be completed by end April using NPK @ 30:30:60 before sowing and Farm Yard Manure. A layer of 3-5 cm mulch should be maintained on ginger crop by adding 50 q of dry leaves or 125 q of green leaves in one Quality Ginger production in open ␀ields French bean production in open ␀ields under mulching 7776",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
