ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_97:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_97,5,"Lumpy Skin Disease (LS), vector-borne conditions like theileriosis, babesiosis, and anaplasmosis. Prompt diagnosis and early reporting are crucial. In case of animal mortality, carcasses must be disposed through deep burial (at least 4 feet) with lime layering to prevent environmental contamination and disease transmission. Swine units must ensure annual vaccination against Classical Swine Fever. Nutritional care of breeding sows includes daily supplementation with 60-80 mL of calcium and 50-60 g of mineral mixture. Pigs should have access to wallowing areas or showers for thermal relief. Deworming using combination drugs like Levamisole and Albendazole should be conducted quarterly. Fisheries Swine RAINY SEASON DISEASE SURVEILLANCE Maintain DO >5 mg/L, pH 7.0-8.5; reinforce bunds and screen inlets to prevent escape. Apply lime @ 200-250 kg/ha; fertilize based on plankton levels. Use prophylactic KMnO₄ (2-5 ppm) or salt (1-2%) baths biweekly. Feed 25-28% CP ␀loating pellets @ 2-3% biomass/day. Stock only acclimatized ␀ingerlings. Prevent livestock runoﬀ in integrated systems. Maintain records for water quality, feeding, and growth. 8180",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_98:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_98,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 SPECIAL ADVISORY FOR COLD ARID ZONES (LAHAUL-SPITI & KINNAUR) In high-altitude cold arid regions, livestock housing must be thermally insulated using dung plaster, mud walls, and locally available materials to conserve body heat during snow-laden months. Animals should be fed dry grasses, willow leaves, and barley, with supplementation of mineral bricks and salt to prevent de␀iciencies. Post-snowmelt, monitoring of yaks and donkeys for respiratory illness, especially pneumonia, is critical. Preventive vaccinations should be completed prior to onset of winter and again before transhumant herds migrate to alpine grazing pastures. Mineral mixture & Urea Molasses Mineral Brick Mineral mixture supplementation Hands-on training on drum silage preparation by CSKHPKV-KVK Mandi Demonstration on Azolla cultivation to women farmers by CSKHPKV-KVK Mandi Field vaccination of migratory Gaddi goats by AICRP on Goat Improvement – Gaddi Field Unit, CSKHPKV, Palampur Ensuring well being of Spiti donkeys: hoof care, minerals, shelter & strategic feeding. Jammu & Kashmir CEREAL CROPS Paddy Soak paddy seed in carbendazim 10 g + streptocyclin 3 g/5 kg seed (in 8 L water)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_98:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_98,2,"for 24 hrs before nursery sowing. In sub-tropical zone, use blast-resistant coarse/semi- ␀ine varieties (SJR-5, Jaya, PR-113, PHB-71, Ratna) and super␀ine types (Jammu Basmati-129, Pusa Basmati 1121). For temperate/sub-temperate areas, prefer early, blast and cold-tolerant types like China-1039, Giza-14, K-84, K-343, K-39. JAMMU Jammu region has three agro-climatic zones; sub-tropical (upto 800 m above msl), sub-temperate (800-1500m above msl) and temperate (above 1500m above msl). Rice is the major crop in irrigated plains, while maize is generally grown in hills under rainfed ecosystem. After Rabi harvest, deep plough ␀ields to utilize high temperatures for killing soil-borne pathogen spores, and take preventive steps to avoid post-harvest pest infestation. The crop-wise agro-advisory for kharif season is presented as below: Blast disease Stem Borer 8382",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_99:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_99,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 SPECIAL ADVISORY FOR COLD ARID ZONES (LAHAUL-SPITI & KINNAUR) In high-altitude cold arid regions, livestock housing must be thermally insulated using dung plaster, mud walls, and locally available materials to conserve body heat during snow-laden months. Animals should be fed dry grasses, willow leaves, and barley, with supplementation of mineral bricks and salt to prevent de␀iciencies. Post-snowmelt, monitoring of yaks and donkeys for respiratory illness, especially pneumonia, is critical. Preventive vaccinations should be completed prior to onset of winter and again before transhumant herds migrate to alpine grazing pastures. Mineral mixture & Urea Molasses Mineral Brick Mineral mixture supplementation Hands-on training on drum silage preparation by CSKHPKV-KVK Mandi Demonstration on Azolla cultivation to women farmers by CSKHPKV-KVK Mandi Field vaccination of migratory Gaddi goats by AICRP on Goat Improvement – Gaddi Field Unit, CSKHPKV, Palampur Ensuring well being of Spiti donkeys: hoof care, minerals, shelter & strategic feeding. Jammu & Kashmir CEREAL CROPS Paddy Soak paddy seed in carbendazim 10 g + streptocyclin 3 g/5 kg seed (in 8 L water)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_99:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_99,2,"for 24 hrs before nursery sowing. In sub-tropical zone, use blast-resistant coarse/semi- ␀ine varieties (SJR-5, Jaya, PR-113, PHB-71, Ratna) and super␀ine types (Jammu Basmati-129, Pusa Basmati 1121). For temperate/sub-temperate areas, prefer early, blast and cold-tolerant types like China-1039, Giza-14, K-84, K-343, K-39. JAMMU Jammu region has three agro-climatic zones; sub-tropical (upto 800 m above msl), sub-temperate (800-1500m above msl) and temperate (above 1500m above msl). Rice is the major crop in irrigated plains, while maize is generally grown in hills under rainfed ecosystem. After Rabi harvest, deep plough ␀ields to utilize high temperatures for killing soil-borne pathogen spores, and take preventive steps to avoid post-harvest pest infestation. The crop-wise agro-advisory for kharif season is presented as below: Blast disease Stem Borer 8382",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_100:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_100,1,"Jammu & Kashmir ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Control weeds manually or use butachlor 5G (1.5 kg/500 m²) or pretilachlor (20 g/500 m²). Apply 30:12:8 kg N:P:K + 8 kg ZnSO₄/acre; split N at puddling, tillering, and panicle stages. Apply full DAP, MOP, ZnSO₄, and 1/3␀␀ N at puddling; split remaining N at tillering and panicle initiation stages, draining water before top dressing. For chemical weed control, use butachlor 12 kg/acre after transplanting or anilophos + ethoxy sulfuron (500 + 60 ml/acre) at 10 DAT. Manage weedy rice with stale seed-bed and glyphosate (0.6 kg/acre) or paraquat (0.32 kg/acre). Prepare nursery beds (dry or wet) with 15 kg FYM, 60 g urea, 50 g DAP per 10 m². Use 16-18 kg/acre seed for ␀ine/coarse varieties (2+ seedlings/hill), 6 kg/acre for hybrids; treat seed with copper oxychloride @ 3 g/kg. Grow hybrids (Ganga Safed-2, Vivek-25, HQPM-1) or composites (Mansar, C-6, C-2); use 8 kg/acre seed for line sowing, 12 kg for broadcast, and 14-16 kg in hills. Treat seed with Thiram/Captan (3 g/kg) or Carbendazim (2 g/kg) + Chlorpyriphos (5 ml/kg) in cutworm-prone areas. Apply 6 t FYM/acre 2-3 weeks before sowing; with FYM, reduce NPK by 25%; otherwise, use 24:16:8",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_100:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_100,2,"kg NPK + 4 kg ZnSO /acre.4 For management of blast, spray the crop with tricyclazole @ 0.06% or azoxystrobin + difenoconazole @ 0.1%. For stem borer, apply Cartap hydrochloride 4G (8 kg/acre) in 5-7.5 cm standing water. Do not drain or irrigate for 72 hours. Spray Cartap hydrochloride 50 SP (240 g/acre) when there are 5% dead hearts or one egg mass/sq.m. Maize Blister Beetle Fall army worm Maintain spacing: 75×20 cm (hybrids), 60×20 cm (composites); use Atrazine @ 0.4 kg/acre or weed manually at 15 & 30 DAS. Keep weed-free till 40 DAS; do earthing-up at 30 DAS for stability and moisture. For pests, apply chlorpyriphos 1.5% D (10 kg/acre) in last ploughing, use light (2/acre) & pheromone traps (6/acre), spray methyl demeton, cypermethrin or cartap hydrochloride in whorls. For Blister Beetle, Cut Worm, Stem Borer & Army Worm in maize, use acetamiprid 20SP @ 0.2 g/L or chlorpyriphos 20EC @ 480 ml/acre, apply chlorpyriphos 1.5% D @ 10 kg/acre in soil for cut worm, cartap hydrochloride 4G @ 8 kg/acre in whorls for stem borer, and adopt trap cropping (okra/arhar) and manual beetle removal for blister beetle. For smuts, treat seed with carbendazim/carboxin @ 2 g/kg; for stalk rot, drench",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_100:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_100,3,"with copper oxychloride 3 g/L or apply bleaching powder @ 10 kg/acre; for leaf blight, spray propiconazole @ 0.1% at disease onset. Use 6-8 kg seed/acre; varieties include Pant U-19, Uttara, Pant U-31, NDU 99-3, KUG 479; spray chlorpyriphos 20EC @ 2 ml/litre or imidacloprid 17.8 SL @ 0.3 ml/litre to manage hairy caterpillar and white␀ly. Use 800 g-1 kg seed/acre in July; for pests like hairy caterpillars and white␀ly, spray chlorpyriphos 20EC @ 2 ml/litre or imidacloprid 17.8 SL @ 0.3 ml/litre. Intercropped with maize (row spacing 75 × 20 cm); sow 9.5 kg seed/acre; treat with copper oxychloride @ 3g/kg; control aphids and anthracnose with chlorothalonil @ 2 g/L spray. Mash (Black Gram) Use 6-8 kg seed/acre; varieties include Pant Mung-6, Pusa Vishal, SML 668, Pusa 0672, Satya; manage YMV and sucking pests with resistant varieties and spray dimethoate 30 EC @ 1 ml/litre or thiamethoxam @ 0.03%. Hybrid Jowar (Sorghum) Rajmash (Bhaderwah Local/Chinta Selection) FODDER CROPS Use 2 kg of hybrid seed/acre, apply 40:24:10 kg NPK/acre, and manage pests like leaf caterpillars and weevils with chlorpyriphos 1.5% D @ 10 kg/acre. OILSEED CROPS Sesame (Til) PULSE CROPS Moong (Green Gram)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_100:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_100,4,"COMMERCIAL CROPS Bajra (Pearl Millet) Sow 5 kg seed/acre with 20:12:6 kg NPK; for insect pests like shoot ␀ly and stem borer, apply cartap hydrochloride 4G @ 8 kg/acre in central whorls at 10-20 DAS. Sugarcane Saﬀron requires 20-24 q corms/acre, with fertigation using 8 kg of Urea, 24 kg of DAP, and 13 kg of MOP, and management involves deep ploughing, raised beds, disease- free corms, and rodent control. Saﬀron Bajra and Jowar are important kharif fodder crops, with varieties like Giant Bajra, FBC-16, PCB 164 for Bajra, and MP Chari, Haryana Chari-260, Proagro Chari (SSG- 998) for Jowar, suitable for both irrigated and rainfed conditions. Grown in parts of Jammu and Kathua, high-yielding sugarcane varieties like COJ-64, COJ-81, and CO-1148 are preferred. Manage termites with chlorpyriphos, borers with cartap, and diseases like red rot and grassy shoot using resistant varieties and appropriate sprays. 8584",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
