ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_101:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_101,4,"COMMERCIAL CROPS Bajra (Pearl Millet) Sow 5 kg seed/acre with 20:12:6 kg NPK; for insect pests like shoot ␀ly and stem borer, apply cartap hydrochloride 4G @ 8 kg/acre in central whorls at 10-20 DAS. Sugarcane Saﬀron requires 20-24 q corms/acre, with fertigation using 8 kg of Urea, 24 kg of DAP, and 13 kg of MOP, and management involves deep ploughing, raised beds, disease- free corms, and rodent control. Saﬀron Bajra and Jowar are important kharif fodder crops, with varieties like Giant Bajra, FBC-16, PCB 164 for Bajra, and MP Chari, Haryana Chari-260, Proagro Chari (SSG- 998) for Jowar, suitable for both irrigated and rainfed conditions. Grown in parts of Jammu and Kathua, high-yielding sugarcane varieties like COJ-64, COJ-81, and CO-1148 are preferred. Manage termites with chlorpyriphos, borers with cartap, and diseases like red rot and grassy shoot using resistant varieties and appropriate sprays. 8584",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_102:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_102,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Mango Guava Irrigate every 4-5 days during the ␀irst month, then every 7-10 days if no rain in the ␀irst two years. Remove side shoots up to 50-75 cm from the base. Ensure proper drainage during monsoon to prevent wilting. Apply fertilizer in July for winter crop. Perform air layering operations. For Zinc and Magnesium de␀iciency, spray 2 g Zinc Sulphate, 2 g Magnesium Sulphate, and 5 g lime in 1 L water every 15 days. Before sowing vegetable seeds, treat the seeds with fungicides like carbendazim, thiram @ 2 gm/kg seed or with Trichoderma virdie @5 gm /kg seed to prevent soil- borne diseases. Apply 8-10 t/acre well rotten FYM at the time of ␀ield preparation, half dose of urea, full doses of DAP and MOP at the time of sowing/transplanting and remaining half dose 30 days after planting. Brinjal Citrus Use varieties like Pusa Purple Long, Pusa Kranti, Pusa Ankur; seed rate is 160-180g/acre with recommended dose of FYM, 82.4 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 20.4 kg MOP. Use delta or sticky traps @ 8/acre for aphids, jassids, and white␀ly; spray Imidacloprid 0.3 ml/l or dimethoate 2 ml/l if pests appear. Install pheromone traps @ 4/acre from 15 days after",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_102:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_102,2,"transplanting for fruit and shoot borer control. Plant saunf or coriander rows to attract natural enemies and spray cypermethrin 1 ml/l every 15 days starting from 20 DAT. Select 6-9 month-old budded plants. Protect new growth from citrus caterpillar after 2-3 weeks. Spray Dimethoate (1.5 ml/L) against citrus psylla, leaf miner, white␀ly, and lemon caterpillar. Ensure proper drainage. For citrus decline, spray copper oxychloride (0.3%) every 15 days or zinc sulphate (1 kg) + lime (500 g) in 200 liters of water. First top dressing per pit: Urea (100 g), SSP (150 g), MOP (75 g), applied 6 inches from the plant. VEGETABLE CROPS Plough mango orchards deep, immediately after harvest to expose the eggs of mealy bugs. Weeding should be done at least once in a month during monsoon. Harvest mangoes at proper maturity, spray mancozeb or copper oxychloride to manage anthracnose. Repeat the spray at 8-10 days interval. Start rainy season plantation for new orchards and gap ␀illing in the old orchards. Procure the plants from authorised nurseries. Ensure that new graft should have at least 4 to 6 ␀lushes with 60 -75 cm height and graft union should be 6''above the soil in the poly bag. FRUIT",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_102:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_102,3,"CROPS Brinjal Fruit & Shoot Borer Jammu & Kashmir Varieties suitable for the rainy season include Arka Anamika, Varsha Uphar, Pusa A-4, Hissar Unnat, Hissar Naveen, Jammu Okra-05, and Punjab Padmini; may be sown at 60×45 cm with a seed rate of 4.8-6.0 kg/acre. Apply 82 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.8 kg Murate of Potash per acre. Weed control: Pre- emergence pendimethlin@0.3 kg/acre, plus one hand hoeing at 30 days. Pest control: For aphids, jassids, and white␀lies, spray Methyl Demeton 25EC (1 ml/lt), Dimethoate 30 EC (2 ml/L), or Melathion 50 EC (2 ml/L) after ␀lowering. Use delta/sticky traps (4/acre) and foliar spray of Imidacloprid 17.8 SL (0.3 ml/L) before ␀lowering. Shoot and fruit borer control: Install Ervit lure (5-6/acre) for mass trapping. Spray Cypermethrin (1 ml/L) or Melathion 50 EC (2 ml/L). Bhindi (Okra) Chillies Tomato Bottle Gourd Grow chillies (NP-46 A, Pusa Jwala, CH- 1, etc.) in sub-temperate/sub-tropical zones using 280-320 g seed/acre at 45×30 cm spacing. Apply 10 t FYM, 82.4 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 20.4 kg MOP per acre; control ␀lower/fruit drop with 50 ppm NAA spray at full bloom. Treat seed for damping-oﬀ; control wilt by drainage, resistant varieties,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_102:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_102,4,"and dipping seedlings in chlorothalonil 0.2% + streptocycline (100 ppm) before transplanting. For mite control, spray dicofol 18.5 EC @ 3 ml/l or wettable sulfur @ 2 ml/l. Varieties such as Pusa Summer Proli␀ic Long, Punjab Long, Punjab Komal, Punjab Round and Pant Loki 4 can be grown at the spacing of 2 m (between rows) & 90 cm (between plants) with seed rate of 2 kg/acre. Apply 80 kg/acre urea, 44 kg/acre DAP and 20 kg/acre MOP. Use varieties like Pusa Ruby, Pusa 120, and Marglobe; transplant 4-5 week-old seedlings at 60×45 cm; apply 100 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.5 kg MOP/acre. Use 5 marla nursery for 1 ha; transplant 4-5 week-old seedlings. Apply 100 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.5 kg MOP per acre. Control early blight with mancozeb @ 0.25%; spray calcium ammonium nitrate to manage blossom end rot (Ca de␀iciency). Prevent fruit cracking (boron de␀iciency) with 3 borax sprays: in nursery (0.3-0.4%), at 3-4 and 5- 6 weeks after transplanting; control buckeye rot with copper oxychloride @ 0.3%. Crinkling in chilli due to mite infestation Okra pod borer 8786",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_103:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_103,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Mango Guava Irrigate every 4-5 days during the ␀irst month, then every 7-10 days if no rain in the ␀irst two years. Remove side shoots up to 50-75 cm from the base. Ensure proper drainage during monsoon to prevent wilting. Apply fertilizer in July for winter crop. Perform air layering operations. For Zinc and Magnesium de␀iciency, spray 2 g Zinc Sulphate, 2 g Magnesium Sulphate, and 5 g lime in 1 L water every 15 days. Before sowing vegetable seeds, treat the seeds with fungicides like carbendazim, thiram @ 2 gm/kg seed or with Trichoderma virdie @5 gm /kg seed to prevent soil- borne diseases. Apply 8-10 t/acre well rotten FYM at the time of ␀ield preparation, half dose of urea, full doses of DAP and MOP at the time of sowing/transplanting and remaining half dose 30 days after planting. Brinjal Citrus Use varieties like Pusa Purple Long, Pusa Kranti, Pusa Ankur; seed rate is 160-180g/acre with recommended dose of FYM, 82.4 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 20.4 kg MOP. Use delta or sticky traps @ 8/acre for aphids, jassids, and white␀ly; spray Imidacloprid 0.3 ml/l or dimethoate 2 ml/l if pests appear. Install pheromone traps @ 4/acre from 15 days after",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_103:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_103,2,"transplanting for fruit and shoot borer control. Plant saunf or coriander rows to attract natural enemies and spray cypermethrin 1 ml/l every 15 days starting from 20 DAT. Select 6-9 month-old budded plants. Protect new growth from citrus caterpillar after 2-3 weeks. Spray Dimethoate (1.5 ml/L) against citrus psylla, leaf miner, white␀ly, and lemon caterpillar. Ensure proper drainage. For citrus decline, spray copper oxychloride (0.3%) every 15 days or zinc sulphate (1 kg) + lime (500 g) in 200 liters of water. First top dressing per pit: Urea (100 g), SSP (150 g), MOP (75 g), applied 6 inches from the plant. VEGETABLE CROPS Plough mango orchards deep, immediately after harvest to expose the eggs of mealy bugs. Weeding should be done at least once in a month during monsoon. Harvest mangoes at proper maturity, spray mancozeb or copper oxychloride to manage anthracnose. Repeat the spray at 8-10 days interval. Start rainy season plantation for new orchards and gap ␀illing in the old orchards. Procure the plants from authorised nurseries. Ensure that new graft should have at least 4 to 6 ␀lushes with 60 -75 cm height and graft union should be 6''above the soil in the poly bag. FRUIT",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_103:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_103,3,"CROPS Brinjal Fruit & Shoot Borer Jammu & Kashmir Varieties suitable for the rainy season include Arka Anamika, Varsha Uphar, Pusa A-4, Hissar Unnat, Hissar Naveen, Jammu Okra-05, and Punjab Padmini; may be sown at 60×45 cm with a seed rate of 4.8-6.0 kg/acre. Apply 82 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.8 kg Murate of Potash per acre. Weed control: Pre- emergence pendimethlin@0.3 kg/acre, plus one hand hoeing at 30 days. Pest control: For aphids, jassids, and white␀lies, spray Methyl Demeton 25EC (1 ml/lt), Dimethoate 30 EC (2 ml/L), or Melathion 50 EC (2 ml/L) after ␀lowering. Use delta/sticky traps (4/acre) and foliar spray of Imidacloprid 17.8 SL (0.3 ml/L) before ␀lowering. Shoot and fruit borer control: Install Ervit lure (5-6/acre) for mass trapping. Spray Cypermethrin (1 ml/L) or Melathion 50 EC (2 ml/L). Bhindi (Okra) Chillies Tomato Bottle Gourd Grow chillies (NP-46 A, Pusa Jwala, CH- 1, etc.) in sub-temperate/sub-tropical zones using 280-320 g seed/acre at 45×30 cm spacing. Apply 10 t FYM, 82.4 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 20.4 kg MOP per acre; control ␀lower/fruit drop with 50 ppm NAA spray at full bloom. Treat seed for damping-oﬀ; control wilt by drainage, resistant varieties,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_103:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_103,4,"and dipping seedlings in chlorothalonil 0.2% + streptocycline (100 ppm) before transplanting. For mite control, spray dicofol 18.5 EC @ 3 ml/l or wettable sulfur @ 2 ml/l. Varieties such as Pusa Summer Proli␀ic Long, Punjab Long, Punjab Komal, Punjab Round and Pant Loki 4 can be grown at the spacing of 2 m (between rows) & 90 cm (between plants) with seed rate of 2 kg/acre. Apply 80 kg/acre urea, 44 kg/acre DAP and 20 kg/acre MOP. Use varieties like Pusa Ruby, Pusa 120, and Marglobe; transplant 4-5 week-old seedlings at 60×45 cm; apply 100 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.5 kg MOP/acre. Use 5 marla nursery for 1 ha; transplant 4-5 week-old seedlings. Apply 100 kg urea, 52.8 kg DAP, and 40.5 kg MOP per acre. Control early blight with mancozeb @ 0.25%; spray calcium ammonium nitrate to manage blossom end rot (Ca de␀iciency). Prevent fruit cracking (boron de␀iciency) with 3 borax sprays: in nursery (0.3-0.4%), at 3-4 and 5- 6 weeks after transplanting; control buckeye rot with copper oxychloride @ 0.3%. Crinkling in chilli due to mite infestation Okra pod borer 8786",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_104:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_104,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Pusa Vishwas, Azad Pumpkin1, Arka Suryamukhi, Arka Chandan, Punjab Samrat varieties can be raised at spacing of 2-2.5m x 75-90 cm with 2 kg seed per acre. Besides, FYM, apply 80 kg urea, 44 kg DAP, 17.2 kg per acre MOP per acre. Cucumber Varieties such as Puas Domausami, Punjab 14, Pusa Vishesh, Kalyanpur Baramasi can be used for summer and rainy season at spacing of 1-2 m × 75-90 cm with seed rate 2 kg/acre. Apply 87 kg/acre urea, 43.5 kg per/acre DAP and 33.2 kg per acre MOP. High nitrogen under High temperature conditions promotes staminate ␀lowers. Varieties such as Japanese, Long Green, Straight Eight, Poinsette and local kheera can be planted at the spacing of 1.0-1.5 m × 60-90 cm with seed rate of 0.8 to 1.2 kg per acre. Apply 34.8 kg urea, 22 kg DAP and 16.8 kg MOP per acre. Avoid excessive use of fertilizers and irrigation. Apply nitrogenous fertilizer at proper dose to avoid the staminate ␀lowers. In cucurbits, control red pumpkin beetle with acetamiprid 20 WP @ 0.2 g/l; for fruit ␀ly, install methyl eugenol traps (2- 4/acre) or spray malathion 1 ml + 10 g gur/l in the evening. Similarly, manage powdery mildew with wettable sulphur @ 0.2%",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_104:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_104,2,"every 7-10 days. Also, prevent fruit rot by keeping fruits oﬀ the soil and harvesting ripe fruits promptly. Pumpkin Mushroom (Button/Oyster) LIVESTOCK Cattle Provide adequate shade, ventilation, and clean drinking water to protect animals from high humidity and heat. Ensure timely deworming and vaccination against prevalent diseases like Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) and Hemorrhagic Septicemia (HS). Cultivate Kharif fodder crops like maize, sorghum, or bajra and ensure silage preparation for consistent feed supply. Sponge Gourd Bitter Gourd Use Pusa Chikni & Pusa Supriya for the rainy season; sow 2 kg seed/acre at 1.5-2.5 m × 75-90 cm spacing; apply 34.8 kg urea, 26 kg DAP, and 20 kg MOP/acre. It Can be processed into pickles, dried, or preserved using steeping solution. Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) Fruit ␀ly and red pumpkin infestation in cucumber Jammu & Kashmir Nutrition awareness is vital for women farmers during the summer season to help maintain their health, energy, and productivity. Here's a concise summary of key points: Consume seasonal foods Small ruminants (Sheep and Goat) KASHMIR Drink 10-12 glasses of water daily. Include traditional drinks like buttermilk, coconut",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_104:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_104,3,"water, bael juice, and mango panna. Choose fresh fruit juices without added sugar for natural nutrition. Avoid waterlogged and parasite-infested grazing areas; rotate grazing sites to minimize overgrazing and disease risk. Provide mobile or makeshift shelters during heavy rains to prevent pneumonia and foot rot. Regularly check for ecto and endo-parasites; ensure timely vaccination against diseases like PPR (Peste des Petits Ruminants) and Enterotoxaemia, ensure deworming before/after migration, and protect against foot rot and pneumonia during wet alpine grazing. NUTRITION ADVISORY FOR WOMEN Balanced diet Include pulses like moong and masoor, as well as milk, curd, and paneer to support body repair and energy. For vitamins, eat green vegetables like spinach, bottle gourd, ridge gourd, and fruits such as watermelon, muskmelon, mango, and litchi to cool the body and boost immunity. Consume millets, peanuts, ␀laxseeds, and sesame seeds to get minerals and strengthen muscles and reduce fatigue. Choose cooling foods like cucumber, bael juice, and melons. Prefer local and fresh produce for better nutrition and easy access. Also use chilled homemade buttermilk using mix curd, water,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_104:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_104,4,"roasted cumin, black salt, and mint. Stay hydrated Soil and Climate: Rice is adaptable to a wide range of soil types, from loamy to clay loams. Optimum growth and higher yield are achieved at day temperatures between 25-33°C and night temperatures between 15-20°C. CEREAL CROPS Nursery Management (Sowing/ Transplanting): Seed treatment and soaking are essential for proper sprouting. Prepare nursery beds 1 m wide and of convenient length, as per the requirement. Construct low poly tunnels using willow sticks and polyethylene sheets over the nursery beds to protect seedlings from chilling injury and to promote healthy growth. The nursery should be weed- Rice Small ruminants 8988",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
