ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_111:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_111,4,"May. Use 40-50 kg seeds/ha. Maintain a spacing of 45 × 10 cm. Recommended Varieties: Shalimar Soybean-1 & Shalimar Soybean-2. All other practices are the same as those for moong. DISEASES OF PULSES Complete sowing in the ␀irst fortnight of May. Use a seed rate of 40 kg/ha. Maintain a spacing of 30 × 10 cm. Recommended Varieties: Shalimar Cowpea-1 & Shalimar Cowpea-2. All other practices are the same as those for moong. Anthracnose: Most striking symptoms appear on immature pods although symtoms also appear on leaves, petioles and stem. Infection appears as brick red colour on the veins on lower surface of the leaves. On veins brownish black lesions appear on pods sunken cankerious spots with lighter or grey centers develop. White Mold: Appearnce of light brown water-soaked discolouration on the stem, leaves or pods and cottony growth on in collar region under humid conditions. Angular leaf spot: Initial symptoms appear on leaves as circular spots in between the veins which attains angular shape which are dark grey in colour and latter turn to reddish brown to dark brown. Cowpea Complete sowing in the ␀irst fortnight of May. Bush type: Seed rate: 60-70 kg/ha & Spacing: 30 × 10 cm.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_111:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_111,5,"Pole type: Seed rate: 30-35 kg/ha & Spacing: 60 × 20 cm. Recommended Varieties: Bush Type: Shalimar Rajmash-1, Shalimar Rajmash-2 and Pole Type: Shalimar Rajmash-3, Shalimar Rajmash-4. All other practices are the same as those for moong. Rust: The rust pustules appear on all the green parts. On the leaves there are numerous small, orange brown pustules each surrounded by a light-yellow halo. Infected leaves wither and may fall. similar rust pustules as on leaves develop on stem. Diseases of Rajmash, moong, cowpea: Symptoms: The infected plants show gradual wilting and drying. Yellowing and premature drying of leaves and stems are noticed. The basal portion of stem and root region becomes black. When the bark of infected root is peeled, black streaks are seen and vascular tissues show discolouration. Leaf spot: Symptoms: Leaves show light brown small spots. Shot holes are formed in due course. Lesions develop on petioles and stem 9594",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Apple Fertilizer Application: Fertilization is critical to meet the nutritional needs of apple orchards. 2ⁿ␀ Dose of Nitrogen (N) & Potassium (K): Apply the second dose of Nitrogen and the remaining Potassium 3-4 weeks after fruit set, as per soil test recommendations. This will help in supporting healthy fruit development during the critical period of cell division. Calcium Spray: Calcium plays a pivotal role in fruit quality, especially during dry spells. Spray Calcium Chloride @ 0.3% during prolonged dry spells (more than 2 weeks) to prevent bitter pit and other related disorders that aﬀect fruit quality. Crop Load Management: A well-managed crop load is essential for achieving optimal fruit size and minimizing biennial bearing. Chemical Thinning: Apply Naphthalene Acetic Acid (NAA) @ 10 ppm when fruitlets are 10-15 mm in size or 7-35 Days After Full Bloom (DAFB). This helps in thinning excess fruit, promoting better growth of the remaining fruits. Hand Thinning: Retain 4-6 fruits/cm² of Trunk Cross-Sectional Area (TCSA) to ensure suf␀icient space for fruit growth. This improves fruit size and helps in reducing biennial bearing. Aﬀected plants",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,2,"appear wilted ripe prematurely and numerous sclerotia bodies develop on infected parts. Adopt cultural practices, use of disease resistant seeds, follow 3-4 year crop rotation. Seed dressing with Captan 50WP @ 3gm/kg seed. Spray the standing crop with carbendazim 5+Mancozeb 75WP @ 0.25%. In case of root rot or damping oﬀ Seed treatment with Talc formulation of Trichoderma viride @ 4g or P. ␀luorescens @ 10 g/kg seed (or) Carbendazim 2 g/kg or Thiram @ 4 g/kg. Spot drenching with Carbendazim @ 1 gm/ litre of water. For the management of Common Mosaic virus: Rogue out the infected plants in the early stages of growth. Spray Fenazaquin @ 1 ml/L on 45 and 60 DAS as prophylactic spray. For the Management of anthracnose disease seed treatment with Captan 50WP @3gm/kg seed. Spray the standing crop with carbendazim+ Mancozeb 75WP @0.25% or chlorothalonil 75WP @ 0.3% carbendazim+ Mancozeb 75WP@2.5gm/Kg of seed. For the management of rusts spray fungicides propiconazole 25EC@0.1% Or ␀lusilazole40EC@0.02%. For the management of Aphids, white ␀ly or bean common mosaic virus application of granular insecticides Thimet @1.5Kg/ha in soil at sowing time followed by foliar spray of Dimethoate",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,3,"30EC@0.05%. FRUIT CROPS Weed & Orchard Sanitation: Maintaining cleanliness in the orchard is essential for preventing pest and disease buildup. Weed Control: Keep the tree basins weed-free to prevent competition for nutrients and water. Sanitation: Remove fallen fruitlets, ␀lowers, and pruned material to reduce disease/pest load and maintain orchard hygiene. Irrigation & Mulching: Proper irrigation and mulching can signi␀icantly improve orchard productivity, especially in challenging climatic conditions. Irrigation: Ensure regular irrigation during the critical cell division stage to support healthy fruit growth. Mulching: In rainfed or water-scarce areas, apply mulch (preferably organic, such as grass/straw) around tree basins. This helps conserve moisture and control weed growth, ensuring better root health. Jammu & Kashmir Foliar fungal disease: Spray Carbendazim 50WP (0.05%) or Thiophanate Methyl 70WP (0.05%) or Dodine 65WP (0.06%). Root Rot: Remove the infected soil and expose the roots to sunlight. Drench the tree basin with Carbendazim 50 WP @ 0.1% or Carbendazim + Mancozeb mix @ 0.5%. Almond, plum, peach, apricot, cherry and Pear Stone fruits (Cherry, Almond, Peach, Plum,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,4,"Apricot etc) Apple Blotch Leaf Miner (ABLM): A major pest that can damage apple orchards. Sanitation: Maintain orchard hygiene by removing infested leaves. Use pheromone traps (1/kanal). Sticky traps placed 10m apart for better pest tracking. Mass Trapping: Install 2 pheromone traps/ kanal. Pesticide Treatment (after ␀irst moth catch): Choose one of the options: Thiamethoxam 25 WG @ 50g/100 L or Imidacloprid 6% + Lambda- Cyhalothrin 4% SL @50ml/100 L or Flubendiamide 39.35 SC @ 40ml/100 L. Fruit Borer (Helicoverpa armigera): Infestations of fruit borers can increase due to climatic variability. Taking prompt action is necessary. Infestation Control: Destroy infested fruits and larvae immediately. Install 8-10 pheromone traps/ha or 1 trap/kanal. Mass Trapping: Use 2 traps/kanal. Pesticide Application: If 1-2 moths/trap for 5 consecutive nights, apply: Chlorpyriphos 20 EC @ 100ml/100L. Quinalphos 25 EC @ 100ml/100 L. Aphids: Aphid populations can explode during certain seasons. Apply Thiamethoxam 25 WG @ 50g/100 litres of water or Thiacloprid 21.7 SC@ 40ml/100 litres of water to manage aphid infestations. Disease Management: Preventing and managing diseases like scab and root rot is",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,5,"vital to maintaining the health of the orchard. Scab & Foliar Diseases: Preventive Measures: Apply fungicides such as Mancozeb 75 WP @ 0.3%, Captan 50 WP @0.3%, or Zineb 75 WP @ 0.3% before the onset of rains. Curative Measures: If symptoms appear, apply curative fungicides like Hexaconazole 5 EC @50ml/100 litres or Flusilazole 40 EC @ 20ml/100 L. Keep stone fruits well-watered during fruit set and fruit developmental stages. Use hail nets when there is colour change in cherry. Pest & Disease Surveillance in Apple and other fruit crops: Eﬀective pest and disease management starts with regular monitoring. Pay attention to common pests such as Apple Blotch Leaf Miner (ABLM), aphids, and fruit borers, along with diseases like scab. Neem Oil: Apply Neem oil (1500 ppm) as a foliar spray at 300ml/100 litres of water during Fruit. Developmental Stage III. This acts as a preventive measure for managing insect pests. San Jose Scale & Wooly Apple Aphid: These pests can cause signi␀icant damage if not controlled eﬀectively. Apply Dimethoate 30 EC or Quinalphos 25 EC @ 100 ml/100 litres of water for pest control. Collar Rot: Clean the aﬀected collar area and apply Chaubatia or Bordeaux paste.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_112:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_112,6,Drench the soil under the tree canopy with Metalaxyl MZ 72 WP @ 0.3% or Copper Oxychloride50 WP @ 0.6%. Fabrea leaf & fruit spot: Spray Thiophanate Methyl 70WP (0.05%) or Carbendazim 50WP (0.05%) or Mancozeb 75WP (0.3%) or chlorothalonil 75 WP (0.25%). 9796,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
