ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_113:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_113,6,Drench the soil under the tree canopy with Metalaxyl MZ 72 WP @ 0.3% or Copper Oxychloride50 WP @ 0.6%. Fabrea leaf & fruit spot: Spray Thiophanate Methyl 70WP (0.05%) or Carbendazim 50WP (0.05%) or Mancozeb 75WP (0.3%) or chlorothalonil 75 WP (0.25%). 9796,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_114:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_114,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Solanaceous Vegetables Recommended varieties/ hybrids are Dilruba (150-200 q/ ha), Pusa Purple Long (150-200 q/ ha), Black Beauty (150-200 q/ ha), Shalimar Improved: (200-225 q/ ha), DBL- 02 (40 t/ha), Shalimar Brinjal Hybrid-1(800 q/ ha), Shalimar Brinjal Hybrid-2 (540 q/ ha) and Pusa Hybrid-5 (520-540 q/ha). Sowing time is Mid April- End of May with seed rate of 500-750 g/ ha for varieties and 300 -400 g/ ha for Hybrid and recommended NPK of 150:120:120 and recommended spacing of 60x45cm VEGETABLE CROPS Brinjal Bell Pepper Recommended varieties/ hybrids are California Wonder (60-70 q/ ha), Chinese Giant (50-60 q/ha), Nishat-1(180-200 q/ ha), Shalimar Capsicum Hybrid-1 (700- 750 q/ ha) and Shalimar Capsicum Hybrid-2(600-650q/ ha). Seed rate for varieties is 1 -1.5 kg/ ha and for Hybrids (300 -400 g/ ha) and recommended spacing is 60 x 45 cm (varieties) and 60 x 60 cm (hybrids). Crop sowing is carried in the month of April to Mid-May. Manures and Fertilizers recommended for the crop is 120:90:30-40 NPK. For higher fruit yield give, 3 sprays of water-soluble fertilizers having combination of NPK as 17:10:27 with a concentration of 0.5% (5g/L) starting",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_114:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_114,2,"from 30 DAT at 10 days interval. Also 3 sprays of micronutrient mixture B (Borax), Zn (Zinc Sulphate), Cu (Copper sulphate), Fe (Ferrous sulphate), Mn (Magnese Sulphate) and Mo (Ammonium molybdate) at a concentration of 0.5% (5g/L) starting from 40 DAT with 10 days interval is recommended for higher fruit yields. In order to increase seed yield of Nishat-1 upto 2.58 q/ ha apply micronutrients as foliar spray. Also spraying of NAA@ 20ppm and pinching of apical shoot is recommended to obtain higher seed yield. Chillies (Hot Pepper) Recommended varieties are Shalimar Long (75-100q/ ha), Kashmir Long 1 (150 q/ ha) and PC-56 (140-150 q/ha). Sowing of chillies can be carried in April-mid May with Seed rate of 1.5-2.0 kg/ ha. spacing of 25 -30cm and using NPK @120:83:60 before transplanting and nitrogen in two split doses (½ at time of sowing and remaining ½ at 30-40 DAT is recommended for the crop. For seed production of chillies and bell pepper an isolation distance of 400 m and 200 m is maintained between two varieties for production of foundation and certi␀ied seed, respectively. Seed yield increases with a foliar application of important micronutrients (Zn, Mn, Cu, Fe and B) at a",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_114:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_114,3,"concentration of 0.5% (5g/ l of water). Tomato Sowing time for tomatoes in Kashmir valley is Mid-March to April with seed rate of 500-600g/ ha. Recommended varieties/ hybrids are S-I (250-275 q/ ha), S-II (200- 210q/ ha), Roma (200-225q/ ha), Pant Bahar (250q/ ha) and PT-3 (300q/ ha). S-I can be transplanted at spacing of 45 x 30 cm and Roma and S-II at 60 x 45 cm. Jammu & Kashmir Integrated nutrient management : Combined application of azotobacter (seed treatment@500g/ ha) + 75% recommended N and 100% P&K (125:60:60) is an optimum nutrient combination for obtaining higher fruit yield. Diﬀerent stages of harvesting Green stage: Fully mature green fruits are harvested to get more price of the produce at early stage. Breaker or turning stage: The fruits are harvested when 1/4 th blossom end of the fruit show pink colour. This is suitable to send the fruits to long distances. Integrated Nutrient Management: Application of vermicompost @ 4.5t/ha along with 50% RFD (75:50:50) is recommended to obtain higher tuber yields. For supplementing Sulphur requirements Copper Sulphate@10kg/ ha is recommended. To improve shelf life in potato tubers spray Calcium Sulphate (0.2% sol) at 50,60 and 70",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_114:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_114,4,"days after planting. Treat tubers with 1% urea and 1% sodium bicarbonate + biofertilizer (Azotobacter + Phosphobacteria) @ 2.5 kg/ ha and apply only 80:75:75 (NPK/ ha) as INM strategy. Potato Cucurbitaceous Vegetables Pink stage: When 3/4th of the surface towards blossom end shows pink colour. These fruits can be used to sale in the local market as well as to send distant markets. Ripe stage: When entire fruit develop pink or red colour but fruits are still ␀irm. This stage is suitable for table or salad purpose and to sale it at farmers ␀ield. Over ripe stage: When fruits attain maximum colour and become soft. Such fruits are suitable for processing purposes. Methods of breaking dormancy:The cutting of tubers in pieces during the advanced stage of dormancy may help in breaking the dormancy. Cut the tubers in pieces having at least three healthy eyes and dip in 1% solution of thiourea for one hour. The planting should be done just after treatment or kept in wet gunny bags for one night. Raising cucurbit seedlings indoors: Seedlings of commercially important cucurbits are raised indoors in warm rooms/ locations with slightly extra care and cost, for getting seedlings early in the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_114:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_114,5,"season. 2-3 seeds are sown in polyethylene bags of 100-gauge thickness and 12 cm x 10 cm in size ␀illed with well crushed Dal weed or garden soil, 4 -5 weeks before the normal date of sowing. The bags before ␀illing are provided with 4 - 5 holes on upper side for proper aeration and 2 -3 holes in the bottom to drain out excess water. When the Varieties recommended for Kashmir valley are Kufri Jyoti( 200-250 q/ ha), Gulmarg Special( 250 - 280 q/ ha), Kufri Giriraj(200-250q/ ha), Shalimar Potato- 1( 350 q/ ha), Shalimar Potato-2( 250-300 q/ ha),Kufri Pukhraj ( 30-35 t/ ha), Kufri Himalini, Kufri Ghirdhari ( 300-350 q/ha) and Kufri Shailja ( 300-350 q/ ha).potato seed tubers can be planted at spacing of 60x20cm and seed rate of 20-25q/ha. First earthing up is done when plants are 10 -15 cm long and Final earthing up is done when the crop is 6 -8 weeks old. 9998",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
