ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_115:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_115,5,"season. 2-3 seeds are sown in polyethylene bags of 100-gauge thickness and 12 cm x 10 cm in size ␀illed with well crushed Dal weed or garden soil, 4 -5 weeks before the normal date of sowing. The bags before ␀illing are provided with 4 - 5 holes on upper side for proper aeration and 2 -3 holes in the bottom to drain out excess water. When the Varieties recommended for Kashmir valley are Kufri Jyoti( 200-250 q/ ha), Gulmarg Special( 250 - 280 q/ ha), Kufri Giriraj(200-250q/ ha), Shalimar Potato- 1( 350 q/ ha), Shalimar Potato-2( 250-300 q/ ha),Kufri Pukhraj ( 30-35 t/ ha), Kufri Himalini, Kufri Ghirdhari ( 300-350 q/ha) and Kufri Shailja ( 300-350 q/ ha).potato seed tubers can be planted at spacing of 60x20cm and seed rate of 20-25q/ha. First earthing up is done when plants are 10 -15 cm long and Final earthing up is done when the crop is 6 -8 weeks old. 9998",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_116:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_116,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Bottle Gourd Variety recommended for growing in Kashmir conditions is Shalimar Improved( 200-250 q/ ha). Seeds can be sown @ 6 -8 kg/ ha directly in Mid-April-May and spacing maintained at 200 -250 cm x100 cm. Entire Recommended dose (NPK@70:30:30 kg/ ha) of P, K, ½ N be applied as basal dose and remaining ½ N can be applied in two equal split doses ␀irst when plants start growth and 2ⁿ␀ when fruiting has started. Bottle gourd responds well to application of plant growth regulators for growth, sex modi␀ication and fruit development. A foliar treatment of 150 ppm (1.5mg/L water) of ethephon at 4 true leaf stage and a second spray of same concentration at ␀ifteen days interval is desirable to achieve better results. Cucumber For Kashmir zone Recommended variety is Arka Harit (80-100 q/ha). Seeds are directly sown in the ␀ield, after being soaked in luke warm water for about 24 hours and then held in wet cloth kept at some warm place, till the seed coat ruptures, 2-3 seeds are planted per hill with seed rate of 5 -6 Kg/ ha can be sown in Mid-April-May and spaced at 150 -200cm x 60cm. NPK recommendation is 60:25:25kg/ ha. Bitter Gourd Recommended",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_116:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_116,2,"varieties/ Hybrids include Japanese Long Green (80-100 q/ ha), Pusa Sanyog (200 q/ ha), Shalimar Cucumber Hybrid-1 (500-600 q/ ha) and Shalimar Cucumber Hybrid-2 (600-650 q/ ha). 2-3 seeds per hill can be sown directly in the ␀ield in the month of Mid-April-May with seed rate of 2.5kg/ ha and 1.2-1.5kg/ ha and spacing of 120cm x 30 cm and 150cm x50cm for Varieties and Hybrids resp. recommended NPK is 70:30:30 kg/ha Seed production of cucurbits: For collecting seeds from various cucurbits care should be taken that the following crops are not raised in one single plot: Sponge gourd and ridge gourd, Muskmelon, longmelon and snap melon, Pumpkin and squash, Watermelon and Round gourd. Besides all cultural practices, the following points should be kept in mind: Maintain isolation distance of 800 meters and 500 meters between two varieties for raising foundation and certi␀ied seed, respectively. Rouge out all oﬀ-types and diseased plants before ␀lowering, during ␀lowering at immature fruit stage, and ␀inally during mature fruit stage. Immature tender fruits may be harvested once from seed plot for consumption rest of fruits and leaving rest of fruits for ripening. Fruits are harvested",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_116:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_116,3,"when fully ripe. Seeds are extracted by cutting the fruits. Seeds are gently rubbed with wood ash and dried. Fruits of bottle gourd, sponge gourd and ridge gourd may be dried or seeds may be extracted as and when required for planting. Fully ripe fruits of pumpkin and squash may be kept for a couple of weeks, before extracting seeds. However, seeds from fully ripe musk melon, water melon, bitter gourd and cucumber are extracted as soon as possible. Well-dried seeds are stored in airtight containers. outside temperature rises (May), the seedlings are transplanted in the open ␀ields along with the polyethylene bag to which a longitudinal cut is given with a sharp blade. Care is taken that the soil ball in these bags does not get disturbed. Plants raised in polyethylene bags are found to give highest early yields. The crop-wise package recommendations are given below. Jammu & Kashmir LIVESTOCK Maintain cleanliness in and around farms and ensure availability of clean water. Ensure that the sheds receive enough sunlight during the day to prevent dampness and to complement the cleaning process. Ensure 6-8 hours of daily grazing to animals if community pastures are available. Concentrate",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_116:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_116,4,"mixture should be fed as per the body weight, production and stage of pregnancy to ensure optimal productive performance. To mitigate scarcity of fodder during winter months, fodder crops such as maize, bajra, and sorghum should be sown, so that it can be preserved through ensiling. Cattle Important management tips for raising cucurbits: Select a plot with an ef␀icient drainage system. Plant the seed when the soil has attained the optimum temperature between 20- 25␀C when the winter is over and follow space planting as recommended. Irrigate twice or weekly during hot summer. Apply fertilizers properly when the vine starts growing. Adopt timely plant protection measures against diseases and insect pests. Harvest the melons (except long melon) when they are mature whereas harvest the gourds when in immature state. Procure the seed of a recommended variety from a reliable source. Hand pollination may be adopted to get higher yields. Do not grow cucurbits under shade, if possible. Do not grow cucurbits under very humid conditions. Do not irrigate heavy soils after sowing. Do not allow tender fruits to go beyond marketable stage. Do not sow the seeds in nursery because cucurbits do not",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_116:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_116,5,"withstand transplanting shock. However, as recommended seedlings can be raised indoors in polythene bags. Leguminous Vegetable French Bean Bush type varieties like Bountiful, Master, Arka Komal, Contender and pole type varieties like Kentucky Wonder, Painted Lady and Asparagus beans can be grown successfully in Kashmir conditions with seed rate of 80-100 kg/ ha, 25-30 kg/ ha and 20-25 kg/ ha and spacing of 30 cm x 10 cm, 100 cm x 50 cm and 100 cm x 50 cm in Bush type, Pole type and Asparagus beans respectively. Sowing can be carried from April - June. Entire FYM, K and ½ N (recommended dose is of FYM is 20-25 t and 30:60:60 NPK at the time of sowing and other ½ N when true leaves emerge. Bhindi (Okra) Pusa Sawani (60-80 q/ ha) is Recommended variety of okra for Kashmir valley. Seeds pre-soaked in hot water at 50°C for 30 minutes and directly sown on the ridge tops which are 15 -20 cm high above ground and 45 cm apart can be sown in Late April- May with seed rate of 15-20 kg/ha. After the seeds have germinated and plant has attained height of about 7-10 cm, plants are thinned to a spacing of 30cm between plants. NPK @120:90:60 can be applied. Seed Production: Besides all cultural",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
