ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_119:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_119,6,"to prevent development of anthelmintic resistance. This involves deworming animals based on parasite risk and fecal egg counts rather than routine blanket treatments. Rotating between classes of anthelmintics and targeting high- risk animals helps preserve the ef␀icacy of dewormers, ensuring long-term parasite control and minimizing drug resistance in the herd. Provide salt licks and mineral blocks. This is essential to meet mineral de␀iciency especially at higher altitudes where soil and forage may lack essential minerals. Trout Fish Backyard Poultry 103102",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_120:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_120,1,"CEREAL CROPS Paddy Farmers are advised to grow upland paddy with varieties like Vandana, Virendra, Abhishek, Swarna Shreya, Anjali, Sahbhagi Dhan, CR Dhaan-320, IR-64, etc., using the Direct Seeded Rice (DSR) method in upland areas. For direct sowing of paddy seeds in upland areas, summer ploughing should be done in May, and land preparation should be completed in the ␀irst week of June. Varieties such as CR Dhaan-320 and Swarna Shreya should be purchased in May itself. Short-duration varieties like Anjali, Sahbhagi, Vandana, and Sushak Samrat are suitable for direct sowing in the ␀irst fortnight of June. For medium land paddy cultivation, to minimize delays due to late monsoon arrival, nurseries for paddy seedlings should be prepared at 10-day intervals in June. Improved variety seeds like Sahbhagi Dhan should be purchased at the end of May. Nursery sowing should be done in the ␀irst week of June to enable timely Rabi crop cultivation. A nursery of 100 m² is suf␀icient for one hectare. For this, 40 kg of OP variety seeds or 15 kg of hybrid seeds should be sown. Paddy seeds should be treated with Carbendazim @ 2 g/kg of seed. Fertilizers should be applied at a rate of 40:20:20 kg",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_120:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_120,2,"N:P:K per hectare. Of the nitrogen, 50% should be applied at sowing, 25% at 30-35 days, and the remaining 25% at 45-50 days after sowing. Entire phosphorus and potassium should be applied at sowing. Farmers are advised to get their farm soil tested and apply fertilizers as per recommended doses. For transplanted paddy, apply fertilizers at a rate of 80:40:20 kg N:P:K per hectare. Nitrogen should be applied in split doses: 50% at transplanting, 25% at 30-35 days, and 25% at 50-60 days after transplanting. Phosphorus and potassium should be fully applied at transplanting. To prevent zinc de␀iciency, apply 25 kg of zinc sulphate during ␀ield preparation. For eﬀective weed control, apply 2.5 litres of Pendimethalin 30 EC mixed in 500 litres of water Jharkhand Jharkhand per hectare within 1-2 days of sowing. Bispyribac 10 SC should be applied at 250 ml/hectare 20-25 days after sowing. In case of chlorosis (iron de␀iciency), spray 1% ferrous sulphate solution (2.5 kg in 250 litres of water) two to three times at weekly intervals, and ensure adequate irrigation. For Terai paddy, seedlings should be prepared as per medium land rice guidelines. Varieties like Rajendra Mahsuri, Rajshree, and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_120:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_120,3,"BPT-5204 should be selected and purchased in advance, preferably in May. Maize PULSE CROPS Farmers are advised to plough the land during May and apply 3-4 quintals of lime per hectare. Seeds should be sown in the ␀irst week of June or at the onset of the monsoon. To control termite populations and larvae, 100-150 quintals of well- decomposed farmyard manure (FYM) along with Methyl Parathion 2% dust at the rate of 25 kg per hectare should be incorporated into the soil during land preparation. Use 20 kg of seed per hectare of recommended maize varieties such as PMH-3, Orange Flint, HQPM-1, or HQPM-5. At the time of sowing, apply 86 kg of urea, 130 kg of DAP, and 68 kg of MOP per hectare. If the ␀ield remains dry, provide irrigation after 30 days. After proper weeding, apply an additional 65 kg of urea. Ensure the ␀ield has proper drainage to prevent water stagnation. Two weeks after germination, apply 10-15 granules of Fipronil 0.3G or Carbofuran 3G in each plant to manage early-stage pests. To control the incidence of Fall Armyworm in the maize crop, spray Emamectin Benzoate 5% SG at the rate of 1 gram per 3 litres of water. Farmers are advised to grow pulses (especially pea,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_120:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_120,4,"chickpea, and lentil) during Kharif season. The recommended varieties for upland ␀ield include: Pigeon pea- Narendra Arhar-1, Narendra Arhar-2, Rajeev Lochan, IPA 203, Malviya Arhar-Mal- 13; Black gram- WBU-109, Birsa Urd -1, PU-31; Green gram- Virat, Shikha, HUM-12, IPM 2-14, IPM 2-3, HUM-16; Horse gram- Birsa Kulthi-1, Payur-2, Madhu, VLG-19 etc. Oil seed crops like Niger- Utkal Niger-150, DNS-4, BNS-3, Pooja, JNS-29, JNC- 6, BNS-1; Sesame-RT-351, Krishna, Sekhar, RT-346, GT-4, GT-6, Punjab-1; Groundnut- K1812, TLG-45, ICGV-00350, K-6, TG-37A, TG-38 Dharni, Grinar-3, TG-51, TCGS- 1043, AK12-14 etc. Management of paddy ␀ield 105104",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_121:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_121,1,"CEREAL CROPS Paddy Farmers are advised to grow upland paddy with varieties like Vandana, Virendra, Abhishek, Swarna Shreya, Anjali, Sahbhagi Dhan, CR Dhaan-320, IR-64, etc., using the Direct Seeded Rice (DSR) method in upland areas. For direct sowing of paddy seeds in upland areas, summer ploughing should be done in May, and land preparation should be completed in the ␀irst week of June. Varieties such as CR Dhaan-320 and Swarna Shreya should be purchased in May itself. Short-duration varieties like Anjali, Sahbhagi, Vandana, and Sushak Samrat are suitable for direct sowing in the ␀irst fortnight of June. For medium land paddy cultivation, to minimize delays due to late monsoon arrival, nurseries for paddy seedlings should be prepared at 10-day intervals in June. Improved variety seeds like Sahbhagi Dhan should be purchased at the end of May. Nursery sowing should be done in the ␀irst week of June to enable timely Rabi crop cultivation. A nursery of 100 m² is suf␀icient for one hectare. For this, 40 kg of OP variety seeds or 15 kg of hybrid seeds should be sown. Paddy seeds should be treated with Carbendazim @ 2 g/kg of seed. Fertilizers should be applied at a rate of 40:20:20 kg",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_121:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_121,2,"N:P:K per hectare. Of the nitrogen, 50% should be applied at sowing, 25% at 30-35 days, and the remaining 25% at 45-50 days after sowing. Entire phosphorus and potassium should be applied at sowing. Farmers are advised to get their farm soil tested and apply fertilizers as per recommended doses. For transplanted paddy, apply fertilizers at a rate of 80:40:20 kg N:P:K per hectare. Nitrogen should be applied in split doses: 50% at transplanting, 25% at 30-35 days, and 25% at 50-60 days after transplanting. Phosphorus and potassium should be fully applied at transplanting. To prevent zinc de␀iciency, apply 25 kg of zinc sulphate during ␀ield preparation. For eﬀective weed control, apply 2.5 litres of Pendimethalin 30 EC mixed in 500 litres of water Jharkhand Jharkhand per hectare within 1-2 days of sowing. Bispyribac 10 SC should be applied at 250 ml/hectare 20-25 days after sowing. In case of chlorosis (iron de␀iciency), spray 1% ferrous sulphate solution (2.5 kg in 250 litres of water) two to three times at weekly intervals, and ensure adequate irrigation. For Terai paddy, seedlings should be prepared as per medium land rice guidelines. Varieties like Rajendra Mahsuri, Rajshree, and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
