ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Arecanut Elakki Banana and G9 are the popular varieties grown in karnataka, apply NPK at 400:240:500 kg/ha along with 40 tons of FYM per hectare before planting. The recommended spacing for Elakki Banana is 1.5 x 1.5 meters in a triangular shape, accommodating 5,120 plants per hectare, while other banana varieties should be spaced at 2.1 x 2.1 meters, accommodating 2,270 plants per hectare. In high-density planting of G9 tissue culture banana, use a 6x6 feet spacing with 2 cm³ pits, resulting in 7,500 plants per hectare and a potential yield of 135 tons per hectare. A spray of Arka Banana Special is recommended starting 5 months after planting and continuing for up to 10 months. Mix 75 grams of Banana Special with 15 liters of water, along with 1 lemon's juice and 1 sachet of shampoo, and spray every 20 days. Rhizome Weevil infestation can be prevented by treating rhizomes with 20% Neem Seed Kernel Extract . To control Leaf-Eating Caterpillars, apply 2.5 ml of Chlorpyriphos per liter of water. For Thrips, use 0.3 ml of Imidacloprid or 1.5 ml of Dimethoate per liter. To manage Leaf Spot Disease, spray 1 ml of Propiconazole per liter of water. Nematode",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,2,"infesatation can be controled by combined application of 12 grams of Pseudomonas, 12 grams of Pachelomyces and 500 grams of Neem Cake. Banana palm includes 500 g Nitrogen, 320 g Phosphorus, and 1200 g Potassium. Cocoa is a common intercrop. Micronutrients like boron and zinc are applied. Drip irrigation is used. Weed management is done by hand weeding. Stem bleeding is managed by root feeding with Hexaconazole. Black-headed caterpillar is managed through the release of Goniozus nephantidis, a biological control agent. Cashew Cashew cultivation requires selecting recommended varieties such as Vengurla-4, Netra Jambu-1, Bhaskar, Ullal-1, Ullal-2, Ullal-3, Chintamani-1, and Chintamani-2. The ideal planting time for Vengurla types is between June and October, while Ullal and Chintamani types should be planted from May to June. For spacing, a 7 m x 7 m arrangement supports about 200 plants per hectare, while an 8 m x 8 m arrangement accommodates approximately 156 plants per hectare. The soil should be red sandy loam with good drainage. Nutrient management includes applying 60:60:60 g of NPK per plant in the ␀irst year, doubling the dose for the second to fourth year, and applying",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,3,"500:250:250 g of NPK per plant from the ␀ifth year onward. Foliar nutrition with 19:19:19 at 2 g/litre should be sprayed once every 15 days during summer. Suitable intercrops for cashew cultivation include turmeric, ginger, and ␀ield crops, excluding sun␀lower and maize. Irrigation should be provided at 40-50 litres per plant, three times per month. Weed management can be done through hand weeding and light intercultivation as needed. Pest and disease management involves spraying Lambda Cyhalothrin @ 0.5 ml/litre or Quinolphos @ 1 ml/litre for tea mosquito bug, spraying COC 50 WP @ 3 g/litre for leaf spot, and swabbing with a 2% COC solution and 2 ml Chlorpyriphos 20 EC for stem borers. Recommended varieties of arecanut include Mangala, Mohitnagar, Sumangala, Swarna Mangala, Theerthalli Local, Channagiri Local, and South Canara Local. Planting is preferably done in May-June or September-October using pit planting (pit size: 90 cm × 90 cm × 90 cm) at a spacing of 2.7 m × 2.7 m or 3.3 m × 3.3 m, with a density of 1372 plants/ha. Wider spacing is preferred when intercropped with high-value crops such Karnataka as banana, cocoa, nutmeg, black pepper, or ginger. Fertilizer",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,4,"recommendation is 100:40:140 g NPK per plant annually, applied in two equal splits - ␀irst in September- October along with 12 kg organic manure and second in February (for irrigated) or June (for rainfed). Additionally, zinc sulfate and borax are applied at 5 g per plant during October-December. Irrigation is usually done through the basin method at 175-200 litres per palm per irrigation, adjusted as per season: every 7-8 days in November- December, every 6 days in January-February, and every 4-5 days from March to May. Drip irrigation is also practiced. Common diseases include bud rot, leaf spot, collar rot, crown rot, foot rot, and yellow leaf disease. Bud rot can be managed with sprays of 1% Bordeaux mixture, 0.3% Copper Oxychloride (COC), or 0.2% Metalaxyl + Mancozeb 72WP, applied before the onset of monsoon and repeated after 30-45 days. Pests such as spindle bug, Pentatomid bug, red palm weevil, mites, root grubs, in␀lorescence caterpillar, and ambrosia beetle aﬀect the crop. Red mite infestations are managed by spraying wettable sulphur (80%) at 0.4%. LIVESTOCK To ensure the health and productivity of livestock during the kharif season, it is essential to implement",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,5,"appropriate management practices. Cattle, buﬀalo, sheep, and goats should be vaccinated against Hemorrhagic Septicemia, while sheep and goats also require vaccination against Enterotoxaemia. Deworming of all animals using Piperazine, Albendazole, or Fenbendazole is recommended to control internal parasites during the rainy season. Along with green fodder, daily feeding of dry fodder to cattle, buﬀalo, and sheep is necessary for better digestion and nutrient absorption. Grazing of maize and jowar seedlings should be strictly avoided, as these can cause cyanide poisoning, potentially leading to animal death. Pesticides, insecticides, and fertilizers must be stored safely away from animals to prevent accidental toxicity. Farmers can prepare animal feed using locally available ingredients, such as cereals (maize, jowar, wheat) 35-40 kg, bran or polish of grains 30-35 kg, oil cakes (groundnut, saf␀lower, cottonseed) 25-30 kg, mineral mixture 2 kg, and salt 0.5-1 kg to make 100 kg of cattle feed. To prevent the spread of Lumpy Skin Disease (LSD), which is a vector- borne illness, livestock should be protected from mosquitoes, house ␀lies, and ticks by using mosquito nets, repellents, and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_134:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_134,6,"washing animals with ectoparasiticidal drugs. Additionally, burning dry neem leaves in the morning and evening can help reduce mosquito bites. Farmers are also encouraged to cultivate improved fodder and crops during the Kharif season, utilizing the monsoon rains. Furthermore, all backyard poultry birds should be compulsorily vaccinated against Ranikhet Disease. Fisheries Maintain 6 feet water in the ␀ish pond for proper growth and development of ␀ishes. Remove unwanted plants and animals prior to release of ␀ishes in the pond. As a supplementary food, ␀loating pallets or groundnut cake (25%), paddy husk (40 %), sweet potato powder (10%), ␀ish meal (24 %), vitamin and mineral mixture (1%) should be mixed and feed scienti␀ically. Continue to feed ␀ishes 3-5 % of body weight on daily basis. The suitable breeds for fresh water aquaculture are catla, rohu, mrigal, amur common carps, jayanti rohu, pungasius, GIFT tilapia, grass carp, silver carp, murrel. Prior to release of ␀ingerlings (15 days) mix cow dung (100 kg/100 m²) in the pond for plankton production. 119118",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
