ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_187:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_187,5,"cucurbitaceous vegetables can be grown in the kitchen garden. Additionally, SHG members can make masks, hand gloves, and cotton clothes for their family members and the neighbouring community, ensuring safety while generating additional income. FPOs should begin their business by producing high-quality seeds and planting materials through organic cultivation of ginger, turmeric, and pineapple, along with value addition. MUSHROOM SELF-HELP GROUP/FPOs 171170",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_188:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_188,1,"Maize Pest Management (Fall Armyworm): Install pheromone traps at the rate of 12 traps/ha during the 3rd to 4th week of May. For control, spray Emamectin Benzoate @ 0.4 ml/l, Spinosad @ 3 ml/l, or use other chemical options such as Spinetoram @ 0.5 ml/l, Lambda- Cyhalothrin + Thiamethoxam @ 0.25 ml/l, or Chlorantraniliprole 18.5% SC @ 0.4 ml/. Alternatively, apply ash or spray soap water into the whorls of aﬀected plants. Avoid chemical sprays once tasselling begins. Varietal Selection: Suitable composite varieties include RCM-75, RCM-1-1, RCM 1- 76, RCM 1-3, and Vivek Sankul. Recommended hybrid varieties are Vivek QPM-9 and HQPM-1. Local varieties such as Mimban and Mimpui are also good choices. However, tall varieties like MZM 11, Ganga Hybrid, and local Popcorn should be avoided in areas prone to heavy rainfall and strong winds, as they are more susceptible to lodging and crop damage. CEREAL CROPS Drainage Management: Farmers are advised to create drainage channels around ␀ields, especially in low-lying areas, to prevent waterlogging. Land Preparation and Sowing: Prepare the ␀ield with at least 3 deep ploughings before sowing. Sow maize seeds at the rate of 20-22 kg/ha,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_188:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_188,2,"maintaining a spacing of 60 cm × 20 cm. Management of Fall Armyworm – FAW in Maize Mizoram Mizoram Upland rice cultivation Upland paddy For rainfed upland paddy cultivation, farmers should begin by treating seeds with Carbendazim (2-3g/kg seed) to prevent fungal diseases and ensure healthy germination. The dibbling method is strongly recommended over broadcasting to optimize seed usage and improve germination rates. Farmers should select from improved drought- tolerant varieties such as Fazu-MZ UPR 4, Maibasa-MZ UPR 25, Bhadepui-MZ UPR 23, Biroin-MZ UPR 24, Sazukthau-MZ UPR 6, Lalron-MZ 28, Idaw-MZ UPR 11, Buhban-MZ UPR 2, and MZ UPR 33, which are specially developed for Mizoram's upland conditions. Implement critical weed management with ␀irst weeding by mid- May followed by a second weeding between the ␀irst week of June to second week of July. For soil conservation in jhum ␀ields with slopes exceeding 30%, construct log wood or bamboo bunds across slopes and dig recharge pits (1×1×1 ft) to prevent severe soil erosion and retain topsoil. Nursery Preparation(2ⁿ␀ Week of June): Prepare raised nursery beds with ␀inely tilled soil and apply 2 t/ha of Farm Yard Manure (FYM) along with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_188:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_188,3,"2 kg of Azospirillum per 1000 square meters. Two to three days before sowing, incorporate 10 quintals of well-decomposed FYM per 1000 square meters into the nursery beds. Use a seed rate of 3.5-4 kg per 100 square meters of nursery area to raise suf␀icient seedlings for transplanting in one hectare. For improved germination, treat the seeds with Zinc sulphate priming before sowing. After sowing, cover the seedbed lightly with a thin layer of soil or compost to ensure proper seed establishment. Harvest physiologically mature cobs (intended for seed) as early as possible to avoid damage from predicted moderate to heavy rainfall. Transplanting (1␀␀-3␀␀ Week of July, Based on Variety): Uproot 25-30-day-old healthy seedlings for transplanting to ensure vigorous growth. For optimal plant density, follow these spacing recommendations: under the normal method, maintain 20 cm × 15 cm spacing with 2-3 seedlings per hill; for Integrated Crop Management (ICM), use 20 cm × 20 cm spacing; and for the System of Rice Intensi␀ication (SRI), adopt a wider 25 cm × 25 cm spacing to promote higher yields in smaller areas. Adjust seed rates accordingly-35-40 kg/ha for ICM and just 3-5 kg/ha for SRI-to",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_188:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_188,4,"maximize ef␀iciency and productivity while conserving seeds. Root dip treatment with SSP/ Rock phosphate + Microbial consortium should be done overnight with uprooted rice seedlings prior to transplanting of rice to address phosphorus de␀iciency in acidic soils Recommended high yielding verities for irrigated lowland such as CAU R-1, CAU R-3, Land Preparation (From 1␀␀ week of June): Begin puddling with the onset of monsoon and ensure proper levelling for uniform water distribution and to prevent water stagnation. Lowland Paddy 173172",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
