ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_189:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_189,4,"maximize ef␀iciency and productivity while conserving seeds. Root dip treatment with SSP/ Rock phosphate + Microbial consortium should be done overnight with uprooted rice seedlings prior to transplanting of rice to address phosphorus de␀iciency in acidic soils Recommended high yielding verities for irrigated lowland such as CAU R-1, CAU R-3, Land Preparation (From 1␀␀ week of June): Begin puddling with the onset of monsoon and ensure proper levelling for uniform water distribution and to prevent water stagnation. Lowland Paddy 173172",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_190:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_190,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Integrated pest management: Spray application of Nuvacron 1.25ml/L or Dimethoate (0.04%) can be used for eﬀective control of leaf folder, stem ␀ly and semilooper like pests. Seed treatment with Imidachloprid @7g/kg of seed reduces the problem of Leaf folder Irrigation: Despite it is a rainfed crop in kharif, Supplemental irrigation is required depending on rainfall patterns. Flowering and pod ␀illing stages are the critical stages of irrigation. Relay cropping: Soybean can be grown as a relay crop with maize, planting between the rows of the maize crop is recommended. local short duration var. Idaw, tai, Buhsakei are recommended for upland/Jhum cultivation with rich alluvial soil OILSEED CROPS Pest & Disease Management: To eﬀectively control Gundhi bugs, deploy 100 rotten crab funnel traps per hectare during the critical milking stage of the crop. For organic pest management, utilize neem-based biopesticides, release Trichogramma egg parasitoids, and install yellow sticky traps to monitor and reduce pest populations. Additionally, conserve natural predators such as spiders, dragon␀lies, and ladybugs by minimizing chemical pesticide use and maintaining",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_190:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_190,2,"ecological balance in the ␀ield. Adopt SRI method in small areas for enhanced yields, conduct regular ␀ield monitoring for pests and nutrient de␀iciencies and maintain proper water management and spacing as per cultivation method. Soyabean Integrated nutrient management: Soybean being a leguminous crop does not require high dose of nitrogen, however 20 kg/ha is suf␀icient for healthy crop stand. A dose of 60 kg P O (SSP) and 30kg K O (MOP) are recommended. FYM @ 5t/ha should 2 5 2 also supplement the chemical fertilizers. Integrated disease management: Seed treatment with Thiram at the rate of 4.5g per kg of seed will control fungal diseases like Leaf Blight, Leaf Spot, Seedling Rot, Frog eye spot and Rust. Varietal Selection: RCS1-1, RCS1-9, RCS1-10, JS335, MAUS 71 is suitable option for Kharif cultivation in Mizoram. Groundnut For optimal groundnut production, farmers should complete sowing between 15th May and ␀irst week of June, using high-yielding varieties like ICGS 76, ICGV 86590, Girnar 4, TS 67 Before sowing, treat seeds with Bavistin (5g/kg seed) for disease prevention and apply Rhizobium + PSB culture for better plant growth. Prepare ␀ields by incorporating lime to",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_190:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_190,3,"address soil acidity and use Butachlor (10ml/litre water) as a pre-emergence weedicide. Apply balanced fertilization at 20:60:40 kg NPK/ha, split into basal and top-dressing applications. To protect crops, spray Dichlorvos (2ml/L) against Blister beetles during ␀lowering and implement monthly preventive sprays of Dichlorvos (2ml/litre) + Bavistin (2g/L) from 30 days after sowing. Ensure light Mizoram VEGETABLE CROPS Pumpkin Carrot Tomato irrigation during ␀lowering and pod formation if rainfall is inadequate, and perform manual weeding (20-25 DAS) and earthing up (35-40 DAS) for better yield. Farmers are recommended to grow indeterminate varieties Solan Lalima , Arka Rakshak and Arka Samrat. Prepare nursery beds by the ␀irst week of May by raising soil 10-15 cm above ground level, incorporating well-rotted FYM/compost. Treat beds with 0.1% Captan/Fytolan solution to prevent damping-oﬀ, cover for 2 days, then mix Malathion 5% dust for insect protection. Sow seeds thinly in 2.5 cm spaced furrows (1-2 cm deep) by second week of May, covering with sand-FYM mix. Prepare main ␀ield pits at 75×30 cm spacing 15 days before transplanting (June 2nd-3rd week), adding FYM and adjusting soil pH",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_190:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_190,4,"through liming. Apply 10t FYM, 75kg N, 60kg P O , and 60kg K O per hectare 2 5 2 (half N basal, remainder top-dressed). Maintain irrigation (4cm every 18-20 days) and weed control (Metolachlor @1kg a.i/ha pre-emergence with grubber at 40 DAP). Manage diseases with 0.25% Mancozeb (late blight), 200ppm Streptomycin (bacterial wilt), and 0.3% Captan (fungal wilt). Regular monitoring and these integrated practices will ensure healthy tomato production. Recommended varieties include Arka Chandan, Arka Suryamukhi, and Pusa Biswas. These varieties are suitable for the region due to their high productivity, nutritive value, good storability, and transport qualities. Pumpkin grows best in slightly acidic sandy loam to loam soils with a pH of 5.5-6.0. It requires a long, warm growing season with an optimum temperature range of 18°C to 30°C. Sowing is typically done during April-May in hilly areas. The ␀ield should be ploughed 4-5 times, and farmyard manure (FYM) should be applied at the rate of 25-30 t/ha. Recommended fertilizers include Urea (145 kg/ha), DAP (130 kg/ha), and MOP (67 kg/ha). Apply the full dose of phosphorus and potassium and half the nitrogen during land preparation. The",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_190:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_190,5,"remaining nitrogen should be applied in three equal splits at 20, 40, and 60 days after sowing. To control termites and cutworms, apply Phorate 10G at 15-20 kg/ha during land preparation. Prior to sowing, soak seeds in Captan solution (2 g/L of water) for 3-4 hours. For oﬀ-season cultivation, seedlings should be raised in polythene bags under a polyhouse and transplanted by late January or early February, which enables an early harvest by 1-1.5 months compared to normal sowing. Harvesting is done 75-180 days after sowing, with expected yields ranging from 250 to 400 quintals per hectare. After harvesting, fruits should be cleaned and damaged ones discarded. Grade the produce based on shape, color, and maturity. Mature pumpkins can be stored for 4-6 months in a well-ventilated storage chamber. Recommended varieties include Pusa Rudhira, Pusa Asita, and Pusa Vrishti. These varieties are generally suitable for sowing in the late summer and early fall. Well- drained loamy soil with an ideal pH of 6.5, though sandy soils are preferable for early 175174",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_191:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_191,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Integrated pest management: Spray application of Nuvacron 1.25ml/L or Dimethoate (0.04%) can be used for eﬀective control of leaf folder, stem ␀ly and semilooper like pests. Seed treatment with Imidachloprid @7g/kg of seed reduces the problem of Leaf folder Irrigation: Despite it is a rainfed crop in kharif, Supplemental irrigation is required depending on rainfall patterns. Flowering and pod ␀illing stages are the critical stages of irrigation. Relay cropping: Soybean can be grown as a relay crop with maize, planting between the rows of the maize crop is recommended. local short duration var. Idaw, tai, Buhsakei are recommended for upland/Jhum cultivation with rich alluvial soil OILSEED CROPS Pest & Disease Management: To eﬀectively control Gundhi bugs, deploy 100 rotten crab funnel traps per hectare during the critical milking stage of the crop. For organic pest management, utilize neem-based biopesticides, release Trichogramma egg parasitoids, and install yellow sticky traps to monitor and reduce pest populations. Additionally, conserve natural predators such as spiders, dragon␀lies, and ladybugs by minimizing chemical pesticide use and maintaining",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_191:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_191,2,"ecological balance in the ␀ield. Adopt SRI method in small areas for enhanced yields, conduct regular ␀ield monitoring for pests and nutrient de␀iciencies and maintain proper water management and spacing as per cultivation method. Soyabean Integrated nutrient management: Soybean being a leguminous crop does not require high dose of nitrogen, however 20 kg/ha is suf␀icient for healthy crop stand. A dose of 60 kg P O (SSP) and 30kg K O (MOP) are recommended. FYM @ 5t/ha should 2 5 2 also supplement the chemical fertilizers. Integrated disease management: Seed treatment with Thiram at the rate of 4.5g per kg of seed will control fungal diseases like Leaf Blight, Leaf Spot, Seedling Rot, Frog eye spot and Rust. Varietal Selection: RCS1-1, RCS1-9, RCS1-10, JS335, MAUS 71 is suitable option for Kharif cultivation in Mizoram. Groundnut For optimal groundnut production, farmers should complete sowing between 15th May and ␀irst week of June, using high-yielding varieties like ICGS 76, ICGV 86590, Girnar 4, TS 67 Before sowing, treat seeds with Bavistin (5g/kg seed) for disease prevention and apply Rhizobium + PSB culture for better plant growth. Prepare ␀ields by incorporating lime to",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_191:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_191,3,"address soil acidity and use Butachlor (10ml/litre water) as a pre-emergence weedicide. Apply balanced fertilization at 20:60:40 kg NPK/ha, split into basal and top-dressing applications. To protect crops, spray Dichlorvos (2ml/L) against Blister beetles during ␀lowering and implement monthly preventive sprays of Dichlorvos (2ml/litre) + Bavistin (2g/L) from 30 days after sowing. Ensure light Mizoram VEGETABLE CROPS Pumpkin Carrot Tomato irrigation during ␀lowering and pod formation if rainfall is inadequate, and perform manual weeding (20-25 DAS) and earthing up (35-40 DAS) for better yield. Farmers are recommended to grow indeterminate varieties Solan Lalima , Arka Rakshak and Arka Samrat. Prepare nursery beds by the ␀irst week of May by raising soil 10-15 cm above ground level, incorporating well-rotted FYM/compost. Treat beds with 0.1% Captan/Fytolan solution to prevent damping-oﬀ, cover for 2 days, then mix Malathion 5% dust for insect protection. Sow seeds thinly in 2.5 cm spaced furrows (1-2 cm deep) by second week of May, covering with sand-FYM mix. Prepare main ␀ield pits at 75×30 cm spacing 15 days before transplanting (June 2nd-3rd week), adding FYM and adjusting soil pH",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_191:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_191,4,"through liming. Apply 10t FYM, 75kg N, 60kg P O , and 60kg K O per hectare 2 5 2 (half N basal, remainder top-dressed). Maintain irrigation (4cm every 18-20 days) and weed control (Metolachlor @1kg a.i/ha pre-emergence with grubber at 40 DAP). Manage diseases with 0.25% Mancozeb (late blight), 200ppm Streptomycin (bacterial wilt), and 0.3% Captan (fungal wilt). Regular monitoring and these integrated practices will ensure healthy tomato production. Recommended varieties include Arka Chandan, Arka Suryamukhi, and Pusa Biswas. These varieties are suitable for the region due to their high productivity, nutritive value, good storability, and transport qualities. Pumpkin grows best in slightly acidic sandy loam to loam soils with a pH of 5.5-6.0. It requires a long, warm growing season with an optimum temperature range of 18°C to 30°C. Sowing is typically done during April-May in hilly areas. The ␀ield should be ploughed 4-5 times, and farmyard manure (FYM) should be applied at the rate of 25-30 t/ha. Recommended fertilizers include Urea (145 kg/ha), DAP (130 kg/ha), and MOP (67 kg/ha). Apply the full dose of phosphorus and potassium and half the nitrogen during land preparation. The",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_191:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_191,5,"remaining nitrogen should be applied in three equal splits at 20, 40, and 60 days after sowing. To control termites and cutworms, apply Phorate 10G at 15-20 kg/ha during land preparation. Prior to sowing, soak seeds in Captan solution (2 g/L of water) for 3-4 hours. For oﬀ-season cultivation, seedlings should be raised in polythene bags under a polyhouse and transplanted by late January or early February, which enables an early harvest by 1-1.5 months compared to normal sowing. Harvesting is done 75-180 days after sowing, with expected yields ranging from 250 to 400 quintals per hectare. After harvesting, fruits should be cleaned and damaged ones discarded. Grade the produce based on shape, color, and maturity. Mature pumpkins can be stored for 4-6 months in a well-ventilated storage chamber. Recommended varieties include Pusa Rudhira, Pusa Asita, and Pusa Vrishti. These varieties are generally suitable for sowing in the late summer and early fall. Well- drained loamy soil with an ideal pH of 6.5, though sandy soils are preferable for early 175174",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_192:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_192,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 LIVESTOCK Farmers are encouraged to begin rearing improved dual-purpose chicken breeds starting from the second week of May, which can contribute to both egg and meat production. For eﬀective disease prevention, administer Ascal feed supplement (20-60 ml per 100 birds) for 10 days. Follow a strict vaccination schedule, starting with the Marek's and Infectious Bursal Disease (IBD) vaccines from May 1␀␀, and the Ranikhet (Lasota strain) vaccine at 4-8 weeks of age (1,000 doses in 20 liters of drinking water). Additionally, maintain biosecurity by regularly disinfecting equipment and the poultry environment using Kohrsolin or Germex spray. For proper nutrition management, provide broilers with starter feed containing 22-23% protein for the ␀irst six weeks, followed by ␀inisher feed with 18-20% protein until they reach market age. To enhance feed ef␀iciency and reduce costs, incorporate 30% Azolla with 70% concentrate feed. It is also essential to store feed properly to prevent spoilage and fungal contamination. crops. Prepare the ␀ield by thoroughly tilling the soil and incorporating 10-15 t/ha of farmyard manure. Apply balanced fertilizers at 60:60:90",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_192:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_192,2,"kg NPK/ha, using urea (80kg), DAP (130kg), and MOP (150kg), with urea split into 2-3 applications at two- week intervals. Implement pest control by spraying Diamethoate (0.05%) for leaf hoppers and drenching soil with Chlorpyriphos (0.1%) for cutworms. Expect yields of 15-30 t/ha, though fresh carrots maintain quality for only 3-4 days under normal storage conditions. Poultry Piggery To maintain healthy and productive pig herds, farmers should implement strict biosecurity measures by regularly cleaning pens every 2-3 days using 1% sodium/calcium hydroxide or 2% caustic soda solution, while disinfecting all equipment and vehicles with 0.03% sodium hypochlorite, 1% formaldehyde, or Virkon S/B-904 (1:100 dilution). Farm workers must disinfect their shoes, clothes, and tools before contact with pigs, and animals should be provided with cooling water baths during peak heat along with clean drinking water refreshed at least thrice daily. Critical health interventions include vaccinating against Swine Fever by the 3rd week of May, administering Ivermectin (200 mcg/kg BW) and Albendazole (5-10 mg/kg BW) for deworming, giving piglets 1ml iron injections on days 4 and 14, and supplementing",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_192:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_192,3,"feed with Ascal (10ml twice daily for 10 days). Nutritional management requires age-appropriate rations: starter (20-22% protein), grower (17-18%), and ␀inisher (14-16%) feeds, ensuring freshness by avoiding mold and not storing beyond 3 months. Additional measures include weekly cypermethrin/deltamethrin sprays (1-2 ml/L) for ectoparasite control, maintaining Improved Housing Structure Mizoram Fisheries proper drainage, and providing immune boosters with cool baths to mitigate heat stress. Regular monitoring and these integrated practices will enhance productivity while preventing disease outbreaks in your piggery operations. CALENDAR OF OPERATION FOR REJUVENATION OF KHASI MANDARIN Trunk borer control - carefully clean infested holes with an iron wire before applying treatment either by inserting a cotton swab soaked in petrol or Dichlorvos, or by injecting 5 mL of 0.2% Dichlorvos solution (prepared at 2ml/L of water) and sealing the hole with mud to eﬀectively eliminate grubs. As spring arrives, continue proper nutrient management by applying the annual dose of 30 kg FYM per tree along with balanced chemical fertilizers (650 g urea, 1220 g SSP, and 450 g MOP per tree). Implement",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_192:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_192,4,"comprehensive plant protection measures including: application of Bordeaux paste on tree trunks up to 60cm height; foliar spraying of Multiplex (2.5g/L) on new leaves; a protective spray of Bavistin (1g/L) combined with Monocrotophos (1mL/L) on new ␀lushes; Micronutrient supplementation through foliar application of Zinc Sulphate (0.5%), Magnesium Sulphate (0.2%), Copper Sulphate (0.4%), and Manganese Sulphate (0.4%). For management of bark-eating caterpillars, inject 0.1% Dichlorvos directly into their tunnels. Complete these spring operations by mulching the basin area to conserve soil moisture and regulate soil temperature. Farmers are advised to prepare their ponds by maintaining a maximum depth of 1.75 meters, which is ideal for growing fry into healthy ␀ingerlings (10-15 cm). Begin by applying an initial dose of cow dung manure at 10,000 kg/ha, followed by regular applications of urea and superphosphate (40-80 kg/ha every 15 days) to promote plankton growth, while maintaining optimal water quality through lime application at 250 kg/ha. For stocking, introduce fry at a density of 1 lakh/ha using recommended polyculture ratios of either 1:2:2 or 3:4:3 for Catla, Rohu, and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_192:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_192,5,"Mrigal species, progressing to ␀ingerling stocking at 5,000-8,000/ha in a 30:30:40 ratio as the ␀ish mature. Farmers are advised to practice Happa breeding for common carp between June 1st and July 31st, and begin stocking of locally produced ␀ingerlings from the ␀irst week of July to ensure better survival rates and disease-free stock. For feeding, provide commercial pellets at 2% of body weight, or alternatively, use a nutritionally balanced 1:1 mixture of rice bran with either mustard oil cake or palm oil cake when pellets are unavailable. 177176",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
