ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_193:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_193,5,"Mrigal species, progressing to ␀ingerling stocking at 5,000-8,000/ha in a 30:30:40 ratio as the ␀ish mature. Farmers are advised to practice Happa breeding for common carp between June 1st and July 31st, and begin stocking of locally produced ␀ingerlings from the ␀irst week of July to ensure better survival rates and disease-free stock. For feeding, provide commercial pellets at 2% of body weight, or alternatively, use a nutritionally balanced 1:1 mixture of rice bran with either mustard oil cake or palm oil cake when pellets are unavailable. 177176",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_194:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_194,1,"Nagaland CEREAL CROPS Paddy Lowland Paddy: Prepare a nursery for kharif paddy on an area of 500-1000 sq. meters to raise seedlings for one hectare with a seed rate of 40 kg/ha. Use Farm Yard Manure (FYM) and Vermicompost in nursery beds for healthy seedling growth. Choose hybrids or high-yielding varieties that are tolerant or resistant to insect pests and diseases, such as Sahsharang, RC Maniphou-14, RC Maniphou-15, and RC Maniphou-16. Prepare the paddy ␀ield with 2-3 ploughings using a power tiller, incorporating 5t/ha of FYM. Transplant 20-25-day-old lowland rice seedlings by mid-June at a spacing of 20 x 15 cm. Ensure timely nursery sowing in May and transplanting in June for better grain quality, water ef␀iciency, and reduced stem borer buildup. For eﬀective weed management, conduct regular manual weeding operations as needed. Rogue out oﬀ-type plants during ␀lowering and at maturity, and remove plants aﬀected by disease. At least two manual weedings are required. Apply Azolla to enhance organic matter and supply nitrogen. To control zinc de␀iciency, apply 60 kg of zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21%) or 40 kg of zinc sulphate monohydrate (33%) per hectare during puddling,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_194:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_194,2,"especially if the previous crop in the ␀ield showed zinc de␀iciency symptoms. If de␀iciency is noticed in the growing crop, apply zinc sulphate as soon as possible. Upland Paddy: Treat seeds of direct-seeded upland rice with Carbendazim @ 2-3 g/kg of seed to protect against seed-borne diseases. Adopt the dibbling method of sowing instead of broadcasting to ensure assured germination and a uniform crop stand. Carry out at least two intercultural operations or manual weedings-␀irst at 25 days after sowing (DAS), ideally from mid-May, and second between the ␀irst week of June and the second week of July. Construct logwood or bamboo bunds across slopes and dig recharge pits (1x1x1 ft) in jhum ␀ields with slopes over 30% to reduce soil erosion and enhance water retention. Rogue out oﬀ-type and diseased plants during 179178 Nagaland Varietal demonstration in maize Fall Armyworm in maize the ␀lowering and maturity stages to maintain varietal purity and reduce disease spread. Pest and Disease Management of Paddy: Install yellow sticky traps, light traps, and pheromone traps in the ␀ield. For organic pest control, apply biopesticides like Trichogramma, conserve biocontrol agents (e.g.,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_194:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_194,3,"coccinellids, spiders, damsel ␀lies), and use Trichoderma harzianum with FYM before sowing. Spray neem oil at 10 DAT and Beauveria bassiana at boot leaf stage. For stem borer control carry out deep summer ploughing to expose the pupae to predators and disrupt the insect life cycle. Release Trichogramma spp. @ 50,000/ha one month after transplanting, followed by 3-4 releases at fortnightly intervals to parasitize stem borer egg masses. To control Gundhi bug, monitor and manually collect nymphs at the tillering stage using sweep nets. Install improved Indigenous Technical Knowledge (ITK)-based crab traps during the milky stage of paddy to reduce un␀illed grains. For blast disease management, ensure proper ␀ield sanitation and treat seeds with Pseudomonas ␀luorescens and Trichoderma viride @ 10 g/kg of seed. Upon disease onset, apply copper oxychloride 0.25% @ 2.5 g/L of water, repeating at 7-10 day intervals until the disease subsides. Maize Farmers are advised for 2-3 deep ploughings followed by sun drying of the ␀ield before the onset of rains to prepare for kharif maize cultivation. Use high- yielding composite varieties like Vijaya Composite, Vivek Sankul, RCM-1-1, RCM 1-3, RCM",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_194:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_194,4,"75, RCM 76, and DMRH 1301, or hybrid varieties like All Rounder, Vivek QPM, VLQPM 45, VLQPM 59, HQPM-1, HQPM-5, and HQPM-7. For short to medium maturity duration (85-110 days), especially suitable for re-sowing after hail damage, choose varieties like HQPM-1, HQPM-5, RCM-76, and Vivek 27. Sow maize @ 20-22 kg/ha with a spacing of 60 cm × 20 cm to achieve an ideal plant population of 60,000-65,000 plants/ha. Apply FYM or compost @ 5 t/ha and NPK @ 120:60:40 kg/ha. Apply nitrogen in three splits: at sowing, knee-high stage, and tasselling stage. Perform green manuring using Daincha, Sunhemp, or cowpea to improve soil fertility. Carry out earthing up twice (at 35-40 DAS and 60-65 DAS) to prevent lodging, and maintain a weed-free crop for the ␀irst 30-45 days. Ensure proper drainage during heavy rains to avoid waterlogging. Under drought conditions, irrigate at the knee-high, ␀lowering, and grain-␀illing stages",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
