ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_201:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_201,5,"ingredients. To prevent de␀iciency diseases, farmers should provide 40-50 grams of mineral supplements per day and ensure adequate water availability, especially during the lean season. Paddy by-products such as rice bran and straw can be used as alternative feed resources. Establishing an agroforestry system with fodder trees is recommended to avoid fodder scarcity. Regular deworming is essential to improve productivity. Administer Ivermectin injections to control ectoparasite infestations eﬀectively. Follow a proper vaccination schedule to prevent disease outbreaks. Mithuns should be vaccinated every six months against Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) to avoid signi␀icant economic losses. Implement rotational grazing in forest areas to optimize forage use and ensure sustainable land and fodder management. Farmers are also encouraged to adopt Mithun-based Integrated Farming Systems (IFS) to maximize resource utilization and improve pro␀itability. Additionally, milking mithuns for their highly nutritious milk and processing it into products like paneer, curd, and lassi can enhance income and promote value addition. 185184",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_202:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_202,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 During Shallow Water in Ponds Due to Insuf␀icient Rains/In␀low: De-silting, repair of bunds of existing ponds, rain water harvesting, liming and adopt low stocking density, deepening of ponds by 1.5 -2metres, restrict use of Manures and fertilizers, Channelizing water to pond if possible, Maintain proper water quality. Integrated farming, air breathing ␀ish to be practiced, avoid fertilization and manuring on supplementary basis, feeding should be minimum to avoid organic loading, short term aquaculture with medium and minor carps, Maintain proper water quality. Prepare pond for the next crop after early harvest, Maintain proper water quality Fishery At the Time of Salt Load Build up in Ponds / Change in Water Quality: Rain water harvesting, deepening, desilting of existing water bodies and removal of debris. Restrict feeding and manure to avoid waste accumulation and eutro␀ication. Odhisha Agro-advisory services are very crucial for Odisha state as the state is heavily reliant on agriculture and allied sectors. Moreover, due to its geographical location, Odisha is vulnerable to climate change like droughts, ␀loods, cyclones, hail storms, uncertain",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_202:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_202,2,"rainfalls etc. Agro-advisories can help timely management of diﬀerent agri- operations and thus, can protect agri-produces ensuring food security and farmers' livelihoods. CEREAL CROPS Drill seeded direct seeded rice (DSR) method may be adopted for which seeds may be sown during last week of May till onset of monsoon. For transplanted rice, timely sowing will result higher productivity. Rice nursery may be prepared with onset of monsoon using certi␀ied seeds. For medium to shallow lowland transplanted rice, varieties like Hasanta, CR 1009 sub-1, MTU 1075, CR Dhan 310, DRR 44, CR Dhan 801, CR Dhan 404, Upahar, Swarna, Pooja, Swarna sub-1 and BPT Rice Be updated with the regular weather advisory on thunderstorm associated with high rainfall and accordingly, take appropriate crop management practices for standing ␀ield and horticultural crops during pre-monsoon season. Take up summer ploughing with the receipt of summer rain. For transplanted kharif rice, dhaincha green manure seeds may be broadcast about 45-50 days before transplanting. Transplanting of vegetables should be done in the afternoon hour to avoid high temperature. Dry out the ␀ish ponds and plough down the pond bottom,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_202:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_202,3,"apply lime and sow dhaincha seeds for green manuring. It is the time for planting of root crops, tuber crops and rhizomes before onset of monsoon. Be aware of weather advisory and accordingly, avoid spraying plant protection chemicals during rainy days. Use protective covers while undertaking spraying of pesticides as safety measures. Adopt soil test-based fertilizer scheduling for improving nutrient use ef␀iciency and reducing cost therein. 187186",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
