ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_205:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_205,6,g Copper oxycloride+1 g Plantomycin per litre of water. 189188,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_206:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_206,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Raise the height of the pond dykes, repair the damaged dykes, if necessary and keep proper outlet to drain out excess water. Put net in the lower dyke or outlet to avoid escape of ␀ish from the pond. Test the water quality parameters mainly pH and alkalinity, and apply lime, fertilizers and manures consulting ␀ishery of␀icers, scientists and extension functionaries. In weed infested ponds, stock some grass carp yearlings (500 no/ha) along with Catla, Rohu and Mrigal to control weeds. Stock yearlings of Indian Major Carps @ 5000 per ha at a ratio of 1500 Catla, 2000 Rohu /Jayanti rohu and 1500 Mrigal at a ratio of 3:4:3 having 2 metres water depth. Adopt sample netting using cast net at every 2-months intervals to check the growth and health of ␀ish. Utilize the seasonal /shallow ponds in villages for ␀ish ␀ingerling production. Rise in water temperature expedites decomposition of organic matter which accumulates at the pond bottom and generates gases. These gases are toxic to the ␀ishes. To overcome the problem, zeolite @ 20 kg per acre should be applied after mixing it with one bag (30 kg) of dry river sand. Fishery supplement azolla @ 1-1.5 kg in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_206:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_206,2,"daily ration of cattle to reduce the feed cost by 20%. Provide supplementary feeding such as broken rice, paddy, cooked rice, azolla etc. to the backyard poultry birds during continuous rain. It is preferable to expose the feed ingredient sacks/bags under sun every week to prevent the feeds getting more moisture. Wash the cattle shed with phenyl (dilution 1:20 ratio with water) and sprinkle bleaching powder around the shed at weekly intervals. Mastitis is a common problem in high yielding cows in rainy season. Keep the cattle shed clean and dry. Clean the udder in soap water daily before milking. Apply Mastilep® ointment over the udder after each milking. Punjab Soil testing is the best tool to ensure optimum and balanced use of nutrients. Improper use of fertilizers leads not only to imbalanced nutrition but also deterioration of the environment. For collection of soil sample scrap away surface litter and make a V-shaped cut with a spade or a khurpa to a depth of 6 inches. Remove about 1"" thick uniform slice of soil from one side of the cut. Similarly, collect samples from 7 to 8 places in the ␀ield of uniform texture and uniform fertility. Put the samples in a clean bucket, tray",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_206:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_206,3,"or cloth and mix it thoroughly. Take approximately half kg of soil in a cloth bag and label it with information such as ␀ield number, name of the farmer, address, date of sampling etc. If the samples are wet, dry them in shade before putting into the cloth bag. Soil and water samples are tested by Soil Testing Laboratory, Deptt. of Soil Science, Punjab Agricultural University, Ludhiana and Soil Testing Laboratory of all KVK's. Punjab's agriculture is characterized by the cultivation of wheat and rice, which together dominate over 80% of the state's total cropped area. Other signi␀icant crops include sugarcane, maize, oilseeds, cotton, and various fruits and vegetables. The state has a high crop intensity, with many ␀ields being sown multiple times annually, contributing to its status as a major food producer in India. Punjab's agriculture faces several challenges, including monocropping, depletion of water resources, excessive use of pesticides and fertilizers, etc. These issues contribute to environmental degradation, economic stress for farmers, and ultimately impact crop production. There is upmost need to educate the farmers with agro-advisories regarding advanced techniques in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_206:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_206,4,"cultivation of ␀ield crops, vegetable & fruit crops, agroforestry and livestock management in order promote the scienti␀ic cultivation along with conservation of natural resources. The following agro-advisory highlights the important points to be followed by the farmers during kharif season to sustain the productivity of ␀ield crops, horticulture crops, agroforestry and livestock. SOIL TESTING 191190",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
