ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Use of farmyard manure (FYM) in kharif crops Rice Water management: Keep water standing in paddy ␀ield only for 2 weeks after transplanting and thereafter apply irrigation 2 days after the ponded water has in␀iltrated into soil. Zinc de␀iciency: Due to zinc de␀iciency the lower leaves of crop become rusty brown near the base and ultimately dry up. To control this malady, apply 25 kg of zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21%) or 16 kg zinc sulphate monohydrate (33%) per acre at puddling in case previous crop in this ␀ield had shown the symptoms of zinc de␀iciency. Basmati Rice Time of nursery sowing and transplanting: For Basmati varieties Punjab Basmati 7, Punjab Basmati 5, Pusa Basmati 1847, Pusa Basmati 1121 and Pusa Basmati 1718, Selection of varieties: To save water and for ease in management of paddy straw, grow PAU recommended short duration varieties. i.e. PR 132, PR 131, PR 130, PR 129, PR 128, HKR 47, PR 127, PR 126, PR 122, PR 121, PR 114, PR 113. CEREAL CROPS Time of nursery sowing: Restrict to timely sowing of nursery (20 May-20 June) and timely transplanting (20 June-10 July) schedule for better grain quality, water saving and low build-up of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,2,"stem borers. Farmyard manure (FYM) is a valuable resource for improving soil health and enhancing crop production, especially for kharif crops. FYM helps in improving soil structure and biomass, and it increases soil organic carbon, nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium, crucial nutrients for plant growth. It also enhances water-holding capacity and microbial activity, contributing to a healthier soil ecosystem. Apply farmyard manure (FYM) in adequate quantities to the soil ensures good tilth and improves soil water-holding capacity. Transplanting: Use 30-35 days old nursery for medium duration varieties and 25- 30 days nursery for short duration variety (PR 126). Transplant seedlings in lines at 20 x 15 cm (33 hills/sq m) and put 2 seedlings per hill. Fertilizer management: Apply fertilizers as per soil test. Omit phosphorus application in rice following wheat that received recommended dose of phosphatic fertilizer. Use nitrogen judiciously based on Leaf Colour Chart (LCC). To obtain higher yield of PR 132, apply 25% less nitrogenous fertilizers than other varieties Plant protection: To control false smut disease, initiate the spray of recommended fungicides at boot stage of the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,3,"crop. Plant hoppers feed at the base of rice plants and are often overlooked. Their damage is noticed only when the crop is hopper burnt. Hence, regular monitoring of the insect population is necessary. Use of synthetic pyrethroids leads to increase in the population of rice planthoppers. Hence, these insecticides should not be used for the control of rice insect-pests. Selection of varieties: Pusa Basmati 1121, Pusa Basmati 1509, Punjab Basmati 5, Punjab Basmati 7, Pusa Basmati 1718, Pusa Basmati 1847 and CSR 30 are the most suitable varieties. Punjab the optimum time of nursery sowing is 1st fortnight of June and transplanting time is 1␀␀ fortnight of July, whereas, for CSR 30 and Pusa Basmati 1509, the optimum time of nursery sowing is 2ⁿ␀ fortnight of June and transplanting time is 2nd fortnight of July. Seedling Treatment: To control Foot rot, smear the seeds with talc formulation of Trichoderma harzianum @ 15 g per kg of seed immediately before sowing and seedling root dip for 6 hrs with T. harzianum @ 15 g per litre of water before transplanting. Alternatively, treat the seed with Sprint 75 WS (carbendazim + mancozeb) by making slurry of 3 g fungicide formulation in 10 ml",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,4,"water for one kg seed before sowing to manage other seed borne diseases of rice. Method of Transplanting: Transplant two seedlings per hill in lines at 20 x 15 cm (33 hills/sq. metre) during the optimum period in a well puddled ␀ield. Suitable soils: Sow DSR only in medium to heavy textured soils. It cultivation is not successful in light textured soils due to severe iron de␀iciency and lower crop yields Pre-emergence: Spray 1.0 litre per acre Stomp/Bunker 30 EC (pendimethalin) or PEPE 25 SE (penoxsulam 1% pendimethlin 24%) in 200 litres of water for control of annual grass weeds and some broadleaf weeds. Direct seeding in tar-wattar ␀ields: Divide the ␀ield into kiyaras of desirable size after laser levelling and apply Rauni irrigation. When the ␀ield comes to tar-wattar (suf␀iciently high but workable soil moisture) conditions, prepare ␀ield kiyara-wise with shallow cultivation followed by 2-3 plankings with load of 3 sandbags on planker and sow immediately. Seed should be placed at 3-4 cm depth in 20 cm spaced rows. Avoid ␀ield preparation and sowing during noon hours for better results. Sowing time: Sowing should be done in the ␀irst fortnight of June for rice and second",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,5,"fortnight of June for basmati rice Seed rate and seed treatment: Use 8-10 kg seed per acre. Imbibe the seed by dipping in 2% potassium nitrate solution (prepare solution by dissolving 200 g KNO₃ in 10 litre water for 8 kg seed) for 12 hours. Dry the seed in shade and treat with 3 g Sprint 75 WS (mencozeb + carbendazim) per kg seed. Nutrition management: Skip phosphorus application if the recommended dose of phosphorus has been applied to the preceding wheat crop. However, in phosphorus de␀icient soils, apply 75 kg of superphosphate per acre before last puddling. Apply 45 kg/ha urea for CSR 30, 90 kg/ha urea for varieties Punjab Basmati 5, Punjab Basmati 7, Pusa Basmati 1718 and Pusa Basmati 1121, and 135 kg/ha urea for Pusa Basmati 1509. Apply urea in two equal splits at 3 weeks and 6 weeks after transplanting. Direct seeding in dry ␀ields: Treated seed should be placed 2-3 cm deep in rows spaced at 20 cm in a dry ␀ield and irrigation is applied immediately after sowing. Suitable varieties: Short and medium duration varieties of rice and Punjab Basmati 7, Pusa Basmati 1718, Pusa Basmati 1121 and Pusa Basmati 1509 for basmati Weed Control Post-emergence: If ␀ields are infested with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_208:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_208,6,"Swank, paddy mothas, Nominee Gold 10 SC (bispyribac sodium) @ 100 ml per acre should be sprayed at 15-25 days after Direct Seeded Rice 193192",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
