ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Selection of varieties: To obtain higher yield, grow Bt cotton variety PAU Bt 2 and PAU Bt 3 and other Bt hybrids recommended by PAU, Ludhiana. Among the non Bt hybrids/varieties, grow F 2228, LH 2108 and desi cotton varieties LD 1019, LD 949 and FDK 124. Pre-sowing irrigation: Apply heavy pre-sowing irrigation preferably with canal water for good germination and early crop establishment. COMMERCIAL CROPS Sub Soiling: Cross sub soiling at 1.0 m spacing should be done before preparing the ␀ield with tractor drawn sub-soiler (chiseler) to the depth of 45-50 cm. This will help in breaking the hard pan, increasing water in␀iltration rate and better root development of cotton plants. Seed rate: For Bt varieties PAU Bt 2 and PAU Bt 3, use seed rate @ 4.0 + 1.0 (refuge) kg/acre, for Non-Bt varieties F 2228 and LH 2108, 3.5 kg/acre and for recommended Bt hybrids, use two pouches of 475 g each (in which refuge Already mixed in seed) Cotton Seed treatment: Soak the cotton seed in a solution of 0.5 g succinic acid in 5 litres of water for 2-4 hours for acid delinted seed or 6-8 hours for non-delinted seed. To prevent attach of jassid at early stage, smear the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,2,"seed with 5 g Gaucho 70 WS (imidacloprid) or 7 g Cruiser 30FS (thiomethoxam) per kg seed. To remove the fuzz of non-delinted seed, rub these seeds with ␀ine earth, cow-dung or ash. Time of Sowing: Sow the crop during 1 April to 15 May. Sowing during this period ensures better yield and escapes the attack of insect pests and diseases. Planting geometry: Sow the seeds with cotton sowing drill or cotton planter with line to line spacing of 67.5 cm. Maintain plant to plant distance of 30 cm for variety PAU Bt 2 and PAU Bt 3; 45 cm for desi cotton varieties; 60 cm for non-Bt hybrid/varieties and 75 cm for Bt hybrids by thinning out extra plants after ␀irst irrigation. Weed management: Hoe the crop two or three times. The ␀irst hoeing should be done before ␀irst irrigation. For control of weeds particularly itsit, madhana/ makra, apply 1.0 litre per acre Stomp 30 EC (pendimethalin) as pre-emergence within 24 hours of sowing. In situations where weeds emerge after ␀irst irrigation or with the rain shower, Stomp 30 EC can also be applied as post-emergence after ␀irst irrigation in 200 litre of water. Alternatively, spray 500 ml per acre Hitweed Maxx 10 MEC (pyrithiobac sodium 6% quizalofop",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,3,"ethyl 4%) by dissolving in 150 litres of water after ␀irst irrigation, in moist soil, to control annual grass and broadleaf weeds. This herbicide also provides eﬀective control of lapeta (guara) vel (Ipomoea sp.) when weed plants are at 2 to 5 leaf stage. Fertilizer Application: Apply urea @162.5 kg to non-Bt varieties, 200 kg to Bt variety (PAU Bt 2 and PAU Bt 3) and 225 kg to all Bt and non-Bt hybrids, DAP @ 67.5 kg or SSP @187.5 kg per ha. Omit phosphorus (DAP or SSP) application to cotton when it follows wheat which had received recommended dose of phosphorus. Reduce the dose of urea by 25 kg when 67.5 kg DAP is applied to cotton. Apply 50 kg muriate of potash and 25 kg zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21%) or 16.25 kg zinc Punjab Sugarcane can be successfully grown on all types of soils ranging from sandy loam to clay loam and it is semi-tolerant to sodicity and salinity. Cross sub-soiling at 1.0 m spacing should be done once in three to four years, before preparing the ␀ield. This will help in breaking the hard pan, increase water in␀iltration rate and better penetration of roots. Time of sowing: Mid-February to the end of March is the optimum time for planting sugarcane in the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,4,"Punjab. Do not plant early maturing varieties after March. Do not plant the crop in a ␀ield where the preceding crop was infected with red rot or wilt. sulphate monohydrate (33%) per ha to cotton in light soils. Apply 62.5 kg/ha of magnesium sulphate. Apply full dose of phosphorus, magnesium sulphate, muriate of potash and zinc sulphate at sowing. Apply urea in two splits at thinning and the appearance of ␀lowers. Foliar application of nutrients: To get higher yields, give 4 sprays of 2% potassium nitrate (13:0:45) at weekly interval starting at ␀lower initiation. Irrigation and Drainage: The ␀irst irrigation should be given 4 to 6 weeks after sowing and the subsequent ones at interval of two or three weeks. The crop must not be allowed to suﬀer from water stress during the ␀lowering and fruiting stages. Cotton during its early growth is very sensitive to water stagnation. Sugarcane Selection of varieties: Grow PAU recommended varieties i.e., early maturing-CoPb 95, CoPb 96, Co 15023, CoPb 92, Co 118, CoJ 85, CoJ 64, mid-late maturing- CoPb 98, CoPb 93, CoPb 94, Co 238, CoPb 91, CoJ 88. Seed treatment: To improve the germination, soak the setts in ethrel solution overnight. To",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,5,"prepare the solution, dissolve 25 ml of Ethrel 39 SL in 100 liters of water. Alternatively, soak the setts in water for 24 hours before planting C h e m i c a l C o n t r o l : P re - e m e rg e n c e a p p l i c a t i o n o f 8 0 0 g p e r a c re Atrataf/Solaro/Masstaf/ Markazine 50 WP (atrazine) or Sencor 70 WP (metribuzin) or Karmex/Klass 80 WP (diuron) or 1000 g per acre Authority NXT 58 WP (sulfentrazone+clomazone) in 200 litres of water within 2-3 days of planting eﬀectively controls the broadleaf weeds and annual grasses. For control of hardy weed like Bans Patta, use only Sencor 70 WP or Karmex/Klass 80 WP. Alternatively, post-emergence application of 1200 g per acre Triskele/Trishuk(2,4-D sodium salt 44% + metribuzin 35% + pyrazosulfuron ethyl 1.0%) WDG or 1000 g per acre Sindica (2,4- D sodium salt 48% + metribuzin 32% + chlorimuron ethyl 0.8%) WDG in 200 litres of water at 3-5 leaf stage of weeds provides eﬀective control of seasonal grass, sedge and broad leaf weeds. For ␀ields infested with dila, post-emergence application of 800 g per acre 2, 4-D sodium salt 80 WP in 200 litres of water is recommended. In Selection of seed and Seed rate: The seed should be free from",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_212:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_212,6,"red-rot, wilt, smut, ratoon-stunting and grassy shoot diseases. Use 20 thousand three-budded setts or 15 thousand four-budded sets or 12 thousand ␀ive-budded setts per acre. Use only the top two-third portion of the selected canes for planting. Weed management: Two or three hoeings can be done with a triphali or tractor mounted tiller or tractor operated rotary weeder. 197196",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
