ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_215:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_215,5,"stay in direct contact with the tree trunk. Avoid deep hoeing. Avoid injuries to the trunk bark and roots. Give two applications of Curzate M 8 as paint (2 g/100 ml of Linseed oil) to the infected trunk portion and drench (25 g/10 litres of water/ tree) the soil at the base of the tree in July-August. During last week of June to August, apply three sprays of Bordeaux mixture (2:2:250) or 50 % Copper oxychloride (3 g per litre of water) at 20 days interval to manage scab which appears as small, dark brown, rough, irregular, raised lesions mostly on under- side of the leaves, do clipping of infected leaves in July Give light and frequent irrigations in May-June and avoid water stress to combat problem of fruit cracking. Fruit Fly in Guava Anthracnose in Guava 199198",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_216:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_216,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 / litre of water) or naphthalene acetic acid (NAA) @ 600 mg/litre during May, when maximum ␀lowers have opened. Withhold irrigation during May and apply fertilizers during June to encourage growth in July-August for getting maximum ␀lowering during August-September for winter season crop. Manage fruit ␀lies by covering the rainy season mature green guava fruit on tree with white non-woven bags at the end of June to middle of July. Regularly remove fallen fruits from the ground and bury the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the ␀irst week of July and recharge the same if required. To manage Fruit rot/ Anthracnose and dieback, rain or irrigation water should not be allowed to stand in the basin around the tree. After pruning, spray the trees with Bordeaux mixture (2:2: 250) or 300 g Blitox in 100 litres of water. The rotten and mummi␀ied fruits which fall on the ground should be buried deep into the soil. Two foliar sprays of 2.0 % potassium nitrate (2 kg/ 100 litres of water) during August and September improve fruit size and increase yield. In pear, Zinc de␀iciency appears on younger leaves as diﬀused",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_216:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_216,2,"interveinal chlorosis, reduction in leaf size and tendency of the leaf edges to curl upward. To correct its de␀iciency, spray the plants with 3 kg zinc sulphate + 1.5 kg unslaked lime in 500 litres of water per acre. Iron de␀iciency, which appears on apical leaves as interveinal chlorosis may be corrected by spraying 0.3 per cent ferrous sulphate (300 g in 100 litres of water). Pear trees need frequent irrigation after transplanting. The interval of irrigation may be 5 to 7 days during summer months and 15 days in July-August. Irrigation should be restricted after fruit harvest. Management of fruit ␀lies involves regular removal of fallen fruits from the ground and burying the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the ␀irst week of June and recharge the same if required. Mango Litchi Litchi should be carefully irrigated at all stages of development. Irrigate young plants twice a week during May-June. In bearing trees, irrigation need is critical during fruit A spray of 10 g sodium salt 2, 4-D in 500 litres of water in the ␀irst week of May controls the pre-harvest fruit drop in Dusehri and Langra cultivars. 2, 4-D should be dissolved in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_216:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_216,3,"a small quantity of alcohol or spirit and then the required volume of water be added. It must be ensured that the spray pump is washed thoroughly with washing soda before and after the spray. Do not repeat the spray of the 2, 4-D solution. To manage fruit ␀lies, regularly remove fallen fruits from the ground and bury the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the third week of May and recharge the same if required. Pear Iron de␀iciency in Pear Punjab development which occurs from the second week of May to the end of June. Twice a week irrigation during this period reduces cracking of fruits to a great extent and helps in proper size development. After the withdrawal of monsoon young orchards should be irrigated at weekly/ fortnightly intervals from September onwards. The bagging of litchi fruit bunches with white and pink polypropylene non-woven bags at 25-30 days after fruit set provide physical protection against fruit nut borer, sun burning, cracking and also improves pericarp color and fruit quality. To manage litchi nut borer follow clean cultivation by removing fallen fruits (mummies) from the orchard and ploughing destroys the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_216:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_216,4,"carry-over of pests to the next crop. Peach Ber Cucurbits (Pumpkin, Bottle Gourd, Bitter Gourd, Sponge Gourd, Ash Gourd, Round Gourd) In peach, fruit development period starts after fruit set and continues upto June till maturity depending upon the variety. This is the critical period of irrigation for the trees. Trees should not suﬀer from any moisture stress particularly 25-30 days before maturity of fruit, because the maximum weight gain is during these days. Correct iron de␀iciency by spraying ferrous sulphate @ 0.3 per cent (3g/litre of water) in June and August. To manage fruit ␀ly infestation, ␀ix PAU fruit ␀ly trap @ 16 traps/acre in May. VEGETABLE CROPS For cucurbits, sow pumpkin in June-July on 2-2.5 m wide beds with 60 cm spacing, using a seed rate of 1.0-1.5 kg/acre, while Bottle Gourd, Bitter Gourd, Sponge Gourd, Ash Gourd, and Round Gourd should also be sown in June-July on 1.5-3 m wide beds with 45-90 cm spacing and a seed rate of 2.0 kg/acre. Apply 8-15 tonnes of FYM per acre; for pumpkin, add 40 kg N (90 kg Urea) in two splits, and for the others, use 28- 40 kg N (60-90 kg Urea), 20 kg P␀O␀ (125 kg SSP), and 20 kg K␀O (35 kg MOP) per acre, with N applied in two",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_216:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_216,5,"splits. Recommended varieties include Punjab Nawab, Prune ber trees during second fortnight of May when the trees are dormant. Pruning by heading back to 8 buds of previous year's growth gives higher yield of better quality fruits. To fully grown ber plants, apply farmyard manure @ 100 kg/tree in May-June. Urea @ 1.0 kg/plant may be split up in two parts-one part to be applied during the rainy season in July-August and the other soon after the fruit set. Litchi Nut Borer 201200",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_217:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_217,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 / litre of water) or naphthalene acetic acid (NAA) @ 600 mg/litre during May, when maximum ␀lowers have opened. Withhold irrigation during May and apply fertilizers during June to encourage growth in July-August for getting maximum ␀lowering during August-September for winter season crop. Manage fruit ␀lies by covering the rainy season mature green guava fruit on tree with white non-woven bags at the end of June to middle of July. Regularly remove fallen fruits from the ground and bury the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the ␀irst week of July and recharge the same if required. To manage Fruit rot/ Anthracnose and dieback, rain or irrigation water should not be allowed to stand in the basin around the tree. After pruning, spray the trees with Bordeaux mixture (2:2: 250) or 300 g Blitox in 100 litres of water. The rotten and mummi␀ied fruits which fall on the ground should be buried deep into the soil. Two foliar sprays of 2.0 % potassium nitrate (2 kg/ 100 litres of water) during August and September improve fruit size and increase yield. In pear, Zinc de␀iciency appears on younger leaves as diﬀused",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_217:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_217,2,"interveinal chlorosis, reduction in leaf size and tendency of the leaf edges to curl upward. To correct its de␀iciency, spray the plants with 3 kg zinc sulphate + 1.5 kg unslaked lime in 500 litres of water per acre. Iron de␀iciency, which appears on apical leaves as interveinal chlorosis may be corrected by spraying 0.3 per cent ferrous sulphate (300 g in 100 litres of water). Pear trees need frequent irrigation after transplanting. The interval of irrigation may be 5 to 7 days during summer months and 15 days in July-August. Irrigation should be restricted after fruit harvest. Management of fruit ␀lies involves regular removal of fallen fruits from the ground and burying the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the ␀irst week of June and recharge the same if required. Mango Litchi Litchi should be carefully irrigated at all stages of development. Irrigate young plants twice a week during May-June. In bearing trees, irrigation need is critical during fruit A spray of 10 g sodium salt 2, 4-D in 500 litres of water in the ␀irst week of May controls the pre-harvest fruit drop in Dusehri and Langra cultivars. 2, 4-D should be dissolved in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_217:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_217,3,"a small quantity of alcohol or spirit and then the required volume of water be added. It must be ensured that the spray pump is washed thoroughly with washing soda before and after the spray. Do not repeat the spray of the 2, 4-D solution. To manage fruit ␀lies, regularly remove fallen fruits from the ground and bury the infested fruits at least at 60 cm depth. Fix PAU fruit ␀ly traps @16 traps/acre in the third week of May and recharge the same if required. Pear Iron de␀iciency in Pear Punjab development which occurs from the second week of May to the end of June. Twice a week irrigation during this period reduces cracking of fruits to a great extent and helps in proper size development. After the withdrawal of monsoon young orchards should be irrigated at weekly/ fortnightly intervals from September onwards. The bagging of litchi fruit bunches with white and pink polypropylene non-woven bags at 25-30 days after fruit set provide physical protection against fruit nut borer, sun burning, cracking and also improves pericarp color and fruit quality. To manage litchi nut borer follow clean cultivation by removing fallen fruits (mummies) from the orchard and ploughing destroys the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
