ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_218:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_218,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Cowpea Okra (Bhindi) Okra should be sown in the North Indian plains as a rainy season crop in June-July, using varieties like Punjab Suhawani, Punjab-8, Pusa Kranti, Varsha Uphar, or A-4 at a seed rate of 4-6 kg/acre with a spacing of 45 × 15 cm. To control jassid and white␀ly, apply 1-2 sprays of Ecotin (Azadirachtin 5%) at 80 ml or PAU Neem extract at 2000 ml in 100-125 litres of water per acre. During the rainy season, when jassid attacks are severe, use chemical control with 40 g Actara 25 WG, 560 ml Malathion 50 EC, or 40 ml Con␀idor 17.8 SL in 100-125 litres of water per acre. Manage spotted bollworms by spraying Coragen 18.5 SC (Chlorantraniliprole) or Sumipleo 10 EC (Pyridalyl) at 50 ml in 100-125 litres of water per acre. Red spider mites, a serious issue during dry, hot summer weather, can be controlled with PAU Dharek extract at 1600 ml in 100 litres of water per acre or with 150 ml Oberon 22.9 SC in 100 litres of water per acre. Monitor for Yellow Mosaic Virus (YMV), rogue out aﬀected plants, and spray Thiomethoxam 25WG at 60 g/acre to control its vector, white␀ly. PPH-1, and PPH-2 for pumpkin; Punjab Bahar, Punjab Barkat, and Punjab Komal",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_218:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_218,2,"for Bottle Gourd; Punjab Karela-15 and Punjab Jhaar Karela-1 for Bitter Gourd; Punjab Nikhar and PSG-9 for Sponge Gourd; PAG-3 for Ash Gourd; and Punjab Tinda-1 for Round Gourd. Irrigate every 6-7 days in summer, totalling 8-10 irrigations, but reduce frequency before harvest to prevent fruit rot. For fruit ␀ly management, install 16 traps per acre in the 3␀␀-4␀␀ week of April for spring crops and the 4th week of June for rainy season crops, or use a bait spray of Malathion 50 EC at 20 ml plus 200 g Gur in 20 L water at 15-day intervals on the lower side of maize plants grown as a trap crop in rows 8-10 m apart. Manage fungal diseases with a mixture of Bavistin 1 g and Mancozeb 2 g per litre of water, and control sucking pests with Imidacloprid at 0.5 ml per litre. Additionally, control white␀ly using 1200 ml of PAU Neem extract in 100-125 litres of water per acre, as recommended by Punjab Agricultural University. For cauli␀lower, sow the nursery in May for the Kharif season and transplant by mid- June using early group cultivars like Pusa Deepali, Pusa Kartiki, and Pant Gobhi-3 with a spacing of 45 × 30 cm and only use early group cultivars avoid physiological disorders for Kharif",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_218:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_218,3,"season to like buttoning. Apply 10-15 tonnes of FYM, 50 kg N (110 kg Urea), 25 kg P₂O₅ (155 kg SSP), and 25 kg K₂O (40 kg MOP) per acre, with full P₂O₅, K₂O, and 1/3 N at sowing, and the remaining N as top-dressing four weeks after transplanting. Irrigate every 6-7 days, totalling 9-11 irrigations, while avoiding over- ␀looding. Add Borax at 8 kg/acre to manage browning in cauli␀lower. To manage leaf spot, blight, and downy mildew, spray Mancozeb at 0.2% or Copper Oxychloride at 0.3%. Control stem borer and fruit borer with Spinosad 45 SC at 80 ml/acre in 200 litres of water, ensuring a waiting period of 5-7 days before harvesting. Cauli␀lower Sow cowpea as a rainy season crop in June-July using the variety Cowpea 263 with a spacing of 45 × 15 cm, applying 45 kg Urea, 100 kg SSP, and 16 kg MOP per acre at sowing, along with seed inoculation using Bavistin and Rhizobium culture. Control sucking pests like aphids and white␀ly with alternate sprays of Neem-based pesticide 1500 ppm at 600 ml/acre and Imidacloprid 17.8 at 70 ml/acre. Manage fungal diseases by treating seeds with Carbendazim at 0.2%, Thiram at 0.3%, or Captan at 0.3%. Punjab AGROFORESTRY Poplar Irrigate poplar at",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_218:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_218,4,"7-10-day interval during summers as it requires a lot of water during its growth period from April to October. However, standing water for long period, especially in heavy soils, is harmful for Poplar, therefore proper arrangement for drainage must be ensured during monsoon. Apply urea to plants according to their age: 170 g for 1-year-old, 260 g for 2-year-old, 350 g for 3-year-old, 430 g for 4-year-old, 520 g for 5-year-old, and 610 g for 6-year-old plants. Distribute the total yearly dose evenly, applying one-third in May, one-third in July, and the ␀inal third in September. For 1- year-old plants, apply in a 1 m diameter ring; for 2-year-old plants, in a 2 m diameter ring; and for 3-year-old plants, in a 3 m wide strip (1.5 m on each side of the tree row). Adjust the dose by reducing 25% in high nitrogen (N) soils and increasing 25% in low N soils. For management of Zinc de␀iciency in Poplar, apply 100 g, 200 g and 300g Zinc Sulphate Heptahydrate (21%) OR 60g, 1 2 0 g a n d 1 8 0 g Z i n c S u l p h a t e Monohydrate (33%) for 1␀␀, 3␀␀, & 5␀␀ year of poplar, respectively, in 1 m diameter during 1␀␀ year, 2 m diameter ring around tree during 3␀␀ year and 3 m wide strip during",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_218:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_218,5,"5␀␀ year, after harvesting of the Rabi intercrop. Mechanical removal of weeds or intercultural operations with tractor drawn implements can be followed to keep the ␀ield weed free. Avoid the spray of herbicides such as Atrazine, Metribuzin, Diuron, 2,4-D, recommended for control of broadleaved weeds in inter-crops like sugarcane & maize, as these may result in mortality of poplar. Poplar Stem Borer damages the tree by making tunnel in the stem and branches, and hollows out the trees. Prune the infected branches in August- September before entry of larvae into main stem. Plug all the holes on trunk with wet clay, except the lowermost hole. Inject kerosene in this lowermost hole and then plug it with wet clay. Leaf spots in poplar generally appear after onset of monsoons, and result in blight like appearance and early leaf fall, thus aﬀecting the growth of poplar. This can be managed by 3-4 sprays of Bordeaux mixture (0.8%) at 15 days interval. During Kharif season, except Paddy, crops like Maize, Sorghum, Bajra, Cowpea, Moong, Mash, Mentha, Arvi, etc., can be successfully cultivated as intercrops during the ␀irst three years of plantation. Avoid pruning of poplar trees during rainy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
