ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_219:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_219,2,"for Bottle Gourd; Punjab Karela-15 and Punjab Jhaar Karela-1 for Bitter Gourd; Punjab Nikhar and PSG-9 for Sponge Gourd; PAG-3 for Ash Gourd; and Punjab Tinda-1 for Round Gourd. Irrigate every 6-7 days in summer, totalling 8-10 irrigations, but reduce frequency before harvest to prevent fruit rot. For fruit ␀ly management, install 16 traps per acre in the 3␀␀-4␀␀ week of April for spring crops and the 4th week of June for rainy season crops, or use a bait spray of Malathion 50 EC at 20 ml plus 200 g Gur in 20 L water at 15-day intervals on the lower side of maize plants grown as a trap crop in rows 8-10 m apart. Manage fungal diseases with a mixture of Bavistin 1 g and Mancozeb 2 g per litre of water, and control sucking pests with Imidacloprid at 0.5 ml per litre. Additionally, control white␀ly using 1200 ml of PAU Neem extract in 100-125 litres of water per acre, as recommended by Punjab Agricultural University. For cauli␀lower, sow the nursery in May for the Kharif season and transplant by mid- June using early group cultivars like Pusa Deepali, Pusa Kartiki, and Pant Gobhi-3 with a spacing of 45 × 30 cm and only use early group cultivars avoid physiological disorders for Kharif",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_219:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_219,3,"season to like buttoning. Apply 10-15 tonnes of FYM, 50 kg N (110 kg Urea), 25 kg P₂O₅ (155 kg SSP), and 25 kg K₂O (40 kg MOP) per acre, with full P₂O₅, K₂O, and 1/3 N at sowing, and the remaining N as top-dressing four weeks after transplanting. Irrigate every 6-7 days, totalling 9-11 irrigations, while avoiding over- ␀looding. Add Borax at 8 kg/acre to manage browning in cauli␀lower. To manage leaf spot, blight, and downy mildew, spray Mancozeb at 0.2% or Copper Oxychloride at 0.3%. Control stem borer and fruit borer with Spinosad 45 SC at 80 ml/acre in 200 litres of water, ensuring a waiting period of 5-7 days before harvesting. Cauli␀lower Sow cowpea as a rainy season crop in June-July using the variety Cowpea 263 with a spacing of 45 × 15 cm, applying 45 kg Urea, 100 kg SSP, and 16 kg MOP per acre at sowing, along with seed inoculation using Bavistin and Rhizobium culture. Control sucking pests like aphids and white␀ly with alternate sprays of Neem-based pesticide 1500 ppm at 600 ml/acre and Imidacloprid 17.8 at 70 ml/acre. Manage fungal diseases by treating seeds with Carbendazim at 0.2%, Thiram at 0.3%, or Captan at 0.3%. Punjab AGROFORESTRY Poplar Irrigate poplar at",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_219:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_219,4,"7-10-day interval during summers as it requires a lot of water during its growth period from April to October. However, standing water for long period, especially in heavy soils, is harmful for Poplar, therefore proper arrangement for drainage must be ensured during monsoon. Apply urea to plants according to their age: 170 g for 1-year-old, 260 g for 2-year-old, 350 g for 3-year-old, 430 g for 4-year-old, 520 g for 5-year-old, and 610 g for 6-year-old plants. Distribute the total yearly dose evenly, applying one-third in May, one-third in July, and the ␀inal third in September. For 1- year-old plants, apply in a 1 m diameter ring; for 2-year-old plants, in a 2 m diameter ring; and for 3-year-old plants, in a 3 m wide strip (1.5 m on each side of the tree row). Adjust the dose by reducing 25% in high nitrogen (N) soils and increasing 25% in low N soils. For management of Zinc de␀iciency in Poplar, apply 100 g, 200 g and 300g Zinc Sulphate Heptahydrate (21%) OR 60g, 1 2 0 g a n d 1 8 0 g Z i n c S u l p h a t e Monohydrate (33%) for 1␀␀, 3␀␀, & 5␀␀ year of poplar, respectively, in 1 m diameter during 1␀␀ year, 2 m diameter ring around tree during 3␀␀ year and 3 m wide strip during",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_219:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_219,5,"5␀␀ year, after harvesting of the Rabi intercrop. Mechanical removal of weeds or intercultural operations with tractor drawn implements can be followed to keep the ␀ield weed free. Avoid the spray of herbicides such as Atrazine, Metribuzin, Diuron, 2,4-D, recommended for control of broadleaved weeds in inter-crops like sugarcane & maize, as these may result in mortality of poplar. Poplar Stem Borer damages the tree by making tunnel in the stem and branches, and hollows out the trees. Prune the infected branches in August- September before entry of larvae into main stem. Plug all the holes on trunk with wet clay, except the lowermost hole. Inject kerosene in this lowermost hole and then plug it with wet clay. Leaf spots in poplar generally appear after onset of monsoons, and result in blight like appearance and early leaf fall, thus aﬀecting the growth of poplar. This can be managed by 3-4 sprays of Bordeaux mixture (0.8%) at 15 days interval. During Kharif season, except Paddy, crops like Maize, Sorghum, Bajra, Cowpea, Moong, Mash, Mentha, Arvi, etc., can be successfully cultivated as intercrops during the ␀irst three years of plantation. Avoid pruning of poplar trees during rainy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_219:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_219,6,season as this is the Zinc de␀iency in Poplar Zinc de␀iency in Poplar Leaf spots in poplar 203202,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_220:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_220,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Apply the fertilizers in 1 m diameter ring around the tree during 1␀␀ and 2ⁿ␀ year. From 3rd to 6th year, the fertilizers should be applied in 2 m diameter ring around the tree. Whole SSP and MOP should be applied in April, however Apply Urea in three equal doses (␀⁄␀ of the mentioned dose in April, ␀⁄␀ in July and remaining ␀⁄␀ in October). Eucalyptus Gall Wasp attack results in formation of galls on leaf midrib, petioles and stems, multiple shoot formation and reduction in leaf size. For its management, neem oil or castor oil @ 30 ml/litre of water can be sprayed. The number and dimensions of compartments may vary based on machine speci␀ications. Fill soil in the frames uniformly up to the top surface. The soil is lifted from both sides of the frames by making shallow furrows/channels. Care must be taken at the time of sowing that there are no hard stones in the soil, which is ␀illed in the frame. Spread 50-60 g of pre-germinated seeds evenly in each compartment to ensure a uniform density of 2 or 3 seeds/cm² in the mat. To ensure uniform seed distribution, use nursery sowing seeder and its length should match the frame width with 1 cm diameter",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_220:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_220,2,"opening along the full length of the roller. Approximately 10-12 kg of paddy seed is enough to sow around 150 growth period of poplar and there are chances of fungal infection if the cut is not made properly. Pruning should be done during winter season, after shedding of the leaves. AGRI-ENGINEERING Eucalyptus For successful mechanical paddy transplantation, a mat-type nursery is essential. The following points should be kept in mind by the farmers while raising mat type nursery in their ␀ields. Choose a nursery location with assured irrigation for optimal growth and close to the transplanting ␀ield to minimize transport. Ensure that the soil of mat type paddy nursery location should be fertile. The ␀ield should be preferably laser levelled and 20 m away from tubewell and trees. It is better to mix farmyard manure before harrowing the ␀ields. Prepare the ␀ields at proper moisture. Spread 50-60-gauge polythene sheet of 90 cm wide with 1.0-2.0 mm diameter perforations over it. Polythene sheet weighing 270 g, about 15 meters long, is enough to prepare seedlings for around 150 mats required per acre. Place iron frames with compartments measuring 58*28*2 cm for self-propelled paddy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_220:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_220,3,"transplanters and 45x21x2 cm for engine-operated paddy transplanters. Eucalyptus can be planted during August-September or February-March. Plant the trees at a spacing of 4x2 m or 3x3 m for block plantation and 2-3 m for boundary plantation. Eucalyptus requires frequent but light irrigation during ␀irst year for better establishment. Irrigate the eucalyptus trees 2-3 times per month during summers, up to ␀irst three years. Flooding should be avoided as it may result in uprooting of plants during strong winds. Apply Urea, SSP, and MOP fertilizers to plants according to their growth year: 65 g of Urea, 120 g of SSP, and 35 g of MOP for the 1st year; 130 g of Urea, 250 g of SSP, and 65 g of MOP for the 2ⁿ␀ year; 200 g of Urea, 375 g of SSP, and 100 g of MOP for the 3␀␀ year; 260 g of Urea, 500 g of SSP, and 135 g of MOP for the 4th year; 325 g of Urea, 625 g of SSP, and 165 g of MOP for the 5␀␀ year; and 390 g of Urea, 750 g of SSP, and 200 g of MOP for the 6␀␀ year. Apply MOP only if there is a de␀iciency of Potash in the soil. Punjab mats needed for transplanting one acre. Gently cover the seeds with thin layer of soil and sprinkle water with sprayer to ensure proper soil settling.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_220:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_220,4,"Lift frames and put at next place. Repeat the above steps for, as many mats required. Two persons can sow seedlings for about 3-4 acres in a day. The uprooted mats are transported to the ␀ield for transplanting. In order to mechanize the sowing operation of raising mat type nursery, PAU Ludhiana has developed a tractor operated seeder for mat type paddy nursery. This machine lays a After sowing, slowly ␀lood the ␀ield to prevent seeds from being washed away. Ensure that the seedling mats remain consistently moist. Spray the paddy seedlings at the rate of 200 g urea dissolved in 15 litres of water per 150 mats in the irrigated ␀ield after 10 days of sowing. The seedling mats are ready after about 20-25 days of sowing. Drain the water completely from the ␀ield a few hours before the nursery uprooting. Iron de␀iciency problem in paddy nursery can be tackled using two sprays of 0.5% ferrous sulphate at one week interval. This de␀iciency can also be controlled by keeping standing water in paddy nursery. Completely drain the water from the ␀ield a few hours before uprooting the nursery. The seedling mats are uprooted by a cut with sharp edge blade/sickle along the boundaries of the mat.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_220:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_220,5,"One person can uproot the mats required for transplanting about 5-6 acres per day. Manual cutting of paddy nurseries requires to adopt awkward postures leading to physical strain and fatigue among farmers. To address these challenges, PAU nursery cutter having cutting capacity of 325-425 mats per hour with uniform cutting can be used. Sowing of mat type nursery with PAU tractor operated mat type nursery seeder Germinated mat type nursery sown with tractor operated mat type nursery seeder Manually raising of mat type nursery at farmers' ␀ield 205204",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
