ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_221:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_221,2,"opening along the full length of the roller. Approximately 10-12 kg of paddy seed is enough to sow around 150 growth period of poplar and there are chances of fungal infection if the cut is not made properly. Pruning should be done during winter season, after shedding of the leaves. AGRI-ENGINEERING Eucalyptus For successful mechanical paddy transplantation, a mat-type nursery is essential. The following points should be kept in mind by the farmers while raising mat type nursery in their ␀ields. Choose a nursery location with assured irrigation for optimal growth and close to the transplanting ␀ield to minimize transport. Ensure that the soil of mat type paddy nursery location should be fertile. The ␀ield should be preferably laser levelled and 20 m away from tubewell and trees. It is better to mix farmyard manure before harrowing the ␀ields. Prepare the ␀ields at proper moisture. Spread 50-60-gauge polythene sheet of 90 cm wide with 1.0-2.0 mm diameter perforations over it. Polythene sheet weighing 270 g, about 15 meters long, is enough to prepare seedlings for around 150 mats required per acre. Place iron frames with compartments measuring 58*28*2 cm for self-propelled paddy",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_221:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_221,3,"transplanters and 45x21x2 cm for engine-operated paddy transplanters. Eucalyptus can be planted during August-September or February-March. Plant the trees at a spacing of 4x2 m or 3x3 m for block plantation and 2-3 m for boundary plantation. Eucalyptus requires frequent but light irrigation during ␀irst year for better establishment. Irrigate the eucalyptus trees 2-3 times per month during summers, up to ␀irst three years. Flooding should be avoided as it may result in uprooting of plants during strong winds. Apply Urea, SSP, and MOP fertilizers to plants according to their growth year: 65 g of Urea, 120 g of SSP, and 35 g of MOP for the 1st year; 130 g of Urea, 250 g of SSP, and 65 g of MOP for the 2ⁿ␀ year; 200 g of Urea, 375 g of SSP, and 100 g of MOP for the 3␀␀ year; 260 g of Urea, 500 g of SSP, and 135 g of MOP for the 4th year; 325 g of Urea, 625 g of SSP, and 165 g of MOP for the 5␀␀ year; and 390 g of Urea, 750 g of SSP, and 200 g of MOP for the 6␀␀ year. Apply MOP only if there is a de␀iciency of Potash in the soil. Punjab mats needed for transplanting one acre. Gently cover the seeds with thin layer of soil and sprinkle water with sprayer to ensure proper soil settling.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_221:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_221,4,"Lift frames and put at next place. Repeat the above steps for, as many mats required. Two persons can sow seedlings for about 3-4 acres in a day. The uprooted mats are transported to the ␀ield for transplanting. In order to mechanize the sowing operation of raising mat type nursery, PAU Ludhiana has developed a tractor operated seeder for mat type paddy nursery. This machine lays a After sowing, slowly ␀lood the ␀ield to prevent seeds from being washed away. Ensure that the seedling mats remain consistently moist. Spray the paddy seedlings at the rate of 200 g urea dissolved in 15 litres of water per 150 mats in the irrigated ␀ield after 10 days of sowing. The seedling mats are ready after about 20-25 days of sowing. Drain the water completely from the ␀ield a few hours before the nursery uprooting. Iron de␀iciency problem in paddy nursery can be tackled using two sprays of 0.5% ferrous sulphate at one week interval. This de␀iciency can also be controlled by keeping standing water in paddy nursery. Completely drain the water from the ␀ield a few hours before uprooting the nursery. The seedling mats are uprooted by a cut with sharp edge blade/sickle along the boundaries of the mat.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_221:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_221,5,"One person can uproot the mats required for transplanting about 5-6 acres per day. Manual cutting of paddy nurseries requires to adopt awkward postures leading to physical strain and fatigue among farmers. To address these challenges, PAU nursery cutter having cutting capacity of 325-425 mats per hour with uniform cutting can be used. Sowing of mat type nursery with PAU tractor operated mat type nursery seeder Germinated mat type nursery sown with tractor operated mat type nursery seeder Manually raising of mat type nursery at farmers' ␀ield 205204",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_222:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_222,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Cooling Systems: Implementing sprinkler or misting systems can alleviate heat stress, while applying whitewash to roofs may enhance sunlight re␀lection or spreading of straw on roof top also gives relief from heat. Feeding Practices LIVESTOCK Foot bath: Make a footbath outside the livestock unit that should carry a mixture of 4-5% Formaldehyde. This helps to avoid the entry of infectious agents in the shed. Washing of shed: Clean the sheds monthly using a 5% phenyl solution. During the rainy season, the washing frequency should be increased to twice a month. For katcha ␀loors, a layer of 1-2 inches of soil may be excavated and substituted with a layer of clean soil. 1.0 m wide perforated polythene sheet (50-60 gauge) over 1.0 m wide soil bed with simultaneous uniform seed placement over the soil bed for raising mat type nursery for mechanical paddy transplanters. Shelter Management Ventilation: Facilitate adequate air circulation in shelters by utilizing exhaust fans, roof ventilators, or open-sided structures. Drainage: Ensure adequate drainage around shelters to avoid water accumulation, which may result in mosquito proliferation and associated",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_222:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_222,2,"diseases. Green Fodder: Employ Kharif crops such as maize, bajra, and sorghum as green fodder. Consider multicut varieties for bajra and sorghum, such as the Napier Bajra hybrid and Pb Sudex Chari No.4, which are both nutritious and abundantly available during this season. Additionally, incorporating leguminous fodders like guara and cowpea with the aforementioned non-leguminous fodders will aid in reducing the reliance on expensive concentrate mixtures. Rate of feeding of fodder should be around 40-50 Kg/animal/day. Silage Preparation: Produce silage from excess green fodder such as maize, bajra, and sorghum to guarantee feed supply during scarcity. Small-scale farmers can utilize polypropylene bags and drums for silage preparation. It is advisable to feed silage post-milking to prevent any smell in the milk. Spreading of straw on shed roof Punjab Non-Conventional feed resources: Azolla cultivation is quite a prospective technology for use as non-conventional feed resource. Health Care Deworming: Implement screening/faecal analysis based deworming to avert parasitic infections, particularly common in humid environments. It is essential to deworm pregnant animals using",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_222:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_222,3,"Fenbendazole, preferably. Additionally, pay close attention to coccidia infestations during faecal analysis. Avoid Spoiled Feed: Elevated humidity levels may result in the development of mould in stored feed and silage. It is essential to conduct regular inspections and remove any spoiled feed and silage. Silage aﬀected by fungus can be utilized in the production of vermicompost. Balanced Diet: Fortify green fodder feeding with a concentrate mixture (having mineral mixture and salt) at a rate of 1 kg per 2 liters of milk produced in buﬀaloes and 1 kg per 2.5 liters of milk produced in cattle to ful␀ill their nutritional needs. Keep in mind that animals usually consume dry matter @ 2.5-3.5% of their body weight. Feeding of Uromin lick is bene␀icial to alleviate the nutritional de␀iciencies. Feed Supplements: Supplement diet with buﬀers (1% in concentrate mixture) and yeast to combat the eﬀect of heat. Frequent freshening/hand mixing of feed/fodder lying in manger (Pushing-up the of ration) in order to release the entrapped heat reduces refusal by animals and improves the feed intake. Water Management Clean Water Supply: Ensure a constant supply of fresh and clean drinking water.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_222:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_222,4,"Utilize shaded water troughs to maintain cooler temperatures. Adding lime to the water troughs not only provides a source of calcium but also helps prevent fungal growth in the cemented trough. Water used for bathing, cleaning the shed and other operations should be managed carefully, with a maximum limit of 100 liters per animal per day. Electrolytes: Incorporate electrolytes into drinking water during periods of extreme heat to avert dehydration and sustain electrolyte equilibrium. Vaccination: Administer vaccinations for prevalent diseases such as foot and mouth disease, Hemorrhagic septicemia, lumpy skin disease, and black quarter prior to the arrival of the rainy season. Vaccination of animals 207206",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
