ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_229:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_229,4,"control of broad leaf weed, apply 900 g per ha 2,4-D ester 38 EC in 450 litres water at 30-35 days after sowing. Application Schedule: Apply the full dose of P, K, Zn, and one-third of N at the time of puddling. The remaining two-thirds of N should be top-dressed in two equal splits at 3 and 6 weeks after transplanting. Incorporate 15 tons of well-decomposed FYM/ha before transplanting. Plant Protection: Fall armyworm: Spray the crop with chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC @ 200 ml or spinetoram 11.7 SC 250 ml or emamectin benzoate 5 SG 200 g in 500 litres of water per ha, for crop up to 20 days old. Maize stem borer: Apply Phorate 10 G or carbofuran 3% granules @ 7.5 kg per ha in the shoot of the plant after 16 to 30 days after sowing. Alternatively, spray 10% solution of neem leaves/kernels after 10-20 days of germination. Armyworm and grasshoppers: Apply Methyl Parathion 2% power @25 kg per ha, summer ploughing in fallow land is advised. Aphids: Apply methyl demeton 25 EC @1 liter per ha in 500 litre of water at the time tasseling. Maydis leaf blight: Spray mancozeb or propinab or carbendazim 0.2 percent solution, repeat the spray in 10-15 days. Suitable Varieties: PR-126, PR-106,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_229:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_229,5,"PR-1121, BK-190, PB-1718, PB-1509, PB-1885. These varieties oﬀer a mix of high yield, stress tolerance, and market preference. Fertilizer Management: Medium duration varieties & Hybrids (e.g., PB-1718, PB- 1509): 150 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O, 25 kg Zinc sulphate per hectare. Early Duration Varieties (e.g., PR-126): 120 kg N, 60 kg P₂O₅, 60 kg K₂O, 25 kg Zinc sulphate per hectare. Nursery Raising: Prepare 1.0-1.5 m wide nursery beds. Generally, 400-500 m2 nursery area is suf␀icient for transplanting in one ha area. Paddy nursery can be raised in second fortnight of May and 24-25 kg seed is suf␀icient for transplanting in one ha area. In nursery paddy seed should be covered properly with sand or with mixture of sand and manure, nursery bed should be always moist without standing water. Transplanting: Manual transplanting: Transplant the seedlings in lines, 2-3 seedlings per hill at a spacing of 15 x 15 cm, Depth of transplanting should not be more than 2-3 cm. Mechanical transplanting: Done by paddy transplanter in puddled and un-puddled conditions. Raising of mat type nursery is required Seed Rate and Seed Treatment: 20-25 kg/ha seed is suf␀icient for transplanting. Treat the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_229:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_229,6,seed with Sprint 75 WS (carbendazim + mancozeb) by making slurry of 3 g fungicide formulation in 10-12 mL water for one kg seed (24 g fungicide in 80-100 mL water for 8 kg seed) before sowing. Time of Nursery Sowing: The ideal window for paddy nursery sowing in Rajasthan is 20 May to 20 June. Rice 213212,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_230:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_230,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Fertilizer Application: Apply 50 kg of N and 20 kg P␀O␀ per hectare in rows at the time of sowing under rainfed and low rainfall conditions. Apply 50 kg of N and 20 kg P␀O␀ per hectare at the time of sowing and another 50 kg N per hectare about one month later under irrigated conditions. Seed Treatment: Prior to sowing treat seed with Thiram @3g/kg, Imidacloprid @5ml/kg. Also treat with Trichoderma or Pseudomonas@5-10g/kg seed, then inoculate with Bradyrhizobium@25 g/kg seed. PULSE CROPS Improved Varieties: Hybrids: CSH 1,5,6,9,10,11, Varieties: SPV 96, 245, 462, 475, CSV 15, 17, 23, Pratap Jowar 1430, Fodder purpose: (i) Multi-cut: MP chari, SSG 59-3, (ii) Single cut: Raj Chari 1, 2, and Pratap Chari 1080 Sowing Time: Last week of June to ␀irst week of July depending upon the rainfall and moisture in the soil pro␀ile. Plant Protection: Coragen (Chlorantraniliprole) 18.5 SC @150 ml/ha, Fame (␀lubendiamide) 480 SC@ 50 ml/ha for rice stem borer and leaf folder. Ulala (␀lonicamid) 50 WG @ 150 g/ha and Osheen (Dinotefuran) 20 SG @ 200 g/ha for plant hoppers. Nativo (tri␀loxystrobin+tebuconazole) 75 WG @200 g/ha in 500 L of water for BLB. Awancer Glow",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_230:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_230,2,"(azoxystrobin 8.3 % + mancozeb 66.7 %) 75 WG @ 1.5 kg/ha for sheath blight. Amistar Top (azoxystrobin + difenoconazole) 325 SC @ 500 ml in 500 L water per ha for blast. Time of Sowing: Optimum period of sowing is mid-June to mid-July; Early green fodder- 2ⁿ␀ fortnight of March- 1␀␀ fortnight of April. Plant Protection: Seed treatment with Slayer (thiamethoxam) 30 FS @10 ml/kg seed for the control of shoot ␀ly. Seed treatment with Sulphur dust @ 4 g/kg seed for grain smut. Mung bean Seed Rate & Spacing: Seed rate of 15-20 kg/ha is recommended. Row to row spacing should be maintained at 25-30 cm and plant to plant at 10 cm. Weed Management: Apply 30 kg butachlor or 15 kg thiobencarb granules/ ha in 4-5 cm deep water at 2-3 days after transplanting. Apply 3.0-liter butachlor 50 EC or thiobencarb EC or 1325 ml Anilophose 30 EC or 2.0-liter Pretilachlor 50 EC or 125 g oxydiazon 80 % WP after mixing with 150 kg sand and broadcast in standing water at 2-5 days after transplanting. Apply 20 g ready mix of metsulphuron and chlorimuron or 125 g ethoxysulphuron 15 % WG or 1 kg 2,4-D ester at 20-25 days after transplanting for the control of broad leave weeds. Broad leaved weeds can also be",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_230:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_230,3,"managed by application of 93.75 ml/ha in 500 liters of water phenoxulam 24 % SC at 8-12 days after transplanting. Apply 250 ml bispyribac sodium 10 % SL/ha in 500 litres of water at 15-25 days after transplanting to manage mix weeds ␀lora in rice. Jowar Seed Rate & Spacing: Grain purpose: 12-15 kg/ha at 45 cm line spacing. Fodder Purpose: 35-40 kg per ha at 25-30 cm line spacing. Rajasthan Weed Management: The critical weed control period is 15-35 DAS. Hand weeding at 20-25 DAS and 35-40 DAS, or using hand hoes/mechanical weeders, is eﬀective. Apply Pendimethalin 30% EC (1.0-1.25 kg a.i./ha) as pre-emergence within 2 days of sowing for broadleaf and grass weeds, and Imazethapyr 10% SL (75-100 g a.i./ha) as post emergence at 15-20 DAS for 2-4 leaf stage weeds. Urd bean Water Management: Irrigate once or twice if dry spells prevail for 10-15 days especially between ␀lowering and pod formation and grain development stages. Light irrigation is recommended. Critical stages for irrigation are ␀lowering and early grain formation/pod ␀illing stages. Improved Varieties: Mukundra Urd-2, Kota Urd-4, Kota Urd-3, KU 96-3 (Azad Urd- 3), Pratap Urd-1, Pratap Urd-2. Improved Varieties: MH-1142,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_230:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_230,4,"MH-421, IPM-410-3 (Shikha), IPM-205-7 (Virat), GM-7, GM-6 & GM-4. Plant Protection: White␀ly can be managed by growing barrier crops (maize, sorghum), using 10 sticky traps/acre, removing weed hosts (Parthenium, Croton), and spraying Thiamethoxam 25 WG (100 g/ha) or Imidacloprid 17.8 SL (0.3 ml/litre) at early infestation. Aphids' population can be minimised by spraying with Neem oil 2% as a preventive bio-insecticide or Dimethoate 30 EC @ 1 ml/litre. Jassids/ lea␀hoppers control by spray with Acetamiprid 20 SP @ 0.2 g/litre or Imidacloprid 17.8 SL @ 0.3 ml/litre at ETL. Thrips managed by avoiding dense sowing and spraying Spinosad 45 SC (0.3 ml/litre) or Fipronil 5 SC (1.5 ml/litre). For pod borer management use of pheromone traps (5/acre for adult moths), spray of Emamectin benzoate 5 SG @ 0.4 g/litre or Spinosad 45 SC @ 0.3 ml/litre at ␀lowering to pod formation stage is recommended. Fertilizer Management: Fertilizers and micronutrients should be applied based on the soil test. In case of soil tests are not available, apply 15-20 kg N, 40-50 kg P␀O␀, 20 kg K␀O, 20 kg S per ha at the time of sowing as basal application. Zinc sulphate @25 kg/ha should be applied at every 2-3",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_230:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_230,5,"years, and 0.5 g/kg sodium molybdate. Disease Management: For yellow mosaic virus, control the white␀ly vector by spraying Thiamethoxam 25 WG (100 g/ha) or Imidacloprid 17.8 SL (0.3 ml/litre) at early infestation. To reduce the Cercospora leaf spot & Anthracnose incidence, spray of Mancozeb (0.25%) or Carbendazim (0.1%) at ␀irst symptom appearance, or treatment of seeds with Thiram/Captan @ 2.5 g/kg is bene␀icial. To control Root rot and Wilt, crop rotation with non-host crops should be taken and seed treat with Trichoderma viride (4 g/kg seed) or carbendazim is recommended. Time of Sowing: Urd bean is advised to be sown with the onset of the monsoon, ideally between mid-June and early July, but can be extended until end of July in case of delayed rains. Seed Rate & Spacing: For sole cropping, a seed rate of 15-20 kg/ha is recommended, while for intercropping, use 8-10 kg/ha. The ideal spacing (R x P) is 30-40x10 cm to optimize growth and yield. 215214",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
