ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_233:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_233,3,"kg/ha P as basal application with sowing and 5 t/ha FYM. Treat seeds with Rhizobium and PSB. For better yield, apply 60 kg sulphur per and 25 kg zinc sulphate heptahydrate (21% Zn) per ha or 15 kg monohydrate (33% Zn) per ha in de␀icient soils. Improved Varieties: Prabhat, PAU-881, IPA-203, Pant Arhar-6, AL-882, ICPAL-88039, ICPAL-87. Weed Management: For eﬀective weed control, apply Pendimethalin @ 0.75 kg a.i./ha pre-emergence. Perform manual weeding at 20-25 and 45-50 days after sowing. Use Imazethapyr @ 100 g a.i./ha post-emergence at 20-25 days to control broadleaf and grassy weeds. Rajasthan ␀lowering and pod initiation. Blister beetles: Deep ploughing, ␀ield sanitation, light traps, and neem-based products (NSKE 5% or Azadirachtin 0.03% WSP @ 2500- 5000 g/ha). Time of Sowing: Ideal time of sowing of mothbean is ␀irst week of July after the onset of monsoon rains in rainfed areas. Apply 25 kg/ha Quinolphos 1.5% in termite- aﬀected ␀ields. Disease Management: Sterility mosaic virus: Use resistant varieties and remove infected plants early to limit virus spread. Spray Neem oil (5 ml/litre) or NSKE 5% every 15 days. Seed treatment with Imidacloprid 70 WS (5 g/kg seed) helps",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_233:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_233,4,"protect seedlings. Alternaria blight: Mancozeb (2.5 g/litre) or Carbendazim (1 g/litre), planting on raised beds for better drainage, and using resistant cultivars. Phytophthora blight: seed treatment with Metalaxyl (8 g/kg), maintaining good drainage, minimizing stem injury, and using resistant genotypes. Seed Rate & Spacing: Sowing done by using 12-15 kg/ha of seed. Before sowing treat seed with Thiram/Captan (3 g/kg), Imidacloprid (5 ml/kg) and Rhizobium + PSB (5-7 g/kg) by mixing well and dry in shade, and sow with 30x15-20 cm spacing (RxP) for early varieties and 45x15-20 cm for late varieties. Improved Varieties: RMO-257, RMO-225, RMO-435, RMO-423, RMO-40, RMO- 2251, CAZRI Moth-2, CAZRI Moth-3, CAZRI Moth-4, CAZRI Moth-5 etc. Manure & Fertilizers: Incorporate 4-5 t/ha well decomposed FYM one month before sowing; at the time of sowing use of basal dose of 15-20 kg N and 35-40 kg P␀O␀/ha is recommended. Spraying of 1% NPK and 500 ppm thiourea at ␀lowering improve podding of crop. Plant Protection: Termite: Apply quinalphos/chlorpyrifos dust @20-25 kg/ha at ploughing and treat seeds with Chlorpyrifos @2 ml/kg. Apply Methyl Parathion 2% dust @20-25 kg/ha against cutworms.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_233:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_233,5,"Jassids- spray Imidacloprid @500 ml/ha is advised. Pod borer: Apply malathion 50 EC, or quinalphos 25 EC @ of 0.5 liters per ha, or broadcast quinalphos 1.5% dust at 20-25 kg per hectare. Disease Management: Yellow mosaic virus: control white␀ly vector by spray of Dimethoate 30 EC or Metasystox (Oxydemeton-methyl) at 0.5 liters per ha along with 0.5 liters of Malathion per ha, using 500 liters of water for uniform coverage. Bacterial bacterial spot: spray a solution of 200 grams of Agrimycin/ha, mixed with 500 liters of water. Soak seeds in 100 ppm Streptocycline for one hour, then treat with 2 g/kg Streptocycline before sowing. For stem blight, spray a solution of 2 kg of Mancozeb dissolved in 500 liters of water per ha is eﬀective. For leaf curling disease, spray a solution of 750 ml of Dimethoate 30 EC or Methyl Demeton 25 EC dissolved in 500 liters of water per hectare. A second spray should be applied 15 days later. For control of angular leaf spots, spray a solution of 500 grams of Carbendazim dissolved in 500 liters of water per ha. Prior to sowing, treat the seeds with 3 grams of Captan Moth bean Water Management: Mostly, it grown in arid/rainfed areas; irrigate once at pod",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_233:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_233,6,"development during dry spells. In irrigated areas, two irrigations at branching/␀lowering and pod formation can be given to enhance productivity. 217216",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Plant Protection: For termites' control in standing crops, mix Chlorpyriphos @ 1.25 L/ha or Fipronil 0.3% GR @ 20-25 kg/ha with irrigation water. Application of Imidacloprid, Dimethoate, or Malathion @ 0.75-1.25 ml/L of water eﬀectively controls sucking pests like jassids, aphids, and white␀ly. Fertilizer Management: Application of 2.5 t/ha of compost or FYM 15 days before sowing. At sowing, apply 10 kg N and 20 kg P␀O␀/ha as basal application. Disease Management: To manage bacterial blight eﬀectively spray with Streptocycline @ 5 g or Plantomycin @ 50 g in 100L water per ha at 35-40 days after sowing is bene␀icial. For Angular leaf spot and Anthracnose management, spray of Zineb @ 2kg in 500L water per hectare at 15-day intervals, at least twice is recommended. Powdery mildew can be controlled by spraying wettable sulphur (e.g., Sulfex) @ 2-3kg/ha, dusting sulphur powder @ 20-25kg/ha, or spraying Dinocap @ 1.5 ml/litre of water. Time of Sowing: Under rainfed conditions, sowing should coincide with the onset of the monsoon, ideally within the ␀irst two weeks of July. Delays beyond ␀irst fortnight of July may lead to a noticeable decline in yield. In",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,2,"irrigated areas, sowing can be extended until the end of July. Time of Sowing: Rainfed Groundnut: Sowing with the onset of monsoon in the last week of June or in the ␀irst week of July. Irrigated Groundnut: Sowing to be done around 20th June or 10-12 days before the onset of monsoon with a pre-sowing irrigation. Weed Management: Two manual weeding at 25 and 45 DAS are usually suf␀icient. Apply Pendimethalin (2.5-3.3 L/ha) within 2 days of sowing as pre-emergence, and Imazethapyr (400 g/ha) at 20-25 DAS as post-emergence for eﬀective weed control. Improved Varieties: RGC 1038, RGC 1017, RGC 936, RGC 1002, RGC 1003, RGC 1033, RGC 1055, RGC 1066, Karan Guar 1 (RGr 12-1), Karan Guar 14 (RGr 18-1), and Karan Guar 15 (RGr 20-15). These varieties are suitable for semi-arid conditions and have high gum content. Seed Rate & Spacing: Seed rate of 15 kg/ha is recommended, prior to sowing treat seeds with Trichoderma @ 4 g/kg or fungicides such as mancozeb or carbendazim @ 2 g/kg of seed, followed by chlorpyrifos @ 2 ml/kg of seed to deter termite attacks. OILSEED CROPS Groundnut Water Management: Lifesaving irrigation during ␀lowering and seed formation should be given if rainfall is",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,3,"de␀icient. Spraying with 0.1% thiourea at 25 and 45 DAS can boosts yield under moisture stress. Cluster bean or 2 grams of Carbendazim per kilogram of seed. To control dry root rot, treat seeds with 2.0 g of Carbendazim or Thiophanate Methyl (70 WP) per kg of seed. Mix 10 g of Trichoderma per kg of seed along with 8-10 kgs of Trichoderma mixed with 400 kgs of moisture-rich farmyard manure. Keep mixture in shade for approximately 72 hours, and then apply it to the soil at a rate of per hectare. Rajasthan Manure & Fertilizer: Apply FYM or compost @ 10-15 t/ha about 15-20 days before sowing. N:P: K @ 20:60:30 kg/ha. Basal application of fertilizers i.e., placing the fertilizers about 4-5 centimeter in the side of the seed and 4-5 centimeter below the seed at the time of sowing. Apply gypsum @ 375 kg/ha for proper development of pods and kernels. Water Management: Pod development stage of groundnut is the most critical for water stress. Farmers should avoid moisture stress at this stage. In case drought or no rainfall, one irrigation should be given at pod development stage. Bio-forti␀ied Varieties: Girnar-4 & Girnar-5 (Rich in Oleic acid). Seed rate & Spacing: Spreading Type",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,4,"Varieties-80-100 kg/ha (45x10 cm); Bunch Type varieties-100-110kg/ha (30x10 cm) Plant Protection: White gurb: Seed should be treated with Fipronil 5 SC @6 ml per kg of seed kernel and Clothianidin 50 WDG @1 g a.i. per kg of seed before sowing. Imidacloprid 17.8 SL @300 ml per hectare at 22 DAS. Biological Control by Beauveria bassiana @ 0.5 g/m² mixed with water in furrows at 15 days after sowing (DAS). Stem rot, collar rot, dry root rot, late leaf spot and rust: Seed treatment with Tebuconazole 2DS @1.5 g/kg of seeds or with Trichoderma sp. @10 g/kg of seed followed by furrow/soil application of Trichoderma viride @ 4 kg enriched in 250 kg FYM/ha. Thrips: Spray Malathion 5% powder @ 1 kg per hectare or dissolve 800 ml of Malathion 50 EC or 750 ml of Methyl Demeton 25 EC in water and spray. Bud necrosis: Treat the land with Carbofuran 3G @15 to 20 kg per hectare before sowing and spray Monocrotophos @1 ml per litre of water after 21 DAS. Termite: Apply Chloropyrifos @ 4 litres per hectare along with irrigation water. Seed Treatment: Treat seed with fungicide Thiram @3 gm or carbendezim @1 gm + Thiram @2 gm or Mencozeb @ 2 gm per kg of seed. For control of termite seed treatment",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,5,"with chlopyriphos 20EC @ 4 ml per kg seed. For seed treatment Trichoderma @10 g or Carbendazim 50 WP @2 g or Tebuconazole 2 DS/kg @ 1.5 g seed kernel may be used before sowing for soil & seed borne disease. Seed should be inoculated with proper strain of Rhizobium culture particularly in those places where groundnut is to be grown for the ␀irst time. Weed Management: Major weed in Groundnut are Amaranthus viridis, Digeria arvensis, Euphorbia hirta, Cyperus rotundus, Dactyloctenium aegypticum, Trianthema portulacastrum, Phyllanthus niruri. To control these weeds following weed management practices should be adopted. Improved Varieties: GJG-37, RG-559, GJG-32, GJG-19, TCGS-1043 (Dharani), HNG- 123, RG-425, RG-510, JL-501, Mallika (ICHG-00440), HNG-69, GJG-31, GJG-9, RSV-87, RS-138, JL-524, RG-141 are cultivated mostly. Post Emergence: Quizalofop-ethyl @ 0.050 g a.i. per hectare, Imazathayper @ 0.050 g a.i. per hectare in 500-600 Litre water. Pre Emergence: Pendimethalin 30% EC @1-2 Litre/ha, Oxi␀lorophen @ 0.25- 0.50 g a.i. per hectare and Diclosulam 22-26 g a.i. per hectare in 500-600 Litre water. Fluchloralin (Basalin) @ 1 kg a.i. per hectare dissolved in 800-1000 litres of water",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_234:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_234,6,can also be used as pre-planting spray. 219218,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
