ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_235:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_235,3,"de␀icient. Spraying with 0.1% thiourea at 25 and 45 DAS can boosts yield under moisture stress. Cluster bean or 2 grams of Carbendazim per kilogram of seed. To control dry root rot, treat seeds with 2.0 g of Carbendazim or Thiophanate Methyl (70 WP) per kg of seed. Mix 10 g of Trichoderma per kg of seed along with 8-10 kgs of Trichoderma mixed with 400 kgs of moisture-rich farmyard manure. Keep mixture in shade for approximately 72 hours, and then apply it to the soil at a rate of per hectare. Rajasthan Manure & Fertilizer: Apply FYM or compost @ 10-15 t/ha about 15-20 days before sowing. N:P: K @ 20:60:30 kg/ha. Basal application of fertilizers i.e., placing the fertilizers about 4-5 centimeter in the side of the seed and 4-5 centimeter below the seed at the time of sowing. Apply gypsum @ 375 kg/ha for proper development of pods and kernels. Water Management: Pod development stage of groundnut is the most critical for water stress. Farmers should avoid moisture stress at this stage. In case drought or no rainfall, one irrigation should be given at pod development stage. Bio-forti␀ied Varieties: Girnar-4 & Girnar-5 (Rich in Oleic acid). Seed rate & Spacing: Spreading Type",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_235:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_235,4,"Varieties-80-100 kg/ha (45x10 cm); Bunch Type varieties-100-110kg/ha (30x10 cm) Plant Protection: White gurb: Seed should be treated with Fipronil 5 SC @6 ml per kg of seed kernel and Clothianidin 50 WDG @1 g a.i. per kg of seed before sowing. Imidacloprid 17.8 SL @300 ml per hectare at 22 DAS. Biological Control by Beauveria bassiana @ 0.5 g/m² mixed with water in furrows at 15 days after sowing (DAS). Stem rot, collar rot, dry root rot, late leaf spot and rust: Seed treatment with Tebuconazole 2DS @1.5 g/kg of seeds or with Trichoderma sp. @10 g/kg of seed followed by furrow/soil application of Trichoderma viride @ 4 kg enriched in 250 kg FYM/ha. Thrips: Spray Malathion 5% powder @ 1 kg per hectare or dissolve 800 ml of Malathion 50 EC or 750 ml of Methyl Demeton 25 EC in water and spray. Bud necrosis: Treat the land with Carbofuran 3G @15 to 20 kg per hectare before sowing and spray Monocrotophos @1 ml per litre of water after 21 DAS. Termite: Apply Chloropyrifos @ 4 litres per hectare along with irrigation water. Seed Treatment: Treat seed with fungicide Thiram @3 gm or carbendezim @1 gm + Thiram @2 gm or Mencozeb @ 2 gm per kg of seed. For control of termite seed treatment",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_235:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_235,5,"with chlopyriphos 20EC @ 4 ml per kg seed. For seed treatment Trichoderma @10 g or Carbendazim 50 WP @2 g or Tebuconazole 2 DS/kg @ 1.5 g seed kernel may be used before sowing for soil & seed borne disease. Seed should be inoculated with proper strain of Rhizobium culture particularly in those places where groundnut is to be grown for the ␀irst time. Weed Management: Major weed in Groundnut are Amaranthus viridis, Digeria arvensis, Euphorbia hirta, Cyperus rotundus, Dactyloctenium aegypticum, Trianthema portulacastrum, Phyllanthus niruri. To control these weeds following weed management practices should be adopted. Improved Varieties: GJG-37, RG-559, GJG-32, GJG-19, TCGS-1043 (Dharani), HNG- 123, RG-425, RG-510, JL-501, Mallika (ICHG-00440), HNG-69, GJG-31, GJG-9, RSV-87, RS-138, JL-524, RG-141 are cultivated mostly. Post Emergence: Quizalofop-ethyl @ 0.050 g a.i. per hectare, Imazathayper @ 0.050 g a.i. per hectare in 500-600 Litre water. Pre Emergence: Pendimethalin 30% EC @1-2 Litre/ha, Oxi␀lorophen @ 0.25- 0.50 g a.i. per hectare and Diclosulam 22-26 g a.i. per hectare in 500-600 Litre water. Fluchloralin (Basalin) @ 1 kg a.i. per hectare dissolved in 800-1000 litres of water",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_235:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_235,6,can also be used as pre-planting spray. 219218,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Water Management: Flowering and pod formation stage in soybean are the most crtical for water stress, 1-2 irrigations should be applied as per the need. Seed Rate: 80-100 kg/ha. Spacing: Row-to-Row spacing 30-45 cm and plant to plant 10 cm. Plant Protection: Stem Fly: to manage apply Quinolphos 25 EC @ 1.5 litre per ha or Thiamethoxam 12.6% + Lamdacyhalothrin 9.5% ZC@ 125 ml per ha. Gridle Beetle: can be manged by application of Dimethoate 30 EC @ 1.0 litre per ha or Thiacloprid 21.7 SC @ 750 ml per ha. Defoliators (Green semilooper, Tobacco caterpillar & gram pod borer): can be manged by application of Spinetoram 12 SC @ 450 ml or Quinolphos 25 EC @ 1.5 litre or Emamactin benzoate 5 SG @ 180 gm or Indoxacarb 15.8 EC @ 300 ml per ha. Seedling Rot: The disease results in poor seedling emergence because of seed rotting. The seed treatment with Thiram at 3.0 g/kg of seeds is bene␀icial. Pod Blight: The pods of aﬀected plant turns yellowish green and later on dry up. The grain becomes shrivelled and mould. Use of resistant varieties, sowing of crop in rotation and spray of 0.5 per cent Zineb can control the disease. Time of Sowing: Soybean sowing should",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,2,"be sown by 15␀␀ June where irrigation facility is available. If irrigation facility is not available, sowing should be done with onset of monsoon. Fertilizer Application: Apply 20 kg N, 40 kg P␀O␀ phosphorus and 40 kg K␀O per ha before sowing. If the seeds not inoculated with rhizobium culture than use 40 kg nitrogen per ha. To get higher yield of soybean foliar spray of water-soluble N:P: K (19:19:19 or 17: 44: 00) @ 0.5% (5 g per litre of water) at 45 and 60 days after sowing is recommended. Soil incorporation of 30 kg sulphur/ha through gypsum before sowing and 1.0 kg boron per ha (borax@ 5 kg/ha) in boron de␀icient soil should also be done. Weed Management: Pre emergence application of Pendimethalin 30 EC at 1.0 kg a.i. per ha (commercial dose 3.3 liter per ha) and one hand weeding at 30-35 days after sowing. Post emergence application of Sodium Aci␀luorfen 16.5 % + Clodinafop Propargyl 8 % EC (ready mix) at 1000 ml per ha at 20-25 DAS eﬀectively control the narrow as well as broad leaf weeds. Seed Treatment: Treat the seeds with Carbendezim or Thiram @ 2g/kg of seed 24hrs before sowing or with talc formulation of Trichoderma viride @ 4 g/kg seed (or) Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,3,"10 g/kg seed. Soybean Improved Varieties: Improved varieties are- NRC 138, RVSM 2011-35, JS 20-116, JS 20- 98, JS 20-94, JS 335, NRC 127, JS 93-05, Pratap Soya 1, Pratap Soya 2 (RKS 18), Pratap Raj 24 (RKS 24), JS 97-52, JS 95-60, Pratap Soya 45 (RKS 45), JS 20-34, JS 20-29 and RKS 113 Sesame (Til) Time of Sowing: Sowing with onset of monsoon and to be completed before mid- July. Crop is highly sensitive to water logging conditions; therefore, proper drainage facilities are must for higher productivity. Yellow Mosaic Transmitted by white ␀ly (Bemisia tabaci). The disease is dangerous and widely spreads. Spray Metasystox 0.2 per cent at 10-15 days interval controls the vector eﬀectively. Rajasthan Water Management: Sesame is very susceptible to drought at various physiological growth stages. The crop requires about 50 cm of water during the entire growth period. Usually, no need to irrigation is required if rains are well distributed. However, in case of long dry intermittent spells, adequate moisture in soil should be maintained with light irrigations. Plant Protection: Phyllody: two time spraying of Dimethoate 25 EC @ 750 ml or Quinalphos 25 EC @ 1 litre per ha, ␀irst at 25-30 DAS",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,4,"or second at 40-45 DAS. Alternatively spray 5 % neem leaf solution twice @ 21 & 35 DAS. Leaf & pod borer: spray quinalphos 25 EC @ 1-1.5 litre per ha in 500-700 liters of water and repeat at an interval of 15 days as per requirement. Hawk moth and Gall ␀ly: Apply Quinalphos (1.5%) powder @ 25 kg per ha. Blight: spraying mancozeb @ 1.5 kg or captan @ 2 kg per ha at the interval of 15 days. COMMERCIAL CROPS Seed Treatment: For management of seed borne diseases treat seed with Thiram 2 g/kg + Carbendazim 1 g/kg or Trichoderma viride 5 g/kg seed. For bacterial blight management soak the seed for 30 minutes in 2 gm solution of Streptomycin in 10 litre of water prior to seeding. By treating seed with Azotobacter and PSB fertilizer 25% nitrogen and phosphorus can be saved. Sowing: The cotton performs well when sown between ␀irst week of May to third week of May. The best time of its sowing is before 15 May. Improved Varieties: RT- 392, RT- 372, RT-346, RT-46, RT-125, RT-127, RT-103, RT- 35, TC-25 (spreading type), Pratap (C-50), etc. Nutrient Management: Farmyard manure or compost is applied @ 20-25 tons per ha 15-20 days before sowing. In suf␀icient rainfall areas, 25 kg phosphorus and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,5,"20 kg nitrogen should be given in furrows at the time of sowing 4-5 cm below the seed. After 4 to 5 weeks, the remaining nitrogen sprinkled during light rain. In areas with less rainfall, reduce the amount of fertilizer and use phosphorus based on soil test. In zinc de␀icient ␀ields, spray 0.5 percent zinc sulphate plus 0.25% lime solution at 50 days after sowing. Use of gypsum 150 kg/ha can increase the yield as well as oil content in sesame. Seed Rate and Spacing: Desi (arboreum): 12-15 kg/ha; (120 x 60 cm), American (Narma): 8.75-10 kg/ha; (90 x 45 cm), Hybrid Bt cotton: 2.4-3.0 kg/ha (75 x 30 cm). These spacings result a plant population of ~40,000-50,000 plants/ha. The seed should be sown at 2.5-3 cm depth and maintain 2-3 plants at point after thinning. Seed treatment: Delinting: Dip seeds in concentrated sulfuric acid (1 L/10 kg seed) for 1-2 minutes until black. Rinse thoroughly and discard ␀loating seeds. Dry in shade. (Use plastic containers only; wear gloves and dispose of acid safely.) Seed Rate: For branching types, the seed rate is 2-2.5 kg per ha with plant geometry of 30-35 cm x 15cm. For non-branching types of varieties (Pratap) the seed rate 4-5 kg per ha with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_236:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_236,6,plant geometry of 30 cm x10-15 cm. Cotton Weed Management: First weeding at 20-25 DAS & Second weeding at 30-45 DAS. Fluchloralin (Basalin) 1 kg a.i. /ha in 800-1000 liters water as pre-planting eﬀectively manage weeds. 221220,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
