ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_237:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_237,3,"10 g/kg seed. Soybean Improved Varieties: Improved varieties are- NRC 138, RVSM 2011-35, JS 20-116, JS 20- 98, JS 20-94, JS 335, NRC 127, JS 93-05, Pratap Soya 1, Pratap Soya 2 (RKS 18), Pratap Raj 24 (RKS 24), JS 97-52, JS 95-60, Pratap Soya 45 (RKS 45), JS 20-34, JS 20-29 and RKS 113 Sesame (Til) Time of Sowing: Sowing with onset of monsoon and to be completed before mid- July. Crop is highly sensitive to water logging conditions; therefore, proper drainage facilities are must for higher productivity. Yellow Mosaic Transmitted by white ␀ly (Bemisia tabaci). The disease is dangerous and widely spreads. Spray Metasystox 0.2 per cent at 10-15 days interval controls the vector eﬀectively. Rajasthan Water Management: Sesame is very susceptible to drought at various physiological growth stages. The crop requires about 50 cm of water during the entire growth period. Usually, no need to irrigation is required if rains are well distributed. However, in case of long dry intermittent spells, adequate moisture in soil should be maintained with light irrigations. Plant Protection: Phyllody: two time spraying of Dimethoate 25 EC @ 750 ml or Quinalphos 25 EC @ 1 litre per ha, ␀irst at 25-30 DAS",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_237:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_237,4,"or second at 40-45 DAS. Alternatively spray 5 % neem leaf solution twice @ 21 & 35 DAS. Leaf & pod borer: spray quinalphos 25 EC @ 1-1.5 litre per ha in 500-700 liters of water and repeat at an interval of 15 days as per requirement. Hawk moth and Gall ␀ly: Apply Quinalphos (1.5%) powder @ 25 kg per ha. Blight: spraying mancozeb @ 1.5 kg or captan @ 2 kg per ha at the interval of 15 days. COMMERCIAL CROPS Seed Treatment: For management of seed borne diseases treat seed with Thiram 2 g/kg + Carbendazim 1 g/kg or Trichoderma viride 5 g/kg seed. For bacterial blight management soak the seed for 30 minutes in 2 gm solution of Streptomycin in 10 litre of water prior to seeding. By treating seed with Azotobacter and PSB fertilizer 25% nitrogen and phosphorus can be saved. Sowing: The cotton performs well when sown between ␀irst week of May to third week of May. The best time of its sowing is before 15 May. Improved Varieties: RT- 392, RT- 372, RT-346, RT-46, RT-125, RT-127, RT-103, RT- 35, TC-25 (spreading type), Pratap (C-50), etc. Nutrient Management: Farmyard manure or compost is applied @ 20-25 tons per ha 15-20 days before sowing. In suf␀icient rainfall areas, 25 kg phosphorus and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_237:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_237,5,"20 kg nitrogen should be given in furrows at the time of sowing 4-5 cm below the seed. After 4 to 5 weeks, the remaining nitrogen sprinkled during light rain. In areas with less rainfall, reduce the amount of fertilizer and use phosphorus based on soil test. In zinc de␀icient ␀ields, spray 0.5 percent zinc sulphate plus 0.25% lime solution at 50 days after sowing. Use of gypsum 150 kg/ha can increase the yield as well as oil content in sesame. Seed Rate and Spacing: Desi (arboreum): 12-15 kg/ha; (120 x 60 cm), American (Narma): 8.75-10 kg/ha; (90 x 45 cm), Hybrid Bt cotton: 2.4-3.0 kg/ha (75 x 30 cm). These spacings result a plant population of ~40,000-50,000 plants/ha. The seed should be sown at 2.5-3 cm depth and maintain 2-3 plants at point after thinning. Seed treatment: Delinting: Dip seeds in concentrated sulfuric acid (1 L/10 kg seed) for 1-2 minutes until black. Rinse thoroughly and discard ␀loating seeds. Dry in shade. (Use plastic containers only; wear gloves and dispose of acid safely.) Seed Rate: For branching types, the seed rate is 2-2.5 kg per ha with plant geometry of 30-35 cm x 15cm. For non-branching types of varieties (Pratap) the seed rate 4-5 kg per ha with",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_237:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_237,6,plant geometry of 30 cm x10-15 cm. Cotton Weed Management: First weeding at 20-25 DAS & Second weeding at 30-45 DAS. Fluchloralin (Basalin) 1 kg a.i. /ha in 800-1000 liters water as pre-planting eﬀectively manage weeds. 221220,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_238:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_238,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Pre-sowing Treatment: Soak dried seeds in water for 6-8 hours. Treat with fungicide (e.g., carbendazim 2 g/kg or Trichoderma 6-8 g/kg seed). Apply systemic insecticide (e.g., imidacloprid 70% WG at 5-7.5 g/kg seed) for early pest control. Establishment of Orchard: The digging of pits should be completed in May. Square and rectangular method is the easiest and convenient for planting orchards. The size of pit should be 60 x 60 x 60 cm at 4 meters rows apart. The plant to plant spacing should be 3 metres. Climate and Soil: Dry and semi-dry climate is very suitable for pomegranate production. Sandy loam soil with good drainage is the most suitable. Pomegranate plants have good capacity to tolerate salt and alkalinity. Improved Varieties: 1. Bhagwa, 2. Sonar Lal, 3. Super Bhagwa Improved Varieties: Desi (arboreum): HD 123, RG 8, RG 542, CICR-1, CICR-3, KR 64. Narma (American): RS 875, RS 810, RS 2814, RS 2013, Bikaneri Narma. Bt Hybrids: RAJ H-HH-16, CSH 198, CSH 238. Buy certi␀ied seeds only and follow refuge planting for Bt cotton. Plant Protection: To control leaf sucking pest & Leaf Curl Virus disease, seed should be treated with 4 g Thiamethoxam 70",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_238:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_238,2,"WS/kg seed before sowing. Keep close monitoring on White ␀ly host plants like vegetables, ␀lower plants, weeds & unwanted plants and from time to time these aﬀected host plants must be uprooted & burn. Some vegetables like Ladies Finger, Brinjal, Tomato & Chilly also act as host plants for white ␀ly, accordingly, as per need these must be sprayed with Thiamethoxam 25 WG @ 0.5g/litre water. To control bacterial blight seed should be treated with soaking in 1 g Streptomycin or 10 g Plantomycin/10 litre water before sowing. Spray Thiamethoxam 25 WG @ 100g/ha and Profenophos 50 EC @1250 ml/ha for sucking pest. Proclaim (emamectin benzoate) 5 SG @250g/ha for pink, spotted and American bollworm Pomegranate Planting Material: Tissue culture saplings are the best to guarantee disease-free planting material and for planting in new areas where there are no pomegranate orchards. Water Management: Light irrigation within 3-4 days of sowing if no rainfall. First full irrigation can be given around 20-30 days after sowing. In water-scarce areas, use drip irrigation and mulching to retain moisture. Fertilizer Application: Incorporate 8-10 tonnes/ha well-decomposed FYM in soil thoroughly before",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_238:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_238,3,"sowing. Apply chemical fertilizers based on soil test recommendations. If no soil test is available, apply 90-100 kg nitrogen/ha for desi cotton and 100-150 kg nitrogen/ha for American cotton, divided into 2-3 split doses. Also apply 20-40 kg P O /ha at sowing. In case of Zinc de␀iciency, apply zinc sulfate at 2 5 25 kg/ha, or spray borax 0.1% during ␀lowering if boron is de␀icient in soil. FRUIT CROPS Planting Time: July-August is the suitable time for planting saplings. The saplings should be planted in the evening. The soil should be pressed well around the sapling after planting. The plant should be irrigated immediately after the plantation. Rajasthan Post Planting Care: The pomegranate plants should be taken care for the ␀irst two years. Pruning is very important in pomegranate. Pomegranate can be pruned in two ways- 1. single stem method 2. multi stem method. The ␀lowering and fruiting improves with pruning. Time of Flowering and Fruiting: Pomegranate ␀lowers three times in a year, which is known as Bahar. Commercially, only one Bahar should be taken in the whole year. Bahar Control: Late Mrig Bahar is the best cropping in water shortage dry areas. Under late Mrig Bahar,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_238:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_238,4,"irrigation is stopped in April-May. In the month of June, manure and fertilizers are given by digging the basins followed by light irrigation. After three days, give one heavy irrigation followed by 2-3 light irrigations till the rain comes. Thus the plant will start growing from July, ␀lowers in July-August and fruits are harvested in January-February. Irrigation Management: Drip irrigation method is very bene␀icial in pomegranate, irrigate for 1.5 to 2.0 hours at an interval of 2-3 days with drip irrigation. During fruit development, suf␀icient moisture should be maintained continuously in the soil and environment. Weed Management: 2 to 3 times hoeing in a year in the ring of the plant keep the crop weed free. Pruning in Pomegranate: Pruning in pomegranate is done twice a year. Immediately after pruning, a solution of copper oxychloride 2 grams per liter of water should be sprayed. Diseased and damaged branches should be removed from time to time. Bacterial Leaf Blight: Fallen leaves and branches should be collected and destroyed. Apply streptomycin sulphate 90%, tetracycline hydrochloride 10% @ 0.5g, copper oxychloride @ 2.5 g per litre of water and spray. Wilt: uproot the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_238:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_238,5,"aﬀected plants from the orchard and burn them. Make a solution of propiconazole 25EC @20ml in 10 litre of water and pour it in the roots of each plant. Repeat its use 3-5 times at an interval of 20 days. Leaf Spot: spray copper oxychloride 50% WP @ 2.5 grams or thiophanate methyl 70% WP @ 1 g/L of water in the initial stage of the disease. In case of severe infestation, spray hexaconazole 5 EC @ 1 ml or difenoconazole 25 EC. @ 0.5 ml per litre of water and spray at an interval of 30-40 days. Flower and Fruit Fall: For management, maintain proper moisture in the soil continuously. At an interval of 15 days, spray two micronutrient mixtures (zinc sulphate @ 0-6%, manganese sulphate @ 0-6%, boric acid @ 0-6% @ 2 grams per litre of water. Spray Plano␀ix @ 4 grams per 15 litres of water. Manure and Fertilizer: For good yield, give appropriate manure and fertilizer according to the age of the plant. Manure and fertilizer should be mixed in the soil by putting it at a depth of 15 to 20 cm in a perimeter of one to one and a half meter around the plants. Disease and Insect Management: 223222",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
