ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_245:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_245,6,"0.01. The drip line should be inspected at an interval of 15-20 days. In case of drip jam, the drip should be run with 2-3 percent solution of phosphoric acid. The crust formed around the plants should be removed with a hoe after 15-20 days of transplantation, to improve the air circulation and plant growth. The balance between the vegetative growth and fruiting of the plant to be maintained. If there are more than 6-7 fruits on each branch, then the weak and small 229228",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 fruits should be removed. Capsicum is a very sensitive to root rot, LCV and anthracnose, etc. They should be properly inspected and treated from time to time. Due to continuous cropping in poly house, the de␀iciency of micro nutrients develops in the soil, especially of calcium. This causes black brown spots on the fruits which start rotting resembling with a fungal disease. In such a situation, gypsum should be applied @ 10-15 kg per 1000 m␀ area. In case of coloured capsicum, only fully developed and matured fruits should be harvested with the help of a knife or secateurs. Sometimes, price of coloured capsicum in the market rules below than that of green capsicum. In such a case the colored capsicum fruits should be plucked at the initial stage. The branches of capsicum plants are generally weak. They break due to the weight of the fruits. They should be tied with the help of a string from time to time. The shoots coming out of the stem of the plants should be removed from time to time. The old leaves should also be removed. Irrigation and Fertilizer: Regular irrigation is recommended along with fertigation with fertilizer solution which is a",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,2,"mixture of nitrogen, phosphorus and potash in the ratio of 5:3:6. From transplantation to ␀lowering, 2000 to 2500 litre of water is given/1000 m␀ of area. Along with this, nitrogen is given @ 1 g/liter, phosphorus @ 0.5 g/liter and potash @1 g/liter of water. From ␀lowering to fruit setting, 3000 to 4000 litre water is applied per 1000 m␀ area along with N, P, and K @ 2 g,1 g and 2 g/liter of water through drip system. The fertigation should be done at 3-4 days interval in summer and 6-8 days interval in winter. Yield: Generally, 200 to 220 t of tomato yield is obtained per hectare from a good greenhouse. About 100 to 120 t of yield can be obtained from cherry tomatoes. Tomato Planting Time and Spacing: Tomato can be planted in greenhouse from July to September. The crop lasts up to April to June or July next year. The period of growing depends on the size and type of greenhouse and the climate. The row to row spacing is kept at 60-70 cm and plant to plant at 50-60 cm. Pruning and Training: In polyhouse, usually 2 to 3 main branches of the plants are allowed to grow and the rest are removed continuously. This process should be repeated at every 10-15 days. Tomato plants are trained",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,3,"upwards supported by plastic ropes which are tied to main iron wire at a height of 9 to 10 feet. Varieties: Badshah, Dev, Abhinav, Himshikhar, Subhrano, Naveen, DT-1, DT-7, ARTH- 4, Nun-7711 and 646. Cherry tomato varieties: BR-124 and HA-818 Plant protection: The aﬀected plants by viral disease TMV should be uprooted and destroyed immediately. Harvesting of fruits: Harvesting should be done with scissors or sharp knives so that tomato plants and other fruits are not damaged. Fruits are harvested only when they are fully ripe (red in colour). They should be graded according to colour, size and weight for getting better price. Storage: If the fruits have to be sold after a day or two, they should be kept at a temperature of 8-10⁰ C in summer. In winter, they can also be kept at normal room temperature. Rajasthan Seed Bed Preparation and Transplanting: Before the nursery is ready, beds should be made in the polyhouse. The height of the beds should be kept 30 cm, one meter wide and length according to the size of the polyhouse. A 60 cm path should be kept between two beds. Proper shelter management during the month of May wherein high temperature and dusty winds blows. The animals",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,4,"should be protected from excessive temperature and heat stress. Prevent young calves from direct sunlight. Due to excess temperature, the animals may suﬀer from heat stroke, and dehydration and loss of appetite etc may Nursery Raising: Generally, direct sowing of cucumber is done but in order to increase crop density in polyhouse, seedlings are prepared in pro-tray. To prepare the nursery, ␀irst the pro-tray is sterilized and a mixture of coco peat, vermiculite and perlite in the ratio of 2:1:1 is ␀illed in the pro-tray. One seed is sown in each cell. Later, water is given daily with the help of a sprinkler. Cucumber seedlings are ready in 12- 15 days depending on the weather. When the plant has two leaves in addition to the cotyledons, then the plant is considered ready for transfer. Varieties: Satisfy, Kian, In␀inity, Hilton, Malistar, Dynamic, Ka␀ka etc. LIVESTOCK Plucking and Yield: The ␀irst plucking is done 30-35 days after planting. Subsequent plucking can be done continuously for the next 60 days. About 20-25 fruits grow per plant weighing about 4 kg. Thus, about 100 quintals cucumber is produced per 1000 m␀. Cattle and Buﬀalo Temperature and Humidity: Optimum temperature",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,5,"for germination is 20° Celsius and 22 to 30 °C is suitable for the growth and development of plants. Relative humidity is 70-80% should be maintained. Cucumber Plant Protection: White ␀ly, aphid and jassid: Spray of Imidacloprid 17.8% SL. Leaf miner: Spraying of 1 ml of propanophos can be done. Leaf and fruit borer pests: Spraying of 25 ml of thiodicarb should be done. Spider: Spraying of 1 ml of abumectin can be done. Nematodes: The beds should be sterilized and then planting should be done. While making the beds, neem or Karanja cake should be added in the beds. Along with this, a trench of 1.5-2 feet should be made around the polyhouse. It can also be controlled with carbofuran. Powdery mildew: It can be controlled by spraying 1 ml of hydrophilic sulfur or karathane. Leaf curl and leaf bunch disease: For its control, the sap sucking pests should be controlled before the disease appears. Mosaic: This disease is also spread by sucking insects; hence these insects should be controlled timely. Wilt disease: Drenching with 1% solution of Ridomil Gold should be done. Training and Grafting of Plants: After 15 days of transplanting, a thread-like structure emerges from the plant. The",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_246:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_246,6,"plants should be provided support at this stage. The plant should be supported upwards with the help of a twine. As the plants grow fast, they should be trained twice a week. The shoots emerging from the main stem should be removed from time to time. 231230",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_247:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_247,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 fruits should be removed. Capsicum is a very sensitive to root rot, LCV and anthracnose, etc. They should be properly inspected and treated from time to time. Due to continuous cropping in poly house, the de␀iciency of micro nutrients develops in the soil, especially of calcium. This causes black brown spots on the fruits which start rotting resembling with a fungal disease. In such a situation, gypsum should be applied @ 10-15 kg per 1000 m␀ area. In case of coloured capsicum, only fully developed and matured fruits should be harvested with the help of a knife or secateurs. Sometimes, price of coloured capsicum in the market rules below than that of green capsicum. In such a case the colored capsicum fruits should be plucked at the initial stage. The branches of capsicum plants are generally weak. They break due to the weight of the fruits. They should be tied with the help of a string from time to time. The shoots coming out of the stem of the plants should be removed from time to time. The old leaves should also be removed. Irrigation and Fertilizer: Regular irrigation is recommended along with fertigation with fertilizer solution which is a",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
