ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_256:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_256,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Organic Package: FYM @ 3 t/ha, Azophos (2 kg/ha), Trichoderma (2.5 kg/ha), vermicompost (1.5 t/ha), Panchagavya (3%) at vegetative, ␀lowering, and grain ␀illing stages. Disease/pest control: NSKE 5% and Bacillus subtilis 0.5% as needed. Foliar spray: 1.5% foliar formulation at ␀lower initiation. Horsegram: Foliar Spray: TNAU Horsegram Wonder @ 5 kg/ha during ␀lowering with wetting agent. Foliar Spray: TNAU Liquid Pulse Wonder @ 5 kg/ha at peak ␀lowering (Greengram/ Blackgram) and 15 days after (Redgram). Land preparation: Raised beds (90 cm) with 30 cm furrows. Seed Treatment: Imidacloprid (5 ml/kg) + Bacillus subtilis (10 g/kg) + Rhizobium & Phosphobacteria (30 g/kg). Agronomy: Spacing 30 × 15 cm; drip irrigation; fertigation 25:50:25:40 NPKS kg/ha. for weed control: Pendimethalin + Imazethapyr (PE) + Quizalofop-ethyl + Imazethapyr (EPoE). TNAU Vigour Plus: Nano-formulated seed coating (20-25 ml/kg) that boosts germination, seedling vigor, and early establishment. Bio-Pulse: Microbial seed bio-priming formulation that enhances yield under pathogenic stress, eﬀective in chickpea, pea and lentil. Finger Millet Newer fungicides for foliar disease",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_256:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_256,2,"management: Foliar spray of tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin (1g/l) or tebuconazole 25 EC (1ml/l), at symptom appearance and 15 days later; eﬀective against powdery mildew and Cercospora leaf spot. TNAU Vigour Plus (Seed Booster): Pre-sowing seed coating with biopolymer matrix containing IAA and GA␀; enhances seed germination and seedling vigour (also helpful in multiple crops like Pulses, Groundnut, Cotton, Paddy, Millets, Vegetables). TNAU Groundnut Rich: A foliar nutrition solution. Applied twice @ 5.0 kg/ha at 35 DAS (50% ␀lowering) and 45 DAS (pod development). Requires 500 litres of water per spray. Enhances pod development and improves yield. Nut Boost: A seed inoculation formulation containing a consortium of phosphate, potash, and zinc solubilizing PGPRs. Applied as a seed treatment. Improves pod yield by 16.5% to 18.1% compared to untreated seeds. Micronutrient Spray (Tomato, Bhendi, Chilli): TNAU multi micronutrient @ 1% during vegetative and ␀lowering stage. Bhendi: Spray WSF 19:19:19 @ 2% + liquid Multi MN @ 1% at 30 DAS, repeated 3 times every 10 days. PULSE CROPS Greengram, Blackgram, Redgram Blackgram Nodule-Associated Plant Probiotics for Blackgram: Blend of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_256:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_256,3,"bene␀icial microbes improving nodulation, drought tolerance, and yield (14% over standard). Newer fungicides for foliar disease management: Foliar spray of tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin (1g/L) or tebuconazole 25 EC (1ml/L), at symptom appearance and 15 days later; eﬀective against powdery mildew and Cercospora leaf spot. Greengram OILSEED CROPS Groundnut Tamil Nadu & Puducherry SPICE CROPS Turmeric Dairy TANUVAS PAM 21: Anionic salt (Salt I & II) @ 20 g + 10 g/day from 16 days pre- to 5 days post-calving to prevent milk fever. TANUVAS GRAND: 10 ml/day in gruel to boost digestion and prevent acidosis. TANUVAS Mastiguard: Teat dip to prevent mastitis. Wormivet: Herbal dewormer @ 15 g twice/day for 2 days. 10 Cent Fodder Model: Co(BN5), COFS 31, Valimasal, tree fodder system yielding 10.5 t/year. Poultry Fisheries Water Quality and Predator Control: Use nylon netting at the water inlet to prevent predatory ␀ish entry and ensure monthly water quality monitoring for all inland ␀ish culture systems. Pond Management and Disease Prevention: Apply manures as recommended, exchange 30% of water regularly to reduce disease incidence, and fence ponds with shade nets to prevent ␀ish escape.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_256:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_256,4,"Ornamental Fish Culture Care: Rear ornamental ␀ish in cement tanks for better pigmentation; use aquatic plants like Hydrilla and Ceratophyllum in breeder tanks for fry protection. Probeads-EC: Patented enteric-coated probiotic supplement. Shrimp Culture Biosecurity: Perform real-time PCR for disease screening before stocking, use proper aeration (1 HP/250 kg biomass), and maintain Vibrio levels with probiotics. Value Addition and Post-Harvest Practices: Promote hygienic dry ␀ish, masala dry ␀ish, and pickles from low-value ␀ishes using solar dryers and preservatives to enhance income and shelf life (up to 2 years for pickles; 6-12 months for dry ␀ish). Inland Fish Culture (Carp farming, Murrel, GIFTilapia culture and Ornamental ␀ish culture): Water intake from natural source should be kept with nylon net in the inlet pipe to prevent the entry of predatory ␀ishes. Proper manuring should be maintained. Quality seed should be selected for fast growth. To maintain proper feeding management (i.e., feeding). Sampling should be done once in three months. Water quality parameters should be analysed at least monthly once. Feeding and Stocking Practices: Maintain proper feeding",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_256:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_256,5,"schedules-e.g., feed Murrel with ␀loating pellets at 5% of body weight-and select quality seeds and advanced ␀ingerlings for better growth and survival. Soil application: TNAU micronutrient mixture @ 15 kg/ha as EFYM-50% basal + 50% top dressing at 90 DAP. LIVESTOCK Murrel Culture: Stocking of advanced ␀ingerlings to increase the survival rate. Feeding of ␀loating pellet feeds at the rate of 5% of body weight. Fencing of farm ponds using 241240",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_257:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_257,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Organic Package: FYM @ 3 t/ha, Azophos (2 kg/ha), Trichoderma (2.5 kg/ha), vermicompost (1.5 t/ha), Panchagavya (3%) at vegetative, ␀lowering, and grain ␀illing stages. Disease/pest control: NSKE 5% and Bacillus subtilis 0.5% as needed. Foliar spray: 1.5% foliar formulation at ␀lower initiation. Horsegram: Foliar Spray: TNAU Horsegram Wonder @ 5 kg/ha during ␀lowering with wetting agent. Foliar Spray: TNAU Liquid Pulse Wonder @ 5 kg/ha at peak ␀lowering (Greengram/ Blackgram) and 15 days after (Redgram). Land preparation: Raised beds (90 cm) with 30 cm furrows. Seed Treatment: Imidacloprid (5 ml/kg) + Bacillus subtilis (10 g/kg) + Rhizobium & Phosphobacteria (30 g/kg). Agronomy: Spacing 30 × 15 cm; drip irrigation; fertigation 25:50:25:40 NPKS kg/ha. for weed control: Pendimethalin + Imazethapyr (PE) + Quizalofop-ethyl + Imazethapyr (EPoE). TNAU Vigour Plus: Nano-formulated seed coating (20-25 ml/kg) that boosts germination, seedling vigor, and early establishment. Bio-Pulse: Microbial seed bio-priming formulation that enhances yield under pathogenic stress, eﬀective in chickpea, pea and lentil. Finger Millet Newer fungicides for foliar disease",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_257:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_257,2,"management: Foliar spray of tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin (1g/l) or tebuconazole 25 EC (1ml/l), at symptom appearance and 15 days later; eﬀective against powdery mildew and Cercospora leaf spot. TNAU Vigour Plus (Seed Booster): Pre-sowing seed coating with biopolymer matrix containing IAA and GA␀; enhances seed germination and seedling vigour (also helpful in multiple crops like Pulses, Groundnut, Cotton, Paddy, Millets, Vegetables). TNAU Groundnut Rich: A foliar nutrition solution. Applied twice @ 5.0 kg/ha at 35 DAS (50% ␀lowering) and 45 DAS (pod development). Requires 500 litres of water per spray. Enhances pod development and improves yield. Nut Boost: A seed inoculation formulation containing a consortium of phosphate, potash, and zinc solubilizing PGPRs. Applied as a seed treatment. Improves pod yield by 16.5% to 18.1% compared to untreated seeds. Micronutrient Spray (Tomato, Bhendi, Chilli): TNAU multi micronutrient @ 1% during vegetative and ␀lowering stage. Bhendi: Spray WSF 19:19:19 @ 2% + liquid Multi MN @ 1% at 30 DAS, repeated 3 times every 10 days. PULSE CROPS Greengram, Blackgram, Redgram Blackgram Nodule-Associated Plant Probiotics for Blackgram: Blend of",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_257:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_257,3,"bene␀icial microbes improving nodulation, drought tolerance, and yield (14% over standard). Newer fungicides for foliar disease management: Foliar spray of tebuconazole + tri␀loxystrobin (1g/L) or tebuconazole 25 EC (1ml/L), at symptom appearance and 15 days later; eﬀective against powdery mildew and Cercospora leaf spot. Greengram OILSEED CROPS Groundnut Tamil Nadu & Puducherry SPICE CROPS Turmeric Dairy TANUVAS PAM 21: Anionic salt (Salt I & II) @ 20 g + 10 g/day from 16 days pre- to 5 days post-calving to prevent milk fever. TANUVAS GRAND: 10 ml/day in gruel to boost digestion and prevent acidosis. TANUVAS Mastiguard: Teat dip to prevent mastitis. Wormivet: Herbal dewormer @ 15 g twice/day for 2 days. 10 Cent Fodder Model: Co(BN5), COFS 31, Valimasal, tree fodder system yielding 10.5 t/year. Poultry Fisheries Water Quality and Predator Control: Use nylon netting at the water inlet to prevent predatory ␀ish entry and ensure monthly water quality monitoring for all inland ␀ish culture systems. Pond Management and Disease Prevention: Apply manures as recommended, exchange 30% of water regularly to reduce disease incidence, and fence ponds with shade nets to prevent ␀ish escape.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_257:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_257,4,"Ornamental Fish Culture Care: Rear ornamental ␀ish in cement tanks for better pigmentation; use aquatic plants like Hydrilla and Ceratophyllum in breeder tanks for fry protection. Probeads-EC: Patented enteric-coated probiotic supplement. Shrimp Culture Biosecurity: Perform real-time PCR for disease screening before stocking, use proper aeration (1 HP/250 kg biomass), and maintain Vibrio levels with probiotics. Value Addition and Post-Harvest Practices: Promote hygienic dry ␀ish, masala dry ␀ish, and pickles from low-value ␀ishes using solar dryers and preservatives to enhance income and shelf life (up to 2 years for pickles; 6-12 months for dry ␀ish). Inland Fish Culture (Carp farming, Murrel, GIFTilapia culture and Ornamental ␀ish culture): Water intake from natural source should be kept with nylon net in the inlet pipe to prevent the entry of predatory ␀ishes. Proper manuring should be maintained. Quality seed should be selected for fast growth. To maintain proper feeding management (i.e., feeding). Sampling should be done once in three months. Water quality parameters should be analysed at least monthly once. Feeding and Stocking Practices: Maintain proper feeding",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_257:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_257,5,"schedules-e.g., feed Murrel with ␀loating pellets at 5% of body weight-and select quality seeds and advanced ␀ingerlings for better growth and survival. Soil application: TNAU micronutrient mixture @ 15 kg/ha as EFYM-50% basal + 50% top dressing at 90 DAP. LIVESTOCK Murrel Culture: Stocking of advanced ␀ingerlings to increase the survival rate. Feeding of ␀loating pellet feeds at the rate of 5% of body weight. Fencing of farm ponds using 241240",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_258:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_258,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Ornamental Fish Culture: Rearing of ornamental ␀ishes in cement tanks will maintain its desired pigmentation. Young ones should be separated from the parents immediately. Provision of aquatic plants like Hydrilla & Ceratophyllum is necessary for breeder tanks for hiding of young ones. Shrimp Culture: Real-time PCR diagnosis is compulsory to check the pH before releasing into the pond. Water quality analysis should be done once in 15 days. Proper aeration should be maintained (every 250 kg of biomass; 1 HP aerator). Adoption of nursery rearing (technology) will reduce operational cost of the farmers. Water and soil should be properly monitored. Maintain the Vibrio count by using probiotics. Hygienic Dry Fish Production: Dry ␀ishes can be prepared from low value marine ␀ishes such as Anchovies (Nethili) and Ribbon ␀ishes (Valaimeen) and Leiognathids and freshwater ␀ishes such as Tilapia and Carps using solar dryer by addition of ␀ish : salt ratio of 1:8 or without salt with ␀inal moisture content of 10-15%; shelf life will be 6-9 months. Value Added Fishery Product Technology: Ready to eat Value added Fishery Products such as ␀ish 65, Bajii, Fish",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_258:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_258,2,"Cutlet, Fish samosa, and Fish cake can be prepared from low value & less bone species such as Indian Mackerel, Tuna, Thread␀in Bream, Prawn/Shrimp and Tilapia by addition of masalas. The shelf life will be 3-5 days at 4°C. Hygienic Masala Dry Fish Production: Hygienic Masala Dry Fishes can be prepared from low value marine ␀ishes such as Anchovies (Nethili) and Ribbon ␀ishes (Valaimeen) and Leiognathids and freshwater ␀ishes such as Tilapia and Carps using solar dryer by addition of ␀ish : salt ratio of 1:8 and masalas (Turmeric and Chilli powder) with ␀inal moisture content of 10-15%; shelf life will be 9-12 months. green shade nets to prevent the escape of ␀ishes. Exchange of water (about 30%) to reduce the occurrence of disease. Pickle Production Technology: Pickles can be prepared from low value and less bone ␀ish species such as Indian Mackerel, Tuna, Ora Fishes, Prawn/Shrimp, Tilapia by addition of masalas with added preservatives such as vinegar & sodium benzoate (permitted @ 0.005%). It should be packed in Glass bottles or HDPE pouches. Shelf life will be 1.5 to 2 yrs. Telangana Farmers are advised to follow the sowing rule to take-up sowing of rainfed crops like Cotton,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_258:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_258,3,"Soybean, Maize, Jowar, Redgram, Greengram etc., only after receipt of cumulative rainfall of 50-60 mm in light soils and 60-75 mm in heavy soils or the soil should be wet up to top 15-20 cm depth after enter of South-West monsoon rains into the state. Paddy Under assured irrigation farmers are advised to raise rice nurseries of long duration (140-145 days) varieties from May 20th to June 20th. Under assured irrigation farmers are advised to raise rice nurseries of medium duration (130-135 days) or short duration (120-125 days) varieties from June 20th onwards. Month of June is not optimum for raising paddy nurseries using Telangana Sona (RNR15048) variety. Take the Greengram as catch crop to preceding rice in areas where the release of water into the canals and tanks is delayed. Green manuring with Sesbania/ Crotalaria / Pillipesara / grain legumes, residues of blackgram / greengram and in situ incorporation before ␀lowering. Varieties: cultivation of long duration (BPT- 5204, WGL-44, RNR 11718 etc.), medium duration (WGL-14, JGL-11470, JGL-384, RNR-28361, JGL-33124 etc), short duration (RNR-15048, KNM-1638, KPS-6251, WGL-362, KNM-118, JGL-24423, RNR-29325, JGL-28639 etc.)",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_258:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_258,4,"varieties. Direct seeding of rice with Seed-cum ferti drill wherever suitable. In Telangana state, dry converted wet and wet direct seeded rice are popular, and the sowing can be started from June ending. Treat seeds with carbendazim @ 3 g/ kg (dry seed treatment) or 1 g/L (wet seed treatment). Farmers are advised to apply the Carbofuran 3CG granules @ 800 g per acre of nursery one week before pulling of the nursery. Root dipping: prepare the slurry with 5 packets (1000 g/ha) of Azospirillum and 5 packets (1000 g/ha) of phosphobacteria or 10 packets of (2000 g/ha) of Azophos, inoculant in 40 lit. of water and dip. the root portion of the seedlings for 15- CEREAL CROPS 243242",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
