ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_259:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_259,4,"varieties. Direct seeding of rice with Seed-cum ferti drill wherever suitable. In Telangana state, dry converted wet and wet direct seeded rice are popular, and the sowing can be started from June ending. Treat seeds with carbendazim @ 3 g/ kg (dry seed treatment) or 1 g/L (wet seed treatment). Farmers are advised to apply the Carbofuran 3CG granules @ 800 g per acre of nursery one week before pulling of the nursery. Root dipping: prepare the slurry with 5 packets (1000 g/ha) of Azospirillum and 5 packets (1000 g/ha) of phosphobacteria or 10 packets of (2000 g/ha) of Azophos, inoculant in 40 lit. of water and dip. the root portion of the seedlings for 15- CEREAL CROPS 243242",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 COMMERCIAL CROPS Deep summer plough to destroy pests and conserve moisture. Optimum sowing window is from June 15␀␀ to July 15␀␀ with medium and long duration. varieties (90- 100 days and 100-120 days) without any yield reduction. Sow medium duration varieties/hybrids DHM-206, DHM-182, DHM-117, Bisco-855, Bio-9637, Bisco-740, Kaveri Ekka-2288, Kaveri -2020, Kaveri-3696 and short duration hybrids DHM-115, Pioneer-3342, KH-5991, DKC-7074 during 15␀␀ June to 15␀␀ July. Sowing can be extended up to July end if monsoon is delayed. Sow on receipt of at-least 50-60 mm rainfall for better germination and complete sowing in a week for reducing the incidence of FAW. Spray NSKE 5% or neem oil 1500 ppm @5ml/l after sowing and at weekly intervals. Dibble seeds with tractor drawn cultivator or seed cum ferti drill on ridges and beds. Intercrop red gram varieties PRG-176, WRG-97 in 2:1 ratio in light soils and in 4:1 ratio in heavy soils to reduce incidence of FAW. Follow IPM for FAW management: summer ploughing, growing single cross hybrids, clean cultivation, intercropping with pulses, balanced fertilization, release of egg parasitoids (Trichogramma sp) and",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,2,"spraying Chlorantraniliprole @ 0.4 ml or spinetoram @ 0.5 ml or Emamectin benzoate @ 0.4 g per litre in plant whorls. As post emergence, spraying of Tembotrione @ 115 ml + Atrazine 400 g or Toperamezone @ 40 ml + Atrazine 400 g or mesotrione + atrazine @1400 ml/acre in 200 litre of water will eﬀectively control weeds. After 30-35 days, crop may be inter-cultivated followed by earthing up is needed for better nutrient uptake and to avoid lodging. Maize 30 minutes in bacterial suspension and transplant. Make 20 cm alleyways at every 2 meters to facilitate free aeration, ease of farm operations and better pest and disease management. Broadcast butachlor @ 1-1.5 l or pretilachlor @ 500-600 ml or 4 kg granules of bensulfuron methyl (0.6%) + pretilachlor (6.0%) with 20 kg sand per acre. Practice alternate wetting and drying in well irrigated areas to save water, better aeration and minimize incidence of BPH besides getting carbon credits with less emission of greenhouse gases. Recommended dose of fertilizers: 40-48 Kg Nitrogen, 20 Kg Phosphorus 16 Kg Potash per acre during Vanakalam. Spray 0.2% ZnSO␀ 2 to 3 times at 5 days interval to manage Zn de␀iciency, particularly in alkaline soils.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,3,"Cotton Sow the crop early by June 1st/2nd week after receipt of suf␀icient good rains at least (60mm). Don't sow cotton crop after July 20th as yields will be reduced drastically under rainfed conditions. Sowing of Cotton on ridge and furrow in medium soil and broad Bed furrow in black soil under rainfed conditions facilitates the crop to moisture conservation and excess water drain out. In a village or area all the cotton cultivating farmers should take up the sowings on community basis and complete within a period of 7 - 10 days. Depending on soil type and rainfal pattern cotton should be sown at a spacing of 120 x 60 cm/ 120 x 45 cm/ 90 x 60 cm/ 90 x 45 cm / 90 x 30 cm. Deep summer plough to destroy the eggs of insect pests and to remove weed stock. Intercrop with greengram/ blackgram/ soybean/ cluster bean in 1:2 or 1:3 ratio, and red gram 4:1 / 6:1 / 8:1 ratio which also helps to manage sucking pests. Telengana Sow high-yielding wilt-resistant varieties (155-165 days) like WRGE-93, WRGE-97, WRGE-121, and medium-duration varieties like WRG-255 and TDRG-4, TDRG-59 & TDRG-272 can be recommended. Sowing should be initiated only after receipt of 60 mm rainfall. The optimum sowing",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,4,"time should be 15␀␀ June to 15␀␀ July at a spacing of 150-180 x 20 cm in black soils and 90-120 x 20 cm in red soils. Seed rate should be 2.5 to 3.0 kg per acre only (plant-to-plant spacing should be mandatory). Treat seeds with thiram or captan @ 3g/kg followed by rhizobium culture @200-400 g/ 3 kgs of seed. The raised bed method or ridge and furrow method should be followed to protect the crop from Phytophthora blight disease, which occurs due to excess and stagnation of rainwater. Intercropping in Red gram + Cotton (1:4/ 1:6), Soybean (1:4/ 1:6), Green gram/ Black gram (1:7) should be followed. Treat the Red gram seed with Trichoderma viride @ 10 g/ kg seed to protect the crop from soil-borne diseases. PULSE CROPS Pre-emergence herbicides like pendimethalin (Stamp extra) @ 700 ml/acre should be applied within 24 -48 hours after sowing with the help of hand sprayer for better control of weeds in cotton. Application of post emergence herbicides like quizalofop ethyl @ 400 ml + pyrithiobac sodium @ 250 ml in 200 L of water at 30 DAS in cotton to control grasses and broad-leaved weeds. Inspect the crop at squaring and ␀lowering stage for presence of PBW larvae within ␀lowers.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,5,"Installation of Pheromone traps @ 8/acre and monitoring ETL at this stage is 10 % damaged ␀lowers. Spray MgSO␀ @ 10 g/l twice at 45 and 75 DAS; Boron @ 1.5 g/l twice at 60 and 90 DAS; 0.5% FeSO␀ with citric acid twice at weekly intervals and ZnSO␀ @ 2 g/l twice at 4-5 days interval at 45 DAS to manage micronutrient de␀iciencies. During excess rainfall, drain excess water and apply 25 kg urea and 20 kg potash per acre. Spray Plano␀ix (NAA 10 PPM) @ 1 ml per 4.5 liters of water twice at 10-15 days interval to manage ␀lower dropping. Spray 1% KNO3 or 19:19:19, 20:20:20, 21:21:21. Follow rotation of insecticide sprays against insect pests for high ef␀iciency. Stem application of ␀ipronil 1: 4 at 30 DAS and Flonicamid / Imidacloprid with water (1:20) at 45, 60 DAS to be done which protects the crop from early season sucking pests like jassids and aphids. Spray pendimethalin @ 1 - 1.5 L in 200 liters of water within 24 - 48 hours after sowing will eﬀectively control the weeds in Red gram Post-emergence application of quizalofop ethyl @ 400 ml/ acre to control grasses and imazethapyr 10 % @ 300 ml/ acre to control grasses and broad-leaved weeds. Both herbicides in the tank mix are also",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_260:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_260,6,"recommended in case both weeds are observed. If there is submergence due to excess rain, drain excess water at the earliest and spray 1% KNO␀ or 19:19:19, 20:20:20 or 21:21:21. Application of Multi K or 13-0-25 @ 10g/l at the time of ␀lowering should be done. Practice nipping at 45 and 60 DAS, wherein terminal branches are removed to facilitate lateral branches, thus improving yields. To control pod ␀ly spraying of Thiomethaxam 25 wg @ 0.2ml/l, Flubendamide 0.2ml/L with Jaggery 5g/L to be sprayed at the time of early pod formation stage. Pigeon pea Grow 2-3 rows of maize or sorghum as border crop as barrier to prevent pests. Treat the seed with imidacloprid 70 WS@ 5 g per kg or thiamethoxam 70% WS @ 4 g per kg followed by Trichoderma viridi or Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 10 g per kg. 245244",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
