ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_261:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_261,6,"recommended in case both weeds are observed. If there is submergence due to excess rain, drain excess water at the earliest and spray 1% KNO␀ or 19:19:19, 20:20:20 or 21:21:21. Application of Multi K or 13-0-25 @ 10g/l at the time of ␀lowering should be done. Practice nipping at 45 and 60 DAS, wherein terminal branches are removed to facilitate lateral branches, thus improving yields. To control pod ␀ly spraying of Thiomethaxam 25 wg @ 0.2ml/l, Flubendamide 0.2ml/L with Jaggery 5g/L to be sprayed at the time of early pod formation stage. Pigeon pea Grow 2-3 rows of maize or sorghum as border crop as barrier to prevent pests. Treat the seed with imidacloprid 70 WS@ 5 g per kg or thiamethoxam 70% WS @ 4 g per kg followed by Trichoderma viridi or Pseudomonas ␀luorescens @ 10 g per kg. 245244",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 OILSEED CROPS Sowing time is generally from June 15␀␀ fortnight- July 15␀␀ during Kharif, Sept 15␀␀ to 30␀␀ October during Rabi, January last week to March 15␀␀ during Summer. Greengram varieties MGG-295, MGG-385, MGG-351, TM-96-2, WGG-37 and WGG-42, Virat, IPM-2-14, Sikha. Blackgram YMV-resistant varieties MBG-1070, PU-31, GBG-1 and TBG-104 are the preferred varieties. Treat seeds with imidacloprid @ 5g or thiamethoxam @ 5g/kg. Intercropping can be done with cotton (2:1 or 1:1 ratio) or redgram (6:1)/(8:1). Greengram can be taken as a preceding crop to Rice and Chilli as green manure for incorporation in the soil. Greengram and Blackgram Groundnut Sow varieties ASB-22, JS-335, AISb-1, JS-93-05 during 15␀␀ June 1␀␀ week of July using seed drill/ gorru/ desi plough/ by tractor drawn seed cum fertilizer drill / broad bed furrow planter. Sowing of Soybean by Broad bed Furrow (BBF) planter or Raised bed method facilitates the crop to withstand heavy rains and moisture stress conditions and to obtain higher yields. Treat the seeds with carbendazim @ 1g or thiram or captan @ 3 g/kg followed by 1.5 ml of imidacloprid (48 %) and Rhizobium culture @ 200 g/10",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,2,"kg seed. Apply 50 kg DAP + 26 kg MOP at the time of sowing and top dressing of urea @ 25 -30 kg/acre at 30 DAS. Pre-emergence herbicides like pendimethalin 30 % @ 1 - 1.5 L/ acre should be applied within 24-48 hours after sowing with the help of hand sprayer for better control of weeds. Post emergence application of quizalofop ethyl @ 400 ml/ acre for control of grasses and imazethapyr + imazomax 40 g /acre or imazethapyr 10 % @ 250 ml/acre to control the grasses and broad-leaved weeds. To control stem ␀ly and stem gridler as a prophylactic application of carbofuran 3G granules @ 8 kg/acre is recommended at 10 DAS. To control of pod blight spraying of tebuconazole + sulphur @ 2.5 g/L is recommended. Dry the seed and maintain the below 12 % moisture during seed storage to avoid incidence of pest and disease. Castor Sow high yielding castor hybrids viz., ICH-5, ICH-66, PCH-111, DCH-519 & ICH-6, PCS-262 from 15␀␀ June to 15␀␀ July in rainy season under rainfed conditions. Intercrop with redgram in 1:1 or greengram in 1:3 ratio, open furrows between rows to conserve moisture in light soils. LIVESTOCK Animal Husbandry & Fisheries Agriculture and allied sectors play a vital role in the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,3,"lives and livelihoods of the majority of Telangana's population. The state is rich in livestock resources and Soybean Seed rate recommended is 237 kg/ha and practice seed treatment with imidacloprid 600 FS @ 2 ml/kg followed by tebuconazole 2 DS @ 1g or Trichoderma viride @ 10g/kg to control early and late leaf spot diseases, sucking pests, collar rot, PSND in the early stages. Application of Gypsum @ 500 kg/ha at pegging stage near podding zone for pod development. Weed management with Diclosulam 84% WDG @31 gm/ha as pre-emergence herbicide followed by post- emergence application of Imazethapyr @ 750 ml/ha at 20 to 25 days after sowing. Telengana livestock production, according to national Livestock census 2019, the total livestock population in the state is 3.26 crore. The livestock sector is a major driver of primary sector growth. The sectors contribution to Telangana's Gross State Value Added (GSVA) at current prices increased from Rs. 96, 908 crores in 2023-24 to Rs. 1,02, 835 in 2024-25. Across India, inland ␀isheries where farmers build ponds on their landholdings to breed ␀ish, is emerging as an important source of additional income to the farmers (Socio Economic Outlook,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,4,"2025). Scarcity of feeds and fodder resources is a big problem limiting animal production. Among all, ␀lood and drought are the major devastating natural calamity leading to a massive loss of vegetation. Oﬀer ample milk or electrolyte water to new born calves to prevent dehydration, heat stroke and death of neonatal stocks. Maintain clean, well-ventilated shelters with proper drainage to prevent diseases during ␀loods. Ensure adequate space: Overcrowding causes stress and disease outbreaks. Local authorities may be informed about the outbreak of the diseases. All animals should be untied/evacuated immediately in case of ␀loods to avoid mortality. All dead animals should be disposed of hygienically and should not be thrown in nearby drainages, water bodies etc. Burial Pit should be of 8 X 9 feet. Sprinkling of disinfectants like bleaching powder, quick lime etc. in the aﬀected areas helps in reducing the spread of diseases. Remove all the ␀lammable items from the area in and around the animal shed. Always maintain a suf␀icient stock of feed, fodder, water and medicines and store them in a safe place. Proper Care should be taken after reallocation of animals after natural disasters.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,5,"During Drought bajra fodder varieties and in water logging areas Para grass may be cultivated. Clean, safe, hygienic water should be provided to the animals. Restrict the transportation of animals to consumer's doorstep for milking. Dairy Disinfect sheds regularly with Phenol 1-2% solution and Washing Soda (4% solution). Deworm all adult stock with broad spectrum antihelmintic, Albendazole (Dose: 10 mg/ kg body weight) during last week of May. Vaccinate animals with Haemorrhagic septicaemia (HS) and black quarter in June @ 5ml per animal subcutaneously. Segregate animals in milk production, dry, pregnant, non- pregnant and heifers. Allow animals to graze early in morning or later in evening. Follow body weight-based feeding regimen. Provide 1 kg concentrate for every 2.5 kg milk for General Guidelines for Livestock Management: To protect animals from the weather ␀luctuations keep them in well-ventilated shelters and under the shade of trees. Restrict the movement of visitors to the livestock farms and practice biosecurity measures in case of disease out breaks. Keep suf␀icient feed, fodder and medicine in hand. Vaccinate animals against Foot and Mouth Disease and Hemorrhagic",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_262:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_262,6,"septicemia (Cows and buﬀaloes), PPR (goats). Except pregnant animals, deworm all animals for external and internal parasites. Keep clean drinking water available at all times. Monitor water intake by animals to protect from heat stress. Supplement herbal immune boosting products in ration to boost immunity. Observe and detect oestrus and inseminate on time. Splash/bath buﬀaloes especially pregnant animals to prevent adverse eﬀect of summer on oestrus and conception and prevent early embryonic mortality/ abortion due to heat waves. 247246",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
