ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_283:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_283,5,"12-15 cm plant to plant within the row. Manures are applied 5-10 t/ha FYM about a month before sowing. Millets per kg of seed as a slurry before sowing further enhances protection. For managing the disease at later stages, foliar spray of Azoxystrobin 18.2% + Difenaconazole 11.4% SC at 500 ml per hectare is recommended, with the ␀irst spray at disease appearance, followed by a second spray after a 10-day interval. Similarly, Fall Army Worm can be controlled through regular monitoring of ␀ields to collect and destroy egg masses, which are covered with hairs and are easily visible on leaves. For crops up to 20 days old, spraying with Chlorantraniliprole 18.5 SC at 0.4 ml per litre of water, Spinetoram 11.7 SC at 0.5 ml per litre, or Emamectin benzoate 5 SG at 0.4 g per litre using 300 litres of water per hectare is recommended. For older crops, the water volume should be increased to 200 litres per acre with a corresponding adjustment in insecticide dosage. To ensure eﬀective control, the spray nozzle should be directed towards the whorl of the plant. Finger Millet cultivation in Uttarakhand 267266",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 the initial stage of crop growth and development. The inter-cultivation and manual weeding should be done at 25 DAS. In line sown crop 2-3 times inter-cultivation and one time hand weeding is suggested whereas, in broadcast seeded crop two hand weeding will eﬀective to minimize the weeds. In assured rainfall and irrigated areas, pre-emergence spray with pendimethalin @ 1.0 kg a.i./ha. (rainfed areas), Oxy␀lurofen @ 0.1 L a.i./ha (irrigated areas) can be done. For post-emergence spray 2,4-D Na salt @ 0.75 kg a.i./ha around 20-25 days after sowing is recommended. Yellow sticky trap (10-12/ha) is advised to control the aphids control. Stem borer is destructive for millets; it can be control with spray of neem oil 5 ml/litre of water or spray ␀ipronil 2ml/litre of water after pest emergence. Field Preparation: As sugarcane crop stands in ␀ield for >1year, it is necessary to give deep ploughing by tracto drawn mould-board plough. The proper time for ploughing is immediately after the preceding crop is harvested or just after a good shower of rain received. The harrowing is done 3-4 times to break clods and to make the land smooth and even to facilitate",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,2,"uniform irrigation, 4-6 ploughings to produce good tilth is recommended and each ploughing should be followed by planking. Spring cane is planted in the month of February-March. March is the best time for cane planting in Uttarakhand, some area also lying under late planting which can be possible after harvesting of wheat (April-May) require special management practices. COMMERCIAL CROPS Sugarcane planting can be done in ␀lat bed method; shallow furrows (8-10 cm deep) are opened tractor operated furrow opener at a distance of 75-90 cm. Three budded settsare planted taking care that on 3-budded sett falls in each running 30 cm length of furrow. After planting, the furrows are covered with 5-7 cm soil and the ␀ield is leveled by heavy planking. After germination 3-4 inter-cultures are recommended at a proper interval to control the weeds and facilitate the tillering. Sugarcane Normally, two groups in sugarcane varieties i.e. early and mid-late/late maturity are observed. Farmers prefer the varieties of high tonnage while, sugar mills prefer the higher sucrose content. Nowadays early maturing, high sucrose and higher tonnage varieties are available and are in higher demand by the",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,3,"farmers and sugar mill owners. These varieties are performing well in the country and accounts for higher sugar production. Early maturity varieties: Co Pant 12221, Co Pant-3220, Co 15023, Co 118, Co 98014, CoS 13235, CoS 17231, CoLK 9709, CoLK 11203, CoLK 14201, CoLK 15201, CoS 88230,CoS 8436 and CoS 3251. Mid-late maturity varieties: Co Pant-12226, Co Pant-13224, Co Pant-97222, Co Pant-5224, Co 5011, CoS 13035, CoLK 14204, CoS 14233, 16233 and CoPb 14185. Sugarcane under Trench planting method Uttarakhand Fertilizer Application: Well decomposed FYM @ 20-25 t/ha with NPK 150:60:50 kg/ha recommended for sugarcane plant crop whereas, ratoon crop fertilized with 25% more N than the plant cane. Full P and K applied at as basal. A dose of 150 kg N/ha, one third given as basal, remaining two third top dressing in equal two splits at 45 and 60 days after plating (end June) gives better cane yield in late planted conditions. Ratoon cane fertilized with N as one-third at 1␀␀ week of ratoon initiation with ␀irst hoeing, one-third at 6␀␀ and rest one-third at 8␀␀ weed after rationing. Phosphorus and potassium (on soil-test basis) should be drilled along the cane rows at the time of ␀irst",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,4,"inter-culture at 1␀␀ week of rationing. Iron de␀iciency symptoms ␀irst appear in young leaves as yellow stripes between the green veins. Later, the veins also turn yellow. In severe cases, leaves become white and the plants remain stunted. Spray the crop 2-3times with 1% solution of ferrous sulphate (1kg ferrous sulphate in 100 litres of water) at weekly intervals soon after the symptoms appear. Weed Management in Ratoon Crop: Two hoeings at 15 and 45 days after ratooning should be adopt for eﬀective control of weeds in sugarcane ratoon. However, under limitations of manpower-availability, cost etc., pre emergence application of either of atrazine @ 2.0 kg a.i./ha or metribuzin @ 1.0 kg a.i./ha (800- 1000 L water/ha) ␀b either of 2,4-D Na salt @ 1.0 kg/ ha a.i. (in 600-800 litres water/ha) or hoeing at 45 days after ratooning can be successfully practiced. Further, trash mulching in alternate rows and hoeing in un-mulched furrow at 1st and 6th weeks after ratoon initiation is also a good option. Weed Management in Sugarcane Plant crop: To manage the weeds in sugarcane, metribuzin 1.0 kg a.i./ha or ametryn @ 2.0 kg a.i./ha as pre-emergence is as eﬀective as earlier recommended",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,5,"pre-emergence herbicide atrazine@ 2.0 kg ai/ha. Either of these herbicides should be coupled with application of 2,4-D @ 1.0 kg a.i./ha at 60 days after planting (DAP) and one hoeing at 90 DAP to sustain cane yield equivalent to three manual hoeings at 30, 60 & 90 DAP. Plant Protection: To control the termite, early shoot borer &root borer application of chlorpyriphos 20 EC @ 5.0 litres/ ha in 1600-1800 litres water (3 ml/l) on cane In heavy or fertile soil farmers can adopt trench planting methods to get the higher cane productivity and pro␀itability per unit area, in trench planting method, single or double row trench opened through tractor mounted trench opener at 120-150 cm apart, two budded setts to be planted in trench with basal application of NPK+FYM+Insecticide mixture in running trench only, then covered the 4 cm soil above the cane setts. If required, summer planting should be done only by half ridge irrigation method of planting for better germination. Management of binding weeds: In sugarcane, application of atrazine @ 2 kg ai/ha or metribuzine @ 1.25 kg ai./ha as pre-emergence followed by DICAMBA @ 350 g ai/ha at 75 DAP is eﬀective for controlling binding weeds in",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_284:006,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_284,6,sugarcane. Tying and Wrapping: These operations are most essential in sugarcane cultivation just to provide mechanical support to the grown-up plants to prevent lodging. The leaves are removed from the plants and wrapped together by taking all canes in one bundle. Tying should be done in the month of August when cane reaches about 2 m height. Green leaves should not be tied up together while tying up the crop. 269268,e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
