ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_287:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_287,5,"Plano␀ix @ 20 ml per 100 liters of water at pea stage of fruits. Keep the suf␀icient moisture in the orchard basin. For the control of Powdery mildew and Die-back diseases, spray of Karathen 48% EC @ 200ml/200lit. Spray Thiamethoxam 25% (Actora) @ 40g/200lit. of water for the control of mango hopper and mealy bug. Peach & Plum Litchi Maintain suf␀icient and consistent moisture during May -June to prevent fruit cracking. Mulching with grass around tree basin is helpful for moisture conservation. Spraying of Neem oil@ 400ml/200 L.of water before ␀lowering to avoid egg laying for the management of Litchi fruit borer. Second spray of Novaluron 10 EC 300 ml/ 200 litre of water after fruit attains the clove size (at 10- 12 days after fruit set) and third spray of Emamectin benzoate 5% SG @ 80g/ 200 L of water during aril (pulp) development stage which comes 25-30 days after fruit set. Spray Zinc sulphate 2 Kg + Lime 1 Kg in 200 liters of water to control die back of branches due to de␀iciency of zinc in the orchard. Copper based fungicide i.e. Copper 271270",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_288:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_288,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 oxychloride 50% WP @ 600 g per 200 litres of water can be applied during rainy season to prevent Anthracnose. Set up Fruit ␀ly trap (Methyl eugenol trap) in the orchard @ 25/ha for the control of fruit ␀ly. Quinalphos 25% EC (Ekalux® @ 2 ml/L + neem oil (Eco-neem Plus @ 3ml/L.) will help in controlling fruit ␀lies under their high population situation in mango Tomato For the control of Gummosis, Canker and Die back problem in the orchard, spray Copper oxychloride 50 % WP @ 600 g/ 200 litres of water during June-July. Spray Zinc sulphate 1 Kg + Lime 500 g in 200 litres of water to control zinc de␀iciency during last week of April and mid of September. VEGETABLE CROPS Varieties Pusa Ruby, Pant T-3 and Hybrid varieties Indam 1313, Himsohna, Kranti, Shivay, Abhilash, Himshikhar etc., are suitable for cultivation. Earthing up and staking in summer tomato may be completed by end of April by adding split N dose. Remaining Nitrogen can be applied at one-month interval thereafter. For Kharif tomato, nursery raising of varieties like Indam 1313, Himsona, Himshikhar etc., may be started in the month of February and transplanting should be completed by mid-April.",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_288:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_288,2,"For the management of Early blight, Buck eye- rot and Fruit rot diseases apply Copper oxychloride @ 3g/L, Rhidomil MZ @ 2.5 g/L and Mancozeb 45 @ 2.5 g or Kavach @ 2g/L respectively as and when symptoms appear. Some other eﬀective fungicides are Azo-oxy-strobin 23%@0.5 -1.0 ml per litre and Tabuconozol 38%@ 1ml per liter. For the management of fruit borer, apply Profenofos @ 1ml/L or Chlorpyriphos @ 2ml or Cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml per litre of water. In areas where blossom end rot is problem apply Calcium chloride @ 5g/L of water as foliar application Capsicum Transplanting of capsicum using California wonder, Hungtinton, Bharat and other suitable hybrids may be completed by end of April using NPK @ 100:75:55 before sowing with Nitrogen in 3 splits (30, 60 90 DAT). For the management of Powdery mildew and Fruit rot diseases use Hexaconazole or Contaf @ 0.5 ml/L and Mancozeb 45 or Rhidomil MZ @ 2.5 g/L as and when symptoms appear in the standing crop. For the management of fruit borer apply Lambda cyhalothrin @ 0.8 ml/L or Acephate @ 1 g/L or Flubendiamide @ 0.2 g/L; and Imidacloprid @ 0.5 ml for sucking pests. Cucurbits Transplanting of cucurbit seedlings must be completed by April",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_288:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_288,3,"end using FYM and Fertilizers (NPK @ 100:50:60 before sowing with Nitrogen in 3 split doses at 30, 45, 70DAT. For fruit ␀ly management, install Fruit Fly traps @ 25 traps per ha in May and use Malathion 30 ml + Gur 150 g per 15 L water at 15 days interval. Use Bavistin 1g + Mancozeb 45 2g per litre of water for management of fungal diseases and Imidacloprid @ 0.5 ml per litre for the management of sucking pests. Citrus Uttarakhand COLE CROPS Brinjal Transplanting of brinjal may be completed by April end. Apply Cypermethrin @ 1ml/L at ␀lowering for management of brinjal Fruit & Shoot borer. For the management of Phomopsis blight apply COC @ 3g/L or Ridomil MZ @ 2.5 g/L French bean Chilli To avoid damping oﬀ disease seed treatment with Carbendazim, Mancozeb can be done. To control viral diseases the infected plants should be uprooted and burnt or buried to avoid further infection. Suitable insecticidal sprays reduce the incidence of viral diseases, since majority of viral diseases are transmitted by insect vectors. Drenching with 1% Bordeaux mixture or blue copper or Fytolan 0.25% may give protection against Fusarium wilt. White ␀ly which is the vector of viral diseases can be",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_288:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_288,4,"controlled by spraying Dimethoate 30% EC @660 ml/ha. Thrips may attack chilli and to control thrips spray Profenophos 20ml or neem seed oil 50 ml in 10 litre water. In case of severe attack, spray Spinosad 3ml/10 litre of water. Transplanting of cole crops in high areas can be started in the month of June using NPK @ 125:75:70 at the time of sowing with Nitrogen in 3 splits (30, 60 90DAT). Borax can be added for the management of browning in cauli␀lower. For the management of cutworms apply Cypermethrin 10EC @ 1ml/L of water Sowing of French bean using high yielding varieties (Bush type: Palam Mridula, Falguni, Anupama, Ragini, Arka Komal, Solan Naina, Contender, Bahaar Pole type: Luxmi, SVM-1, Moraleda, Padmini) could be completed by end of April or ␀irst week of May. Apply NPK @ 25:65:65 at the time of sowing following seed inoculation with Bavistin and Rhizobium culture. For weed management use pre-emergence herbicide Pendimethalin @ 1.5 kg/ ha. Management of Anthracnose and angular leaf spot diseases can be achieved by applying Bavistin @ 1g/L as and when symptoms appear in end May Okra Pusa Bhindi-5, Pusa Sawani, Pusa Makhmali can be sown during February-March for lower hills/",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_288:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_288,5,"plains and April to Mid-May in mid hills as summer crop and July for rainy season crop. Management practices should be followed to protect the vegetable crops from hot air. Irrigation management should be done early in the morning, at evening or during night time in vegetable crops as per availability and requirement of crop. For management of fruit borer in okra take a spray of Cypermethrin 10 % EC @ 15 ml or Quinalphos 25 % EC @ 20 ml per 10 liter of water. Harvesting of mature vegetables should be done early in the morning. Ginger For management of Rhizome rot seed can be treated with PBAT-3 like Carbendazim, Mancozeb, Copper oxychloride. Spraying of Axostrobin and tebuconazole @ 1.5-2 g/L of water can be done. Varieties like Himgiri, Rio De Janeiro can be sown during June month. 273272",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
