ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_300:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_300,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Select upland or medium up-land with good drainage facility for planting of seedling. Planting should be done in broad raised bed and furrow to avoid or minimize damage of planted seedling during heavy rain. Ensure mulching to reduce nutrient loss and conserve moisture. Barrier cropping with maize may be suitable option for sucking pest management. Marigold can be grown as trap crop for shoot and fruit borer, along with pheromone traps and Heli NPV. For controlling mites spraying of Diafenthiuron @ 12.5 g/15 L of water is or Etoxazole@ 1.5 ml/L is recommended. To improve fruit setting and to minimize ␀lower or immature fruit drop spray soluble B @ 1.5 g/L and NAA 4.5% W/W (Plano␀ix) @ 0.2 ml/L alternately at 10-12 days interval. Chilli leaf curl complex is the main threat and for controlling leaf curl complex a holistic approach is required. Scienti␀ic management of nursery bed through covering with 45 nylon mesh; carbofuran 3 G @ 2.5 kg/bigha during ␀inal land preparation and sowing of maize around the main ␀ield as border crop at 15 days prior to transplanting of chilli seedlings; spraying of castor oil @ 3 ml/L of water at 20 DAT; spraying",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_300:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_300,2,"Ofchlorfenapyr 10 SC @ 75 g a.i./ha at 35 DAT; spraying of Pymetrozine 50 WG + moringa root extract 10% w/v as tank mix @ 200 g a.i./ha + 5 ml/L of water at 55 DAT and spraying of Spirotetramat 11.01% + Imidacloprid 11.01% SC @ 55 g a.i./ha at 70-75 DAT. To control white␀ly in the main ␀ield installation of 60 yellow sticky traps/ha and spraying Pyri␀luquinazon of @ 1 g/L or Dimpropyridaz @ 0.5 ml/L at 15-day intervals is advocated or alternatively moringa root extract (10%) + A␀idopyropen/Flupyradifurone in 10:1 ratio can be used. Spraying of Flonicamid @ 0.5 g/L or A␀idopyropen@ 1 ml/litre to control aphid and jassid is recommended. Chilli Select improved varieties like Andhra Jyoti, Punjab Lal, and Arka Lohit, Arka Tejasvi etc. Seeds must be treated with Mancozeb + Carbendazim @ 2 g or T. viridae @ 10 g by dissolving in 10-12 ml water per kg seed. of water) after 7 days of sowing to control. To overcome bacterial wilt use grafted brinjal seedlings. Apply bleaching powder @ 15-18 kg/ha to soil before 1 month of planting to reduce the chance of bacterial wilt. Apply organic amendments like neem cake (5 q/ha) to reduce wilt incidence. Consider pre-colonized Trichoderma harzianum or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_300:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_300,3,"Pseudomonas ␀luorescens in soil applications for biocontrol. Select improved varieties for cultivation. Some improved varieties of cucumber are Japanese Long Green, Poinsette, Pusa Barkha, KPCH 2, Pusa Barkha, Pusa Uday, Pusa Barkha, Pusa Long Green, Swarna Sheetal etc. Some improved varieties of pumpkin- Arka Surjamukhi, Arka Chandan, Solan Badami can be grown. Cucumber and Pumpkin Seeds must be treated before sowing in nursery bed with Mancozeb + Carbendazim 2 g or Trichoderma viridae 10 g by dissolving in 10-12 ml water per kg seed. Select upland or medium up-land with good drainage facility. Seeds should be done in broad raised bed to avoid or minimize damage of planted seedling during heavy rain. West Bengal Select upland or medium up-land with good drainage facility. Seeds should be sown in broad raised bed to avoid or minimize damage of planted seedling during heavy rain. Ensure mulching to reduce nutrient loss and conserve moisture. To improve fruit setting and to minimize ␀lower or immature fruit drop spray soluble B @ 1.5 g/L and NAA 4.5% W/W (Plano␀ix) @ 0.2 ml/L alternately at 10-12 days interval. Train plants on trellis for better growth. Prune excess branches for",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_300:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_300,4,"sunlight and spray copper fungicides. Apply Ethrel @ 1.5-2.0 ml/10 L at 2-3 leaf stage and again, after 7 days for enhanced ␀lowering. Prefer foliar feeding over top dressing during rainy spells. Install cue-lure traps @ 20 nos./ac and replace lures every 15-20 days for controlling fruit ␀ly. Palam traps can also be installed @ 20 nos./ac to control male fruit ␀ly. To control white␀ly in the main ␀ield installation of 60 yellow sticky traps/ha and spraying Pyri␀luquinazon of @ 1 g/L or Dimpropyridaz @ 0.5 ml/L at 15-day intervals is advocated or alternatively moringa root extract (10%) + A␀idopyropen/ ␀lupyradifurone in 10:1 ratio can be used. For controlling fungal diseases apply spray Bavistin 1 g + Mancozeb 2 g/L of water or Trichoderma viridae @ 3 g/L of water. Ensure mulching to reduce nutrient loss and conserve moisture. To improve fruit setting and to minimize ␀lower or immature fruit drop spray soluble B @ 1.5 g/L and NAA 4.5% W/W (Plano␀ix) @ 0.2 ml/L, alternately at 10-12 days interval. Train plants on trellis for better growth. Prune excess branches for sunlight and spray copper fungicides. Apply Ethrel @ 1.5-2.0 ml/10 L at 2-3 leaf stage and again after 7 days for",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
