ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_302:001,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_302,1,"ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisory 2025 Maintain the boroz organically, as much as possible, with only organic manure, bio-pesticides and life saving irrigation. Avoiding inorganic fertilizers will increase plant defence against biotic and abiotic stresses. Spray micronutrient mixture having Ca, Zn, Mn, B and Mo @ 2 g/L of water at 2 months interval. Tricontanol (0.05%) should be sprayed thrice monthly during post-monsoon. To control white␀ly in the main ␀ield installation of 60 yellow sticky traps/ha & spraying pyri␀luquinazon of @ 1 g/L or Dimpropyridaz @ 0.5 ml/L at 15-day intervals is advocated or alternatively moringa root extract (10%) + A␀idopyropen / Flupyradifurone in 10:1 ratio can be used. Pre- and post- monsoon soil drench with 1% Bordeaux mixture followed by soil amendment with T. harzianum and P. ␀luorescens mixed compost/mustard oil cake during the month of May can prevent collar rot and during June to October can control Phytophthora foot rot and leaf rot. Farmers may sow seeds @ 250-300 gram/ac in the month of July and August under the low-cost shade house or net house for best result to get early seedling. Raised sapling may be planted in broad raised bed in open. However,",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_302:002,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_302,2,"for better result, one can cultivate it under poly-tunnel also. Betel Vine structure. Control weed applying pendimethalin @ 2 ml/L water as pre-emergent herbicide or oxy␀luorfen @ 1 ml/L at 10-15 DAT and/or oxygold @ 2 ml/L water, if weed infestation is heavy and yellowing of tip occurs. Select upland or medium up- land with good drainage facility. Saplings or vine cutting should be planted in broad raised bed to avoid or minimize damage of planted seedling during heavy rain. Use farm yard manure as much as possible. Application of ZnSO₄ @ 6 kg/ac as basal and spraying of chelated zinc @ 0.5 g/L of water and boron @ 1-1.5 g/L of water is recommended for better crop performance. In order to control thrips & aphids use Dimethoate @ 2 ml/L or Imidachloprid @ 1.5 ml/L of water. Tip burn is very common in kharif onion and to control it spray hexaconazole @ 2 ml/L water/acre. Elephant Foot Yam Treat soil with formalin at 1:50 ratio at least 30 days prior to planting. Treat vine cuttings by soaking in Streptocyclin solution (1 g/4 L of water) for 25 min followed treatment with 0.5% Bordeaux mixture. Select upland or medium up-land with good drainage facility. Saplings or vine cuttings",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_302:003,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_302,3,"should be planted in broad raised bed to avoid or minimize damage of planted seedling during heavy rain. Use 50% agro-shade net to maintain favourable micro-climate. Prune vines at 2 m height. Maintain boroj height of 2.5 m and apply soil rings at base after 2 m growth. Keep rhizosphere clean and ensure good drainage facility to reduce chance of collar rot disease. If symptoms appear then application of FYM and neem cake mixture (10:1) inoculated with Trichoderma harzianum @ 2.5 kg/t of FYM-neem cake mixture (KAU POP 2024) or spraying of Carbendazim + Mancozeb @ 2 g/L water is recommended. Early Cauli␀lower and Cabbage SPICE CROPS West Bengal Weeding and earthing up should be done within 45 to 60 days after planting. Crop may be aﬀected by rhizome rot, blight, anthracnose disease which can be controlled by soil application of Trichoderma and Pseudomonas @ 7.5 kg/ha or spraying of Carbendazim + Mancozeb @ 2 g/L of water. Pests like rhizome borer, leaf roller, aphid, scale insect may damage the crop and these can be controlled by apply Neem oil 10000 PPM @ 2 ml/L of water. Ginger Farmer are advised not to take full crop but to take only 30-40 % of present fruit stand and rest 60-70%",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_302:004,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_302,4,"should be sacri␀iced to obtain a good harvest in next winter (when the market price of the produce usually remains high). To remove/shed major portion of ␀lower or small fruit, spray 15% urea solution (150 g/L of water) or 50 ppm NAA (Plano␀ix @ 1.1 ml/L) and stop irrigating the crop. To control further fruit drop, spray NAA 4.5% W/W (Plano␀ix) @ 0.2 ml/L at 10-12 days interval. Weeding and earthing up should be done within 45 to 60 days after planting. Crop may be aﬀected by rhizome rot, blight, anthracnose disease which can be controlled by soil application of Trichoderma and Pseudomonas @ 7.5 kg/ha or spraying of Carbendazim + Mancozeb @ 2 g/L water. Pests like rhizome borer, leaf roller, aphid, scale insect may damage the crop and these can be controlled by apply Neem oil 10000 PPM @ 2 ml/L of water. FRUIT CROPS Mango Guava Turmeric To control fruit drop spray NAA 4.5% W/W (Plano␀ix) @ 0.2 ml/L at 10-12 days interval. For better fruit development, spray n-triacontanol (Miraculan) @ 0.5 ml/L at 15 days interval. Keep suf␀icient moisture in the orchard basin. Mulching with straw or grass may be practiced for better soil moisture conservation. Apply Emamectin benzoate @ 0.5 g/L or",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025:pdf_page_302:005,ICAR_KHARIF_STATE_ADVISORIES_2025,initial_verified_action_rag,ICAR Kharif Agro-Advisories for Farmers 2025,Indian Council of Agricultural Research,regional_policy,frozen_regional_policy_context,"State-specific chapters; this registry uses only the Haryana & Delhi, Karnataka, Maharashtra and Rajasthan chapters for compatible kharif sites",rice;maize;soybean;other kharif crops,fertilizer;crop_protection;crop_establishment,https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/Circulars/ICAR-En-Kharif-Agro-Advisories-for-Farmers-2025.pdf,2025-05-31,,May 2025,pdf_page_302,5,"Spinetoram @ 0.6 ml/L to control fruit and shoot borer. Install methyl eugenol pheromone traps @ 30/ha and change lure every 15-20 days interval for controlling fruit ␀ly of mango. In order to control anthracnose disease in mango spray Tri␀loxystrobin + Tebuconazole @ 0.5 g/L water. Wrapping of fruits should be done with transparent polythene packets with a paper piece inside it to protect the fruit from direct sunlight. For better fruit colour and quality, apply amonium sulphate as source of N-fertilizer. For better fruit growth, soluble fertilizers like 19:19:19 @ 3 to 5 g/lit and any mixed micronutrient @ 1.5 to 2 g/L may be applied at 10-12 days interval. Spray N- triacontanol (Miraculan) @ 0.5 ml/L at 15 days interval. Install methyl eugenol pheromone traps @ 30 nos./ha and change lure every 15-20 days interval or spray poison bait (10 g jaggery + 2 ml dichlorvos in 1 L of water) for controlling fruit ␀ly of mango. Apply T. harzianum to the root zone, mixed with compost, to prevent Fusarium wilt. 287286",e674cd3b6a214696d24d6876892cee6ffab3ae7e9499017f573c25690e1b901e
