ICAR_CRIDA_PB_LUDHIANA_CONTINGENCY:pdf_page_1:001,ICAR_CRIDA_PB_LUDHIANA_CONTINGENCY,expanded_icariisr_crida,"ICAR-CRIDA district weather contingency document — Ludhiana, Punjab",ICAR–Central Research Institute for Dryland Agriculture,district_historical_context,historical_district_context_only,"Ludhiana, Punjab district",rice,weather contingency,https://icar-crida.res.in/CCP/PB/Ludhiana/3.11.pdf,,,historical_date_not_extracted,pdf_page_1,1,"Unusual rains (untimely, unseasonal etc) (for both rainfed and irrigated situations) Condition Suggested contingency measure Vegetative stage Flowering stage Crop maturity stage Post harvest Outbreak of pests and diseases due to unseasonal rains Rice - Blight develops more in high humid conditions. Farmers should not allow stagnation of water in the fields. If high humidity and cloudy weather prevails the crop may be sprayed with Blitox/ Copper oxychloride 50 WP @ 500 g in 200 litres of water/acre to control False smut and after 10 days of its application spray Tilt @ 200 ml/acre in 200 litres of water. Start the spray at the boot stage. -",b6d230844add42814781869d3c9e46a2daa456bfd0207332ca0e5b605b1f6921
