ICAR_CRIDA_PB_PATIALA_CONTINGENCY:pdf_page_1:001,ICAR_CRIDA_PB_PATIALA_CONTINGENCY,expanded_icariisr_crida,"ICAR-CRIDA district weather contingency document — Patiala, Punjab",ICAR–Central Research Institute for Dryland Agriculture,district_historical_context,historical_district_context_only,"Patiala, Punjab district",rice;wheat,weather contingency,https://icar-crida.res.in/CCP/PB/Patiala/3.11.pdf,,,historical_date_not_extracted,pdf_page_1,1,"Unusual rains (untimely, unseasonal etc) (for both rainfed and irrigated situations) Condition Suggested contingency measure Vegetative stage Flowering stage Crop maturity stage Post harvest Outbreak of pests and diseases due to unseasonal rains Rice Blight develops more in high humid conditions. Farmers should not allow stagnation of water in the fields. If high humidity and cloudy weather prevails the crop may be sprayed with Blitox/ Copper oxychloride 50 WP @ 500 g in 200 litres of water/acre to control False smut and after 10 days of its application spray Tilt @ 200 ml/acre in 200 litres of water. Start the spray at the boot stage. Wheat",0ee25ae7a55b89c60cc947a4cb4ced615d2ba2e4140daec47e9e20d8611ce6ec
ICAR_CRIDA_PB_PATIALA_CONTINGENCY:pdf_page_2:001,ICAR_CRIDA_PB_PATIALA_CONTINGENCY,expanded_icariisr_crida,"ICAR-CRIDA district weather contingency document — Patiala, Punjab",ICAR–Central Research Institute for Dryland Agriculture,district_historical_context,historical_district_context_only,"Patiala, Punjab district",rice;wheat,weather contingency,https://icar-crida.res.in/CCP/PB/Patiala/3.11.pdf,,,historical_date_not_extracted,pdf_page_2,1,"Cotton Sugarcane Horticulture Crop1 In case of occurrence of root damage due to water stagnation in Pear, Peach etc. apply 10 g Bavistin 50 WP + 5 g Vitavax 75 WP in 10 litres of water along the trunk after draining out the excess water and drying of soil. Prune the dried ends of the branches alongwith 5-8 cm of the live wood.",0ee25ae7a55b89c60cc947a4cb4ced615d2ba2e4140daec47e9e20d8611ce6ec
